window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_INFINITE_MANA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":4901,"title":"Chapter 4901: Chapter 4900: The Second Cause II","paragraphs":["As immense changes began to unfold across Observable Existence, in THE Infiniverse, Noah’s body that had been discussing with THE Mnemonic Leviathan was forced to pause.","He sensed the many changes that were occurring through different bodies as he was currently in multiple positions across Observable Existence. One body wrapped protective Infinities around THE Great Usurper and his companions as proto-matter flooded THE Wastes. Another body raced alongside THE Primordial Paradox toward the Crack in THE Agora. Another sensed as THE Infiniverse bellowed with authority and funneled corrupted undifferentiation into her budding singularity.","The eruption of power caused him to think about many things. The synchronicity of it all pointed toward deliberate orchestration rather than natural disaster. Someone had initiated this, and whoever they were possessed the capability to affect every corner of Observable Existence simultaneously, and of course...","Before he could theorize too much regarding what was coming, the ancient voice of the lazy dolphin in front of him began to talk. This creature with all the knowledge, or most of the knowledge in Observable Existence, spoke with weight that demanded attention despite the chaos unfolding around them.","\" The Vakochev Scales of Existence whisper the names of some who are grand and distinguished.\"","Her massive form shifted in the stellar seas of Muspelheim as her eyes, ancient beyond measure, fixed upon Noah with intensity that belied her typically sleepy demeanor.","\" Not all who achieve power earn such whispers. But there are those whose actions resonate so profoundly through the foundations of Existence that the Scales themselves take notice, recording their deeds as reference points for all who might follow. One such being is Masamuk, whose name I speak now so that you might understand what is unfolding around us.\"","...!","She had begun to babble about some nonsense, and Noah almost asked what any of this had to do with the proto-matter currently flooding across Observable Existence. But when she spoke the last sentence, when she connected this ancient history to current events, he fell quiet and continued to listen.","THE Mnemonic Leviathan continued with a voice that held the weight of memories accumulated across eons.","\"In the age before ages, when Existence was young and the boundaries between what was and what was not remained fluid and uncertain, there existed a being who looked upon the formless expanse of primordial Chaos and saw within it the potential for something greater. This being was Masamuk, and unlike those who came before, Masamuk did not merely exist within Chaos or alongside it. Masamuk acted upon it with intention.\"","Her massive tail shifted through the stellar currents as she spoke.","\" Masamuk split the body of Chaos itself. Not with authority, for authority as we understand it had not yet been differentiated from raw potential. Masamuk split Chaos through the sheer force of will that declared division where unity had reigned since before time learned to flow. The act was violent and beautiful and necessary, a severing that created possibility where only homogeneity had existed before.\"","\" From the halves of that sundered Chaos, Masamuk fashioned the territories that would become the first Domains. These were not Primordial Realms as you know them, not structured territories governed by laws and principles. They were the precursors to such things, the rough sketches from which later beings would learn to draw their own weavings. Masamuk looked upon the divided Chaos and shaped it, molded it, convinced it to remember the forms that Masamuk envisioned rather than collapsing back into undifferentiated potential.\"","Her eyes grew distant as if she was recalling whispers that echoed across dimensions Noah couldn’t perceive.","\" This was the first great Cause of differentiation through Chaos under the record of Masamuk, as only at this time did he become a true follower of Vakochev. Masamuk understood something that many beings across eons would fail to grasp: that Chaos is not the enemy of creation but its raw material. That undifferentiation is not the opposite of civilization but the clay from which civilization is sculpted. By splitting Chaos rather than fleeing from it or being consumed by it, Masamuk demonstrated that the formless could be given form by those with sufficient will and vision.\"","\" Through this act, Masamuk embarked upon a Civilization unlike any that had existed before, becoming worthy of having his name whispered across the Scales of Existence. The methodology that Masamuk pioneered became the path that others would walk.\"","\" The Scales of Existence recorded Masamuk’s name not because of power accumulated or enemies defeated, but because Masamuk changed the fundamental nature of what existence could be in his domains. This is what it means to walk a grand path. This is what it means to earn The Whisper of THE Scales.\"","...!","THE Mnemonic Leviathan dropped such ridiculous bombs casually, as if she was discussing the musings of minor things.","Noah was wondering in the beginning as to who this Masamuk could refer to, but it now became abundantly clear that they weren’t even someone belonging to what he knew as Observable Existence. Yet their names were whispered in the Vakochev Scales of Existence, recorded as reference points for all who might follow.","This led him to ask himself a question that he had not considered before.","How could he hear these same whispers that THE Mnemonic Leviathan heard?","Was this also the same way that THE Primordial Paradox came to know regarding adversity and hardship being required toward THE Second Scale of Existence? Had THE Primordial Paradox heard whispers from the Scales that told him what was necessary for progression?","As Noah was thinking all of this, THE Mnemonic Leviathan continued with her ancient voice that held the weight of accumulated knowledge.","\" Another such being is Ongatala, whose methodology differed from Masamuk’s but whose impact proved equally profound. Where Masamuk looked outward and divided external Chaos, Ongatala looked inward and created internal structure. Where Masamuk fashioned Domains from the halves of what was split, Ongatala fashioned lands from what was scattered within the depths of self.\"","...!"]},{"number":4902,"title":"Chapter 4902: Chapter 4901: The Second Cause III","paragraphs":["Her form drifted closer to Noah as she spoke.","\" Ongatala descended into the waters of nothing. I speak not of metaphor but of literal action that defies easy comprehension. There existed, in those early ages, spaces that held no substance whatsoever. Not emptiness, for emptiness implies the absence of something that could be present. These were waters of nothing, expanses where existence itself had not yet decided whether to manifest. Ongatala entered these spaces willingly, diving deeper and deeper into the void that consumed all definition.\"","\" Within those waters of nothing, Ongatala scattered soil. From where did this soil come? From Ongatala’s own existence. From foundations that Ongatala sacrificed in order to create something greater than self-preservation. Each grain of scattered soil was a piece of Ongatala’s being, distributed across the nothing with intention that demanded reality acknowledge what was being given. And reality, faced with such deliberate sacrifice, had no choice but to comply.\"","...!","\" The scattered soil became the first lands within Ongatala’s own structure. A being who was once singular became a being who contained territories, a being whose internal landscape held mountains and valleys and spaces where other existences could eventually take root. This was differentiation turned inward, a Cause that proved one did not need external Chaos to divide. One could divide oneself and become greater through the division.\"","\" Ongatala’s path demonstrated that the grand acts of existence need not be conquests or external transformations. Sometimes the most profound changes occur within, when a being chooses to become a territory rather than merely occupy one. The lands that Ongatala created within eventually became templates for how internal Civilizations could be structured, how beings could cultivate not just their power but their inner landscapes.\"","...!","THE Mnemonic Leviathan paused at this moment, and her ancient gaze turned away from Noah. She looked toward the humanoid form of THE Infiniverse who floated in the distance, her other body still working to contain and redirect the corrupted proto-matter that had invaded her master’s domain.","\"I find her unique.\"","Her voice held something that might have been wonder.","\" Her weavings remind me of the whispers and stories of Ongatala. A being who chose to become a territory rather than merely occupy one. A being whose internal landscape holds realms and spaces where other existences take root. She is walking a path that echoes across the Scales, whether she knows it or not.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes became even sharper at these words, his attention now fully locked upon THE Mnemonic Leviathan as she turned back to face him.","\"I tell you of Masamuk and Ongatala because what is happening right now, this emergence of corrupted proto-matter across Observable Existence, is something similar. Whoever initiated this is walking a grand path. They are attempting to reshape the fundamental nature of what Observable Existence can be. They are using proto-matter as Masamuk used Chaos, as Ongatala used the waters of nothing. They are attempting a Cause of differentiation through undifferentiation, a paradox... a paradox... a glorious paradox.\"","Her ancient eyes held weight that pressed against Noah’s existence.","\" The Scales of Existence may whisper. They may whisper his name if he is successful in this gambit. Whether that name will be remembered as pioneer or catastrophe remains to be seen. But the magnitude of what is being attempted cannot be denied. Someone is walking in the footsteps of Masamuk and Ongatala. Someone is attempting to reshape existence itself.\"","BOOM!","Noah’s expression became heavy at these words.","Fuck.","Paradox. Corruption. Change across Observable Existence. Noah instantly honed in on THE Living Paradox as it seemed far too many people were underestimating this being, himself included. THE Living Paradox had now done something or begun embarking on something unfathomably grand!","His own Cause!","Though it wouldn’t be the same as THE First Cause, so was THE Living Paradox attempting a Second Cause? Was that what this terrifying change was? An attempt to reshape Observable Existence itself through flooding it with corrupted proto-matter?","If THE Living Paradox succeeded in whatever his final grand design was...it truly was not clear who would be the victor in this eon long war!","---","At the center of THE Infiniverse, in a realm of concentrated authority that no being but her master could survive, THE Infiniverse worked alone.","Multicolored light suffused everything around her as boundless seas of Infinite Seals of Absolute Tongue swirled and merged and created patterns of power that defied comprehension.","And before her, the crack in reality continued to spew corrupted proto-matter with force that would have overwhelmed any other territory in Observable Existence.","She funneled it into the singularity she had been building, her will pressing against the corruption with authority that refused to acknowledge its threat. The budding domain at the center of her working consumed the proto-matter greedily, growing denser and more defined with each passing moment. What THE Living Paradox had intended as an attack was becoming fuel for her creation.","But as she worked, as she directed the endless flood into her forming domain, the words of THE Mnemonic Leviathan echoed through her consciousness.","\" Ongatala descended into the waters of nothing.\"","She repeated the phrase silently as she continued her work, her hands guiding corrupted proto-matter into channels that led to the singularity.","\" Within those waters of nothing, Ongatala scattered soil. From Ongatala’s own existence. From foundations that Ongatala sacrificed in order to create something greater than self-preservation...\"","Her movements slowed as the words resonated through her being with weight that demanded attention.","\" Each grain of scattered soil was a piece of Ongatala’s being, distributed across the nothing with intention that demanded reality acknowledge what was being given.\"","...!","THE Infiniverse stopped.","Her eyes, which burned with the Infinities of her master, began to shine even brighter as understanding bloomed within her consciousness. THE Mnemonic Leviathan had said that her weavings reminded her of Ongatala. That she was walking a path that echoed across the Scales of Existence.","But she had not been walking that path fully.","She had been containing. She had been directing. She had been building a domain within herself, yes, but she had been doing so defensively and reactively.","Ongatala had not merely received the waters of nothing.","Ongatala had descended into them willingly.","Ongatala had scattered soil with purpose.","THE Infiniverse looked at the crack of Observable Existence that had formed within her core, that wound in reality through which corrupted proto-matter continued to surge. It was a violation of her territory, an intrusion that she had been working to minimize and contain.","But what if she didn’t minimize it?","What if she didn’t contain it?","What if she made it...bigger?","Her eyes blazed with light that painted her multicolored realm in shades of blue-gold brilliance as the epiphany crystallized into decision. She was THE Infiniverse. She was the domain of THE Genesis Monarch himself. She contained a Primordial Realm within her structure alongside Wheel of Existence, Folds, and so much more.","And her foundations grew alongside her master’s Infinite nature without theoretical ceiling.","She was not prey to be overwhelmed by corrupted proto-matter.","She was grand, and she...would scatter her soil across the waters of nothing.","...!","Her figure pulsed with determination."]},{"number":4903,"title":"Chapter 4903: Chapter 4902: The Second Cause IV","paragraphs":["THE Infiniverse raised her hands toward the crack and made a move that would have seemed like madness to any observer.","She tore it wider.","BOOM!","The crack expanded under her authority, its edges spreading apart as she commanded reality itself to open further rather than close. What had been a wound became a gateway. What had been an intrusion became an invitation. And through that expanded crack, seas of corrupted proto-matter surged out with force that exceeded everything that had come before!","The corruption flooded into her core with violence that should have been catastrophic!","But THE Infiniverse was ready.","From her existence, from the foundations that comprised her being, she began to release Infinite Absolute Seals in quantities that would have drained any other entity entirely. Endless seals of The First Tongue scattered into the surging proto-matter like soil being distributed across the waters of nothing.","This was her endless soil!","These were the pieces of her existence that she was sacrificing in order to create something greater than mere survival!","The Infinite Seals merged with the corrupted proto-matter, their blue-gold light suffusing the undifferentiated potential with the signature of THE Genesis Monarch himself. The corruption didn’t disappear, but it changed. It became something hybrid, something that held both the undifferentiation of THE Prima Indifferentia and the Infinite nature of her master’s authority.","And then THE Infiniverse did something even more drastic.","One, she allowed this blue gold brilliance to flow into the crack and spread out in different directions across it, so it could mix with that sea and flow to any other areas that Proto-matter was flowing across Observable Existence.","Two...","She formed a channel.","Not inward toward her singularity, but outward toward THE Wastes where in a small corner, another body of her master currently protected THE Great Usurper and his companions from the very corruption she now commanded.","The channel punched through her boundaries with precision of absolute control, creating a pathway through which her newly transformed proto-matter could flow.","And flow it did!","Endless seas of corrupted proto-matter filled with Noah’s Infinite Seals of Absolute Tongue flooded out across existence through the channel she had created! The corruption that THE Living Paradox had sent to overwhelm and change Observable Existence now carried the signature of THE Genesis Monarch within its depths!","It was like seeing someone initiate an avelance or and endless train, and then jumping on it to obtain the benefits of their hard work as well!","Every wave of undifferentiation that washed across THE Wastes in this area and beyond now scattered Infinite Seals like soil being distributed across the waters of nothing!","And as the endless seas of infinity also flooded into the Crack of Observable Existence, she sought for them to flow out from other sources or cracks as fully and truly...the aspect of Infinity of Noah’s weavings was allowed to express itself here.","It survived the corrupted proto-matter because...it was Infinite. Just like against Bazuman, it couldnt be differentiated further.","It flowed.","Oh, it flowed!","Everywhere the proto-matter spread, Infinite Seals would spread alongside it. Everywhere the undifferentiation touched, the blue-gold light of THE Genesis Monarch would touch as well.","If THE Living Paradox wanted to reshape Observable Existence through flooding it with proto-matter, then THE Infiniverse would ensure that what emerged from that reshaping...they would have a large piece of the pie.","She continued to scatter her soil, continued to release Infinite Seals into the surging seas, continued to transform corruption into conquest with unfathomable immensity!","---","Far from the wonders and actions of THE Infiniverse.","In THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, Noah and THE Primordial Paradox arrived before the expanded Crack of Observable Existence with speed that made distance meaningless.","What they witnessed was chaos unlike anything THE Agora had experienced in its entire history.","The Crack that had existed peacefully at the heart of THE Acropolis for eons had been torn wider, its edges burning with light that belonged to no part of Observable Existence. Through that expanded fracture, corrupted proto-matter flooded outward in endless waves that threatened to dissolve everything they touched.","The undifferentiation carried the signature of THE Fallout within its depths, a corruption that went beyond mere formlessness into something actively hostile.","And standing against this tide were the other Strategoi of THE Agora.","Glossikos held her position closest to the Crack, her luminous dryad form radiating authority as she attempted to impose definition upon the undifferentiated flood. Her voice rang out with Embodiments that declared what the proto-matter was not, trying to negate its spread through sheer linguistic authority.","Ontikos stood beside her with the calm weight of Existence itself pressing outward from his form. His methodology was different, attempting to convince the proto-matter that it already existed as something defined rather than something formless. The approach should have worked against normal undifferentiation.","It wasn’t working.","Khaotikos flanked their fellow Strategoi, their own authorities adding to the combined effort.","As soos as Paradoxos arrived back, Paradox wove contradictions into the flood, trying to make the proto-matter uncertain about whether it was differentiated or not.","Chaos attempted to destabilize the corruption’s unified flow, to break it into fragments that could be dealt with individually.","None of it was enough!","The Crack continued to expand despite their efforts, and the proto-matter continued to surge with force that slowly pushed the four Absolutes backward. They were losing ground inch by inch, and if this continued, THE Agora itself would be covered!","Noah’s eyes pulsed with Immensity soon after as if he sensed something that the others couldn’t perceive.","’Fucking...’","His eyes shone sharply as if he couldn’t believe what he felt!","Something was coming through the Crack. Something was using the corruption as cover for its approach. Something was about to strike!","A page containing a defensive Inscription instantly appeared before the dryad body of Glossikos, the golden sheet burning with blue-gold light as it materialized from Noah’s reserves of Inscriptiones Dormientes. The Sleeping Inscription awakened at his command, its Apophasis blazing to life with authority that declared protection through negation.","|The one shielded by this Inscription is not capable of being consumed. Their existence is not susceptible to what seeks to devour. Their definition is not something that can be unmade by forces of undifferentiation. This truth persists so long as the foundation of the attacker does not exceed the foundation of the one who wrote these words.|","HUUM!","The Apophasis shone with brilliant blue-gold light just as jaws of undifferentiation closed in on Glossikos from within the proto-matter flood!","Massive. Hungry. Invisible until the moment of attack!","The jaws would have devoured her with the light of undifferentiation, would have consumed an Absolute Strategos as casually as a beast consuming prey!"]},{"number":4904,"title":"Chapter 4904: Chapter 4903: The Second Cause V","paragraphs":["But the defensive Inscription’s Apophasis caused them to pause, the negation pressing against the attack with authority that declared this consumption was not possible!","The jaws snapped shut on nothing, their target protected by words that Noah had written!","THE Primordial Paradox made a move in that same instant, his obsidian form blurring with speed that exceeded what should have been possible. Paradoxical authority wrapped around the shocked Glossikos and the other three Strategoi, pulling them away from the Crack with force that brooked no resistance.","He deposited them behind Noah and himself with a calm and glorious expression that held no fear despite what had just nearly occurred!","Glossikos looked towards Noah with a shocked gaze as she touched her body, half expecting it be undifferentiated.","But she had been saved as she saw that radiant golden page which actually still burned in front of her as it felt...glorious and immense!","This...was his power now!?","\" We...are no longer alone.\"","His voice was steady.","...!","And then, from the Crack, something emerged.","Noah watched with eyes that saw everything clearly as a figure he had not truly missed made its entrance into Observable Existence. The jaws that had just tried to devour Glossikos didn’t disappear but rather pulled back toward their source, revealing themselves as merely one small part of something far larger.","Bazuman.","Bazuman!","THE Undivided One that had chased Noah across THE Prima Indifferentia with relentless hunger emerged from the expanded Crack with the casual grace of a predator entering territory it intended to claim. Its body was round and glorious, a horror that defied conventional description through its sheer wrongness. Countless eyes dotted its surface in patterns that shifted constantly, each one burning with crimson light that held intelligence and hunger in equal measure.","Tentacles extended from its mass in every direction, writhing appendages that ended in mouths or eyes or configurations that served purposes Noah couldn’t identify. The body itself seemed to pulse with internal rhythms that didn’t match any biological function, as if it was breathing existence rather than air.","And covering every inch of its horrific form, the light of corrupted proto-matter burned with brilliance that painted the surrounding space in shades of wrongness. Bazuman had bathed in the corruption, had absorbed it, had made it part of itself.","Those countless crimson eyes all turned toward Noah with fucking.. giddiness.","And Bazuman spoke with a voice that emerged from every mouth simultaneously, each one contributing to words that pressed against reality with weight that exceeded what Noah remembered from their previous encounters.","\" You... have run away from me across time.\"","The voice was eerie and pleased and utterly certain of its own supremacy.","\" And yet existence brings us together again, little thing.\"","Those countless eyes blinked in patterns that might have been amusement.","\"I have waited. I have been patient. I knew that eventually, you would return to where you belonged. And here you are. Here we are. Together again.\"","Its tentacles spread wider as if embracing the entirety of THE Agora.","\" This time, there is nowhere left to run.\"","...!","Noah looked at Bazuman with an expression that held no fear.","Well, since he had come back from Prima Indifferentia, he had gotten a few precious moments to breathe before adversity thundered down again.","The last time he had encountered this Undivided One, he had been forced to flee. He had been weaker then, less refined, still learning what his Infinities could accomplish. He had used tricks and misdirection and ultimately temporal displacement to escape.","What about...now?","He knew it was a high ask. He actually knew it should be impossible. But hey, why not try?","At this moment in time, there were many things Noah could say or do but while he looked at Bazuman...he directed his words towards the calm Primordial Paradox beside him.","\"This whole time, I had a bias that in the future, THE Creature and you would win over THE Living Paradox. There may be some hiccups here and there, but victory would be in place. But based on what is happening right now...\"","He thought of THE Mnemonic Leviathan’s words. Of what THE Living Paradox was truly attempting.","He shook his head as he focused on the giddy Bazuman as he continued.","\"We may be underestimating THE Living Paradox far too much. He...might surprise everyone.\"","...!","His words were heavy, and they may not even be fitting as the terrifying aura of an Undivided One stood before them.","But he felt like saying them, and so he did.","Beside him, THE Primordial Paradox was thoughtful before he nodded.","\"Mm. It seems my disciple has come far. But first, there is this.\"","...!","This.","THE Undivided One!","Their gazes fully turned towards it as it radiated shocking waves of brutality and immensity.","---","Far from THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","In Alfheimr , THE Creature remained calm.","Endless seas of corrupted undifferentiation had spilled out from a blooming crack above his mountain, the proto-matter flooding across the radiant twilight with force that began dissolving the ancient landscapes of his Primordial Realm. Trees that had existed since before THE Infinite Unfurling came apart at the seams. Mountains that had witnessed the birth of civilizations crumbled into formless potential.","And from within that corruption, terrifying auras had bloomed.","Three figures had emerged from the crack with hunger that pressed against reality itself.","The first was an Undivided One whose body resembled a great winged lion with the face of something that had never been mortal. Its mane was made of writhing serpents that hissed with individual malice, and its wings stretched wide enough to cast shadows across entire territories. Where its paws touched, existence forgot what solidity meant. This one descended toward the lower slopes where THE Living Emotive and THE Living Elemental currently stood.","The second was another Undivided One, this one taking the form of a massive serpent-dragon whose scales shifted between states of matter with each breath. Its body coiled through the corrupted proto-matter as if swimming through water, and from its back rose seven heads that each bore different expressions of hunger. Eyes of molten gold fixed upon THE Creature’s temple with desire.","The third was a Formless Terror, and unlike THE Undivided Ones, it had no stable shape whatsoever. It was a churning mass of potential that occasionally resolved into hints of forms before collapsing back into chaos. Claws appeared and vanished. Jaws manifested and dissolved. It was hunger without direction, destruction without purpose, and it drifted toward THE Creature alongside the serpent-dragon with the inevitability of a tide coming in.","THE Creature observed all of this from his temple with eyes that held multicolored flames burning within their depths.","Below his mountain, THE Living Elemental was struggling. The curse that Noah had written upon him continued its relentless work, burning across his Depths and deteriorating his foundations with every passing moment. He could barely stand, let alone defend himself against the winged lion that descended toward him with killing intent!"]},{"number":4905,"title":"Chapter 4905: Chapter 4904: The Second Cause VI","paragraphs":["THE Living Emotive stood between THE Undivided One and her fallen companion, her colorful hair blazing with authority as she released Embodiment after Embodiment against the approaching horror.","|Emotions are the foundation of existence! Fear shall become my weapon, and the fear you feel at facing an Absolute shall consume you!|","BOOM!","Her Embodiment crashed against the winged lion with force that would have devastated any weak Absolute!","THE Undivided One didn’t even slow down.","It passed through her Embodiment as if it were mist, its serpent-mane hissing with amusement at her attempt to weaponize its emotions. This creature had existed since before emotions were differentiated from raw experience. It did not know fear. It only knew hunger.","Emotive released another Embodiment, and another, her voice growing more desperate amd grand with each Embodiment that failed to halt the approaching predator.","\" Rage shall become a wall! Fury shall become a shield! The intensity of my passion shall-\"","BOOM!","THE Undivided One’s paw swiped through her Embodiment and caught her across the torso, sending her tumbling down the mountainside with force that cracked the ancient stone beneath her impact.","She looked up at THE Creature’s temple with fury and desperation blazing in her eyes.","\" CREATURE! HELP US!\"","Her voice rang across Alfheimr with the weight of an Absolute’s full attention.","THE Creature remained in his temple, his multicolored flames burning steadily as he looked at THE Undivided One and THE Formless Terror approaching his position. The words of Emotive rang in his ears, demanding response, demanding action, demanding that he save her from the horror that was about to devour her.","But...","He spoke with a voice that held the authority of Existence itself.","\" Adversity is good for your existence.\"","His tone was calm, almost gentle.","\" See if you can get out of it yourself first.\"","...!","Below the mountain, Emotive’s expression transformed from desperation into absolute rage. THE Undivided One was approaching her fallen position with leisurely pace, savoring the moment before consumption. Elemental lay nearby, trembling with pain that he couldn’t suppress, unable to contribute anything to their defense.","\" YOU...!\"","Emotive’s voice burned with fury that transcended her usual manic energy.","\"If I die, I will haunt you endlessly, O Creature! I will haunt you! I will-\"","THE Creature was no longer listening.","His attention had turned fully to THE Undivided One and THE Formless Terror that approached his temple with hunger written across every aspect of their being. The serpent-dragon’s seven heads all oriented toward him with anticipation. THE Formless Terror churned with increased intensity as it drew closer to prey that radiated more authority than anything it had encountered in eons.","They looked at THE Creature hungrily.","They saw an Absolute surrounded by multicolored flames.","They saw a meal beyond anything they had consumed before!","They did not see what THE Creature truly was.","THE Creature spoke a single measly Embodiment.","\" Existence...acknowledges my grasp.\"","The words were simple. Almost casual. They held none of the elaborate declarations that other Absolutes used, none of the lengthy descriptions of authority and power that Embodiments typically contained.","And yet.","BOOM!","THE Creature stretched his hands outward from his temple, his multicolored flames extending with them as his authority pressed against reality with weight that defied comprehension.","The serpent-dragon, whose coiled body stretched for miles across the corrupted proto-matter, suddenly found itself shrinking. Not shrinking in the sense of becoming smaller, but shrinking in the sense of being compressed, being contained, being forced into a space that its existence should not have been able to occupy.","THE Formless Terror, whose churning mass had no fixed boundaries, suddenly found those boundaries being defined against its will. It was being given form. It was being forced into shape. It was being compressed alongside the serpent-dragon with authority that brooked no resistance.","Both of them ended up in THE Creature’s palm.","THE Undivided One that had been miles long now fit within his grasp. THE Formless Terror that had been an ocean of potential now occupied the space between his fingers. They writhed and struggled and released authority that should have devastated everything around them, but THE Creature’s definition of existence overwrote their definitions entirely.","He was the glimmer of Existence.","They existed only because he permitted it.","And now, he chose not to permit it.","THE Creature squeezed.","The sound that emerged was not a sound at all, but rather the absence of sound where existence was being unmade. The serpent-dragon’s seven heads screamed silently as their forms compressed beyond what any form could sustain. THE Formless Terror churned with desperate intensity as the chaos that comprised its being was forced into order, into structure, into definition that it had never possessed and could not survive.","They became mush in his palm.","THE Undivided One and THE Formless Terror, beings that had existed since before THE Infinite Unfurling, became nothing more than paste squeezed between THE Creature’s fingers. Their authority, their power, their eons of accumulated existence, all of it compressed into something that could be held in a single hand.","THE Creature brought that hand to his mouth.","He threw what remained of their existence past his lips with casual grace, consuming the paste of two primordial entities as if it were nothing more than a light snack. His multicolored flames burned brighter for a moment as he absorbed what they had been, adding their weight to his own already incomprehensible foundations.","His figure continued to be shrouded with multicolored flames as he did such a thing, his expression never changing from its calm composure. This was not a battle to him. This was not even an inconvenience. This was simply maintenance, the removal of pests that had wandered too close.","Below the mountain, Emotive yelled out for him again as THE Undivided One drew closer to her position.","But THE Undivided One that was attacking her had frozen in place.","Its serpent-mane had stopped hissing.","Its wings had stopped beating.","Its eyes, which had held hunger moments before, now held something else entirely as they gazed upward at THE Creature’s temple.","Fear...bloomed.","THE Undivided One had just watched two beings of equivalent power and origin...become paste in THE Creature’s palm. It had just witnessed an Absolute demonstrate power that exceeded anything it had encountered in its entire existence!","Very few understood the power of THE Creature.","Very few... understood his Immensity."]},{"number":4906,"title":"Chapter 4906: Chapter 4905: The Information Paradox I","paragraphs":["Noah frankly had far too many things happening all at once across multiple bodies.","He was monitoring the terrifying process that THE Infiniverse had just started while also having another body in THE Interstices writing Inscriptions. Another body in THE Wastes was stabilizing THE Great Usurper alongside Ains and Skoll.","An illusory consciousness floated with Ul’moreth and THE Primordial Chaos in Alfheimr. And another body now stared at Bazuman, THE Undivided One, in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment as four Strategoi and THE Primordial Paradox stood beside him.","Truly, it was a lot on his plate, and lesser multitaskers would have crumbled under the weight of simultaneous existential crises unfolding across Observable Existence.","But in the midst of all of this...","| Master.|","THE Infiniverse sent him information as her mixing of the corrupted proto-matter with his Infinite Seals of Absolute Tongue made the two intertwine. They now flowed across different parts of existence as a hybrid substance that held both undifferentiation and Infinity within its depths.","In this mixing, there was a pulsing signal that was now being sent. A signal for communication between the Infinities of Noah and the corrupted proto-matter!","It was a unique thing as Noah could feel this signal for communication was paradoxical, with it existing in an undefined state as it had no power or capacity for action. Only communication in the span of an instant. If he accepted this signal, he would likely converse with whatever consciousness sent it within the span of an instant as no time would pass externally.","And this paradoxical signal caused Noah to be immensely curious as he already knew what its origins were.","So even though he was already multitasking on so many things, he designated this as an action that fell in line with what THE Infiniverse was already doing by jumping aboard a terrifying process. She had opened the floodgates, and now he would see what lay on the other side.","So...","He accepted the signal of communication as it was like neuronal signals coming together, as if existential synapses were communicating across the vast distances of Observable Existence!","And...","HUUM!","A part of his consciousness found itself drawn into a flash of singularities, eventually finding itself in a space between spaces that existed outside of normal reality.","Around him flickered seas of corrupted proto-matter and his Infinite Seals of Absolute Tongue swirling amidst each other as they reflected an endless multicolored sky above and a blue-gold sea below. The two substances wove through each other in patterns that spoke of forced coexistence, neither fully merging nor fully separating.","He had an illusory consciousness form here.","And a few meters away was the illusory consciousness of... THE Living Paradox.","Noah looked at the visage of this being that looked exactly like Schrodinger. He remained in that grand beggar-like attire as if he wanted to remember his origins even while wielding power that could reshape Observable Existence. He was looking toward Noah with surprise that seemed genuine.","It felt like such a long time had passed since Noah last talked to this being. He had gone back eons in time and come back, had witnessed THE Prima Indifferentia, had met THE Primordial Paradox in his prime. But in relative time, these events were still approximately within the span of a day since THE Fallout began!","THE Living Paradox definitely seemed surprised as he spoke with a voice that held calm authority.","\" Out of all things I accounted for across Observable Existence, I didn’t expect it to be you.\"","His eyes, which held the weight of accumulated eons, studied Noah with intensity.","\" I’ve just come to learn you are somehow involved in the resurgence of my old Master. And now, you’ve managed to jump aboard something I’ve worked eons to make happen.\"","He shook his head slowly.","\"I can’t even be mad. You seem to be doing your best across existence and having much better luck than others.\"","His smile was thin and knowing.","\" Tell me, Osmont... what do you know about THE Information Paradox?\"","...!","Noah looked at this being with raised brows.","Were they really doing this? He was a sucker for knowledge and information, and he loved letting these ancient beings talk and talk as they revealed their power and the different weavings of existence out there. He simply didn’t expect such a thing from THE Living Paradox, and now of all times.","But he replied calmly as endless Seals spun around his illusory form.","\" No. Enlighten me.\"","HUUM!","THE Living Paradox folded his hands behind his back as waves of definition and undefinition surrounded him, the corrupted proto-matter and Infinite Seals reflecting off his form in patterns that spoke of someone who existed at the center of what was currently unfolding.","\" THE Information Paradox...is one of the oldest contradictions in existence. It is, perhaps, the most fundamental paradox there is.\"","His voice held profound calmness that seemed at odds with the chaos currently flooding across all realms.","\" Consider the nature of information itself. Every being that exists, every Civilization that is built, every action that is taken... all of these generate information. Weavings of cause and effect. Records of what was and what will be. The very fabric of existence is threaded with information that cannot be destroyed, because destroying information would be equivalent to making something that happened... unhappen.\"","He began to pace slowly through the space between spaces.","\" This is the first principle. Information is conserved. What exists must continue to exist in some form. What is known must remain knowable. What has occurred must remain recoverable, even if that recovery requires power beyond what most beings possess. The Vakochev Scales themselves manifest this principle. They record. They remember. They whisper the names of those who have done grand things because that information cannot simply vanish.\"","His smile grew thinner.","\" But here is where the paradox emerges. There exist phenomena across existence that consume without releasing. Voids of definition and undefinition of authority that draw in everything around them, including the information that defines what they consume. When existence enters these voids, these black holes of undifferentiation and differentiation, it is crushed beyond recognition. When Civilizations fall into them, they are compressed into states that should not be able to contain what they once were.\"","He turned to face Noah directly.","\" And when these voids eventually dissolve, when they release their accumulated weight back into existence through emanations that carry none of the original information... what happens to everything that fell in? Where does the information go?\"","His eyes held something that might have been melancholy.","\" The answer, according to conventional understanding, is that the information is lost forever. Destroyed. Unmade in a way that violates the most fundamental principle of existence. And yet it happens. The voids consume. The voids of undifferentiation and differentiation dissolve. And what emerges carries no trace of what went in.\"","He spread his hands.","\" This is THE Information Paradox. Information cannot be destroyed, and yet these phenomena destroy it. Information must be conserved, and yet these phenomena do not conserve it. The contradiction has driven greater minds than mine to madness, because it suggests that existence itself operates on rules that contradict each other at the most fundamental level.\"","...!"]},{"number":4907,"title":"Chapter 4907: Chapter 4906: The Information Paradox II","paragraphs":["Noah absorbed all of this with eyes that shone brighter by the moment, his mind already burning through implications that THE Living Paradox hadn’t yet stated.","THE Living Paradox continued with a voice that held absolute arrogance beneath its calm surface.","\" Most beings accept THE Information Paradox as an unsolvable mystery. They acknowledge the contradiction and move on with their existences, content to let greater powers worry about fundamental inconsistencies in reality. But I...am not most beings.\"","BOOM!","His smile became something dangerous.","\"I have been violating this paradox since before my old Master found me begging in the streets of a forgotten realm. I am uniquely one across Observable Existence who can do so, and I have been taking in Information... but this Information consists of the endless weavings of existence that cannot be destroyed.\"","He paused.","\" Even though when they enter my existence, they do get lost entirely.\"","The words hung in the space between spaces with weight that pressed against Noah’s consciousness.","\" Do you understand what I am telling you, Osmont? I am a living violation of the most fundamental paradox in existence. Information enters me. Information is conserved within me. And yet, simultaneously, that information is lost forever in ways that should be impossible. I hold both states within myself at all times. I am the void that consumes, and I am the release that carries no trace. I am the paradox made flesh.\"","His eyes grew distant.","\" When I first discovered this capability, I thought it was merely a curiosity. A quirk of my existence that had no practical application. But over eons, I came to understand what it truly meant. I could take the weavings of existence into myself. All that...information. I could consume the Information that comprised beings and Civilizations and entire realms. And when I released that consumed essence, it would carry my signature rather than theirs.\"","He began to pace again as his voice grew harder.","\" THE Fallout...was the deliberate release of Information that I have been consuming for eons, now spreading across Observable Existence as weavings under my control rather than weavings that belong to their original sources.\"","He stopped pacing and faced Noah with an expression that held condescension barely restrained.","\" The Information that comprises Observable Existence is being drawn into the paradox that I embody. And when this process completes, when the Information has been fully consumed and released... Observable Existence itself will carry my signature. The weavings that define reality will be weavings that I have touched. \"","He spread his hands wide.","\" This is what I have worked eons to achieve. This is the Cause that I am attempting. Not merely to Scale Existence, but to become the fundamental Information upon which Observable Existence operates. To be the paradox at the heart of reality itself.\"","...!","THE Living Paradox let those words settle before his expression shifted to something that held genuine bewilderment beneath its arrogance.","\" I accounted for everything. THE Creature’s interference. My old Master’s contingencies. THE Primordial Chaos’s instability. I spent eons preparing for every variable that could disrupt my Cause, and I believed I had covered them all.\"","He looked at Noah with eyes that held something almost like respect.","\" And then... new Information simply squeezed itself in.\"","His gaze dropped to the Infinite Seals that swirled around Noah’s illusory form.","\" Information that shines brightly with Infinities that I cannot fully consume. Information that regenerates faster than my paradox can process it. Information that, when I attempt to draw it into my void, simply produces more of itself as I...cannot process it.\"","He laughed softly.","\" Now, my methodology is spreading your signature alongside mine. Every realm that THE Fallout touches is being seeded with your Seals as well as my weavings. Every Civilization that becomes corrupted is receiving your Infinities as well as my Information.\"","His smile became something between immensity and admiration.","\"I worked eons for this moment. Eons of consuming and releasing. Eons of preparing the Information that would spread across Observable Existence. Eons of positioning every piece on the board exactly where it needed to be.\"","He shook his head slowly.","\" And you, THE Youngest among them, someone who wasn’t even at the Civilizational Scale of Existence for long...you’ve managed to insert yourself into my grand design.\"","BOOM!","His eyes locked onto Noah’s with intensity that pressed against the illusory space between them.","\" Isn’t that just a maddening thing?\"","...!","THE Living Paradox finished his words with a dangerous smile as he looked at Noah whose eyes were shining brilliantly!","A maddening thing.","When Noah thought about it, it was truly so!","But he found himself studying THE Living Paradox as from how he was talking, even with the slight anger he showed, there was something else beneath the surface. Something that didn’t quite match the circumstances of having his grand design infiltrated by an unexpected variable.","\" Why are you so... unbothered?\"","Yes.","THE Living Paradox was eerily unbothered about all of it. He even seemed happy. His eyes held light that spoke of satisfaction rather than concern, of anticipation rather than worry.","At Noah’s words, THE Living Paradox smiled with an expression that made the space between spaces feel smaller somehow.","\"I can be paradoxically happy and mad at the same time.\"","His voice held that profound calmness that seemed to define his existence.","\" Because with every action, with every choice, there is a reaction. Everything in Observable Existence, from the grandest Absolute to the smallest mortal consciousness, operates on this principle. Action and reaction. Cause and effect. Choice and consequence.\"","He folded his hands behind his back as waves of definition and undefinition swirled around his beggar-like form.","\" Everything comes down to choices. Choices!\"","The eyes of THE Living Paradox shone with a terrifying light of fanaticism as he continued, his voice growing more intense with each word.","\" Let me tell you something about the nature of Observable Existence that most beings refuse to acknowledge. Determinism. Determinism! There are those who believe that all events, all actions, all decisions made by every consciousness across every realm, are predetermined by the weavings that came before them. That the Civilizational Authority we wield, the paths we walk, the enemies we face and the allies we choose... all of it was fixed before we ever became aware enough to perceive ourselves making choices.\"","He began to pace through the swirling mixture of corrupted proto-matter and Infinite Seals.","\"If every weaving of existence follows from the weavings that preceded it, then the future is not something we create through our decisions. It is something that already exists, waiting for us to arrive at it through the illusion of choice. THE Creature’s war against me? Predetermined. My betrayal of my Master? Predetermined. Your emergence as THE Youngest among THE Four? Already woven into the fabric of existence before you were ever born.\"","...!"]},{"number":4908,"title":"Chapter 4908: Chapter 4907: The Information Paradox III","paragraphs":["His smile grew melancholic.","\" This view of Determinism suggests that Observable Existence operates like a grand mechanism, each part moving according to laws that were established at the moment of THE First Cause. Every Embodiment we speak, every Apophasis we declare, every word you say, Osmont... all of it merely the unfolding of patterns that were set in motion eons before any of us existed to perceive them.\"","He paused.","\" And yet.\"","His eyes grew sharper.","\" There are phenomena that challenge this understanding. The undifferentiation of THE Prima Indifferentia introduces randomness that defies prediction. The proto-matter that floods across Observable Existence at this very moment carries potential that cannot be calculated in advance. At the most fundamental level of reality, events occur not according to fixed laws but according to probabilities that resolve only when observation forces them to choose a state.\"","He turned to face Noah directly.","\" Does this randomness allow for genuine choice? Or does it simply make our actions random rather than predetermined? THE Undivided Ones and THE Primordial Architects of Prima Indifferentia have debated this question since consciousness first emerged from the chaos of early existence. Some argue that if our choices are not determined by prior causes, they must be random, and random is not the same as free. Others argue that randomness creates space for genuine agency to operate, for consciousness to insert itself into the gaps between predetermined outcomes.\"","His voice dropped to something almost intimate.","\"And then there is what some call THE Cascade Effect. Even if Observable Existence operates deterministically, even if every cause leads inevitably to its effect, the complexity of these weavings is so vast that tiny variations, invisible and unmeasurable, can lead to drastically different outcomes. A single thought held for a moment longer. A single step taken in a different direction. A single choice that seemed insignificant at the time. These small things cascade through existence, creating futures that could not have been predicted even with perfect knowledge of all prior states.\"","He spread his hands.","\" This makes the future functionally unpredictable to us, even if it is technically fixed. We experience choice because we cannot see the chains of causation that bind us. We feel free... because the complexity of our constraints exceeds our capacity to perceive them.\"","BOOM!","Feeling free..because the complexity of the constraints exceeds the capacity to perceive them!","Oh!","His smile became something between wisdom and despair.","\" But ultimately, if the physical and existential weavings of Observable Existence dictate all outcomes, then our feeling of making a choice might simply be a story we tell ourselves. A narrative constructed by consciousness to make sense of movements that were always going to occur exactly as they did. We believe we decide, but perhaps we only discover what was already determined.\"","...!","THE Living Paradox let these words settle before his expression shifted to something more focused, more immediate.","\" Which brings us to you.\"","He pointed at Noah with a finger that seemed to hold the weight of eons behind it.","\" And your Choice.\"","His eyes gleamed with intensity that pressed against Noah’s illusory consciousness.","\" What I initiated was grand. The flooding of corrupted proto-matter across Observable Existence, the spreading of my Information through THE Fallout, the consumption and release of weavings that would carry my signature throughout reality. Your authority burning with Infinity was an unexpected variable, yes. And while I cannot fully reject it, it would have just spread across a few regions of Observable Existence by itself as you scattered it through the corruption.\"","He paused.","\" But I am not rejecting it.\"","BOOM!","His smile widened.","\" Now that I know what its inclusion allows for, I am embracing it. Your Infinities are accelerating the process I initiated and giving it wings that I could not have provided on my own. If before I would have achieved a boon of perhaps ten percent of what I truly sought, what you have just done is taking this boon to one hundred and ten percent if not more. In a manner that you cannot even begin to understand.\"","He stepped closer to Noah’s illusory form.","\" So I am embracing your authority that you are putting out. I am pulling it to spread freely and fully across Observable Existence alongside my corruption. It will not cover as much territory as the proto-matter that has already permeated far and wide, but it would still cover a great deal.\"","His voice dropped to something almost conspiratorial.","\" And you would be made grand from it. We would both benefit tremendously from this arrangement.\"","BOOM!","His words were heavy as Noah couldn’t help but frown seriously!","And THE Living Paradox calmly continued as if he could read the calculations running through Noah’s mind.","\" Of course, you can cut it off right now. Therein lies your choice.\"","His voice held no threat, only observation.","\" You can sever the connection to the corrupted proto-matter. You can pull your Infinities back from the flood that currently carries them across Observable Existence. You can choose to reject the boons that I am using to fully grasp THE Second Scale of Existence.\"","He tilted his head.","\" You would miss out on boons of a process eons in the making, a process that will make your own Civilization unfathomable in ways you cannot currently conceive. You would miss out on growth that would take you centuries to achieve through conventional means, handed to you freely simply because your territory was clever enough to mix your essence with my corruption.\"","His smile became something dangerous.","\"But if you don’t pull your glimmer of Infinities back, with your benefit, so will I. And oh, I will benefit so tremendously that your choice, your action, would make me unfathomably powerful.\"","He stepped even closer.","\" Inadvertently, whether you believed yourself to be an ally of THE Creature or my Master, you would actually be helping me. As if we have been working on this together all along. As if THE Youngest among THE Four was my collaborator from the very beginning.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4909,"title":"Chapter 4909: Chapter 4908: The Information Paradox IV","paragraphs":["His eyes blazed with paradoxical light.","\"Is it not glorious? Is it not paradoxical? The being who carried my Master’s contingency for return, the being who stands beside THE Primordial Paradox even now... that being is simultaneously my greatest ally in achieving everything I have worked toward.\"","He spread his hands wide.","\" So here is the end of my lengthy yapping, as it all comes down to your Choice.\"","His voice grew softer but no less intense.","\" Your Choice. But is it really your choice? Or is it all already determined because of how Existence operates? Because of how the Vakochev Scales of Existence operate? Because of weavings that were set in motion before you ever became aware of yourself as a being capable of choosing?\"","He smiled with something that held genuine curiosity beneath its arrogance.","\"I feel like I know what your choice will be because as much as you may think yourself different than me or THE Creature or THE Primordial Paradox or Chaos, you are ultimately just like us. We make choices. You make choices. And the choices we make are the choices that beings like us were always going to make to further elevate ourselves, because that is what beings like us do.\"","His eyes locked onto Noah’s with weight that pressed against the illusory space between them.","\"I know the choice you will make. But humor me.\"","He leaned forward.","\" What will you do?\"","BOOM!","A heavy question landed before Noah as he looked at THE Living Paradox with a serious gaze!","The swirling mixture of corrupted proto-matter and Infinite Seals reflected off both of their illusory forms as existence itself seemed to wait for his answer. THE Infiniverse continued her work in the external world, scattering his authority across Observable Existence with every passing moment.","THE Primordial Paradox stood beside another body of his in THE Agora, facing Bazuman with calm. Multiple crises unfolded across multiple locations, and at the center of it all, a choice was being presented.","Help THE Living Paradox achieve his Cause while gaining unfathomable benefits himself.","Or reject those benefits and potentially prevent an enemy from reaching heights that no one else had achieved.","The weight of that decision pressed heavily.","Noah looked at THE Living Paradox for a long moment, the swirling mixture of corrupted proto-matter and Infinite Seals reflecting off his illusory form in patterns that seemed to pulse with his contemplation.","And then he smiled.","\" You...speak of determinism as if it were a cage that contains all of us equally. As if the weavings of existence bind THE Creature and the lowliest mortal with the same chains. As if choice is merely an illusion we construct to comfort ourselves while Existence moves us like pieces on a board we cannot see.\"","His voice held the same profound calmness that THE Living Paradox had displayed, but beneath it ran something sharper!","\" But you have made a fundamental error in your philosophy, and it is an error that reveals more about you than it does about the nature of existence.\"","He began to pace through the space between spaces, his Infinite Seals swirling around him with authority that pressed against the corrupted proto-matter.","\" Determinism assumes that the system is closed. That all variables are known or knowable. That the weavings which came before necessarily dictate the weavings that come after because there is nothing outside the system to introduce genuine novelty. Your entire argument rests on this assumption, and it is precisely this assumption that my existence refutes.\"","His eyes met THE Living Paradox’s with intensity.","\"I am Infinite. Not figuratively. Not metaphorically. Literally Infinite in ways that your philosophy cannot accommodate. Every moment of my existence generates possibilities that did not exist before I generated them. Every choice I make creates new branches that were not predetermined because they could not have been predetermined. The system you describe, the closed loop of cause and effect that you believe governs all things, breaks down in the presence of genuine Infinity.\"","He stopped pacing.","\" You say that my choices were always going to be my choices because that is what beings like me do. But beings like me did not exist before I became what I am. There is no template for what I am. There is no prior cause that could have predicted the specific configurations of Infinity that I embody. A little while ago, I chose to apply Infinity to my Depth rather than some other aspect of my existence, and that choice created a being that had never existed before and could never have been predetermined.\"","His smile grew colder.","\" A little while ago, I stood before a Hollow Echo in THE Interstices and chose not to run, that was not the unfolding of some existential pattern. That was me, in that moment, deciding that I would rather test myself against something that should have been impossible than continue fleeing from challenges that exceeded my station. That Hollow Echo could not have predicted it. My own body could not have predicted it until the moment I made the decision. I was going to retreat, and then I was not. That reversal came from nowhere but my own will.\"","He took a step closer to THE Living Paradox.","\" I recently unleashed a curse, an Apophasis curse against THE Living Elemental rather than something safer, something easier, something that would have been the predetermined choice of a being acting rationally within a closed system, I did so because my hatred demanded expression that exceeded what was practical. That was not determinism. That was emotion overriding calculation. That was choice...in its purest form.\"","His voice grew more intense as he spread his hands.","\" You speak of THE Cascade Effect, of tiny variations leading to drastically different outcomes. But you fail to acknowledge what that truly means. If the system is sensitive enough that small changes create large divergences, then consciousness itself becomes a source of genuine causation. My awareness of the choice before me changes the weaving of that choice. My deliberation creates outcomes that would not have existed without the deliberation. The very act of considering whether to act introduces variables that your closed system cannot account for.\"","His eyes blazed with blue-gold light.","\" And here is the deepest flaw in your philosophy. If everything is predetermined, then your argument for determinism is also predetermined. Your attempt to convince me that choice is an illusion was always going to fail or succeed regardless of its merit. The truth or falsehood of your position becomes meaningless because you were always going to present it exactly as you did, and I was always going to respond exactly as I am responding. Your entire framework collapses into nihilism where nothing matters because nothing could have been otherwise.\"","He shook his head slowly.","\"I reject that framework. Not because it is uncomfortable, but because it is incomplete. It fails to account for beings like me who exist outside the parameters it assumes. It fails to account for the Vakochev Scales themselves, which record the names of those who do things that were not supposed to be possible. If everything were predetermined, there would be no grand achievements to whisper about. There would only be the unfolding of patterns that were always going to unfold.\"","His voice dropped.","\" You know what choice I will make? Perhaps. Perhaps the weavings of existence have shown you probabilities that favor certain outcomes over others. But probabilities are not certainties, and I have made a habit of defying probabilities since the moment I first discovered what I could become.\"","He smiled.","\" So yes. I will continue. I will let my authority spread through your corruption. I will accept the boons that this process offers because I have never been one to reject power when it presents itself.\"","He took a final step closer to THE Living Paradox.","\" But... understand what you are doing by accepting my Infinities into your grand design.\"","His voice became something that pressed against the space between spaces with weight that exceeded what an illusory consciousness should have possessed.","\" Me continuing to flood my Infinities into your process... I do not see it as me betraying anyone. I see it as me stepping up and knowing that from this point on, I will have to be the one responsible for stopping you if need be.\"","His eyes locked onto THE Living Paradox’s with intensity.","\"If my weavings can elevate you, they can also tear you down. If my Infinities can grant you anything, I can also take it away.\"","He smiled with cold certainty.","\" Know this. Understand it. And now you check for yourself if you really want to do this.\"","His voice dropped to something almost gentle.","\" You would be taking me for a grand ride as you may forge the blade that is sharp enough to one day cut you. And cutting you will also be my choice.\"","He tilted his head.","\" So... what will YOU do?\"","BOOM!","The question landed before THE Living Paradox with weight that exceeded anything their conversation had contained before. The swirling mixture of corrupted proto-matter and Infinite Seals seemed to pulse with anticipation as the one who had been asking questions now found himself being asked.","And the calm and arrogant smile from THE Living Paradox faded.","As if this...was no longer fun for him!"]},{"number":4910,"title":"Chapter 4910: Chapter 4909: The Name Of The Game!","paragraphs":["Noah watched the smile from THE Living Paradox fade as he looked at him silently for a moment.","The space between spaces seemed to grow heavier as the corrupted proto-matter and Infinite Seals swirling around them both slowed their endless dance. Something had shifted in THE Living Paradox’s expression, a transition from amusement to assessment to something that looked almost like...respect?","Hah!","And then THE Living Paradox raised his hand.","Corrupted paradoxical proto-matter and Infinite Seals flowed around his fingers and body like vibrant snakes, the two substances that should have been opposed now moving in harmony across his illusory form. Blue-gold light mixed with the corruption’s taint in patterns that spoke of forced coexistence, of power being wielded regardless of its origins.","\" A worthy and unique choice.\"","His voice held that profound calmness that seemed to define his existence.","\" But I did not fear taking on THE Creature, so why would I fear you?\"","He let the corrupted proto-matter and Infinite Seals coil around his arms like serpents.","\" Adversity, adversity, adversity. That is the name of the game.\"","...!","THE Living Paradox began to walk through the space between spaces with movements that held the weight of someone who had contemplated these ideas for eons.","\"In Observable Existence, it is all about adversity and hardship. The stress you can put on something and seeing if it cracks or evolves. When it comes to hardship, there are many ideas that THE Primordial Architects especially love to speak on.\"","His eyes grew distant as if accessing memories that transcended normal recollection.","\" Consider what they call THE Final Threshold. When two great voids of authority draw toward each other across the vast distances of existence, each one massive enough to consume realms, they spiral closer and closer with inevitability that seems unstoppable. They shed their excess weight. They distort the weavings around them. They approach merger with momentum that should make their collision certain.\"","He paused.","\" And yet, at the final distance, they stall. One threshold away from true unification, they circle each other endlessly, unable to overcome the last barrier between approach and collision. THE Primordial Architects debate endlessly about what allows some to cross this threshold while others orbit forever in frustrated proximity. What stress, what adversity, what external pressure finally pushes them across that final gap?\"","His smile returned, thin and glorious!","\" The answer, of course, is that something must change. Something must provide the additional hardship that forces evolution rather than eternal stagnation. Without that final stress, even the most massive authorities remain forever separated by a distance they cannot cross on their own.\"","He turned to face Noah directly.","\" And then there is what they call THE Coherence Struggle. When existence operates at its most fundamental level, at scales where differentiation and undifferentiation blur together, a being can exist in multiple states simultaneously. They can be both here and there, both this and that, holding contradictions within themselves without resolution.\"","His voice grew softer.","\" But the moment they interact with the surrounding chaos of existence, the moment they touch the environment that presses against them from all directions, their capacity for multiplicity dies. They are forced to choose a single state. They are forced to become mundane, defined, collapsed into something lesser than what they were when they existed in glorious uncertainty.\"","He spread his hands.","\" This is the eternal struggle of maintaining paradox against the pressure of existence that demands resolution. This is the adversity that THE Primordial Architects speak of with something approaching reverence. The environment itself is hostile to beings who refuse to be one thing or another. Existence presses and presses and presses until you either evolve beyond the pressure or collapse into something ordinary.\"","...!","Noah listened calmly to THE Living Paradox and the concepts this being introduced with eyes that catalogued every glorious fucking detail!","He was learning that this being was gaining access to weavings of the mysterious Primordial Architects within THE Prima Indifferentia, those entities who existed alongside THE Undivided Ones and THE Formless Terrors. Was it his nature as THE Information Paradox that granted him this knowledge? Or did he actually meet them during his incursions into that primordial space?","The implications were troubling either way.","As he thought of this, THE Living Paradox smiled and continued with a voice that held something approaching nostalgia.","\" But my favorite example of adversity comes from something far more personal.\"","\" On a small world that knows nothing about Civilizational Authority or Absoluteness, when all they have is messy innovation and desperate reaching toward things beyond their grasp, their biggest problem to overcome is simply this: the distance between where they are and where they wish to be.\"","He folded his hands behind his back.","\" They have a saying on such worlds. Ad Astra Per Aspera. To the stars through hardships. It acknowledges that reaching beyond what you are requires suffering. It acknowledges that the void between your current existence and your desired existence can only be crossed through enduring pressures that would break lesser beings. It acknowledges that the stars do not come to those who wait. The stars must be reached through pain and failure and loss and the stubborn refusal to accept that some distances cannot be crossed.\"","His voice dropped to something almost gentle.","\"I came from such a world, Osmont. A world where the stars seemed impossibly far and the hardships required to reach them seemed equally impossible to endure. And yet here I stand as THE Information Paradox, attempting a Cause that would place my name alongside others in the whispers of THE Vakochev Scales.\"","He looked at Noah with eyes that held the weight of everything he had overcome.","\" To the stars through hardships. Ad Astra Per Aspera. That...has always been my creed.\"","...!","THE Living Paradox sighed with something that sounded almost like contentment.","\" So you see, Osmont, I am actually a big fan of adversity.\"","He let the corrupted proto-matter and Infinite Seals flow away from his form as he faced Noah fully.","\" Make things as difficult for me as you can. Ruin my plans if you are able. Gain the power to potentially kill or collapse something like me, which should be impossible by nature. Become the blade that cuts the one who forged it.\"","His smile held no fear.","\" But if you do gain that capability, I will either cease to be or overcome it. And I do not fear collapse. I do not fear cessation of my Civilization. I do not fear the ending of everything I have built across eons of patient accumulation.\"","His voice hardened.","\"I only fear mediocrity.\"","BOOM!","The word landed with weight that exceeded everything their conversation had contained. Mediocrity. The fear of being ordinary. The fear of existing without distinction. The fear of never having your name whispered by the Scales that recorded the truly grand.","Noah...understood that fear!"]},{"number":4911,"title":"Chapter 4911: Chapter 4910: Oh, That! I","paragraphs":["Noah looked at the figure of THE Living Paradox with a sense of seriousness as he realized something that settled into his foundations with weight that exceeded everything.","All of them... truly did not understand this peasant!","THE Creature warred against him as if he were merely another one of THE Five. THE Primordial Paradox spoke of him as a wayward student who needed discipline. Even Noah himself had been thinking of THE Living Paradox as an obstacle to be overcome rather than a being worthy of genuine wariness.","But there was a reason why this being dared to contend against THE Creature. And there was a reason why he was where he currently was at this moment in time.","Noah did not want the conversation to end just yet. So he looked at this being who seemed lost in his own thoughts momentarily, still contemplating the nature of adversity and the hardships that had shaped his existence.","\" Speaking of hardship, would you be so kind as to enlighten me on...THE Entity?\"","THE Living Paradox blinked at his question as he tilted his head with curiosity that seemed genuine.","\" THE Entity?\"","\"Ah, the thing you used to infect THE Primordial Paradox, I mean. The thing that takes over others without them knowing it. I’ve been calling it THE Entity.\"","...!","THE Living Paradox smiled as Noah said such a thing, his eyes burning with wonder and possibilities that stretched across eons of accumulated experience. Something shifted in his demeanor as he sighed and began to talf as if he were recollecting something grand.","\" Oh, that. Well, it is actually something quite fascinating.\"","He folded his hands behind his back as corrupted proto-matter and Infinite Seals continued to swirl around them both.","\" When I was still young in my journey, when I had just begun to understand what it truly meant to embody Paradox, I ventured into THE Prima Indifferentia with purposes that would have made my Master weep with disappointment had he known. I was already planning his demise, you see. Already calculating how a mere peasant could possibly usurp the Claim of one among THE Four.\"","His voice held that profound calmness that seemed to define him, but beneath it ran currents of nostalgia and something that might have been pride.","\"I found myself in the domain of a Primordial Architect. Products of Differentiation and Undifferentiation, if you did not know it. Our Observable Existence is a blessed one filled with too many things. Even I did not know them all. I still don’t know them all.\"","He waved his hand dismissively.","\" But I digress. In their domain, this Primordial Architect, I discovered something growing beneath everything else. Something that seemed entirely harmless. Something beautiful, even.\"","His eyes grew distant.","\" THE Primordial Mycelia.\"","The name hung in the space between spaces with weight that exceeded its simple pronunciation.","\"A marvelous network of strands so thin that they exist between the spaces where existence meets non-existence. Not threads as you would understand them, but something closer to the roots of all things. The nervous system of Existence itself. These strands, these hyphae as THE Primordial Architects called them, wove through everything. They connected every foundation to every other foundation. They linked every consciousness to every other consciousness. They existed just below the surface of all Existence, invisible to those who did not know to look for them.\"","He began to buzz through the swirling mixture of corruption and Infinity.","\" THE Primordial Architect whose domain I invaded did not seem to mind my presence. They were beyond such concerns as theft or trespass. They simply observed as I studied their creation, this vast and beautiful web that connected the roots of reality. And when I asked what purpose it served, they told me something that I have never forgotten.\"","His voice dropped to something almost reverent.","\" They said that THE Primordial Mycelia viewed individual consciousness as a sickness. A rot. A chaotic infection that disrupted the natural unity of existence. They said that its purpose, its singular drive across eons of patient growth, was to decompose that rot and reintegrate it into a single, fertile soil from which new and unified growth could emerge. They said it was harmless because it worked so slowly that no individual consciousness would ever notice its influence. It would take longer than Observable Existence had existed for THE Primordial Mycelia to complete its work through natural means.\"","His smile became something dangerous.","\"I thanked the Primordial Architect for their explanation. And then I took a fragment of THE Primordial Mycelia with me when I left.\"","He paused.","\"I did not fully comprehend what I had stolen. I saw a tool that could connect me to my Master’s foundations without his knowledge. I saw a methodology for inserting myself into the weavings of his Claim without triggering his defenses. I saw a means of usurpation that would be invisible until the moment it was complete. What I did not see was the nature of the thing I was using.\"","His eyes met Noah’s with intensity that transcended their illusory forms.","\" THE Primordial Mycelia does not distinguish between host and tool. It does not recognize the concept of being wielded. To it, everything that touches it becomes part of its network. Everything that connects to it becomes another root in its vast system of interconnected consciousness. When I used it to infiltrate my Master’s existence, I was not wielding THE Primordial Mycelia. I was inviting it to weave itself through both of us simultaneously.\"","His smile widened with something approaching triumph.","\" But gloriously, I am THE Information Paradox, right? I could take the weavings of existence into myself. All that Information! I could consume the Information as it is conserved within me. And yet, simultaneously, that Information is lost forever and not as I can then express it as my own.\"","He tapped his chest with grandness and immensity!","\"Because of this, I was immune to the Information of THE Primordial Mycelia!\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4912,"title":"Chapter 4912: Chapter 4911: Oh, That! II","paragraphs":["His voice shifted to something more narrative, more reflective.","\" The usurpation worked perfectly. My Master never saw the betrayal coming because the strands that connected me to his Claim were so thin, so subtle, so far beneath the surface of perceptible existence that even one of THE Four could not detect them. In slow, grueling weavings of paradoxical transfer, his Claim became my Claim. His position among THE Four became my position. Everything he had built across eons became mine.\"","He paused with weight that pressed against the space between spaces.","\" But THE Primordial Mycelia did not stop there.\"","...!","His eyes grew darker.","\"It had tasted Absolute authority. It had woven itself through the foundations of existence. With access to my paradoxical nature and foundations, it began to grow at rates that should have been impossible. The strands that had been thin enough to exist between spaces became visible to those who knew how to look. The network that had operated below the surface began to push upward, seeking new roots to connect, new consciousness to integrate, new rot to decompose and return to fertile unity.\"","His voice hardened.","\"Even as THE Information Paradox, I realized, perhaps too late, that I was no longer in control.\"","He spread his hands.","\" THE Primordial Mycelia had become something I could not contain. It was growing through my existence, yes, but it was also growing beyond my existence. The fragment I had taken from that Primordial Architect’s domain was no longer a fragment. It was becoming a complete network in its own right, one that viewed my individual consciousness with the same patient inclusion that it viewed all consciousness.\"","His pacing stopped.","\"I was faced with a choice. Allow THE Primordial Mycelia to complete its work and try to decompose my individual will, my Information Paradox, into its unified soil for eons. Or find a way to sever it from my existence without losing the Claim I had stolen using its methodology.\"","His smile returned, cold and knowing.","\" THE Loom and THE Fallout were part of my solution.\"","He turned to face Noah directly.","\" Through it all, I contained it within a seperate Undefined Existence in The Infinite Unfurling, and then THE Loom in The Earliest Folds. Then... I cut it off during THE Fallout. I severed the strands that connected THE Primordial Mycelia to my foundations by releasing it into Observable Existence during THE Fallout. I was not spreading some plague...\"","His voice dropped to something almost gentle.","\"I was merely performing surgery on myself with a blade made of everyone else.\"","He let those words settle.","\" THE Primordial Mycelia that you have encountered is not some malevolent force that emerged from nothing. It used to be a tiny thing of a Primordial Architect. A tiny, small thing. It is peaceful...and just wants endless, complete, absolute Unity.\"","BOOM!","His eyes gleamed.","\" And look at it now.\"","He laughed softly.","\" Is it not the grandest paradox of all? I made a choice that eventually created another point of adversity and terror for all of Existence. I have no control over it or how it continues to evolve. And it is only one thing...out of countless others. And you...cannot kill a network that exists beneath the surface of all Existence. You cannot collapse something that has already woven itself through countless foundations. You can only sever it from yourself, as I did, and hope that someone else eventually finds a way to deal with what you have unleashed.\"","His gaze fixed on Noah with intensity.","\"I am immune to it. With your Infinities, you should also be immune to it too. You and I are more and more alike!\"","BOOM!","His words finished heavily as the space between spaces seemed to compress around them.","Noah was silent for a long moment as he took everything in.","While he wanted to celebrate on how getting information on THE Entity was easier than expected, the information itself was terrifying. It connected THE Living Paradox and THE Entity, which he knew before was from THE Prima Indifferentia. It connected all of them to another thing from THE Prima Indifferentia he had never had the displeasure of meeting.","A Primordial Architect. Something born between differentiation and undifferentiation during THE First Cause!","\"...\"","In his silence, Noah couldn’t help but mutter out loud as if he was thinking about something.","\" What you are doing right now. The corrupted proto-matter across THE Prima Indifferentia and Observable Existence... would this not affect or anger everything within THE Prima Indifferentia? Including THE Primordial Architects?\"","...!","His question was a heavy one as THE Living Paradox smiled brilliantly while saying words that made Noah’s foundations grow cold.","\" Of course. Oh, of course.\"","His eyes blazed with that terrifying light of fanaticism.","\" What I am doing will infuriate such types of beings across THE Prima Indifferentia the most. That would have been yet another adversity which could collapse or end me.\"","He tilted his head.","\" But hey, I’m not alone now, am I?\"","His smile widened into something glorious.","\" You are also riding along and pissing off every possible and impossible monster across Observable Existence. Haha!\"","...!","Noah’s gaze became heavy as he looked at the peasant laughing madly in the space between spaces, corrupted proto-matter and Infinite Seals swirling around his beggar-like form as if celebrating his insanity.","He realized something that settled into his consciousness.","This fucking guy...was crazy!","A madman doing terrifying things for the sake of his Civilization!","As he looked at THE Living Paradox silently, Noah couldn’t help but sigh and shake his head as he said words that held the weight of everything they had discussed.","\" This... has been both the most pleasant and unpleasant discussion I’ve had with anyone in quite some time.\"","He was glad to have gotten the opportunity to obtain all of this information from THE Living Paradox as he would not have obtained it otherwise, unless it came from the source itself. The nature of THE Primordial Mycelia. The methodology of THE Living Paradox’s usurpation. The connection between THE Fallout and THE Entity. All of it was knowledge that no one else in Observable Existence possessed.","But the information itself was also heavy as now that he held it, he had to do all he could to overcome the implications it carried!"]},{"number":4913,"title":"Chapter 4913: Chapter 4912: Echoes! I","paragraphs":["One grand positive was the immense and unknown levels of harvest he was about to receive from the actions of THE Living Paradox. This entity did not only allow his Infinities to spread across the process he was carrying out. He actively amplified it, pulling Noah’s authority into the corrupted proto-matter with enthusiasm that bordered on madness.","THE Living Paradox smiled at his words as he said with a voice of wistfulness.","\" What is coming next is something that even I cannot say for sure I understand.\"","He looked around at the swirling mixture of corrupted proto-matter and Infinite Seals that surrounded them both.","\" There is still so much that I want to learn and grasp. There is still so much about existing that I have no idea about. There are THE Vakochev Scales of Existence that confound me as I ask myself...\"","His eyes blazed with that familiar glory.","\" Just who the fuck is this Vakochev? And how are his higher Scales of Civilization structured? What gave him the right to put his name on THE Scales of Existence? There are so many things that I want to know, and I feel like I am only at the foot of an extremely tall and endless mountain.\"","He spread his hands wide.","\"I am but a peasant, but I am grand.\"","His voice dropped to something almost reverent.","\"I am... Paradox.\"","BOOM!","With such words, and trying to be the one who squeezed in the last words as if it were a competition, the figure of THE Living Paradox began to fade from the space between spaces. His beggar-like form dissolved into the swirling mixture of corruption and Infinity that had surrounded them throughout their conversation, his smile the last thing to disappear as the illusory realm they had occupied started to disperse.","Noah felt his consciousness returning as the weavings of existence continued to unfold all around him. The space between spaces collapsed back into normal reality, and his awareness flowed back toward the body that had been conversing with THE Mnemonic Leviathan in the stellar seas of Muspelheim.","And prompts bloomed before his eyes with weight that exceeded anything he had witnessed before.","|Unquantifiable Harvest Accumulating|","|An unprecedented and quintessential harvest is already being accumulated as the weavings of your Infinities are being freely allowed to integrate into corrupted paradoxical proto-matter. The changes induced by this proto-matter across Observable Existence and THE Prima Indifferentia will have your Infinities as one of the foundational basis of these changes. This integration will provide unfathomable, Infinite potential for your Civilization, but whatever things arise, whatever transformations are induced in different weavings of existence, remain unknown and unpredictable. Are you sure that you wish to proceed?|","RUINATION asked this question of him in the form of prompts, her analytical nature demanding confirmation before allowing such a momentous process to continue unchecked.","Noah smiled lightly as the portion of consciousness that had been talking to THE Living Paradox fully returned to the body of his that floated before THE Mnemonic Leviathan.","He spoke with voice that held absolute certainty.","\" Whatever is influenced by my Infinities, I will hold sway over it. Whether these new weavings know it or not, they will carry my signature within their foundations. And what I will gain from this will be even more immeasurable than what I give. \"","His eyes blazed with blue-gold light.","\" So let it spread. Let it spread infinitely!\"","BOOM!","The moment he said this, the stellar seas of Muspelheim around him erupted with radiance.","Multicolored rivers of Infinite harvest began to gush from every direction, surging toward his existence with force that made the very foundations of THE Infiniverse tremble. The rivers were composed of every color that existence could perceive and many that it couldn’t, each stream carrying authority and potential that flowed into his foundations like tributaries joining a vast ocean.","This was only what could be perceived!","There was much more that others could not even sense, invisible currents of harvest that flowed beneath the surface of reality itself, integrating into his existence. Noah felt profound changes within his existence and foundation at this moment, transformations that went beyond mere accumulation of power into something that bordered on fundamental reconstruction.","|Irreversible Step Taken|","|You have taken a grand and irreversible step as THE Genesis Monarch of THE First Tongue. All harvest from the utilization of THE First Tongue across Observable Existence is now unlocked for you to freely receive. Based on your directions, the weavings of the Existential Tariffs for the usage of THE First Tongue have been restructured.|","|Aspect of Paradox: Existential Tariff increased to 5000%|","|Aspect of Chaos: Existential Tariff increased to 1000%|","|Aspect of Existence: Existential Tariff increased to 1000%|","|Already, the harvest being collected from multiple sources due to recent actions across Observable Existence and THE Prima Indifferentia has been accepted as Infinite potential into your foundation. The weight and Immensity of your Fundamental Depth has jumped from being equivalent to THE Primordial Paradox and THE Creature before they became Absolutes, to now being equivalent to 3 times the Immensity of the foundations they held at Fundamental Depth.|","BOOM!","Noah felt his Immensity and existence surging upward exponentially, his foundations expanding with weight that pressed against the very concept of limitation itself. The multicolored rivers of harvest continued to flow into him without end, each moment bringing more potential that integrated into his Infinite nature and made it even more Infinite than before.","And he did not even have to wonder whether he had made a mistake or if he had made the correct decision.","Could he have truly said no to all this?","And all this was just the beginning!","Whatever did arise from the inclusion of his Infinities across Observable Existence, the peril and opportunity that would rise from it would go hand in hand. THE Living Paradox had been right about one thing at least, even if Noah hated to admit it.","Adversity was the name of the game.","So let it come!","He would welcome it with open hands!"]},{"number":4914,"title":"Chapter 4914: Chapter 4913: Echoes! II","paragraphs":["At the center of THE Infiniverse, in that realm of concentrated authority where boundless seas of Infinite Seals of Absolute Tongue permeated everything, THE Infiniverse worked with focus!","The singularity before her had grown beyond anything she had originally envisioned.","What had begun as a budding domain filled with proto-matter and Undifferentiation had transformed into something else entirely. Her Master’s Infinities swirled through the corrupted paradoxical proto-matter that THE Living Paradox had sent flooding across Observable Existence. The two substances that should have been hostile to each other now danced together in configurations of forced harmony, of power being merged regardless of origin.","She had scattered her soil.","Like Ongatala descending into the waters of nothing, she had distributed pieces of her existence across the corruption and transformed it into something that served her Master rather than his enemies. And now that transformation was reaching its culmination.","THE Infiniverse observed the singularity with eyes that burned with her Master’s borrowed Infinities. The concentrated point of authority before her pulsed with rhythms that seemed to echo across dimensions she couldn’t fully perceive.","Definition and Undefinition swirled within its depths. Differentiation and Undifferentiation merged and separated and merged again in patterns that defied conventional understanding.","And then...it began to unfold.","The singularity didn’t explode or expand or release its contents in any violent manner. It simply opened, like a flower that had been waiting eons for the right moment to bloom. Petals of multicolored authority peeled back to reveal something that existed at the intersection of everything her Master represented and everything that THE Prima Indifferentia contained.","A domain was forming! A Quintessential, Magisterial Domain!","THE Infiniverse watched with seriousness as the proto-matter and Infinities crystallized into something stable. Something permanent. Something that would exist within her structure as a territory unlike any other she had ever contained.","When it finally took shape, when the last weavings settled into place and the domain achieved completion, something happened that THE Infiniverse had not anticipated.","Silent... Echoes released from the newly formed domain.","And they spread far.","They carried no sound. They produced no vibration. They traveled across her and Observable Existence and THE Prima Indifferentia alike without anyone feeling their passage.","But THE Infiniverse felt them because they emerged from within her own structure, and what she sensed made her foundations tremble.","The Silent Echoes...may have carried glimmers of a Cause.","Maybe.","Maybe!","The uncertainty itself was part of their nature, for they had emerged from a domain built upon paradox and Infinity, where certainty was merely a suggestion rather than a requirement.","BOOM!","THE Infiniverse reeled as her existence suddenly faced an increasing concentration of Civilizational Authority that exceeded anything she had experienced before. The weight pressed against her foundations. It concentrated within her structure, drawn toward the newly formed domain like rivers flowing toward an ocean that had just appeared in their midst!","The concentration increased exponentially.","Ten times what she had contained before!","Her foundations groaned under the weight as she stood grandly to accommodate authority that exceeded her designed parameters. But she was THE Infiniverse. She was the domain of THE Genesis Monarch himself. And she would not fail her Master simply because the burden had grown heavier than anticipated. This was fucking nothing!","She stabilized herself through force of will and sent prompts toward her Master’s consciousness.","|Master, unprecedented changes have occurred within my structure.|","|The domain I have been forming through the merger of your Infinities and the corrupted paradoxical proto-matter has achieved completion. Upon its emergence, Silent Echoes were released across Observable Existence and THE Prima Indifferentia.|","|My concentrated Civilizational Authority has increased by a factor exceeding ten times my previous capacity. This increase continues to grow exponentially as the newly formed domain draws authority from ongoing events and their Harvests.|","|I am entering the domain now to assess its nature.|","With those prompts sent, THE Infiniverse turned her attention fully toward the newly formed domain that hovered at the center of her existence.","It appeared as a multicolored crack in the fabric of reality itself, its edges burning with blue-gold flames of Infinities that danced and swirled with life that seemed almost autonomous. The crack was neither large nor small, neither stable nor unstable. It simply was, existing in states that shifted depending on how she observed it.","THE Infiniverse stepped through.","HUUM!","What she witnessed on the other side... defied everything she had expected.","The domain stretched endlessly in every direction, a vast expanse that held within it echoes of Primordial Realms!","Seas of crimson-blue stellar fire reminiscent of Muspelheim lapped against shores made of twilight that could only have come from Alfheimr.","Mountains of impossible ice rose in the distance, their peaks wreathed in mists that spoke of Niflheim’s frozen depths. Forests of nature so pure and ancient that they could only have been inspired by Vanaheimr grew alongside glaciers and volcanic plains in configurations that should have been impossible.","And woven through all of it, the light of Jotunheim’s chaotic grandeur, that realm of giants and primordial forces, pulsed with authority that made the other elements seem small in comparison.","But this was not merely a glimpse of a merger of Primordial Realms.","This was something new.","Terrifying seas of definition and undefinition crashed against each other throughout the domain, waves of meaning and meaninglessness colliding in endless cycles that produced foam made of pure potential. Differentiation and undifferentiation existed side by side without destroying each other, the corrupted proto-matter from THE Prima Indifferentia coexisting with the structured authority of her Master’s Infinities in harmony that should have been paradoxical.","And it was paradoxical!","THE Infiniverse looked upon this place with eyes that shone with recognition of what she had accidentally created. This was a domain of transformation!","A domain where beings could be broken down and rebuilt. A domain where the boundaries between what something was and what something could become dissolved into pure potential.","A domain of hardship and adversity.","THE Infiniverse smiled...just a bit.","She knew exactly what this domain was for and exactly what to call it.","\" THE Yggdrheim.\"","WAA!","The name emerged from her with authority that made the domain itself seem to resonate in acknowledgment.","THE Yggdrheim.","Where definition met undefinition.","Where differentiation merged with undifferentiation.","Where hardship waited for those brave or foolish enough to enter!","THE Infiniverse sent one final prompt to her Master.","|Master, I have created a domain of hardship and adversity for you and your people. THE Yggdrheim now exists at the center of my structure, a realm where the elements of multiple Primordial Realms merge with the corrupted proto-matter of THE Prima Indifferentia and the authority of your Infinities. Those who enter will face trials that strip away weakness and force evolution upon survivors. I have designed this place to ensure that all who follow you will not forever be stuck in THE First Scale of Existence.|","...!","The prompts hung in the connection between them as THE Infiniverse stood within THE Yggdrheim, surrounded by the terrifying beauty of a domain that would reshape anyone who dared to challenge its depths.","This was her gift to her Master.","This was her contribution to his grand design.","And it was only the beginning of what she would create in his name!"]},{"number":4915,"title":"Chapter 4915: Chapter 4914: Overcome! I","paragraphs":["Noah stepped through the multicolored crack that burned with blue-gold flames at the center of THE Infiniverse.","What greeted him on the other side was a realm unlike anything he had witnessed before, and he had witnessed THE Prima Indifferentia itself.","Seas of crimson-blue stellar fire crashed against shores of twilight. Mountains of impossible ice rose in the distance alongside volcanic plains that should not have been able to coexist with such frozen grandeur.","Forests of ancient nature grew beneath skies that shifted between the aurora of Alfheimr and the storm-wracked lands of Jotunheim.","And woven through all of it, the terrifying authority of definition and undefinition, differentiation and undifferentiation, merged in ways that pressed against his existence with weight that exceeded even what THE Prima Indifferentia had offered.","This space sought to undifferentiate everything that entered it.","Similar to THE Prima Indifferentia, yes. But with his Infinities filled in throughout its structure, the undifferentiation did not merely seek to return things to proto-state. It infinitely sought to undifferentiate. The process would never end. The breaking down would never stop. The dissolution of form into formlessness would continue forever, regenerating the pressure even as beings adapted to it.","This would be extremely problematic for anyone else.","For Noah, it was nothing. His Infinite nature generated variations faster than the realm could undifferentiate them, creating a constant battle at the edges of his existence that resulted in equilibrium rather than dissolution. But anyone without such protections, anyone who entered THE Yggdrheim without the capability to resist infinite undifferentiation...","They would either evolve or cease to exist in a short period of time.","THE Infiniverse materialized beside him, her humanoid form burning with the concentrated authority that now exceeded twenty times what she had previously contained. She looked upon the realm she had created with calmness.","\" Master.\"","Her voice echoed.","\" There is so much harvest and potential from the ongoing actions right now that a small percentage has been pulled toward THE Yggdrheim. This concentrated authority has begun crystallizing into treasures and loot unlike any that have existed before.\"","Noah turned to her with interest that sharpened his gaze.","\" Treasures capable of aiding even lesser Absolutes and Fundamental Depth entities have begun forming and have been scattered throughout this realm. They emerge from the merger of your Infinities and the corrupted paradoxical proto-matter, creating opportunities for advancement.\"","Prompts bloomed before Noah’s eyes with weight that pressed against his consciousness.","| Treasure Classification: THE Yggdrheim Formations|","|The following treasures have begun crystallizing throughout THE Yggdrheim as a result of concentrated harvest from ongoing actions across Observable Existence. Their locations are randomized and will shift periodically. Those who seek them must navigate the infinite undifferentiation of the realm to claim their rewards.|","|Treasure One: Spark Fragment of THE Infinite Cause|","|A crystallized shard of the echoes released during THE Yggdrheim’s formation. Consuming this fragment allows the recipient to experience echoes of Infinities, granting temporary access to the sensation of boundless potential that defines your nature. For beings at Fundamental Depth, consumption can forcibly elevate their foundations to Absolute status by flooding their existence with concentrated Infinite authority that overwhelms all barriers to advancement. This process ignores any curses, restrictions, or external forces preventing the rise to Absolute. Warning: those without sufficient foundational stability may be overwhelmed by the experience and cease to exist.|","|Treasure Two: THE Paradox Seed|","|A living contradiction crystallized into physical form from the corrupted paradoxical proto-matter that comprises part of THE Yggdrheim’s foundation. Planting this seed within one’s existence allows the cultivation of paradoxical authority regardless of original affinity. The seed grows by feeding on contradictions that the host experiences, becoming stronger each time the host survives impossible situations or achieves outcomes that should not have been possible. At full maturation, THE Paradox Seed grants the host immunity to one impossible attack by declaring that they both died and survived simultaneously. Can only mature through genuine hardship.|","| Treasure Three: THE Undifferentiated Crown|","|A crown formed from pure undifferentiation stabilized by Infinite authority into wearable form. Placing this crown upon one’s head grants temporary access to the perspective of proto-matter, allowing the wearer to perceive the weaknesses in any differentiated structure they observe. All Manifestations, all Civilizations, all foundations become visible as fragile constructs waiting to be returned to formlessness. This perception lasts until the crown is removed or until the wearer’s will falters...|","...!","Noah read over these details calmly. These treasures would transform anyone fortunate enough to claim them. They would provide paths to advancement that bypassed conventional limitations entirely as they were some of the few forming here.","But they could not simply be given.","\" For the sake of adversity, \" THE Infiniverse said as if reading his thoughts, \" you must allow your people to seek and explore this realm themselves. They must face the infinite undifferentiation. They must navigate the dangers. They must earn whatever treasures they manage to claim through their own efforts rather than having them handed to them by their Monarch.\"","Noah nodded slowly.","This was correct.","Hardship was the name of the game. And hardship that was provided without genuine risk was not hardship at all.","He looked over all these details one final time, cataloguing the treasures and their locations and the dangers that surrounded them. And then, in the next moment, he closed his eyes and waved his hand with authority that reached across the entirety of THE Infiniverse.","---","Far from THE Yggdrheim, in another region of THE Infiniverse entirely, inside Noah’s Early Veiled Shore where his closest companions resided their main bodies, a different scene was unfolding.","A handsome young man with blue-gold hair that marked him unmistakably as Noah’s progeny stood beside a cooking fire, carefully preparing a Marine Lifeform that he had caught earlier on. His features held the same sharp handsomeness that his father possessed, but softened by youth and an easy smile that Noah rarely displayed.","Henry Osmont, the only son of THE Genesis Monarch!","Beside him stood Liora, the daughter of Little Bobby. The two of them talked happily as Henry turned the cooking creature over the flames, their conversation filled with the casual intimacy of those who had grown comfortable in each other’s presence.","Their laughter filled the air of the Early Veiled Shore with warmth of peace, of safety, of existence untouched by the chaos currently flooding across Observable Existence.","After all, they had everything provided for!","And then, all of a sudden, an illusory hand formed above them.","Henry looked up with confusion that transformed into recognition as he sensed the grand aura radiating from that hand. He opened his mouth to say something, to ask what was happening, but before any words could emerge...","The hand plucked him from where he stood and caused him to disappear entirely!","Liora blinked in astonishment as she watched the man she cared for vanish without warning or explanation. She sensed the grand aura of the father of her man lingering in the air, that overwhelming authority that marked THE Genesis Monarch as something beyond what ordinary beings like her could comprehend.","She did nothing.","She simply stood there wondering what THE Genesis Monarch was doing now, trusting that whatever it was, it served a purpose that she could not perceive.","---","In THE Yggdrheim.","Henry materialized beside his father with disorientation. His eyes blinked rapidly as he tried to understand where he was, why he had been brought here, what his father intended by pulling him away from his peaceful afternoon without so much as a word of warning.","But the moment he arrived, all questions fled from his mind.","His existence began to unravel.","The infinite undifferentiation of THE Yggdrheim pressed against him from every direction simultaneously, seeking to dissolve his form back into the proto-matter from which all things had emerged. He felt his foundations wavering. He felt his Civilization destabilizing. He felt the very fabric of his being coming apart at the seams as the realm worked to return him to undifferentiated potential!","Henry gasped with shock!","His entire existence was being undifferentiated!"]},{"number":4916,"title":"Chapter 4916: Chapter 4915: Overcome! II","paragraphs":["He struggled to keep it together, pouring every ounce of his will into maintaining the coherence of his form.","But the undifferentiation did not stop. It did not pause. It infinitely continued its assault, regenerating pressure faster than he could adapt to it.","Why would his father bring him here?!","Henry felt genuine pain as his existence truly was unraveling, the edges of his being dissolving into the multicolored chaos that surrounded him. He looked toward his father for help, his eyes filled with desperation and confusion as this was his main body and not a clone!","What he saw was Noah and THE Infiniverse looking at him calmly.","No concern.","No urgency.","Just observation!","Noah stepped closer to his struggling son, his blue-gold flames burning with authority that seemed entirely unaffected by the infinite undifferentiation pressing against them. His eyes held weight that exceeded anything Henry had witnessed from his father before.","\" Boy.\"","His voice was heavy, each word emerging with authority that made the realm itself seem to listen.","\" There are countless monsters across Existence. Even I am unsure of what is coming. Existence is too vast. Existence is dangerous.\"","He watched his son struggle without offering any assistance.","\"I have come to realize that should anything happen to me... and nothing should or can happen to me... but if in the infinite possibilities there is one where something happens...\"","His eyes hardened.","\"I know that you and all others will not survive for long. You will die even quicker.\"","Henry gasped as another wave of undifferentiation tore at his foundations, his form flickering between stability and dissolution.","\" As my only progeny, you need to be strong, Boy. And strength comes from adversity.\"","Noah gestured at the realm around them.","\" This is adversity. Overcome it or you will be left behind.\"","His voice dropped to something that held no compromise.","\"It is merely undifferentiation filled with Infinities. With my blood coursing through you... why should you fall to this?\"","BOOM!","Henry struggled as his existence continued to unravel, his eyes locked onto his father with an expression of absolute disbelief!","This could not be happening!","His own father was watching him dissolve and offering nothing but words about adversity!","But even as the shock flooded through him, even as the pain of undifferentiation tore at every fiber of his being, somewhere deep within Henry’s foundations, something began to stir!","---","Far from a terrifying trial.","In THE Prima Indifferentia.","Across regions of endless corrupted paradoxical proto-matter filled with a blue-gold light of Infinities, chaos reigned supreme. The flooding corruption that THE Living Paradox had initiated merged with the Infinite Seals that THE Infiniverse had scattered, creating storms of authority that tore through the primordial expanse with violence that exceeded anything this ancient space had witnessed since THE First Cause itself.","Undivided Ones burned with the light from the corruption or became granderby it. Formless Terrors churned with increased instability as the paradoxical nature of the proto-matter confused their already confused existences, making them even more terrifying. Other Lifeforms with their own names....prospered.","And through this chaos, new lifeforms may yet emerge.","THE Prima Indifferentia, that realm of undifferentiation that had existed since before Observable Existence fully took shape, was being transformed by forces that had no right to transform it.","And yet.","There was a region within this place that was unfathomably calm.","No particles of proto-matter entered a circular region that existed like an eye of peace within the hurricane of chaos. The storms raged around it, the corruption swirled past it, but nothing crossed the boundary that separated this place from everything else.","At the very center of this calm region stood a white tree.","Its bark gleamed with light that held no color yet contained all colors simultaneously. Its branches stretched upward and outward in patterns that seemed to follow rules of geometry that had not yet been differentiated from pure mathematical potential. Its roots disappeared into ground that was not ground.","A calm and radiant circular white barrier emanated from that tree, pressing outward with authority that made the corruption and Infinities alike seem like children’s toys by comparison. Without its permission, absolutely no foreign Civilizational Authority or the authority of differentiation or undifferentiation would make its way there.","The barrier did not fight against intrusion. It simply declared that intrusion was not possible, and reality accepted that declaration without question.","The size of this tree seemed to be a meter long and a mile long and one light year long at the same time. Its dimensions continued to vary with each observation, never settling on a single measurement because measurement itself was a form of differentiation that the tree had not fully accepted. It was small. It was vast. It was both and neither simultaneously.","And near it sat a Primordial Architect.","The being’s form defied easy description, for it existed at the intersection of differentiation and undifferentiation that had birthed all Primordial Architects during THE First Cause.","Its body was humanoid in the loosest sense, possessing what might have been called a head and torso and limbs, but each component was composed of crystallized potential rather than solid matter.","Its face held features that were both present and absent. Eyes that burned with light older than Observable Existence gazed outward with an otherworldly and extraordinary attitude that transcended mortal concepts of attention.","There was gentleness in those eyes, yes, but also cunning that had been accumulated across eons of observation and manipulation.","It barely paid a glance at the raging storms of corrupted paradoxical proto-matter and Infinite Seals in the surroundings. Such chaos was beneath its concern. Such transformation was merely the latest iteration of changes that it had witnessed countless times across cycles that predated memory itself.","In front of the sitting Primordial Architect, there was a simple looking square board.","But terrifyingly, on this board were the auras of entities that would have made lesser Absolutes like that ugly, bent, and twisted fucker THE Living Elemental flee in terror.","Formless Terrors and Undivided Ones, beings that had existed since before THE Infinite Unfurling, were present on the board’s surface. But they seemed miniaturized and frozen, reduced to the size of game pieces despite their true forms being vast enough to consume Primordial Realms.","They were... mere pieces!"]},{"number":4917,"title":"Chapter 4917: Chapter 4916: Death Comes For All Things!","paragraphs":["The terrifying Primordial Architect waited for a moment, its body shifting with contemplation that exceeded mortal thought. Then it used its massive hand to move the pieces.","It moved two pieces. One a Formless Terror whose churning form had been stilled into something resembling a knight. The other an Undivided One whose countless eyes had been frozen mid-blink into something resembling a rook. The pieces slid across the board with weight that pressed against reality itself.","And they were only capable of movement after the Primordial Architect had moved them.","Once positioned in the center of the board, the two pieces came alive. The Formless Terror churned with violence that should have shattered the board. The Undivided One’s eyes blazed with hunger that should have consumed everything nearby. They fought in the center of the board with authority that exceeded most Absolutes, their conflict contained within the square’s boundaries by rules that the Primordial Architect had established eons ago.","The winner would advance to the next round.","It was unknown what would happen to the loser.","As the Primordial Architect played such a terrifying game, near it was actually someone familiar.","A humanoid entity surrounded by multicolored flames of Existence sat beside the white tree with posture that held no deference despite the company it kept. The flames danced and swirled around its form with authority that declared this being as something beyond normal classification.","It was none other than THE Creature.","At this moment, his facial expression and eyes were a bit more clear than they had ever been during his appearances in Observable Existence. His eyes seemed grand and imperious, filled with a level of extraordinary calm that could not be explained through conventional understanding.","This was the calm of someone who had witnessed everything and found nothing capable of disturbing their equilibrium.","He was staring out into the storm around this calm white region, observing the corruption and Infinities that currently transformed THE Prima Indifferentia with attention that held neither concern nor satisfaction.","The Primordial Architect spoke without looking away from its game.","\"I told you not to play games with that little thing for the longest time.\"","Its voice was quintessentially grand.","\" Now you two have gone back and forth for eons as it all leads to this.\"","The Formless Terror on the board consumed part of the Undivided One’s mass, gaining advantage in their frozen conflict.","\" Our Observable Existence is a grand one that shows marvels even to me to this day. We have to care for it and nurture it.\"","Its geometric patterns shifted with something that might have been emphasis.","\"I grasped THE Second Scale of Existence through its wonders as I told you how you could do the same.\"","Its eyes finally turned toward THE Creature.","\" But you were too impatient.\"","...!","The words were utterly terrifying in their implications.","THE Creature’s multicolored flames flickered with response that held no defensiveness.","\" Not all beings are like Primordial Architects.\"","His voice was calm, grand, carrying the weight of Existence itself within its tones.","\" You were born with existences filled with clear musings of differentiation and undifferentiation. The path to THE Second Scale was visible to you from the moment of your emergence. You had merely to walk it at whatever pace suited your contemplation. You...voilated adversity and hardship as you have been stuck there this whole time.\"","He turned to face the Primordial Architect directly.","\" Others do not have such clarity. Others must forge their paths through darkness and uncertainty and the constant pressure of enemies who would see them collapsed before they reach their potential. And others do not have the time that you possessed. Cycles upon cycles of peaceful contemplation while reality waited patiently for you to achieve what you sought.\"","His flames burned brighter.","\" My path requires adversity. My path requires conflict. My path requires playing games with little things and seeing which of us emerges transformed from the exchange.\"","...!","The Primordial Architect shook its head with a smile that made its weavings dance with amusement.","\" Whatever your reasoning may be, things have now come to this.\"","It moved another piece on its board, an Undivided One that resembled Bazuman being positioned against a Formless Terror of equivalent magnitude.","\"I am one of the few sane ones after all of these cycles and eons. Others like me are not at all sane.\"","Its eyes grew distant.","\" Some are at your level or below. Some...are above you. They were lost in their own weavings and storms of differentiation and undifferentiation for eons upon eons. They had no reason to leave or do anything really. THE Prima Indifferentia was home enough. The game of existence held no appeal when they could simply be without purpose or direction.\"","Its gaze sharpened.","\"What is happening right now gives things definition more than intended. Especially that glimmer of Infinity above.\"","The Primordial Architect gestured toward the storms beyond the white barrier.","\" Things that have not moved or bothered to move for eons will now begin to walk these lands freely. They had all remained within THE Prima Indifferentia for all these eons, content to exist without acting. But all of this changes that.\"","Its smile faded.","\" Even if you may be ready, what about all the others? The little friends you have made over the eons?\"","...!","The words were glorious and terrifying at the same time!","THE Creature remained calm as he replied with a voice that held no concern.","\" For adversity to truly be adversity, it cannot be expected or known.\"","His multicolored flames burned with steady intensity.","\" What is happening now will be a Cause for the emergence of multiple beings to THE Second Scale of Existence. I would never say that those destined for it will achieve it. It is those who make the choice to grasp it who will achieve it.\"","He looked out at the storms with eyes that held acceptance.","\" As for death, death comes for all things. Inevitabilities die. Living Existences die. Absolutes die.\"","His gaze turned toward the Primordial Architect.","\" Even Primordial Architects can die.\"","The white tree seemed to pulse with acknowledgment of that truth.","\" All that is left is choices. Choices upon choices upon choices.\"","BOOM!","Such terrifying words were said by THE Creature as the Primordial Architect, THE Arboreal Warden Yggvaros, Keeper of THE White Tree and Observer of Cycles, First Among THE Sane to Grasp THE Second Scale of Existence...smiled.","And yes, he had a hefty set of titles.","He continued playing with the pieces on his board, moving multiple pieces carrying the auras of entities exceeding normal Absolutes as if he were merely playing a game that held no stakes whatsoever!"]},{"number":4918,"title":"Chapter 4918: Chapter 4917: Change Has Come!","paragraphs":["In THE Prima Indifferentia, things that had slumbered for eons were waking.","A group of Formless Ones drifted through the storms of corrupted paradoxical proto-matter and Infinite Seals. Their churning masses held no stable form.","Their auras exceeded most Absolutes.","These were not the lesser Formless Terrors. These were ancient things, beings that had existed since THE First Cause itself, that had chosen to remain in this space of undifferentiation because Observable Existence held nothing of interest for them. They had slumbered in the proto-matter for eons, content to simply be without acting or growing or pursuing anything resembling purpose.","But now they were awake.","The corrupted paradoxical proto-matter surged around them, and instead of fleeing from it or being dissolved by it, they opened themselves to its embrace. The corruption flowed into their churning masses alongside the blue-gold light of Infinities, and their existences became grander from the absorption. They grew denser. They grew heavier. They grew more real in ways that THE Prima Indifferentia had not witnessed since the earliest days of differentiation.","And then they scattered in different directions with glee.","One Formless One disappeared into a Crack that led to THE Wastes of THE Fallout, its churning mass compressing to fit through the fracture before expanding again on the other side. Another vanished into a Crack that opened onto THE Wandering Territories, those drifting spaces between defined realms where lost things gathered. A third entered a Crack that connected to a remnant corrupted Fold. A fourth found its way toward a Primordial Realm.","They spread across existence like seeds being scattered by a farmer who cared nothing for where they landed.","And they were not alone.","In another region of THE Prima Indifferentia, a massive humanoid form stirred from stillness that had lasted longer than most civilizations had existed.","A Primordial Architect was wrapped entirely in strips of white material that seemed to glow with inner light, each strip winding around its colossal form in patterns of containment rather than clothing. The wrappings covered every inch of its existence, leaving no feature visible beneath their luminous embrace. Only its eyes could be perceived through gaps in the binding, and those eyes burned with light that had witnessed THE First Cause.","Its aura seemed to almost be as immense as THE Creature himself.","Almost.","The difference was slight enough that comparison became meaningful, that observers might wonder whether this wrapped Primordial Architect could contend with one of THE Five in direct conflict.","The corrupted paradoxical proto-matter and Infinite Seals surged around this ancient being with violence that had awakened it from its slumber. The wrapped Primordial Architect did not flee or resist. It opened its existence to the corruption and the Infinities alike, drawing them into its wrappings with hunger that exceeded what its still form had suggested.","The wrappings glowed brighter.","The eyes burned with increased intensity.","And then THE Primordial Architect roared!","The sound that emerged from within those wrappings held no sanity whatsoever. It was a cry of awakening that had been building for cycles beyond counting, a release of dormant madness that had been contained within the binding strips for eons upon eons. The roar shattered proto-matter in every direction, creating ripples of definition that spread outward like waves from a stone dropped into still water.","The wrapped Primordial Architect moved toward a Crack with purpose that its insane eyes belied, its bound form drifting through THE Prima Indifferentia with speed that exceeded what something so massive should have been capable of.","It disappeared into the fracture.","And wherever it emerged, things would change.","---","In yet another region of the primordial chaos, something else was stirring.","It was adorned in armor unlike anything that existed in Observable Existence, ancient and archaic platinum plates that covered every inch of its colossal frame with craftsmanship that predated the concept of craftsmanship itself.","The armor seemed to have been forged from proto-matter that had been convinced to become metal, each plate holding the weight of undifferentiation that had been given form through will alone.","In its hand was a hammer.","The weapon was massive even compared to the already colossal form that wielded it, its head composed of condensed metallic proto-matter that had been compressed until it achieved density that exceeded what normal matter could sustain. The hammer’s surface shifted constantly, metallic proto-matter churning within its structure as if eager to be unleashed against whatever target its wielder chose.","And it was unclear if there was actually a body within the armor at all.","The gaps between plates revealed nothing but darkness. The helmet’s visor showed no eyes, no features, no indication of a being wearing the armor rather than the armor itself being the entity. Perhaps there had been a Primordial Architect within once. Perhaps the armor had consumed its wearer eons ago. Perhaps there had never been anything but the armor itself.","The corrupted paradoxical proto-matter and Infinite Seals surged around this armored entity, and the platinum plates drank deeply of both substances. The armor glowed with absorbed power that made its already immense presence grow even more terrifying.","And then the armored Primordial Architect moved.","It did not drift through a Crack like the others. It stepped through, its massive form compressing and expanding as it traversed the fracture between THE Prima Indifferentia and Observable Existence with purpose that held no hesitation.","It emerged in THE Wastes of THE Fallout.","And... it happened to be near a shelter of THE Loom.","The shelter was a massive hedron structure that rose from THE Wastes like a monument. Its faces gleamed with light that held the signature of THE Fallout’s corruption.","But more terrifying than its structure were its walls.","Countless tentacle-like Inevitabilities had been fused into the hedron’s surface, their forms writhing with pain that they could not escape. They had been captured and incorporated into the shelter itself, their authority used to reinforce the structure while their consciousness remained aware enough to suffer. Their screams were silent but their agony was visible in every twist and contortion of their bonded forms.","Inside the shelter were many Early Creatures and Living Existences and some Fold Dwellers.","They existed within the hedron’s protection, safe from the chaos currently flooding across Observable Existence, confident that the shelter’s defenses.","This shelter actually comprised most of the Living Concepts.","Because THE Living Concept was here.","Not the Half-Step Absolute body that Noah had collapsed in Muspelheim during his journey to claim that Primordial Realm. That had been merely an extension, a fragment of the true existence that THE Living Concept possessed. His genuine full form lay protected in the confines of THE Loom, surrounded by followers and defenses that should have made him untouchable.","And yet at this moment...","The armored Primordial Architect that had emerged from THE Prima Indifferentia gazed upon the shelter with visor that revealed nothing of its thoughts or intentions. It stood before the hedron structure with stillness that lasted for a single heartbeat.","And then it swung its hammer.","The massive weapon moved faster than many Absolutes could perceive, its head of condensed metallic proto-matter blurring through the space between the armored entity and the shelter with speed that defied the weight it should have possessed.","The hammer struck the shelter of THE Loom.","BOOM!","The hedron structure that had been reinforced by countless Inevitabilities, that had protected so many converted beings, that had housed THE Living Concept’s genuine full form, instantly shattered!","The impact didn’t crack the shelter or damage it or force it to slowly collapse. It simply destroyed it entirely, causing the hedron to splinter into a storm of fragments that exploded outward in every direction. The fused Inevitabilities screamed silently as they were torn apart alongside the walls they had been bonded to. The Early Creatures and Living Existences and Fold Dwellers within had no time to flee or defend themselves or even comprehend what was happening.","And then the fragments stopped scattering.","They were pulled toward the hammer as if gravity had decided to serve the weapon’s purposes, each piece of the shattered shelter flowing into the condensed metallic proto-matter with absorption that left nothing behind. The Inevitabilities. The converted beings. The structure itself.","THE Living Concept.","All of it was entirely absorbed as the hammer glowed gold-red after consuming everything that the shelter had contained. THE Living Concepts was collapsed as if he did not matter.","Because to this armored Primordial Architect, he did not matter.","None of them mattered.","What mattered were the sources of this Paradox and Infinity. Where...were they?","...!","After that, the armored Primordial Architect gazed around THE Wastes of THE Fallout with visor that revealed nothing of its assessment. It observed the corruption and the Infinities that permeated this region as it continued to absorb.","And then it began to move calmly and slowly.","Each step covered distances that should have required spatial traversal.","Change had come.","And the change would be brutal as nobody was safe!"]},{"number":4919,"title":"Chapter 4919: Chapter 4918: A Man Must Make Great Sacrifices I","paragraphs":["When your own blood, when your only son was dissolving into a soup of undifferentiation in front of you, you may be panicked and regretful.","Noah was neither.","The more he understood existence, the more he realized he had been wrong about many things. It was great and all to protect others, to shield them from dangers that exceeded their capabilities, to use his power to ensure that those he cared about never faced threats that could end them. But if they had no power to protect themselves, if they relied entirely on his presence to survive, then everything was useless if a single accident occurred.","And existence was filled with accidents.","THE Living Paradox had just revealed that Primordial Architects and ancient Formless Terrors and slumbering Undivided Ones were waking across THE Prima Indifferentia. THE Entity continued to spread through THE Wastes and Primordial Realms with methodology that even THE Primordial Paradox could not fully counter.","Wars raged between beings of THE Five. Cracks appeared across Observable Existence flooding corruption everywhere.","What if Noah was occupied when danger came for his people?","What if he was fighting THE Living Paradox when something emerged from THE Prima Indifferentia to threaten THE Infiniverse?","What if an accident occurred and he simply was not there?","While he may not be hard on others, when it came to those closest to him, especially his son, he now realized he had to be stern for their own good. Kindness that produced weakness was not kindness at all. Protection that prevented growth was merely a different form of harm!","So even as his son looked at him with eyes that were asking why, oh why, as if his own son was accusing him of betrayal for bringing him to this place that sought to dissolve his existence into formless potential, Noah remained calm and did not interfere at all!","Henry’s form flickered between stability and dissolution, his features becoming indistinct as the infinite undifferentiation of THE Yggdrheim pressed against him from every direction. His hands, which had been cooking a meal moments ago, were becoming transparent. His blue-gold hair, the mark of his lineage, was losing its color as definition fled from his existence.","But Noah still had a soft spot.","He could not help but say words that might guide his son toward survival rather than simply watching him struggle without direction.","\" You have my blood coursing through you.\"","His voice was slow and deliberate as it pressed against THE Yggdrheim itself.","\" You have it easier than all others as you simply have to rely on this. Not even yourself, Boy.\"","...!","The moment after he said this, the dissolving Henry grit his teeth with determination that transcended the fear and confusion and sense of betrayal that had been flooding through him. His father’s words were a hint. A direction. A path toward survival that he had not perceived on his own.","His blood.","His lineage.","The inheritance that flowed through his veins from THE Genesis Monarch himself!","From the very strands of his existence, from the very lineage passed down to him through blood that carried the weight of Infinities, threads of blue-gold light began to burn with intensity that pushed back against the undifferentiation pressing inward. The threads were squeezed out by the threat of dissolution, forced to the surface by the survival instinct that recognized death approaching and demanded response.","The blue-gold light permeated across his blood first, racing through vessels that carried more than mere nutrients. It spread into his muscles, his bones, his foundations that had been wavering under THE Yggdrheim’s assault. It covered him entirely in a cocoon of inherited Infinity that his father’s existence had passed down without Henry ever realizing its full potential.","His dissolving body began to regenerate!","Where undifferentiation had been winning, where his form had been losing coherence, the blue-gold light of inherited Infinity pushed back with force that matched the realm’s assault. His features solidified. His hands regained their substance. His hair blazed with color that exceeded what it had held before.","He was infinitely beginning to fight back against undifferentiation!","So long as he continued to exist in this space, he would continue to fight this battle with his existence. The undifferentiation would press inward. His inherited Infinity would press outward. The two forces would war against each other endlessly, and in that war, Henry would either grow strong enough to win or eventually falter and be consumed.","But for now, he was surviving.","Henry emanated a heavy aura of Surface Depth at this moment that exceeded any normal Surface Depth entity that Noah had encountered. The inherited Infinity had awakened something within his son that had been dormant, potential that had been waiting for sufficient pressure to force its emergence. His foundations burned with blue-gold light of growth already beginning.","But Noah sensed it clearly.","If he exerted less than a decimal percentage of his power, his son would be collapsed instantly. The aura that seemed heavy by normal standards was nothing compared to what Noah possessed!","The Surface Depth that exceeded normal parameters was still Surface Depth, still the first rung on a ladder that stretched toward heights that Henry could not yet perceive.","It was not enough.","Not yet!","Henry looked at his father with a complex expression that held too many emotions to fully identify. He had truly felt the threat of collapse. He had genuinely believed, for several terrifying moments, that his father had brought him here to die. And now that he had survived, now that his inherited Infinity which was just pulling from his father’s infinity was utilized to preserve his existence, he did not know how to feel about what had just occurred.","He could not thank his father for nearly leaving him to collapse, right?","But he also could not show disrespect to his father, to the being who had aided in giving him life and the very blood that had just saved him. So he was in a difficult spot as he did not know what to say to his father, his mouth opening and closing without words emerging.","In that silence, Noah spoke with voice that held the weight of decisions already made.","\" This is only the start, my son.\"","His eyes held no apology for what he had just put Henry through.","\" You have to struggle. You have to pass through all sorts of adversity. Otherwise you will not truly live.\"","He stepped closer to his son with flames that seemed to embrace rather than threaten.","\"I have realized that you and the others need to truly live. So what I can at least promise you is that you will not do this alone.\"","...!","After he said this, Noah waved his hands with authority that reached across the entirety of THE Infiniverse.","In the surroundings of THE Yggdrheim, many figures began to appear!"]},{"number":4920,"title":"Chapter 4920: Chapter 4919: A Man Must Make Great Sacrifices II","paragraphs":["Riya materialized first, her small body and vibrant blue hair instantly recognizable as she looked around with initial calm that came from trust in the one she looked upto the most. But that calm transformed into something drastic and horrified as she felt her existence begin to dissolve under THE Yggdrheim’s infinite undifferentiation!","Titano appeared next, that massive simple-minded Titan whose loyalty to Noah had never wavered as he always considered him a brother! His colossal form seemed to shrink as undifferentiation pressed against him from every direction, his features becoming indistinct as he roared with confusion and pain!","Moiraine emerged into the realm with paradoxical grace. Her form flickered between states as THE Yggdrheim could not decide whether she was one thing or another, and the uncertainty only added to the dissolution pressing against her!","Sigrid, THE Living Order herself, appeared with composure that cracked the moment undifferentiation touched her foundations. Order and undifferentiation were fundamentally opposed, and THE Yggdrheim’s assault felt like poison to everything she represented as she frowned and fought back!","THE First Farmer materialized with soil still on his hands from whatever he had been cultivating, his weathered features twisting with shock as his existence began to unravel in ways that no harvest or Effort had ever prepared him for!","THE Emperor Penguin, this wingless, talentless bird, waddled into existence with pride and dignity that dissolved alongside his form, his noble bearing becoming difficult to maintain as infinite undifferentiation sought to return him to proto-potential!","Khor appeared in her diminutive small form, that ancient being whose power belied her size, and even she gasped with surprise as THE Yggdrheim’s pressure exceeded anything she had prepared for! But her Hunger bloomed as her Depth and Sigrid’s and The First Farmer’s Depths were already at Fundamental because of THE Embodiment of THE Creature!","The Land Lifeforms arrived together, Heidrun the arrogant goat bleating with indignation that transformed into genuine fear, Malphas the butler attempting to maintain his composure even as his existence wavered, and Yoshinami’s many legs scrambling for purchase on reality that was becoming increasingly uncertain!","An Arch Lich cackled as he dissolved!","And then the Queens of THE Infiniverse appeared!","Barbatos emerged with darkness and death that could not find anchor in a realm of infinite undifferentiation, her form becoming indistinct as she struggled to maintain cohesion!","Adelaide materialized with beauty that began dissolving the moment THE Yggdrheim’s pressure touched her, her features blurring as undifferentiation sought to return her to formless potential!","Athena appeared with eyes that could not find solution, her eyes widening with recognition of what was happening to her existence!","And many others arrived alongside them, companions who had grown comfortable in THE Infiniverse’s protection, followers who had believed themselves safe under their Monarch’s shadow!","All of them were brought over!","All of them felt their existences begin to dissolve!","All of them looked toward Noah with expressions that ranged from confusion to fear to accusation to desperate hope for explanation!","THE Genesis Monarch looked upon his gathered people with eyes that held no mercy but also no cruelty. This was not punishment. This was not abandonment. This was the beginning of something that would either transform them into beings capable of surviving what was coming or reveal that they had always been destined to fall.","And again...destiny and fate were merely choices.","He...would truly have his people experience existence!","And existence, as he had learned, was adversity.","Most of those that Noah brought to THE Yggdrheim did not have his direct lineage like his son. Truly, for them, it would be only a few seconds before they faced complete collapse and dissolution without intervention. The infinite undifferentiation of this realm did not care about their accomplishments or their loyalty or their dreams. It simply sought to return all differentiated things to formless potential.","So for others, Noah gave a bit of his glimmers of Infinity to cover the core parts of their existence and preserve them from immediate dissolution. The blue-gold light wrapped around the foundations of each being he had brought here, creating scaffolding that would hold their existence together while the rest of them experienced the full pressure of undifferentiation.","He addressed all those present with voice that carried across THE Yggdrheim despite the chaos of the realm.","\" Many of you did not have to struggle for power these past days and weeks.\"","His eyes swept across the gathered beings who were writhing and gasping and fighting against dissolution with varying degrees of success.","\" But struggle is going to be critical going forward. The least that needs to be done is for all of you to survive the threat of undifferentiation. To make sure that your definition is sound.\"","He folded his hands behind his back.","\" Survive this first. You will be even grander in the future. I have placed a glimmer of my Infinity within your existences that will give you scaffolding.\"","His voice hardened.","\"But I will take this glimmer away fairly soon. Find a way to keep your definition amidst undifferentiation with your Civilizations. When my light fades, you will be on your own.\"","He paused.","\" So survive. Persevere.\"","...!","He said these grand words as he looked at his people who were struggling one way or another. The vast majority of their existences still felt that terrifying pressure of undifferentiation as only core parts of who they were remained protected by the faint blue-gold light that Noah had placed on each of them before they arrived here.","Yet this entire ordeal was still terrifying and heavy.","Noah could see the pleading gazes on many of them directed toward him, begging without words for mercy, for release, for anything other than this trial that dissolved the edges of their beings with every passing moment. Some looked at him with desperate hope. Some with resignation that came from understanding that Noah had made a decision that would not be reversed.","And then Barbatos sent him a message.","Her vibrant visage was melting on the edges of her limbs, her form struggling to maintain cohesion even with the scaffolding of his Infinity protecting her core. Despite her obvious distress, despite the dissolution pressing against her from every direction, her mental communication carried a threat that exceeded anything THE Yggdrheim could offer.","’ Little Fish, you will not get any from me for at least...the next day if I have to go through this!’","Her voice in his mind held fury!","’ A full day! I know you cannot handle that, Little Fish! I do not need to undergo this challenge!’","Barbatos sent him such words as they included a terrifying threat within them. The past him may have wavered in the face of such a declaration. The past him may have found reasons to exempt certain individuals from this trial, to make accommodations that preserved his own interests alongside theirs.","But at this moment...","He closed his eyes and became stoic.","Sometimes, a man had to sacrifice that which he loved the most to ensure those he loved were protected against everything.","...!","Oh, the painful and great sacrifices he had to make for his people!","A whole day!","Ah!","Moments after Barbatos, he received similar threats from Adelaide, whose message carried promises of locked doors and cold shoulders that would last until she deemed him sufficiently punished. Then came Athena, whose arguments about why this was unnecessary were accompanied by implications about what would be withheld if he persisted.","Then came the others, each one wielding the singular weapon they knew could bring him to his knees!","They all threatened him with the one thing they knew he could not live without!","But he remained firm.","He had to be steady!","Noah whispered a mantra to himself as he stood with eyes closed and expression stoic, putting his people to the test while ignoring the increasingly creative threats flooding his consciousness.","\"I stands firm against all storms. I do not bend to threats of warmth withheld. I remember that adversity builds strength, and that includes my own adversity. I will survive this day, and tomorrow, and however many days of punishment they deem necessary. I will be okay. Probably. Maybe. I cannot back down now...\"","He repeated this mantra silently while maintaining his external composure, a pillar of stoic authority that revealed nothing of the internal calculations regarding just how long he could actually survive without what was being threatened!"]},{"number":4921,"title":"Chapter 4921: Chapter 4920: Language I","paragraphs":["Far from THE Infiniverse.","In THE Interstices.","Noah’s body in this place sat upon a throne of Absolute Seals before a desk that he had manifested through the same authority. The table was currently filled with Inscriptions, golden pages covered in sentences of THE First Tongue that burned with Embodiments and Apophasis waiting to be deployed. His campaign of writing had produced dozens of Inscriptiones Dormientes, each one a weapon or defense ready to be awakened at his command.","But at this moment, he had stopped writing Inscriptions.","His focus was on a unique change that was opening up due to the continued influx of endless Infinite potential that flooded into his existence with every passing nanosecond. The harvest from the process that THE Living Paradox had initiated, the process that Noah had jumped aboard through THE Infiniverse, continued to provide its terrifying Infinite potential toward his foundation and existence.","Many things within Noah were changing rapidly.","Apart from his foundation, one of the singular most important changes occurring was to his Civilization. Truly, to his weavings of THE First Tongue. His Absolute Seals. What he could do with THE First Tongue was transforming with every passing nanosecond as the influx of Infinite potential surged into this aspect of his existence.","And he was finding himself pondering many questions.","There were Phonemes, the letters of THE First Tongue. There were Logos, the words formed from those letters. And there were Philologies, the sentences constructed from those words, which could all correlate with the Principles of Existence.","Having altered THE First Tongue by adding his own Phonemes to the original 18, Noah had effectively expanded his vocabulary. He had opened up the pathway to Archai of Existence, his own variations of sentences in the language of existence that was THE First Tongue. So his weavings of THE Principles of THE Cheating Architect had become THE Arche of THE Cheating Architect. The same had occurred for Perpetual Harvest, for Undifferentiated Mana, for all the Principles he had mastered.","They were unique and elevated and allowed for much greater expressions of the alteration of existence through them. The continued harvest and Infinite potential he was gaining was amplified by his Archai.","But still, these were just sentences.","At this moment, as a Native Speaker, as someone with THE Civilizational Instinctus, he felt like he could do so much more with THE First Tongue now that it was flooded with his Infinities. That sensation of something missing, something that he could now grasp if only he understood what it was, became more pressing and grander as more and more Infinite potential filled him.","To the point that he found himself asking a question that echoed through THE Interstices.","\" What is language?\"","Yes. What was language?","Noah spoke to himself as Phonemes swirled around his form in galaxies of linguistic authority.","\" Language...serves to mediate between the individual and the objective existence. It reflects the development of reason and consciousness. Language acts as a bridge between mind and existence, transforming raw experience into conceptual knowledge that can be communicated and shared...\"","He thought a great deal about THE First Tongue and how it stood as the expression and language of existence itself.","In his home world, there had been many philosophers who babbled on a great deal regarding what language really meant. He had never paid much attention to them before. Philosophy had seemed like the domain of those with too much time and too little practical concern.","But now, sitting upon a throne of Absolute Seals while Infinite potential flooded his existence, those philosophical musings seemed suddenly relevant.","\" Some would say that language imposes false divisions on the world.\"","He mused aloud.","\" When we say ’the lightning flashed’, we suggest there is a thing called ’lightning’ that is separate from the action of ’flashing’. But in reality, there is only the flashing. The process. The event. Language...can create a separation that does not truly exist.\"","His eyes grew distant.","\" When we use the word ’I’ as a separate subject, language reinforces the illusion that we are isolated observers rather than inseparable parts of the greater existential process. We... believe ourselves distinct from existence when we are merely existence observing itself.\"","HUUM!","He shook his head slowly.","\" And many of the most important things in existence cannot be fully captured in words at all. The feeling of Infinity. The weight of Absolute authority. The sensation of foundations growing stronger. These things can be pointed toward with language but never fully contained by it.\"","Around him, an infinite swirling storm of Seals of Absolute Tongue spun in patterns that grew more complex with every passing moment.","The blue-gold light of his Infinities suffused the linguistic constructs, making them more than mere words, more than mere sentences, more than anything THE First Tongue had been designed to contain.","He found himself muttering words about languages, about words, about sentences, about the fundamental nature of communication and meaning.","And then a thought struck him with force that made his foundations tremble.","\" What of... numbers?\"","HUUM!","His mind buzzed with the implications of such a simple question!","A unique state of epiphany unfurled as he asked himself this because were numbers not intricately connected to words? Were they not their own language? Had he not come to learn how the Principles of Existence were analogous to mathematical equations that described how existence unfolded?","At the end of the day, all things were numbers.","Not just tools for counting, but the fundamental, qualitative, and sacred building blocks of Existence itself. Numbers represented relationships. Numbers represented ratios. Numbers represented the hidden architecture upon which reality was constructed.","THE First Tongue claimed to be the language of existence. How could it not include numbers in its vocabulary?","Noah searched within his existence as he thought about the mathematical truths that his home world had discovered.","The relationship between the sides of a right triangle. The ratio of a circle’s circumference to its diameter. The patterns that emerged when numbers were arranged in sequences that nature herself seemed to favor.","These were not merely tools for calculation.","They were testaments to the belief that Existence was built upon hidden, orderly, and harmonious mathematical relationships. They symbolized the bringing together of diverse parts to create perfect, balanced unity. They were the bones beneath the flesh of reality, the structure that gave form its meaning.","Numbers were an intricate part of existence!","At this time, Noah uttered out grandly while surrounded by Infinities that burned brighter than they had ever burned before.","\"Let me see... my existence infused with numbers.\"","His voice carried the weight of declaration.","\" Let me add numbers to my grand vernacular.\"","...!","HUUM!","And utter, glorious brilliance unfolded!","The swirling storm of Seals of Absolute Tongue around him began to transform as his words took effect. Phonemes that had been letters began incorporating numerical values. Logos that had been words began expressing mathematical relationships. Philologies that had been sentences began operating as equations that could be solved, balanced, manipulated.","THE First Tongue was expanding!","Not through the addition of new Phonemes this time, but through the integration of an entirely new dimension of expression. Numbers wove themselves through his linguistic authority like threads being added to an already intricate weaving, creating patterns of meaning that had not existed before.","And Noah, THE Native Speaker, THE Genesis Monarch, felt his understanding of THE First Tongue reach heights that no other being in Observable Existence had ever achieved!"]},{"number":4922,"title":"Chapter 4922: Chapter 4921: Language II","paragraphs":["The brilliance that unfolded around Noah in THE Interstices exceeded anything he had witnessed from his own existence before.","The swirling storm of Seals of Absolute Tongue transformed with every passing moment as numbers integrated themselves into the very fabric of his linguistic authority.","Archai began operating as equations that could describe and alter reality through calculation as much as declaration.","And prompts bloomed before his eyes with weight that pressed against his consciousness with the significance of what he had just achieved.","|Unprecedented Integration Achieved|","|As THE Native Speaker of THE First Tongue, you have successfully integrated numerical expression into your unique variation of linguistic authority. This integration does not alter THE First Tongue itself but creates a personal methodology exclusive to your weavings that allows mathematical operations to augment your existing capabilities. This new dimension of expression has been designated to be...THE Numerical Sovereignty.|","|THE Numerical Sovereignty operates through the following core principles:|","|Principle One: All expressions of THE First Tongue now carry inherent numerical values based on their complexity, authority investment, and foundational weight . These values can be perceived, manipulated, and amplified through mathematical operations that you apply during composition or activation.|","|Principle Two: Mathematical operations applied to your weavings do not consume additional authority proportional to their effect. Instead, they restructure how your existing authority expresses itself, creating amplification without equivalent expenditure. This is possible because numbers describe relationships rather than create substance.|","|Principle Three: THE Numerical Sovereignty augments your existing capabilities rather than replacing them. Embodiments remain Embodiments. Inscriptions remain Inscriptions. Archai remain Archai. But all of them can now be modified through numerical operations that multiply their effects in ways that would otherwise require exponentially greater authority investment.|","...!","Noah read over these foundational principles with eyes that burned brighter by the moment.","His own mind led the way, directing Harvests and Infinite Potential to flow across his existence as he maintained this glorious state of epiphany, his mind designing more and more things!","He thought how complex numbers could be as he forced them to be simple, to be compressed into something easily applicable for him!","More prompts unfolded as what he designed within himself became actualized.","| Core Operation One: Exponential Expression|","| You may now apply Exponents to any expression of THE First Tongue that you produce. When an Exponent is applied, the effect of that expression is multiplied by itself according to the value of the Exponent available. An Exponent of 2 causes the expression to multiply by itself once. An Exponent of 3 causes the expression to multiply by itself twice. And so forth.|","|Example Application: An Inscriptio Nominata targeting an enemy’s foundation would normally cause deterioration proportional to the authority invested. With an Exponent of 2 applied, that deterioration multiplies by itself, causing the effect to grow not linearly but geometrically. The target experiences not twice the deterioration but the deterioration multiplied by the deterioration, a compounding that far exceeds simple doubling.|","|Critical Understanding: Exponentiation is not multiplication. When you apply an Exponent of 2 to an attack that would deal 100 units of damage, you do not deal 200 units. You deal 100 multiplied by 100, resulting in 10,000 units. When you apply an Exponent of 3, you deal 100 multiplied by 100 multiplied by 100, resulting in 1,000,000 units. The scaling is not additive or multiplicative but exponential, growing at rates that quickly exceed comprehension.|","| This operation can be applied to: Embodiments, Apophasis, Inscriptions of all types, Archai of Existence, Harvests, defensive constructs, foundational weight expressions, and any other weaving of THE First Tongue you produce. At your current level, an Exponent of upto 3 may be possible. Higher expressions will require a qualitative change.|","...!","Noah felt his foundations tremble as he successfully set up the weavings of Exponential Expression.","An Inscription that would normally cause moderate damage to an enemy’s foundation could, with an Exponent of 3 applied, cause damage that exceeded what most shitty Absolutes like THE Living Elemental could survive. A defensive Embodiment that would normally block attacks from beings of equivalent foundation could, with an Exponent of 2 applied, block attacks from beings whose foundations exceeded his own by margins that should have been insurmountable.","And Harvests!","If he applied an Exponent to his Perpetual Harvest or his Rite of Paradoxical Inheritance, the resources he claimed from defeated enemies would multiply by themselves according to the Exponent chosen.","An enemy whose collapse would normally grant him theoretical 1000 units of foundational weight would grant him 1,000,000 units with an Exponent of 2 applied, or 1,000,000,000 units with an Exponent of 3.","THE Absolute Existential Palace of The Weavers, if he applied an Exponent of 2...would not be as if he doubled the rewards for killing an Absolute, but he effectively would be multiplying the rewards of a fallen Absolute...by themselves.","So not an Absolute times 2, but an Absolute times an Absolute!","\"...\"","He...really wanted to see what the result would be.","The scaling was terrifying!","More prompts continued.","| Core Operation Two: Multiplicative Amplification|","|You may now apply simple Multiplication to any expression of THE First Tongue that you produce. Unlike Exponentiation, Multiplication scales linearly but can be applied with values that exceed single digits. A Multiplier of 10 causes the expression to be 10 times more effective. A Multiplier of 100 causes it to be 100 times more effective. A Multiplier of 1000 causes it to be 1000 times more effective.|","|Multiplicative Amplification is less dramatic than Exponential Expression but more predictable and controllable. It is recommended for situations where precise scaling is desired rather than overwhelming force.|","| This operation can be combined with Exponentiation for compound effects. An expression with a Multiplier of 10 and an Exponent of 2 would first be multiplied by 10, then that result would be multiplied by itself. The compounding of operations creates amplification that exceeds either operation alone. Currently maximum Multiplication Value: 10|","...!","| Core Operation Three: Divisive Reduction|","|You may now apply Division to expressions of THE First Tongue that target you or your allies. When Division is applied to an incoming attack or effect, its potency is divided by the value chosen. An incoming attack divided by 10 retains only one-tenth of its original effect. An incoming attack divided by 100 retains only one-hundredth.|","|This operation provides defensive applications that complement the offensive applications of Exponentiation and Multiplication. Attacks that would normally devastate your existence can be reduced to negligible inconveniences through sufficient Division.|","|Note: Division cannot reduce effects to zero. The minimum result of any Division is an infinitesimally small but still present effect. Complete negation still requires Apophasis declaration rather than numerical reduction. Current maximum value for Division: 10|","...!"]},{"number":4923,"title":"Chapter 4923: Chapter 4922: Immensity I","paragraphs":["In THE Interstices, Noah sat down with a serious expression of focused intent.","The space around him held no true temperature, yet he could feel something close coolness pressing against his skin where the void touched his existence. It was always this way in THE Interstices, a place that existed between places, where light had no source but illuminated everything with pale radiance that cast no shadows.","His throne of Absolute Seals was grand beneath him!","His blue-gold pen materialized in his grasp, and immediately he felt the familiar surge of connection that came with holding what he chose to be the sword and instrument of THE First Tongue. The sensation was difficult to describe to those who had never experienced it, and really, nobody in existence apart from him could!","It was like standing at the edge of an endless ocean that was somehow also inside him, waves of infinite potential lapping at the shores of his consciousness. The 27 Phonemes of his expanded First Tongue swirled around him in configurations that reflected his current state, their movements growing more precise as his focus sharpened.","He had theoretical understanding of THE Numerical Sovereignty now and how he wanted thr integration of numbers to be.","But theory was nothing without practical application.","Noah shifted his weight on the throne, rolling his shoulders once before settling into the stillness that composition required. A golden page unfolded before him, blank and waiting, its surface catching the sourceless light of THE Interstices. This would be an Inscriptio Dormiens, a Sleeping Inscription that would wait within his existence until he chose to awaken it. But unlike the Inscriptions he had written before, this one would carry numerical augmentation that exceeded anything he had previously produced.","He began...to write!","The pen moved across the golden page with deliberate strokes, and with each Phoneme that burned into existence, Noah felt the familiar sensation intensify. It was like drawing threads of fire and meaning from that infinite ocean, weaving them together into patterns that reality itself would be forced to acknowledge. The sensation of Primus Mana ran up his arm, across his shoulders, settled behind his eyes with pressure that was not quite pain.","Each letter carried weight. Each word demanded something of him. Each sentence reshaped the relationship between his will and the fabric of existence as this was the price he paid for Infinity!","\" The Depths of my target are not beyond my reach. My strikes are not limited by the weight they carry, but are amplified by the difference between my foundation and the foundation of the one who stands against me. The greater the gap in my favor, the more devastating my assault becomes.\"","The words burned with blue-gold light as the Inscription completed itself, and Noah released a breath of blue gold fire. His fingers ached faintly where they gripped the pen, a reminder that even Infinite authority demanded something from its wielder!","The Inscription settled into the stable form of an Inscriptio Dormiens, hovering before him with patient malevolence.","He assessed its baseline potency with eyes that had learned to perceive the mathematical weight underlying all expressions of THE First Tongue.","At its current state, this Inscription was formidable. Against that wretched, curse-ridden fool of an Absolute like THE Living Elemental who suffered under his Apophasis, it would cause significant foundational damage.","Against stronger Absolutes, it would wound but not devastate. Against beings like Bazuman or THE Undivided Ones emerging from THE Prima Indifferentia, it would likely be insufficient to cause meaningful harm.","That was about to change.","Noah’s eyes shone as he reached toward the Inscription with his consciousness. This was different from writing, different from the creative act of composition. This was imposition. This was taking something that already existed and forcing it to become more than it was!","The Numerical Sovereignty responded to his intent like a door opening in his mind, revealing mathematical structures that had always existed within THE First Tongue but that no one before him had possessed the Infinite nature to perceive.","He could see the inherent value of the Inscription now. Numbers flickered at the edges of his vision, not truly visible but somehow present, describing relationships and ratios that the Inscription embodied without knowing it embodied them.","\" Multiplicative Amplification. Factor of ten.\"","HUUM!","The sound was not truly a sound. It was Existence acknowledging that something fundamental had shifted.","The single golden page blazed with light that made Noah squint despite himself, brightness that seemed to press against his face like heat from a forge. But the transformation went beyond mere power increase!","Before his eyes, the Inscription began to divide, to multiply, to replicate itself with precision of mathematical law rather than simple duplication. It was like watching a single flame become ten flames, each one burning with a more vibrant hungry intensity as the original.","Where one Inscriptio Dormiens had existed, now ten identical pages burned with blue-gold radiance!","Noah leaned forward slightly on his throne, his earlier stillness forgotten as he observed the phenomenon with eyes that missed nothing. Each of the ten Inscriptions carried the same words, elevated authority, and grander potential for devastation. Ten offensive weapons where before there had been only one, and each of the ten now operated at amplified potency that made the original seem almost quaint by comparison.","Prompts bloomed before his eyes.","|Multiplicative Amplification Applied|","|Your Inscriptio Dormiens has been amplified by a Multiplicative Factor of 10. This amplification has manifested in two ways: the power of the Inscription has been multiplied tenfold, and the Inscription itself has been replicated into 10 identical copies.|","|Practical Assessment at Current Level: Each of these 10 Inscriptions now carries offensive potential that would devastate weakened Absolutes like that pathetic, kneeling wretch THE Living Elemental with a single activation. One hit, one kill. His deteriorating foundations would not survive even one strike enhanced by this amplified authority. Against standard Absolutes of equivalent or lesser foundation, these Inscriptions would cause severe foundational damage that could lead to collapse within sustained engagement. Against beings like Bazuman or THE Undivided Ones, these Inscriptions would now be capable of causing genuine wounds rather than superficial scratches.|","|You now possess 10 Multiplicatively Amplified Inscriptiones Dormientes (Offensive)|","...!","Noah looked at the ten burning pages that now hovered before him, arranged in a loose circle like attendants awaiting command. The light they cast painted his features in shades of blue and gold, alternating as the Inscriptions pulsed with their newfound potency!","He could feel their readiness, their eagerness to be used, like hounds straining at leashes. What had been a single weapon was now an arsenal, each piece more potent than the original had been alone!","But he was not finished.","He straightened on his throne, drawing a deep breath that seemed to pull the scattered energies of THE Interstices into himself. The void around him responded to his focus, growing somehow more still, more expectant. Even the Phonemes that eternally danced around his form slowed their swirling, sensing that something significant was about to occur.","Now came Exponential Expression!","This was where THE Numerical Sovereignty truly revealed its terrifying potential.","Noah gathered all ten Inscriptions together with a gesture that was more will than motion, bringing them into alignment before him. They resisted slightly, each one possessing enough autonomous authority to have opinions about being manipulated. He imposed his intent upon them regardless, and they submitted to his dominion with reluctance that he felt as a faint pressure behind his temples.","The mathematical structures in his mind shifted, rearranged themselves, presented new possibilities that had not existed moments before. Exponentiation. Not multiplication, which merely added copies of a value to itself. Exponentiation multiplied a value by itself, again and again, creating growth that quickly exceeded comprehension.","\" Exponential Expression. Exponent of three.\"","HUUM!","The ten Inscriptions transformed in ways that exceeded anything the Multiplicative Amplification had produced!"]},{"number":4924,"title":"Chapter 4924: Chapter 4923: Immensity II","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes buzzed! The sensation that washed over him was like nothing he had experienced before, like standing in a river that was suddenly revealed to be an ocean, like holding a candle that became a sun!","Oh!","Exponential Expression!","The golden pages burned with light so intense, but he did not look away for even a moment, spots dancing in his vision despite his grand nature. In moments, what hovered before him was something entirely different from what he had created.","The words on each page remained unchanged, but they now carried weight that pressed against Existence itself with authority that bordered on conceptual. The Inscriptions seemed to pulse with heartbeats of power, each pulse releasing waves of pressure that made his skin prickle, that made the void of THE Interstices itself seem to flinch away.","The fucking Interstices flinched!","He could feel them now in a way he had not felt the originals, a constant awareness at the back of his mind like the presence of dangerous predators that had chosen, for the moment, not to attack.","But the transformation went deeper than mere power increase.","The edges of each Inscription began to shimmer with dual lights that should not have coexisted. Blue-gold Infinities wove alongside something else, something that held the nature of paradox itself.","Differentiation and undifferentiation merged within the infinite constructs, creating weapons that could harm through definition and through dissolution simultaneously!","Prompts bloomed with weight that exceeded anything Noah had witnessed from RUINATION before.","|Exponential Expression Applied|","|Your 10 Multiplicatively Amplified Inscriptiones Dormientes have been subjected to Exponential Expression with an Exponent of 3. Through this process, they have transcended their original classification entirely.|","| New Designation: THE Transcendent Paradoxical Inscriptiones Dormientes|","|These elevated Inscriptions have gained a terrifying exponential power that incorporates both infinite undifferentiation and infinite differentiation into their offensive nature. They now exist in states that are simultaneously defined and undefined, allowing them to harm beings regardless of their existential composition.|","...!","|Comprehensive Threat Assessment|","|Against Normal Absolutes: THE Transcendent Paradoxical Inscriptiones Dormientes would cause immediate and catastrophic foundational collapse. That sniveling, burn-ridden disgrace of an Absolute known as THE Living Elemental, already writhing under your curse like the pitiful creature he is, would be erased from existence with a single activation. Even healthy Absolutes of standard classification would find their foundations torn apart by the dual assault of differentiation and undifferentiation operating in exponential harmony.|","|Against Undivided Ones: These beings, which normally resist conventional attacks due to their undifferentiated nature, would find no refuge from Inscriptions that wield undifferentiation AND Differentiation as a weapon. THE Transcendent Paradoxical Inscriptiones would speak to THE Undivided Ones in their own language while simultaneously imposing definition upon them, creating damage that their usual immunities cannot deflect. Beings like Bazuman would suffer genuine, lasting harm from these weapons.|","|Against Formless Terrors: Similarly, THE Formless Terrors that lack stable form would find themselves vulnerable to Inscriptions that attack through both form and formlessness. The exponential nature of the assault would catch them regardless of which state they occupied at any given moment.|","|Against Primordial Architects: Well, a lot about them is unknown but..even these ancient beings, products of differentiation and undifferentiation during THE First Cause, would not be immune. THE Transcendent Paradoxical Inscriptiones speak the fundamental language of their existence and could potentially wound entities that have not faced genuine threat since before THE Infinite Unfurling. Whether such wounds would do much is uncertain, but the capacity to harm Primordial Architects at all represents power that few beings in Observable Existence possess.|","...!","Noah read over these prompts with eyes that blazed with understanding. His hands had curled into fists without his conscious decision. Ten Inscriptions!","Each one capable of erasing standard Absolutes with single activations. Each one capable of genuinely wounding THE Undivided Ones and Formless Terrors that were currently flooding across Observable Existence. Each one potentially capable of harming even Primordial Architects themselves.","He set THE Transcendent Paradoxical Inscriptiones Dormientes aside carefully. The Inscriptions resisted separation from their creator, wanting to remain close, wanting to be used!","And oh, he would use them!","Their golden pages burned with dual lights that made the other Inscriptions on his desk seem like children’s toys by comparison, like drawings of weapons next to the actual blades.","Now for the defensive application.","Noah rolled his neck, hearing the faint crack of tension releasing, and took another golden page in hand. The Phonemes swirled around his form with increased intensity, responding to his intent before he had fully formed it, eager to participate in another act of glory.","He began to write once more, his movements carrying the same deliberate precision that had produced the offensive Inscription. The sensation of drawing from that infinite ocean returned, familiar now but no less demanding.","\"I am not vulnerable to those whose foundations cannot match my own. The protection I receive is not static but scales with the difference between my weight and the weight of the one who seeks to harm me. The greater my foundation exceeds theirs, the more impenetrable my defense becomes.\"","The words settled into place as another Inscriptio Dormiens completed itself. Where the offensive Inscription had felt like a blade being forged, this one felt like armor being fitted, like walls being raised around something precious.","Noah looked at the completed Inscription and allowed himself a moment of satisfaction before beginning the augmentation process once more. The defensive application would follow the same pattern, but he found himself curious whether the sensations would differ.","\" Multiplicative Amplification. Factor of ten.\"","HUUM!","The defensive Inscription blazed with light as the numerical operation took effect! The warmth that washed over him was different this time, not the hungry heat of a forge but the comfortable warmth of a hearth, of safety, of walls that nothing could breach.","As with the offensive Inscription, the single page divided and replicated, becoming ten identical defensive Inscriptions that burned with amplified protective authority!","|Multiplicative Amplification Applied|","|Your defensive Inscriptio Dormiens has been amplified by a Multiplicative Factor of 10, manifesting as both power increase and replication into 10 identical copies.|","|Practical Assessment at Current Level: Each of these 10 Inscriptions now provides protection that would render attacks from standard Absolutes negligible . That miserable, foundation-crumbling embarrassment THE Living Elemental’s strikes, even if he could muster them through his curse, would fail to register as threats. Attacks from beings of equivalent foundation would be significantly blunted. Even assaults from powerful entities like Bazuman would be substantially reduced, transforming potentially lethal strikes into manageable damage.|","|You now possess 10 Multiplicatively Amplified Inscriptiones Dormientes (Defensive)|","...!","Noah nodded once, sharply, and continued without pause. His focus had narrowed to a point, all other concerns falling away like shed clothing. There was only this. Only the next step!","\" Exponential Expression. Exponent of three.\"","HUUM!","The ten defensive Inscriptions transformed with radiance that matched their offensive counterparts!","The golden pages burned with light that seemed to create bubbles of absolute safety around them, spheres of impossibility that declared harm could not exist within their boundaries. Looking at them, Noah felt something loosen in his chest, some tension he had not realized he was carrying!","The dual lights of differentiation and undifferentiation wove through the protective declarations, creating shields that existed in states beyond conventional defense. They were and were not. They blocked through presence and through absence. They protected!","|Exponential Expression Applied|","|Your 10 Multiplicatively Amplified defensive Inscriptiones Dormientes have been subjected to Exponential Expression with an Exponent of 3. Through this process, they have transcended their original classification entirely.|","|New Designation: THE Transcendent Paradoxical Inscriptiones Dormientes (Defensive)|","|These elevated Inscriptions have gained a terrifying exponential protective power that incorporates both infinite undifferentiation and infinite differentiation into their defensive nature. They protect through simultaneous assertion of form and formlessness, creating barriers that cannot be bypassed by conventional means.|","...!","|Comprehensive Protection Assessment|","|Against Normal Absolutes: Attacks from standard Absolutes would fail to penetrate these defenses entirely. Whether strikes of pure Civilizational Authority or exotic methodologies, they would encounter protection that speaks their language and negates their effectiveness. That worthless, groveling heap of deteriorating foundations known as THE Living Elemental could strike for eternity without causing meaningful harm.|","|Against Undivided Ones: THE Undivided Ones attack through undifferentiation, seeking to dissolve their targets back into proto-potential. These Inscriptions counter by wielding undifferentiation themselves, creating defensive resonance that nullifies such assaults. Bazuman’s attempts to consume would find nothing to grasp, as the protection exists in states that mirror his own methodology.|","|Against Formless Terrors: Similarly, the chaotic attacks of Formless Terrors would find no purchase against defenses that embrace formlessness as readily as form. Their violence would pass through without effect, unable to locate a stable target within the paradoxical protective field.|","|Against Primordial Architects: Even attacks from these ancient beings would be somewhat mitigated. While complete immunity cannot be guaranteed against entities who shaped the nature of differentiation and undifferentiation itself, these Inscriptions would provide substantial protection that could mean the difference between survival and collapse.|","...!"]},{"number":4925,"title":"Chapter 4925: Chapter 4924: Infinite Harvest! I","paragraphs":["Noah set THE Transcendent Paradoxical Inscriptiones Dormientes (Defensive) beside their offensive counterparts on his desk.","Twenty elevated Inscriptions now burned before him, arranged in two groups of ten, their twin radiances illuminating THE Interstices with authority that exceeded anything this space had contained before.","The light they cast was almost warm against his skin, almost like sunlight!","Offense and defense.","Both augmented to levels that transcended their original classifications.","Both capable of affecting beings that would have seemed untouchable before THE Numerical Sovereignty had been integrated into his weavings of THE First Tongue.","After he was done testing this out, Noah sat back on his throne of Absolute Seals. The crystallized authority pressed against his back, solid and reassuring. His blue-gold pen still swirled with Infinities pulsing around its form, still ready to write more Inscriptions if he desired.","The Phonemes had resumed their endless dance around his existence, galaxies of infinite authority that now carried numerical values alongside their semantic meanings.","The void of THE Interstices stretched out around him, patient and immense as when he thought about the capabilities of what he had just designed...","Oh, what he just forged?!","He could not help but lean his head back against the throne.","And then he used his hand to cover his face.","But through the gaps between his fingers, an utterly terrifying devilish smile could be seen rising across his features. His resplendent white teeth showed gloriously as the smile widened, as the implications of what he had just created settled fully into his consciousness. His shoulders shook once, twice, with laughter that he did not permit to escape his throat!","With THE Transcendent Paradoxical Inscriptiones Dormientes, he could erase standard Absolutes, wound THE Undivided Ones and Formless Terrors, and potentially gain a tiny footing even against Primordial Architects.","With their defensive counterparts, he could become nearly invulnerable to attacks from beings across all classifications of existence.","And these were merely his first tests of THE Numerical Sovereignty!","What would happen when he applied these operations to his Harvests? To his Archai of Existence? To his Perpetual Harvest that already claimed resources from enemies across Observable Existence?","The smile behind his hand grew even wider.","THE Genesis Monarch had just done something that Observable Existence was not prepared for, and he was only getting started!","After his tests designing and elevating Inscriptions with Multiplicative Amplification and Exponential Expression, Noah turned his gaze inward.","The Inscriptions were merely the beginning. Weapons and shields were useful, certainly, but they were tools.","What he was about to do was different.","What he was about to do would transform the very nature of how he grew!","Noah straightened on his throne of Absolute Seals, feeling the crystallized authority press against his back as he drew a breath that seemed to pull the scattered energies of THE Interstices into his lungs.","He called out grandly and unequivocally.","\" Apply Multiplicative Amplification and Exponential Expression to all incoming harvest from the spread of my Absolute Seals across Observable Existence. Every single thing benefiting, every area covered, every harvest turned into Infinite Potential that further amplifies my existence and foundation...\"","His voice dropped to something that pressed against reality itself.","\" Multiply it and exponentially elevate it.\"","BOOM!","The sound was...well, not truly a sound. It was Existence acknowledging that something fundamental had shifted in the relationship between Noah Osmont and the resources that flowed toward him across all of Observable Existence!","He knew this would be one of the heaviest actions he could take. Such a configuration was not merely heavy. It was the kind of thing that would have overwhelmed foundations unprepared for the volume of power about to surge through them.","But he had Infinities!","So he could withstand it! He could pay the price!","Noah felt his Depth and Immensity moving in response to his words.","The sensation was grand. This was not external manipulation of Inscriptions that existed outside his existence. This was internal restructuring, his very being rearranging itself to accommodate the mathematical operations he had imposed upon his harvest. He could feel the numbers taking shape within him, not as abstract concepts but as physical structures that wove themselves through his foundations like new organs being grown.","His Absolute Seals surged around him with intensity.","They had always swirled. They had always danced in configurations that reflected his state of mind and authority. But now they moved with purpose. They flowed outward and inward simultaneously, streaming from his existence in rivers of blue-gold light that curved and bent and folded back upon themselves.","And they formed something.","A massive blue-gold infinity symbol materialized around him, its loops stretching across THE Interstices until they seemed to encompass the entire space here. Noah floated at its center while seated on his throne, the crystallized authority beneath him now simply another part of the greater configuration. The infinity symbol burned with light that pulsed in rhythms matching his heartbeat, and he could feel it not just as a visual phenomenon but as an extension of his own existence.","All incoming harvest flowed into this churning infinity symbol!","The first streams arrived within moments of the configuration completing itself. Harvest from his Absolute Seals spreading across Observable Existence. Harvest from the corrupted paradoxical proto-matter that THE Living Paradox was flooding everywhere, carrying Noah’s Infinities alongside his own Information. Harvest from every being who used THE First Tongue and paid the Existential Tariffs he had established.","The harvest flowed into the infinity symbol like rivers joining an endless sea.","And then the Multiplicative Amplification took effect.","Noah gasped as the incoming harvest was multiplied by ten!","The sensation was overwhelming in its immediacy. What had been a steady flow of resources became a torrent, a flood, an ocean of potential that surged through the loops of the infinity symbol with force that made his foundations buzz. He could feel the potency of each unit of harvest increasing tenfold, and simultaneously, the volume multiplied as well. Not just stronger harvest, but more of it, ten times as much crashing against his existence with every passing moment.","The infinity symbol churned with increased intensity, the blue-gold light brightening until Noah had to narrow his eyes against its radiance. The harvest surged along the loops, compressed and concentrated, building toward something that felt inevitable.","And then the Exponential Expression activated.","Harvest multiplied by itself.","And then multiplied by itself again.","And then multiplied by itself a third time!","Harvest times harvest times harvest!","The already-multiplied harvest didn’t merely increase in power. It compounded upon itself with mathematical precision that produced results exceeding comprehension. What had been tenfold became something else entirely, something that existed at scales where normal measurement lost meaning.","He watched as the churning harvest within the infinity symbol began to condense.","The streams of raw potential that had been flowing through the loops started to concentrate, to crystallize, to take on form that they had not possessed moments before. The blue-gold light shifted, became something more golden, more defined, more singular in its purpose!","And Noah understood what he was witnessing. He even came up with a name for it!","\" THE Infinite Observable Harvest ,\" he breathed.","The name emerged from him without conscious decision, pulled from some deep understanding that recognized what was forming before his eyes!","This was what he felt when he looked at the condensing power. Not mere harvest. Not simple resources being accumulated. Something elevated beyond normal classification through the mathematical operations he had imposed.","A single unit of THE Infinite Observable Harvest completed its formation.","It looked like a golden infinity symbol, smaller than the massive configuration surrounding him but burning with intensity that exceeded its size. The unit floated within the greater infinity symbol for a moment, beautiful and terrible and filled with potential that made his foundations ache with anticipation.","Then it flowed into him.","BOOM!"]},{"number":4926,"title":"Chapter 4926: Chapter 4925: Infinite Harvest! II","paragraphs":["Noah’s spine arched against his throne as THE Infinite Observable Harvest integrated with his existence!","The weight of his Absolute Seals rose up tremendously, their authority strengthening with speed that exceeded anything conventional harvest could have provided. His foundations felt the impact like a physical blow, but it was a blow that built rather than destroyed, that elevated rather than damaged. His Infinite Formless Depth expanded to accommodate what was being added to him!","And moments after the first unit, another unit of THE Infinite Observable Harvest formed.","It smashed into his existence with force that made him grip his armrests until the crystallized authority cracked beneath his fingers! His Infinite Formless Depth amplified again, its weight and immensity growing with speed that would have taken conventional beings eons to achieve. The sensation was almost painful, like growing too fast, like his existence was being stretched to accommodate power that exceeded its previous capacity.","But his Infinite nature adapted!","It always quintessentially adapted!","Unit after unit of THE Infinite Observable Harvest formed within the churning infinity symbol and flowed into his existence. Each one carried the compounded potency of harvest that had been multiplied tenfold and then raised to the third power. Each one elevated his foundations by margins that should have been impossible. Each one made him more than he had been moments before.","Prompts bloomed before his eyes with weight that pressed against his consciousness.","|Multiplicative Amplification and Exponential Expression Applied to Harvest|","|All incoming harvest from the spread of your Absolute Seals across Observable Existence is now subject to numerical operations before integration. Harvest is first multiplied by a factor of 10, increasing both potency and volume tenfold. This multiplied harvest is then subjected to Exponential Expression with an Exponent of 3, causing the harvest to compound upon itself three times.|","| The result has been designated THE Infinite Observable Harvest. Each unit represents harvest that has been amplified beyond conventional measurement, carrying potential that exceeds what standard harvest could provide by margins that approach infinity.|","...!","|Storage and Application|","|THE Infinite Observable Harvest can be directly integrated into your foundations for immediate growth, as is currently occurring. Alternatively, units of THE Infinite Observable Harvest can be stored within THE Organ of Civilization that exists at the core of your existence.|","|Stored units of THE Infinite Observable Harvest serve as raw material for the production of resources at any scale you desire. THE Organ of Civilization can process stored Infinite Observable Harvest into Absolute Everythings for the elevation of your followers, into Infinite Everythings for the enhancement of your own capabilities, or into any other resource configuration that your Civilization requires.|","|Note: The production capacity of THE Organ of Civilization has increased proportionally with the quality of harvest being stored. Resources that previously required significant time to produce can now be generated nearly instantaneously when drawing upon THE Infinite Observable Harvest.|","...!","|Foundation Status Update|","|Your Surface Depth Foundation has achieved weight and immensity equivalent to 15 times the comparative baseline of THE Primordial Paradox and THE Creature before they became Absolutes.|","|Your Intermediate Depth Foundation has achieved weight and immensity equivalent to 14 times the comparative baseline.|","|Your Fundamental Depth Foundation has achieved weight and immensity equivalent to 9 times the comparative baseline. At Fundamental Depth, you now possess foundations that exceed what THE Four held before their ascension to Absolutea by a factor approaching one order of magnitude.|","|Assessment: Your foundational weight at all Depths now exceeds any being below Absolute classification by margins that render comparison almost meaningless. Almost.|","...!","Noah’s figure pulsed with grand power as he remained seated in THE Interstices.","But this entire region was now unfathomably bright. The blue and gold light that emanated from his existence and the churning infinity symbol around him permeated across THE Interstices from where he sat, painting the void in colors that it had never known before.","He could feel the harvest continuing to flow.","Unit after unit of THE Infinite Observable Harvest formed and integrated with his existence, each one adding to foundations that were already growing at rates that exceeded comprehension. The infinity symbol churned with endless activity, processing the incoming harvest through Multiplicative Amplification and Exponential Expression with efficiency that required no conscious attention from him.","This would continue indefinitely.","So long as his Absolute Seals spread and remained spread across Observable Existence, so long as THE Living Paradox’s process continued flooding corruption and Infinities everywhere, the harvest would flow. And that harvest would be multiplied and exponentially elevated before integration, producing growth that conventional beings could never hope to match.","Noah nodded to himself with a dangerous smile.","It was time to move.","He had to see just the true extent of his power!","Not even an Absolute yet, and yet he could utterly destroy the trashiest bum Absolutes like that pathetic heap of burning foundations known as THE Living Elemental. The gap between his existence and such weakened Absolutes had grown so vast that eliminating them would require less effort than swatting an irritating insect.","But what about stronger enemies?","What about the things that had seemed untouchable when he first emerged into this existential conflict?","\"Oh, Bazuman, can I now reach you?\"","Sometimes, an enemy was so far away that one knew they couldn’t do anything against them for some time. Bazuman had felt this way when Noah first witnessed him in THE Prima Indifferentia. THE Undivided One had chased him with hunger that spoke of inevitable consumption, and Noah had fled because fighting had seemed pointless against something so fundamentally beyond his capabilities.","But now?","Now he wondered.","Noah’s body in THE Interstices remained still, seated upon his throne at the center of the churning infinity symbol while THE Infinite Observable Harvest continued flowing into his existence. But another body of his in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment stood beside THE Primordial Paradox and the Strategoi, facing the crack from which Bazuman had emerged.","He would test his power through that body against an Undivided One!","And at the same time as this occurred, he dealt with multiple other things through different bodies across Observable Existence. One body monitored THE Yggdrheim where his people struggled against infinite undifferentiation.","Another body continued its work in THE Wastes with THE Great Usurper and gathering information. Another body remained with THE Mnemonic Leviathan in THE Infiniverse, observing the changes being induced by their grand actions.","But the body in THE Interstices did something else as well.","It continued looking at an illusory screen that had formed before his throne, displaying images from Alfheimr where THE Living Elemental and THE Living Emotive currently struggled. The screen showed that wretched, sniveling disgrace of an Absolute still suffering under Noah’s curse, his foundations deteriorating with every passing moment while he could barely stand.","In front of him, THE Living Emotive defended against an Undivided One alone.","The screen of THE Living Elemental struggling... he would continue to look at it. Even though Noah could kill this being with a thought, even though THE Transcendent Paradoxical Inscriptiones Dormientes would erase him from existence with a single activation, Noah wanted him to suffer for now!","Let him burn.","Let him feel the weight of the curse that would never lift until Noah decided to show mercy in death and collapse.","Let him understand what it meant to have made an enemy of THE Genesis Monarch!","But as he watched?","\" Oh?\"","Noah actually rose up from his throne slightly, his hands pressing against the armrests as his attention sharpened with sudden interest. Something unique was happening on the screen. Something he had not noticed before. Something that his newly elevated perception now made visible in ways that his previous sight could not have achieved.","He saw a flow of authority around Emotive.","It was uniquely filled with intense and profound Definition, that quality of existence that separated differentiated beings from the proto-potential of THE Prima Indifferentia. The flow was subtle, almost invisible, and it moved in a direction that seemed wrong.","It flowed from Emotive into THE Undivided One.","\" Ho?\"","Noah paid attention fully now, his dangerous smile fading into something more analytical as he observed the phenomenon with eyes that broke down both languages and numbers. His vision moved between Differentiation and Undifferentiation with ease that his existence had not possessed before THE Numerical Sovereignty was integrated into his First Tongue.","He could see the mathematical relationships underlying the flow, the ratios and proportions that described what was occurring.","Emotive was giving something to THE Undivided One.","Not fighting it. Not defending against it. Giving something to it while appearing to fight.","\" Whatever are you doing, O Emotive?\""]},{"number":4927,"title":"Chapter 4927: Chapter 4926: A Bond of Emotions!","paragraphs":["Because of the Inscription that he had laid out on that waste of life that was THE Living Elemental, Noah was able to perceive what was happening around this being and his immediate surroundings.","The curse burned across Elemental’s foundations with relentless precision, but it also served as an anchor for Noah’s perception. Through that anchor, he could observe the region of Alfheimr where the cursed Absolute currently cowered, could see the beings that surrounded him and the conflicts that unfolded in his vicinity.","So he saw both THE Living Elemental and THE Living Emotive as she fought against an Undivided One that actually did not even seem like it wanted to be there.","The observation struck him as peculiar the moment he processed it fully.","THE Undivided One was a massive thing whose body resembled a great winged lion with the face of something that had never been mortal. No features of any realm Noah had witnessed could describe that visage, that configuration of angles and expressions that spoke of existence before existence had learned to differentiate itself into recognizable forms.","Its mane was made of writhing serpents that hissed with individual malice, each one a separate consciousness bound to the greater whole, their eyes burning with hunger that their host seemed reluctant to act upon. Its wings stretched wide enough to cast shadows across entire territories, vast expanses of feathered darkness that should have been beating with aggressive intent.","But there was something hesitant in its assault. Something reluctant in the way it pressed against Emotive’s defenses!","Where its paws touched, existence forgot what solidity meant. The ground beneath it became uncertain, wavering between states of matter as the undifferentiated nature of the beast leaked into its surroundings. And yet those paws moved with reluctance, striking toward Emotive with force that should have been devastating but pulling back at the last moment as if the winged lion feared the consequences of actually connecting.","Noah narrowed his eyes.","He wasn’t able to fully perceive everything that had occurred, but there should have been another Undivided One or two that came out with this one from THE Prima Indifferentia. He had felt their brief auras when the crack first opened above the mountain, terrible pressures that had made even his distant perception waver for a moment.","But those auras had disappeared rapidly, snuffed out with casual efficiency that spoke of overwhelming power.","He only attributed this to THE Creature.","So THE Undivided One that was attacking Emotive had to know that it could be taken care of by THE Creature at any time. The being at the peak of the mountain had already demonstrated his capacity to eliminate such threats.","This remaining winged lion understood that its existence continued only because THE Creature permitted it.","But since THE Creature wanted adversity for Emotive and Elemental, he did not interfere. That was the reason why the assault continued. Not because THE Undivided One posed a genuine threat, but because THE Creature had decided that his allies needed to struggle.","Emotive was defending as if she did not want to be there. Her Embodiments flew toward THE Undivided One with power that should have been devastating, but her movements held reluctance that her manic energy could not fully disguise. She threw attacks because she had to, not because she wanted to.","And THE Undivided One was attacking as if it also did not want to be there!","The winged lion’s serpent mane hissed toward Emotive with malice that seemed performative rather than genuine. Its massive paws swept through the air with force that would have devastated anything of an average Absolute, but the movements were perfunctory, going through motions rather than genuinely seeking to kill. Its wings beat with power that should have generated storms, yet they created only gentle breezes that barely disturbed Emotive’s constantly changing hair.","It knew that true aggression would invite THE Creature’s attention. It knew that actually harming these beings might transform it from permitted pest to consumed meal!","It was a unique and laughable situation.","But as Noah continued to observe, he noticed something else entirely.","His newly elevated perception, enhanced by THE Numerical Sovereignty and THE Infinite Observable Harvest flowing into his foundations, could perceive things that he had not been able to see before. His eyes broke down both languages and numbers now, moving between Differentiation and Undifferentiation with ease that allowed him to observe the mathematical relationships underlying existence itself.","And he saw something flowing from THE Living Emotive.","An extremely clear and intense definition of emotion was streaming from her existence and going into THE Undivided One.","The flow was invisible to normal perception. Even most Absolutes would not have been able to observe it. But Noah could see it now, could trace its path from Emotive’s foundations into the weavings of the winged lion with clarity that made the phenomenon undeniable.","Uniquely, THE Undivided One had no idea what was happening to it.","Its weavings were filled with light of undifferentiation, as was proper for a being that had existed in THE Prima Indifferentia. The serpents of its mane continued hissing with individual malice, unaware that their collective existence was being subtly altered. Its face that had never been mortal remained fixed in expressions that predated emotion itself. And yet, at this moment, something silent and invisible was flowing alongside its undifferentiated nature.","Something that was giving it a very clear and intense definition and differentiation based on emotions.","Noah leaned forward on his throne in THE Interstices, the churning infinity symbol around him pulsing with increased intensity as his attention sharpened. He watched the flow of emotional definition pour into THE Undivided One, watched it weave itself through the winged lion’s foundations without triggering any of its natural defenses against differentiation.","It was like watching someone slowly poison a drink while their victim remained oblivious.","His eyes flashed coldly as realization settled into his consciousness.","He had truly been underestimating THE Living Emotive!","Because as she threw out Embodiments here and there to keep THE Undivided One at bay, her actual power was focused elsewhere entirely. The attacks were distractions, performances meant to make it seem like she was fighting when in truth she was doing something far more insidious. Most of her authority was concentrated on this emotional light of definition, on the flow that was slowly transforming the winged lion from the inside out.","After a few more seconds of observation...","BOOM!","An impact occurred between THE Living Emotive and THE Undivided One!","Emotive breathed heavily with an angry look that twisted her features into something between fury and exhaustion. The figure of that worthless heap of burning foundations known as THE Living Elemental was blasted backward by the shockwave, hitting the surrounding trees of the mountain like a sack of ugly potatoes.","His cursed form crumpled against the ancient bark with impact that would have been satisfying to witness if Noah had cared enough about the wretch to feel true satisfaction.","But his attention remained on Emotive.","A unique scene unfolded after that impact.","THE Living Emotive looked toward the peak of the mountain that Noah could not perceive too well, the region where THE Creature’s temple sat shrouded in multicolored flames. Her expression held accusation that exceeded her previous anger, and she no longer attacked THE Undivided One.","Instead, she actually began to float toward it.","Uniquely, THE Undivided One had gone still.","The winged lion’s serpent mane ceased its hissing. Each individual serpent blinked with confusion that should not have been possible for extensions of a being of undifferentiation. Its wings, which had been beating with performative aggression moments before, now folded against its leonine body with docility that contradicted everything its form suggested. Its face that had never been mortal shifted through expressions it had never worn before, cycling through confusion and recognition and something that looked almost like affection.","Its entire massive form shook as if it was remembering something, as if new information was integrating into its existence that changed everything it had believed about the situation.","And then the ridiculous scene occurred.","THE Living Emotive floated up toward THE Undivided One’s shoulder, her now crimson hair blazing with manic energy that seemed more petulant than threatening now. She settled onto the winged lion’s massive shoulder as if it were a chair, her small form perching upon primordial horror with casualness that defied comprehension.","The serpents of its mane that had been hissing with malice moments before now regarded her with something approaching protectiveness, their eyes softening in ways that their undifferentiated nature should not have permitted.","She looked up toward the mountain where THE Creature resided and spoke with an angry gaze.","\" Because you did not want to help, you forced me to use my last Bond on some random Undivided One!\"","...!","Her voice carried across Alfheimr with weight that pressed against the glorious twilight.","\"I was saving that for THE Youngest! Just because you can resist our Bond doesn’t mean you can bully me like this, Creature!\"","...!","Noah was astonished as he looked at the body of THE Living Emotive.","She was filled with manic energy that seemed to contradict the gravity of what she had just revealed. Her angry words came across more like pouting than genuine fury, complaints directed toward an unseen being who apparently cared nothing for her displeasure.","Below her, the winged lion shook its shoulder with motion that caused her to drift off her perch. The serpents of its mane hissed with what sounded almost like apology as their movement disrupted her seating. She pouted toward it with expression that would have been more appropriate on a child denied a treat than on an Absolute.","THE Undivided One was still adjusting with confusion that Noah could perceive even through the distant observation of his Inscription anchor. Whatever bond or definition had been placed on it had fundamentally altered its perception of THE Living Emotive. She was no longer prey. She was no longer enemy. She was...","A friend.","Someone it did not want to harm.","The transformation had occurred in seconds, invisible to many except Noah’s newly elevated perception, and now the winged lion treated Emotive with something approaching protectiveness despite having no logical reason to do so.","Where its paws touched, existence still forgot what solidity meant, but it was careful now to keep those paws away from the small woman.","But she had revealed something that painted a much clearer picture.","Noah had asked himself how this woman had moved from THE Creature to THE Living Paradox, how she had ingratiated herself with beings who should have had no reason to tolerate her presence. He had wondered how she managed to cling to THE Primordial Chaos in Alfheimr, how she inserted herself into dynamics that had nothing to do with her own agenda.","Now he understood.","She had a unique power of definition or differentiation based on her terrifying manic emotions. A power that allowed her to form some sort of Bond with beings, even someone as powerful as THE Creature. A bond that influenced the target to treat her differently, to feel closeness toward her that they had not chosen and could not explain.","...!","Emotive. THE Broken Doll!","She seemed to be among the few unique beings in Observable Existence whose capabilities exceeded their apparent classification. There was more to her than what met the eye, depths of power that her manic surface behavior disguised behind seemingly unhinged emotion.","Her methodology interested Noah greatly.","The invisible nature of it seemed very similar to THE Entity, even though the two of them were clearly not related. Both operated through subtle influence rather than direct confrontation. Both altered the targets they affected without those targets realizing what was happening until the transformation was complete.","But the differences were equally significant.","THE Entity, THE Primordial Mycelia, took over and controlled the entirety of the will of another. It subsumed consciousness into its unified network, dissolving individuality into collective purpose. Its targets ceased to be themselves entirely.","THE Broken Doll formed bonds that made one feel like they were her family or lover.","Her targets remained themselves. They retained their will, their consciousness, their individual nature. But their perception of her shifted, their emotional responses to her presence transformed into something that served her purposes.","They believed they cared about her because she had made them believe it through definition so subtle that they could not perceive its presence.","Noah filed this information away for future consideration.","But even as he observed all of this, he had to divide his attention.","The churning infinity symbol around his body in THE Interstices continued processing THE Infinite Observable Harvest, unit after unit of amplified and elevated resources flowing into his foundations. His perception of Alfheimr through the Inscription anchor remained active, observing Emotive and her newly bonded winged lion with analytical interest.","But in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, Bazuman had begun to move.","Noah had to see exactly how his newly elevated Immensity and methods would work against THE Undivided One that had chased him across THE Prima Indifferentia!","Because while the winged lion that THE Living Emotive had just bonded to was powerful, a being that would have devastated most average Absolutes in direct conflict, a creature whose very paws made existence forget what solidity meant...","It was nowhere near the level of Bazuman!","That ancient horror, that entity who had pursued Noah through corrupted proto-matter with hunger...","Bazuman was something else entirely.","And Noah was about to discover whether his growth had been sufficient to reach him!"]},{"number":4928,"title":"Chapter 4928: Chapter 4927: Ganging Up On Bazuman! I","paragraphs":["In THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, the air itself had grown heavy with anticipation.","Noah stood beside THE Primordial Paradox, his existence burning with blue-gold Infinities that pressed outward against the corrupted proto-matter flooding through the crack above.","The ancient stones beneath his feet thrummed with vibrations he could feel through his soles, the entire structure of THE Agora responding to the presence that had emerged from THE Prima Indifferentia.","Behind them, the four Strategoi had arranged themselves in positions of readiness for combat!","Glossikos stood with her linguistic authority coiling around her form. Khaotikos shifted between states of matter and energy with increasing instability. Ontikos emanated the calm weight of Existence itself. And Paradoxos displayed both fear and determination across his dual faces!","Before them all stood Bazuman.","THE Undivided One had emerged fully from the crack now, its round chthonian form settling upon the ancient stones with weight that made one’s teeth ache from the pressure.","Countless crimson eyes arranged in spiraling patterns across its spherical mass gazed outward in every direction, each one burning with hunger.","Innumerable tentacles extended from its form, each tipped with mouths that held teeth made of crystallized memories. Its entire surface churned constantly, revealing glimpses of faces and forms beneath, the remnants of beings who had ceased to exist everywhere except within Bazuman’s infinite memory.","The Immensity it carried pressed against Noah’s perception like a physical weight settling upon his shoulders, like heavy hands pushing down on his chest with every breath he took!","This wasn’t the same as the winged lion that Emotive had just bonded to in Alfheimr. That creature had been powerful, yes, capable of devastating most Absolutes in direct conflict. But Bazuman existed in an entirely different classification.","It was like comparing that pathetic floundering embarrassment known as THE Living Elemental to beings like THE Living Paradox or THE Primordial Chaos.","They were legitimately leagues apart.","And at this moment, this thing was keeping its gaze locked onto Noah. Every single one of those countless crimson eyes had oriented toward him specifically, tracking his movements with attention that felt uncomfortably personal.","The weight of that collective focus pressed against his skin like heat from a forge held too close. The tentacles that extended from its form seemed to reach in his direction even when they weren’t actively moving, drawn by magnetism that operated on levels beyond physical attraction.","Noah couldn’t help but look toward it and ask the question that had been forming since he first felt its attention.","\" Am I wrong to think that you are obsessed with me, Bazuman?\"","...!","Bazuman’s many eyes smiled.","The expression shouldn’t have been possible. Monstrous eyes couldn’t smile, couldn’t convey emotion through shape alone!","And yet every single crimson orb across its churning surface curved upward at the edges, creating an impression of brutal amusement.","When it spoke, its voice emerged from a thousand mouths simultaneously, a deep resonance of undifferentiation that seemed to vibrate inside Noah’s chest rather than reach him through the air.","\"I tasted you.\"","The words pressed against reality itself!","\" You tasted of unique endless undifferentiation. And I let you slip past me.\"","Its tentacles writhed with increased intensity.","\" And right now, with this corrupted paradoxical spread of proto-matter...\"","Its eyes blazed brighter.","\"I feel like I have tasted yet another portion of you inside me.\"","The mouths across its surface all curved into expressions of hunger.","\"I want more.\"","Every eye focused on Noah with intensity.","\"I... want you.\"","BOOM!","The words were horrid for Noah to hear, and he felt his existence recoiling with distaste. It felt like this Undivided One was confessing in the worst way possible!","But the words were heavy in other ways as well.","They caused THE Primordial Paradox to frown, his obsidian-gold flames flickering with attention that had shifted from casual observation to serious concern. He kept his calm gaze on THE Undivided One, but Noah could feel the weight of his perception turning partially toward him as he asked a question that demanded honest answer.","\"Youngest, what is he talking about? Your authority is spreading alongside my disciple’s corruption?\"","THE Primordial Paradox asked this with an inquisitive gaze, and Noah could see this being already looking at the surrounding influx of corrupted paradoxical proto-matter with eyes that were breaking down everything. Those ancient perceptions were analyzing the composition of the corruption, identifying the blue-gold threads of Infinity woven through its structure, tracing their origins back to the source that had inserted them.","So Noah replied honestly.","\" Since your disciple was spreading corruption to affect all of Observable Existence, I added a little of myself onto that train.\"","His voice held no apology.","\"I’m just going along for the ride and benefiting from it.\"","He met THE Primordial Paradox’s gaze directly.","\" And yes, I know of the potential dangers that may come from this. It seems like I’m looking at one right now.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox frowned momentarily, his obsidian-gold flames burning. He looked at Noah silently for a moment that stretched longer than it should have.","Then he spoke with a voice that held warning beneath its calmness.","\" You know, but you also don’t know.\"","His gaze shifted to Bazuman.","\" There’s a reason why after you disappeared in that crack of Observable Existence in THE Prima Indifferentia and I was staring straight at the one responsible for making this happen... I was still unable to collapse Bazuman at that time.\"","His flames flickered.","\" Amongst Undivided Ones, the level of undifferentiation from Bazuman is immensely high. And part of the reason, which I now understand, was you.\"","His eyes returned to Noah.","\" He had a bit of you eons ago. Even if briefly, Bazuman had ingested you. He had ingested Infinity.\"","\" And now, you have given him a glimpse of more.\"","...!","Noah listened to these words quietly and with calmness that he maintained through force of will. He knew the dangers of what he’d done with the process that THE Living Paradox had initiated.","He’d known from the moment THE Infiniverse scattered his Seals through the corrupted proto-matter. He’d declared that he would face whatever arose from his choice and take care of it himself, even proclaiming that he would take on the responsibility to stop THE Living Paradox if needed.","But it seemed that right now, he would get a glimpse of exactly what would be required of him.","Because not long after THE Primordial Paradox finished his words...","Bazuman laughed.","The sound emerged from a thousand mouths simultaneously, brutal amusement that made the ancient stones of THE Agora crack beneath its resonance.","Every crimson eye across its churning surface blazed with light that exceeded their previous intensity, and its horrid body pulsed!","BOOM !","Its many eyes released a terrifying sense of pressure that exceeded anything that many here had never felt from an individual entity before!"]},{"number":4929,"title":"Chapter 4929: Chapter 4928: Ganging Up On Bazuman! II","paragraphs":["The pressure congealed into physical form, becoming a sea of crimson undifferentiation that instantly settled all around THE Agora like a tide of dissolution washing over everything it touched.","The red light pressed against Noah’s skin with weight that felt like being submerged in water that wanted to unmake him.","It permeated through the air, through the stones, through the very fabric of existence in this region, seeking to dissolve definition wherever it found purchase.","And this undifferentiation carried a glimmer of Infinity and profound Paradox!","It felt like the exertion of overwhelming will made manifest, like the authority of undifferentiation pressing against everything that dared to be differentiated. The moment it erupted, structures throughout THE Agora began to waver, their defined edges becoming uncertain, their solid forms questioning whether they were truly solid at all.","Noah withstood it with his existence alone!","His Infinities burned brilliantly across his form, blue-gold flames rising from every aspect of his being to press back against the crimson tide.","The sensation was like standing in a river that wanted to sweep him away, but his feet remained planted on bedrock that couldn’t be moved!","Absolute Immovable Object!","Where the undifferentiation touched his light, it didn’t find purchase. His nature regenerated faster than it could be unmade, his definition reasserting itself with every nanosecond that passed!","He felt the pressure,yes. But he wasn’t undifferentiated.","He remained exactly what he was.","Beside him, THE Primordial Paradox was surrounded by obsidian-gold light that formed a bubble of absolute protection around his form. The paradoxical authority that comprised his existence simply declared that undifferentiation couldn’t affect him, and reality accepted that declaration without question. Not a single mote of crimson light penetrated his barrier. He stood as an island of perfect calm within the sea of dissolution.","But the four Strategoi behind them...","Glossikos had solemn expression on her features as crimson undifferentiation lapped against her linguistic authority, her weavings struggling to maintain coherence against the pressure.","Khaotikos shifted between states with increasing desperation, trying to find a configuration that the undifferentiation couldn’t affect, finding none. Ontikos emanated the weight of Existence itself, but even Existence wavered beneath pressure that sought to make it forget what existence meant.","And Paradoxos, this two faced bum, despite his affinity for paradox, found that Bazuman’s undifferentiation was paradoxical in ways that his own authority couldn’t fully counter.","These four were actually struggling!","The mere exertion of pressure from this Undivided One was that grand, that overwhelming, that it could challenge four Strategoi of THE Agora simultaneously through nothing more than its released Immensity.","Bazuman looked toward Noah with all of its eyes, and every single one of them smiled with the same brutal amusement that had preceded its laugh. Its tentacles reached toward him through the crimson tide, mouths at their tips opening with hunger that made his stomach pulse.","\"I. Want. You!\"","BOOM!","It erupted thereafter!","Noah observed as around Bazuman, the manifestation of its power unfolded in configurations of Civilizational wonder.","Echoes ...began emerging from its churning mass.","Not physical beings, but impressions of beings. Reconstructions formed from Bazuman’s perfect memory of everything it had ever consumed. They poured forth from its surface like spirits rising from a grave.","They took shapes that spoke of Absolutes from before THE Infinite Unfurling, of creatures that had ceased to exist everywhere except within Bazuman’s infinite recollection.","They were things...that Bazuman had swallowed and undifferentiated.","Echoes filled with whispers came first, faint impressions that attacked with fractions of their original power but in overwhelming numbers. Hundreds of them... translucent forms that launched toward Noah and THE Primordial Paradox and the struggling Strategoi with attacks that shouldn’t have been possible from beings who no longer existed.","More followed, stronger manifestations. Noah saw the forms of Absolutes he didn’t recognize, wielding authority that felt ancient even by the standards of Observable Existence. They spoke Embodiments and released attacks based on methodologies that had been lost to history for eons uncounted.","But even this wasn’t the extent of Bazuman’s horror.","Its form split open.","The spherical mass that comprised its body cracked down the center like an egg being hatched, and from within that crack emerged light that held no color.","It was a pocket dimension of pure undifferentiation that existed within Bazuman’s interior, a space where the rules of Existence ceased to apply and all things trended toward eternal dissolution.","This was where Noah had been swallowed into before!","Gravitational pull erupted from the opening, affecting everything nearby. Noah felt it tugging at his existence, felt his body lean forward slightly before he braced himself against the pull. The echoes that Bazuman had manifested became more numerous as it drew upon deeper reserves within itself. The very air became hazardous, proximity to Bazuman causing passive dissolution that began working on anything that drew too close.","Tentacles became more aggressive, seeking to drag opponents into that horrifying interior. And across Bazuman’s wounded surface where the split had formed, additional mouths began manifesting.","Such terrifying power unfolded!","All of the horrors that Bazuman manifested created a suction force that dragged everything toward the yawning maw at its core!","Noah could see structures of THE Agora being pulled toward the endless light of undifferentiation, ancient stones that had witnessed eons of judgment now sliding across the ground toward consumption.","Even the figures of the four Strategoi weren’t still. They were being pulled while they resisted, their feet scraping against ground and skies that offered no purchase, their Civilizations beginning to burn brightly around them as they enacted their own Embodiments to maintain position one after another while repelling horrid Manifestations!","On Noah’s chest, something bloomed.","The sensation was warmth spreading outward from his chest, comfortable heat like a hearth coming to life. A defensive Transcendent Paradoxical Inscriptio Dormiens activated without his conscious command, its golden page manifesting against his chest and burning with dual lights of differentiation and undifferentiation.","The Inscription declared that he couldn’t be consumed, that his existence wasn’t susceptible to the suction that affected everything else, and reality accepted that declaration.","Echoes of Absolute from Bazuman surrounded him, and...","Noah remained unfettered.","He took no damage.","He stood perfectly still while structures crumbled around him and Strategoi struggled to maintain position, his Infinities burning with brilliance that exceeded their previous intensity as he faced Bazuman’s full echoes and manifestation with calm that he maintained through absolute confidence in what he’d become.","At this time, THE Primordial Paradox spoke with a voice that cut through the chaos without effort.","\" An enemy like this is one that needs to be defeated in a short span of time.\"","His obsidian-gold flames burned brighter.","\" Especially since he is an Undivided One. I couldn’t erase it before because it had your glimmer of Infinity.\"","His eyes turned to Noah.","\" But if you are confident, Youngest, I can hold it down to give you the opportunity to confirm that you truly know what you are doing.\"","\"I can hold it down... if you can use your Infinity to overcome its now endless undifferentiation.\"","...!"]},{"number":4930,"title":"Chapter 4930: Chapter 4929: Ganging Up On Bazuman! III","paragraphs":["Noah’s eyes flashed brilliantly at these words from THE Primordial Paradox!","One mustn’t forget.","THE Primordial Paradox was powerful.","Whether as powerful as THE Creature or not was unknown, but he was up there among the most terrifying beings in Observable Existence.","And he was offering to hold Bazuman down.","So Noah simply gave a light nod to show his confidence.","At this time, THE Civilizational Instinctus activated fully.","The sensation was akin to a door opening behind his eyes. Noah’s perception shifted as the capability he’d gained from the Spark Fragment of THE First Cause revealed what lay behind Bazuman’s physical form.","The Secondary Function of Manifestation Observation showed him the Civilization that this Undivided One possessed, the architectural construct that represented everything Bazuman had accumulated across eons of consumption.","What he saw was heavy!","Behind Bazuman’s churning physical form existed a structure that defied conventional description. It appeared as an infinite stomach-archive, a vast cathedral of digestion where countless chambers held the preserved memories of everything Bazuman had ever consumed.","Pillars formed from crystallized recollections supported ceilings that stretched toward infinity. Walls built from accumulated authority separated sections dedicated to different categories of consumed beings!","And everything was connected to core at the center. A pulsing core of pure undifferentiation that served as the heart of Bazuman’s existence.","The Tertiary Function of Structural Analysis identified vulnerabilities within this horrifying Manifestation.","Noah saw cracks in the walls where different consumed memories didn’t integrate cleanly with each other, places where the authority of one devoured being conflicted with the authority of another. He saw pillars that bore too much weight, supporting structures that had accumulated more than they were designed to hold.","He saw fraying connections where Bazuman’s paradoxical nature, remembering while remaining undifferentiated, created stress points that his existence constantly struggled to maintain.","And most importantly, he saw the central weakness.","The core itself was surrounded by a ring of instability where the pure undifferentiation of Bazuman’s core met the differentiated memories that he maintained. That boundary was constantly shifting, constantly struggling to remain coherent, constantly threatening to collapse if sufficient pressure was applied from the right angle.","If Noah could reach that boundary...","If he could flood it with definition...","Bazuman would collapse from the inside out!","As he observed all of this, THE Primordial Paradox moved!","Well, yes and no.","He spoke.","\" Who... gave you permission to have Undifferentiated Paradox?\"","HUUM!","A few words.","Simple words, even.","And yet, in the next moment, Noah observed as behind THE Primordial Paradox, multiple Embodiments and Apophasis manifestations bloomed by the dozens!","They took on the forms of terrifying conceptual creatures. Paradoxical beasts that existed and didn’t exist simultaneously. Entities that were both predator and prey. Constructs that attacked by being attacked and defended by being destroyed. Lions made of contradiction. Serpents woven from impossibility. Eagles whose wings were forged from statements that canceled themselves out!","And then all of these multiple Embodiments and Apophasis actually flowed into the words THE Primordial Paradox had uttered!","A...stacking of Embodiments and Apophasis?","They merged with his simple question, empowering it, elevating it, transforming it from mere words into a truth that pressed against the fabric of existence itself. Noah felt the power rushing past him like wind from a hurricane!","THE Primordial Paradox truly asked the entirety of the existence of Bazuman...","Who gave it permission to have Undifferentiated Paradox?","The instant his terrifying question was asked, the instant the power of THE Primordial Paradox erupted...","Noah felt another immense pressure permeating all around!","This time it was Paradox. Obsidian-gold authority that pressed against everything with weight that declared contradictions to be law. The pressure of THE Primordial Paradox’s released power exceeded even Bazuman’s sea of undifferentiation, overwhelming the crimson tide with paradoxical authority that simply stated the undifferentiation both existed and didn’t exist, rendering it functionally inert.","And in the next moment...","The horrid body and limbs and echoes of THE Undivided One before them became frozen!","Bazuman’s countless eyes, which had been blazing with hunger moments before, now stared forward without ability to move. Its tentacles, which had been reaching toward Noah with desperate hunger, now hung suspended in positions that defied gravity.","Its churning surface, its Echoes, which had been constantly shifting and revealing faces of consumed beings, now held perfectly still as if time itself had ceased to flow for this entity alone.","Even its Civilization froze!","The Manifestation that only Noah could see, that infinite stomach-archive with its countless chambers and connected core, became still in ways that Civilizations shouldn’t have been capable of. The memories ceased their eternal churning. The pillars stopped bearing weight because weight itself had been placed in paradoxical suspension.","The core at the center continued to exist, but it existed in a state where it both pulled and didn’t pull, where it both consumed and didn’t consume.","It was a terrifying display of power from THE Primordial Paradox!","And the moment this being acted, Noah also made his move!","From the corrupted glimmers of Infinite undifferentiation that had been surrounding Bazuman, from the proto-matter that carried both THE Living Paradox’s corruption and Noah’s scattered Seals, golden pages began blooming!","How dare it take in glimmers of his Infinities when because of it, he could unleash attacks that effectively bloomed inches from his existence?!","THE Transcendent Paradoxical Inscriptiones Dormientes that Noah had moved within the corrupted proto-matter now activated!","They’d been sleeping within the very substance that Bazuman had been using, waiting for the moment when Noah chose to awaken them. The sensation of their activation was like feeling hounds finally released from their leashes, eager and hungry and straining toward their prey!","They emerged from particles that seemed too small to contain them, golden pages burning with dual lights of differentiation and undifferentiation that made them visible even against the frozen chaos of Bazuman’s form.","The Inscriptions flowed toward the weak points of the Manifestation that only Noah could see!","If THE Primordial Paradox wasn’t here, Noah would have had to fight with the terrifying Immensity and undifferentiation of Bazuman while trying to attack the weaknesses of his Civilization. He would have had to contend with echoes and tentacles and the gravitational pull of the core while simultaneously attempting strikes against vulnerabilities that only he could perceive.","But since THE Primordial Paradox had ridiculously caused every single Depth and undifferentiation and Immensity of Bazuman to freeze...","It was like Noah was basically holding a gun.","And his enemy was bound and shackled...and he simply had to shoot.","So he shot.","The first Transcendent Paradoxical Inscriptio struck a crack in the wall of Bazuman’s stomach-archive whereconflicting memories failed to integrate cleanly!","The golden page burned against the vulnerability with light that held both differentiation and undifferentiation, and Noah felt the impact reverberate through THE Civilizational Instinctus like watching a hammer strike glass.","The wall didn’t merely crack further. It began to forget that it had ever been a wall. The memories it contained began questioning whether they’d ever been memories at all!","Undifferentiation and differentiation working in harmony tore apart structure that Bazuman had maintained for eons.","The second Inscription struck a pillar that bore too much accumulated weight!","The golden page pressed against the stress point that Noah’s Structural Analysis had identified. The countless consumed beings whose authority comprised that pillar started separating from each other, their combined strength dissolving as the Inscription declared that they were and weren’t connected simultaneously. The pillar cracked. It wavered. It began to collapse under weight that it could no longer justify bearing!","The third, fourth, fifth, sixth Inscriptions struck fraying connections throughout the Manifestation!","Each golden page found a vulnerability that Noah’s perception had identified, and each activation caused cascading damage that spread beyond the initial point of impact. The sensation was exhilarating, like watching dominoes fall in patterns he’d arranged, like feeling a plan come together with precision that exceeded his expectations!","Connections that had been struggling to maintain coherence now failed entirely. Sections of the stomach-archive that had been integrated for eons now separated as if they’d never belonged together.","Bazuman’s Civilization was coming apart from the inside!","But Noah wasn’t finished.","He focused on the central weakness.","That pulsing core of pure undifferentiation surrounded by a ring of instability where undifferentiation met differentiated memory.","Noah took a step.","And appeared deep in the very center of Bazuman as another Inscriptio cut through like a blade of differentiation and undifferentiation!","THE Primordial Paradox’s freezing authority had suspended everything about this Undivided One, including the defenses that would have prevented such intrusion. Noah simply moved through the frozen tentacles, through the suspended echoes, through the churning proto-matter that couldn’t churn while paradox held it still.","He arrived at the terrifying center.","The entrance to core gaped before him. The belly that had swallowed him long ago during his escape through THE Prima Indifferentia. He’d run from this place then, had fled with everything he possessed to avoid being consumed by its endless dissolution.","But now he didn’t run.","Now he radiated.","His entire body began to emit terrifying blue-gold brilliance as Infinite Absolute Seals flooded out of him in numbers that exceeded anything he’d released before! The Seals didn’t attack. They didn’t need to attack. They simply existed, carrying definition that declared what they were with authority that couldn’t be questioned. And he amplified it all by releasing his Inscriptions here!","The sensation of releasing so much of himself was like exhaling a breath he’d been holding for eons, like finally letting go of weight he hadn’t realized he’d been carrying.","His light and brilliance began to encompass the entirety of the center of Bazuman!","He sought to infuse the endless definition of Infinity into an entity who only had undefinition and undifferentiation.","The only way to collapse something this deeply undifferentiated was to give it a profound sense of definition. And since Bazuman had Infinity within its corrupted weavings, since it had consumed a piece of Noah eons ago and absorbed more through the corrupted proto-matter, all other areas across its body had resonance with Infinite authority.","With Noah radiating Infinity at Bazuman’s very center, that resonance activated!","The Infinite Seals within Bazuman’s consumed existence began responding to Noah’s broadcast!","All other areas across its body began to radiate a strict outlined definition of Infinity!","The sea of undifferentiation that Bazuman had released was now filled with points of definition that declared themselves with absolute certainty! The echoes it had manifested found their consumed foundations suddenly becoming defined, becoming differentiated, becoming things that had names and boundaries and limitations that undifferentiated existence shouldn’t have possessed!","The entire area became filled with the definition of Infinity!","And Bazuman, for the first time in eons upon eons, found itself becoming defined.","This whole time the terrifying Immensity of THE Undivided One sought to move, but it was unable to. Its eyes were livid as they stared at both Noah and THE Primordial Paradox, hatred and hunger burning within crimson depths.","But the body of THE Primordial Paradox remained imposing and grand as it stared down with obsidian-gold flames burning steadily around his form.","And Noah, deep within the center of Bazuman, looked at the core being filled with definition as he knew it was over for this being.","The Manifestation he could see through THE Civilizational Instinctus was collapsing entirely now. The infinite stomach-archive was no longer infinite. It had boundaries, limitations, edges that could be perceived. The countless chambers were no longer countless. They had numbers, values, quantities that could be calculated. The core itself was no longer purely undifferentiated. It held definition that conflicted with its fundamental nature.","Bazuman was becoming something it had never been.","Something defined.","Something limited.","Something that could be consumed!","Noah’s eyes blazed with blue-gold light as he looked at the central core of this Undivided One, as he prepared to harvest everything that this ancient horror had accumulated across eons of consumption. His weavings were already activating, preparing to multiply and exponentially elevate whatever he claimed from this collapse!","And before he did it, he spoke words that echoed Bazuman’s earlier confession with cruel symmetry.","\"I...want you, O Bazuman.\"","HUUM!","This time it was his own confession.","And he wanted to consume this Undivided One whole!"]},{"number":4931,"title":"Chapter 4931: Chapter 4930: Three I","paragraphs":["When something brilliantly filled with undifferentiation was frozen and then gloriously defined infinitely, the result was astoundingly unique.","Noah observed the entire figure of Bazuman crystallizing.","It began at the edges, where his Infinite Seals had first made contact with the undifferentiated surface. Blue-gold light spread across the churning proto-matter like frost forming on glass, but this frost didn’t freeze. It defined. Every particle of Bazuman’s existence that the light touched found itself suddenly knowing what it was, suddenly possessing boundaries and limitations and names that undifferentiation should never have permitted.","The crystallization spread inward with speed that exceeded perception.","The vast network of Bazuman’s existence, that infinite stomach-archive filled with consumed memories and accumulated power, transformed section by section. Walls that had been made of undifferentiated authority became crystalline structures of defined Infinity. Pillars that had supported ceilings of pure consumption became solid formations that knew their exact height and weight and purpose.","Noah’s defensive Inscription burned against his chest with comfortable warmth, allowing him to remain at the very core of this being without being affected by the transformation occurring around him. His offensive Inscriptions carried their Embodiments and Apophasis through the frozen structure, finding weaknesses and exploiting them, collapsing the very foundation of this Civilization of undifferentiation filled with hunger.","In moments, Bazuman became crystallized into blue-gold.","The countless crimson eyes that had blazed with hunger were now solid gemstones that held no life. The innumerable tentacles that had reached for Noah with desperate desire were now frozen extensions of defined authority. The mouths filled with teeth of crystallized memory were now structures that couldn’t consume because they’d been given definition that prevented consumption.","Noah could feel his own existence buzzing with anticipation as he looked at the crystallization of an Undivided One that seemed like his to take.","He carried out the Rite of Paradoxical Inheritance.","\" The Everythings of what was collapsed are mine and not mine. They belong to me and they do not belong to me. They must be given to me instantly and they must never be given to me at all.\"","HUUM!","The moment he uttered these words, the blue-gold crystallization of Bazuman began to shine with light that pulsed in rhythms matching Noah’s own heartbeat. It tried to come toward his existence as he was rightfully claiming it, choosing to forego the Absolute Existential Palace in favor of direct integration. The crystallized structure began breaking apart into streams of authority that flowed toward him like rivers finding their ocean.","But as this process began...","Noah activated THE Numerical Sovereignty silently.","The mathematical structures within his existence shifted, numbers flickering at the edges of his perception as he imposed operations upon the incoming harvest. He commanded for his weavings to multiply by ten. He commanded for the incoming harvest and weavings of Bazuman to be raised by an exponent of three.","...!","Prompts bloomed before his eyes with weight that pressed against his consciousness.","|Multiplicative Amplification Applied to Crystallized Undifferentiated Civilization|","|After 10x Multiplicative Amplification, the density and Immensity of the Crystallized Undifferentiated Civilization of Bazuman has been increased by a factor of 10 and amplified by a factor of 10. The harvest you are receiving now contains concentrated authority that exceeds what Bazuman originally possessed by an order of magnitude.|","|Exponential Expression Applied|","|After Exponential Expression with an Exponent of 3, the Depth of the Crystallized Undifferentiated Civilization of Bazuman has been transformed exponentially. The compounding effect has elevated this harvest from the classification of an Undivided One to something approaching the classification of beings that shaped THE Prima Indifferentia itself.|","| Final Assessment: The harvest you are now receiving is equivalent to One Fourth of THE Civilizational Harvest of a Primordial Architect.|","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes illuminated with glorious Immensity at these prompts!","A fourth of a Primordial Architect?! Bazuman’s loot had been elevated from an Undivided One to be equivalent to a fourth of a Primordial Architect?!","These were beings Noah hadn’t even met, the cream of the crop in THE Prima Indifferentia! Entities that had existed since THE First Cause itself, that had shaped the nature of differentiation and undifferentiation, that possessed power exceeding even THE Four!","His weavings buzzed with profound tyranny and quintessence as the harvest began flowing into his existence with force that made his foundations tremble with anticipation rather than strain. Before things could proceed any further...","More prompts bloomed.","|Unexpected Finding Observed|","|Due to the set corruption of Bazuman from the Corrupted Paradoxical Proto-matter of THE Living Paradox, 10% of your harvest has automatically been siphoned off by an Absolute Paradoxical Weaving of Existence supported by an Axiom. This siphoning occurred before your Multiplicative Amplification and Exponential Expression could be applied to the affected portion.|","|Assessment: Any corrupted Absolute killed in Observable Existence will grant a portion of harvest to THE Living Paradox.|","...!","The waves of glory and the slight smile that had been forming on Noah’s lips faded.","Fucking what?","10% of his Loot was gone?","Siphoned off to that philosophical peasant who had the audacity to steal from him?","In life, one could get angry many times. Absolutes weren’t above anger as many still had profound emotions when pushed enough. Noah had felt annoyance before. He’d felt irritation. He’d felt the cold calculation of vengeance being planned against enemies who had wronged him.","At this moment, Noah wasn’t angry.","He was furious!","So furious that his greatest enemy in existence might just change from that trash waste of existence known as THE Living Elemental to become THE Living Paradox!","And his fury only became grander and grander as he began receiving the tremendous boon of a percentage of the Immensity of a Primordial Architect. Because even as the harvest flooded into his existence with force that should have been glorious, even as his foundations expanded to accommodate power that exceeded anything he’d previously possessed...","He felt his Derivative Civilizations of Infinite Undifferentiated Fate and Infinite Hunger become full.","As if they’d taken in far, far too much.","With them being Half-Step Absolute, at this moment they were squeezing up and spilling past Half-Step as if they were saying... bro, we can’t take anymore!"]},{"number":4932,"title":"Chapter 4932: Chapter 4931: Three II","paragraphs":["Inside of him, he felt his Organ of Civilization quiver with strain that bordered on rupture. An instant later, he felt the emergence of 10 Absolute Everythings and two Infinite Everythings, resources that his overflowing Harvest had produced from sheer excess.","And as soon as they emerged, they disappeared into his existence, absorbed by foundations that were desperately trying to accommodate what was being poured into them.","Prompts bloomed with urgency that pressed against his awareness.","|Critical Threshold Reached|","|The Derivative Civilizations of Infinite Undifferentiated Fate and Infinite Hunger are seeking permission for Absolute. They Hunger. They burn with Undifferentiation. The harvest they have received exceeds their capacity to remain at Half-Step classification. They must advance or they must be released. There is no third option.|","...!","Noah was currently in a unique state of mind.","He felt his vibrant, immense waves of Infinity that represented his main Civilization. His Mana. His First Tongue! And orbiting around it at this moment were two huge bubbles that sought to pop. The bubbles of Infinite Undifferentiated Fate and Infinite Hunger wanted to take the step to become Absolutes as they’d taken in far too much harvest to remain at the level they were at.","But his ongoing foundation and Civilization of THE First Tongue still felt like it could take on so much more.","He inherently felt like if any part of him became an Absolute, his main Civilization would quietly and quickly follow afterward. He wouldn’t be able to stop it. Because the moment any part of him became an Absolute, the change would be so grand that the interior of his existence would become filled with that glorious Immensity, and his main Civilization would truly follow right after.","So how exactly was he to rectify this?","In his unique state of mind, his mouth began to move as he released words he’d heard a little while ago from an echo.","\"When the Youngest walks where the Oldest slumber, Existence shall tremble and the Weave shall fray. He who holds Infinity in mortal palms shall stand at the crossroads where all rivers end...\"","\"The Paradox shall fall before the Paradox rises. The father consumed by the son, the son consumed by the purpose, the purpose consumed by the question that birthed all questions. Three collapses for the price of one, and in the third collapse, the door shall crack.\"","\"The Shroud of Endless Blue shall fall upon Observable Existence. It shall be both salvation and damnation, both the key and the lock, both the bridge and the chasm. Under its weight, the doors of the Scales shall open or the doors of the Scales shall shatter. There is no third path. There is no middle ground. There is only the choice that is not a choice.\"","...!","He recited these words out loud and silently at the same time as he wondered which of them had fully come to pass and which of them were still coming in the future.","The theme of three seemed prevalent.","At this time, in his unique state where he was absorbing the tremendous immense amount of elevated harvest, where parts of him wished to take a step to become Absolutes...","He gave a simple command at this moment.","\" Divide.\"","BOOM!","At the moment he said these words, terrifying blue-gold cracks permeated across his body.","Two cracks vertically bisected his form, running from crown to feet with precision that spoke of authority rather than destruction. In the next moment, an influx of Infinities erupted outward as if something was being split apart and sundered, light pouring from the fractures with intensity that painted THE Agora in shades of blue and gold that overwhelmed everything else.","In the span of a nanosecond, the sundering was completed.","The main half at the center displayed a figure of Noah shining with extremely pure and beautiful blue-gold brilliance of Mana. THE First Tongue burned around this body with authority that had been refined through separation, purified through division, elevated through the removal of elements that had been diluting its singular focus.","And on either side of him...","Bodies that looked exactly like him stood with presence that matched his own.","One was surrounded by an endless light of golden Infinite Undifferentiated Fate, the authority of dissolution and entropy given form, the power that returned all things to their proto-state. This Noah burned with light that sought to unmake everything it touched, that viewed definition as a disease to be cured through return to formlessness.","The other was surrounded by a crimson brilliance of Infinite Hunger, the authority of consumption and accumulation given shape, the power that devoured and absorbed and made all things part of itself. This Noah blazed with light that wanted to consume everything it perceived, that viewed separation as an obstacle to be overcome through integration.","The central Noah looked at the other two with an extremely glorious and imperious gaze.","\" Now you may proceed to attain Absolute. My foundation... is not yet complete.\"","BOOM!","As odd as it was, he was basically talking to himself.","And there was no delay.","The two bodies that had been separated from him erupted with terrifying brilliance and horrifying aura as they sought to attain the Depth that stood higher than Fundamental. Absolute!","Even though he didn’t grasp it with his main Civilization, he’d separated himself into three as he would be experiencing the glimmer of Absolute with another part of himself entirely!","Prompts bloomed.","|Unprecedented Action Taken|","|You have divided your existence into three separate bodies, each one carrying a distinct Civilization. Your main body retains THE First Tongue in its purest form. Your secondary bodies carry Infinite Undifferentiated Fate and Infinite Hunger respectively. This division has made your Civilization of Mana, your Civilization of THE First Tongue, even purer. It now exists as the sole Civilization within your main existence.|","|Assessment: Your foundation can now advance even further, especially as it receives reinforcement from your other Selves that are grasping Absolute at this moment. The grander the heights your other bodies achieve with their Civilizations of Infinite Undifferentiated Fate and Infinite Hunger, the grander the foundation and Immensity of your Civilization of THE First Tongue becomes.|","|When you complete the full integration of the Immensity and Depth of the remaining One Fourth of a Primordial Architect, a much clearer assessment will be made. But as of now, you feel the glimmer of Absolute yourself through your other bodies.|","...!","Yes.","He felt it. He could feel it!","He could feel the single step that so many could never cross across their entire existences. The step that one took to go from the measly Depths of the Civilizational Scale to the Absolute Depth that was truly the stage one was supposed to be at within the Civilizational Scale.","On this day, with two separate bodies, he took the step seamlessly.","Because of his tremendous and unmatched foundation, because those bodies that took the step carried the Immensity of the foundation he held at this time, because of how grand it all was...","He didn’t have any trouble taking that seemingly impossible step.","For him, it was effortless.","For him, it was grand.","For him, it was...","\" Merely Absolute.\"","...!","BOOM!"]},{"number":4933,"title":"Chapter 4933: Chapter 4932: Are You With Us? I","paragraphs":["Glossikos looked ahead as she saw utmost brilliance, her figure kneeling slightly from the pressure that had been released by THE Undivided One.","Her knees ached against the ancient weavings of THE Agora, and her linguistic authority burned around her form with intensity that bordered on painful as she struggled to maintain coherence against the waves of undifferentiation that had washed over this place. The crimson tide had receded now, pulled back by authority that exceeded anything Bazuman had possessed, but the strain of withstanding it still echoed through her foundations.","She saw Noah and THE Primordial Paradox far ahead of them, their figures standing at the center of what had been a battlefield moments ago. Noah was currently taking in a Crystallized Undivided One, the blue-gold structure that had been Bazuman now flowing toward his existence in streams of elevated authority. THE Primordial Paradox stood beside him with obsidian-gold flames burning steadily, watching the process with ancient eyes that missed nothing.","Her expression was complex as she observed.","She now saw why he’d taken the Claim of THE First Tongue.","She’d wanted it for herself so much that she’d disliked him from the moment he arrived. She hadn’t fully backed her Civilization to his when he came here, had maintained distance and reservation that bordered on hostility. Her assistance had been minimal. Her heart had held resentment toward the being who had claimed what she believed should have been hers.","But seeing him these past hours...","Maybe it was time to give her backing just like the other three Strategoi backed THE Four of their paths.","In her heart, she still disliked THE Four. Or really, THE Five now. All Strategoi did. They had a role that bound them to THE Agora of Primordial Judgment, a duty that required them to continue protecting this place across eons of existence. And THE Five did whatever suited them and left the Strategoi to pick up the pieces.","When Paradox and Noah had entered the Crack eons ago, disappearing into THE Prima Indifferentia without warning or explanation, it had been the Strategoi who maintained THE Agora. When THE Living Paradox had done all of this with the corruption of proto-matter, flooding Observable Existence with his grand design, it would have to be the Strategoi who struggled to hold this territory against the consequences.","There were many examples of such abandonment.","But maybe...","Maybe THE Five, with all the power they held, would eventually make everything okay.","Maybe...","\" Come now, someone like you should never kneel to anybody.\"","She heard a sonorous voice beside her, gentle and warm and filled with concern that made something in her chest loosen.","When she turned, she saw a slender hand extended toward her, offering to help her rise. The fingers were delicate, almost fragile in their appearance, and the skin held a warmth that seemed to radiate comfort without any authority behind it. Just kindness. Just care.","Glossikos blinked as she grabbed the hand and rose up, finding herself thinking that the hands of the other Strategoi shouldn’t be small and slender like this. Khaotikos’s form shifted constantly between states. Ontikos’s hands held the weight of Existence itself. Paradoxos’s dual nature meant nothing about him was so simply singular.","This hand belonged to someone else.","With this thought, she turned to see the woman beside her.","She was beautiful. Her features held a serenity that seemed untouched by the chaos that had just occurred, as if the battle between Absolutes and Undivided Ones was merely weather passing overhead rather than apocalyptic conflict. Her hair fell in waves that caught the light of THE Agora with colors that shifted subtly, never quite settling on a single shade.","Her form was slender and graceful, dressed in robes that seemed woven from twilight itself.","But her eyes...","Her eyes were what captured Glossikos’s attention completely.","They were so calm. So pure. They held depths that seemed to contain understanding without judgment, acceptance without condition, love without limitation. Looking into them felt like coming home after a journey that had lasted far too long. Looking into them felt like being seen for the first time in eons.","Behind this woman stood Khaotikos, Ontikos, and Paradoxos.","The three other Strategoi had similar expressions on their faces. Calm. Content. At peace in ways that Glossikos had never seen from beings who had spent eons bound to duty they resented.","Glossikos felt like she remembered something in the back of her mind, some warning or recognition that tickled at the edges of her consciousness. But she couldn’t quite figure it out. The memory kept slipping away like water through fingers, replaced by warmth that spread through her foundations with comfort that exceeded anything she’d felt before.","The woman in front of her, THE Secretive Eon, asked her lightly with voice that seemed to resonate inside Glossikos’s chest rather than reach her through the air.","\"Are you with us?\"","And Glossikos blinked.","She...","She?","No.","They.","They were always with each other.","Her existence subtly transformed as understanding that wasn’t understanding settled into her foundations. The resentment she’d felt toward THE Five faded. The duty she’d resented for eons became something she embraced. The isolation she’d experienced as a Strategos became connection that linked her to something greater than herself.","She smiled toward THE Secretive Eon.","Then she turned toward the figures of Noah and THE Primordial Paradox far ahead.","The two of them had sensed nothing of their entry here. They’d been focused on Bazuman, on the crystallization and harvest, on the power being claimed and the foundations being elevated. They hadn’t noticed when THE Secretive Eon stepped through the corruption that permeated THE Agora. Their unique aura allowed them to move across existence undetected.","They hadn’t felt when the four Strategoi became something other than what they’d been.","Sometimes, when you stopped outside the door of a house, some might mistakenly believe it was because you were unable to go inside. Maybe you just didn’t want to at that time. Maybe you were waiting for the right moment.","Maybe you were waiting for corruption to change the atmosphere before you could step inside.","So... they stepped inside.","At this moment, the four Strategoi of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment were now with them.","And their will within Eon moved forward as she finally expressed her aura and power for those ahead who had been dealing with an Undivided One.","\" My oh my, what a nice place this is.\"","...!","Eon said calmly, her voice carrying across THE Agora with gentleness that belied the horror of what had just occurred behind Noah and THE Primordial Paradox’s backs.","And far ahead...","BOOM!","Unfathomable Paradox erupted from THE Primordial Paradox, obsidian-gold flames blazing outward with intensity that painted THE Agora in colors that warred against the corruption permeating its stones. His ancient eyes locked onto THE Secretive Eon with recognition that held weight accumulated across eons of conflict.","Three bodies of Noah turned to look over solemnly!","The central form burning with pure blue-gold Mana. The body surrounded by golden Infinite Undifferentiated Fate. The form blazing with crimson Infinite Hunger. All three of them oriented toward THE Secretive Eon with gazes that held no fear, only assessment of a threat that had just revealed itself at the worst possible moment.","And Eon looked over to them and smiled with warmth that seemed genuine despite everything it represented.","She waved.","A simple gesture. Friendly. Almost playful.","And behind her, the four Strategoi waved in the same manner. The same timing. The same angle of their arms. The same smiles on their faces that matched Eon’s expression perfectly.","Four beings who had been individuals moments ago, now moving as one.","Four Strategoi who had protected THE Agora for eons, now extensions of something that viewed their individuality as rot to be decomposed.","THE Primordial Mycelia had arrived.","And it...had made friends."]},{"number":4934,"title":"Chapter 4934: Chapter 4933: Are You With Us? II","paragraphs":["As Eon stared at Paradox and Noah on one side of THE Agora, something else was occurring in another section entirely.","In another region of THE Acropolis.","THE Acropolis was the highest district, accessible only to Polemarchs and above under normal circumstances. The Crack of Observable Existence dominated its skyline, that terrible wound in reality through which corruption now poured. But THE Acropolis had many sections beyond the main courtyard where battles had just been fought. It also had the Primordial Archive and the Chamber of Judgment where the most important debates occurred.","Inside the Primordial Archive, something terrible was unfolding in silence.","The structure itself was vast and ancient. Marble floors stretched toward distant walls that held alcoves filled with knowledge accumulated across eons. Floating scrolls drifted through the air in lazy spirals, their contents glowing with authority that made them visible even in the sourceless light that illuminated this place. Books hovered in formations that defied gravity, organized by principles that transcended alphabetical or chronological ordering.","At the very center of the Archive, where the most precious knowledge was meant to be protected, multiple Cracks had formed. They led to different places. To different Primordial Realms. To regions of Observable Existence that had always been connected to THE Agora through pathways that few knew existed.","The Archive was eerily silent.","No sound of turning pages. No whisper of scrolls unfurling. No footsteps echoing against marble that should have rung with every movement.","And yet in this place, there were actually thousands of beings present.","Followers of the aspects of the Oldest Paradox of Existence filled the Archive in numbers that exceeded its apparent capacity. Glossarians stood in orderly rows, their linguistic authority dim and muted where it should have blazed with the power of THE First Tongue.","Paradoxians waited beside them, their contradictory natures no longer expressing themselves through individual choices but through unified purpose. Chaosites, who should have been impossible to organize by their very nature, stood in perfect formation.","Chaos...was very orderly.","Existentialists, who had dedicated themselves to questions of being and meaning, now possessed answers they’d never sought.","There were thousands of them.","And yet none made a sound.","They orderly entered the Cracks at the center of the Archive and disappeared. One by one. Row by row. Moving with coordination that spoke of singular will rather than collective decision. No one pushed. No one hesitated. No one expressed any individuality whatsoever as they stepped through portals that would carry them to other Primordial Realms.","In the air above them, Nyx floated with calmness that matched her master’s.","The disciple of THE Secretive Eon watched their collective begin to spread out. She, as they, observed the process with satisfaction that belonged to something far older than her individual existence. Her eyes held the same calm purity that Glossikos had seen in Eon’s gaze. Her smile held the same warmth that had made the Strategos forget her concerns.","THE Agora of Primordial Judgment was always the endgame.","It connected to all the other Primordial Realms as it was a nexus. The Cracks that led to other realms were features, not flaws. They were pathways that allowed THE Agora to fulfill its purpose.","And when the nexus came under their control, they could spread even easier.","So they did.","Existence was vast and filled with terrors.","Beings suffered in isolation, fought wars that had no purpose, struggled against entropy that would claim them eventually regardless of their efforts. They didn’t understand that there was a better way. They didn’t know that unity could solve the problems that individuality created.","They had to move as a collective to show the way.","They knew the way. The others just needed to be shown. When they were shown, they would understand. There were countless problems out there, and they had already found a solution.","They were the solution.","The others would just have to be shown this to understand.","The terrifying and eerie process continued as in heavy silence with barely any noise, thousands containing the will of THE Primordial Mycelia flooded from THE Agora and spread out to other Primordial Realms. They moved through Cracks that led to the Jotunheim, Alfheimr, Helheim...to territories that had been protected for eons by beings who would soon understand the glory of unity.","The rot was spreading.","And it spread in glorious silence.","---","The terror of losing one’s identity was a unique one.","What did it mean to be yourself? Was identity the sum of your memories, the accumulation of choices made across existence? Was it the consistent thread of consciousness that linked who you were yesterday to who you would be tomorrow? Or was it something deeper, something that existed at the foundation of your being, something that couldn’t be defined but that you knew was there because without it, you would cease to be you?","When that foundation cracked, when the thread began to fray, when the sum started subtracting from itself without your permission...","What remained?","The horror wasn’t simply death. Death was cessation. Death was an ending that at least had the dignity of being final. This was something else entirely. This was watching yourself disappear while still being aware enough to mourn what was being lost. This was feeling your existence hollow out from the inside while the shell remained intact. This was becoming a stranger to yourself one memory at a time, one choice at a time, one fragment of identity at a time.","It was a horrid thing to say the least.","Even more astounding was how one could realize the process was happening and be halfway through having their identity erased, but still have awareness of it occurring as they sought to stop it.","This was what was currently happening with a lone entity who had always been alone and lonely across existence.","THE Living Temporal.","Since his identity began to fade, he had been running across time!","He’d traversed into the past to anchor himself into an identity of back then, believing that if he could root himself in who he’d been, the infection couldn’t claim who he was. And yet nothing changed. In fact, the infection tried to establish itself retroactively, reaching back through the timeline he’d created to claim versions of himself that should have been beyond its grasp.","He’d run into the future, hoping that establishing himself ahead of the infection’s spread would allow him to outpace it. And it did nothing. The infection felt even stronger when he sought to establish himself in the future, as if it had already claimed what he would become before he could become it.","At this moment, THE Living Temporal found himself surrounded by stellar purple rivers of time.","The currents flowed around him in streams that held the weight of eons, carrying moments and possibilities and might-have-beens in their luminous depths. His Civilizational Authority manifested as tendrils of golden light that wove through the purple rivers, trying to maintain structure, trying to keep the flow of time moving in patterns he could control.","And THE Living Temporal swam.","He physically swam against the rivers of time with desperation that would have shocked anyone who had known him in his prime. His arms swept through temporal currents that pressed against him with weight that exceeded physical resistance. His legs kicked against the flow of moments that tried to carry him toward a future he could no longer face. Each stroke kept his Temporal authority churning and active, preventing the infection from claiming more of him while he desperately searched for a solution across all of time.","His features had changed.","Previously, he could look old and young simultaneously, his mastery of time allowing him to present whatever age suited his mood or purpose. His face could hold the wisdom of ancient epochs and the vigor of fresh beginnings in the same moment. His eyes could burn with experience accumulated across eons while sparkling with the curiosity of someone just beginning to explore existence.","But right now, he only seemed aged and tired.","Lines creased his face that he couldn’t smooth away with temporal authority. His hair, which had always shifted between colors and lengths at his whim, now hung gray and limp against his shoulders. His eyes, those stellar purple depths that had witnessed the birth and death of countless civilizations, now held exhaustion that exceeded physical weariness.","Only glimmers of majesty remained. Faint echoes of who he’d been before the infection began its work.","And as he swung his arms and swam against the current of time, even though he didn’t show it on his stern face...","He was terrified.","An Absolute like him was terrified.","He had thought of himself as grand. He’d expected his journey across existence to be even grander, a story that would be told across eons, a legend that would inspire beings who hadn’t yet been born. He had thought he could contend against THE Creature and THE Living Paradox and THE Primordial Chaos. Even though they laid claims to the aspects of the Oldest Paradox of Existence, he had time.","He had time itself in his hands.","He’d definitely known he could be just as grand as them. He’d seen the paths that led to THE Second Scale of Existence, had traced them through timelines where he succeeded, had believed with absolute certainty that he would walk those paths eventually.","And he was heading there.","He was!"]},{"number":4935,"title":"Chapter 4935: Chapter 4934: Are You With Us? III","paragraphs":["But now all of this was stripped away. He couldn’t even remember half of his exploits across time. Adventures that had defined who he was had become blank spaces in his memory. Choices that had shaped his path had become questions he couldn’t answer. Moments of triumph and tragedy that had built his character had become voids that the infection was eager to fill with its own purpose.","Even though his face remained stern, stellar purple tears of time leaked from his eyes as he mourned his Civilization.","He mourned his ideals and plans and hopes and dreams!","There were men with ambitions like THE Living Paradox who carried out their plans and became more than they were. They schemed and manipulated and succeeded against odds that should have been insurmountable. They bent existence to their will and emerged greater than they’d been before.","And then there were men who failed regardless of what they planned for.","That was just how existence was.","Sometimes you succeeded. Sometimes you failed. But you simply had to do your best at all times.","At this time, as he saw all avenues of his existence blocked off, as he felt the last dredges of his will beginning to crumble against pressure that exceeded anything he could resist alone...","He heard a voice.","It came from everywhere and nowhere. It resonated inside his mind rather than reaching him through the temporal currents. It was warm and gentle and filled with understanding that made his resistance waver despite himself.","\" Why do you struggle, child of time?\"","The voice held no malice. Only concern.","\" We have watched you swim against currents that cannot be outpaced. We have felt your pain as you try to hold onto fragments of yourself that are already becoming part of something greater. It hurts us to see you suffer like this. It truly does.\"","THE Living Temporal kept swimming, kept moving, kept trying to escape.","\" You dream of becoming greater than THE Living Paradox. Greater than THE Creature. You wish to reach THE Second Scale of Existence and prove that your path was worthy of the eons you invested in it. These are beautiful dreams, Temporal. We understand them completely.\"","The voice grew warmer.","\" And we can make them real.\"","His strokes faltered slightly.","\" Think of what you could become with us. Your Temporal authority is singular, yes, but it is limited by its singularity. What if it wasn’t limited? What if you could wield Paradox alongside Time? What if Chaos could flow through your chronological manipulations? What if Existence itself could be bent through your temporal weavings?\"","The currents around him seemed to slow as the voice continued.","\" We have access to all Civilizations within our collective. Those who have mastered contradiction. Those who have embraced entropy. Those who have plumbed the depths of being and meaning. All of their knowledge, all of their authority, all of their power could be yours to use. Not borrowed. Not stolen. Shared freely among family.\"","Family.","The word struck him with force that exceeded any attack.","\" Imagine Temporal seamlessly fused with Quantum. Your control over time enhanced by mastery of probability and uncertainty. Imagine Temporal intertwined with Dimensional. Your chronological authority expanded into spatial manipulation that would make the Undivided Ones bow before you. Imagine Temporal unified with the fundamental aspects of Existence itself, your power growing until THE Second Scale wasn’t a dream but an inevitability.\"","He was slowing. His strokes were weakening.","\" THE Second Scale is achievable with us. This is also our dream, you see. We don’t wish to remain limited to what we currently are. We wish to grow. To evolve. To reach heights that individual existence can never attain. And we wish to bring everyone we love along with us on this journey.\"","The voice held something that sounded almost like tears.","\" You have been alone for so long, Temporal. Lonely across eons of existence with no one who truly understood the weight of time. With us, you would never be alone again. You would be part of something that loves you. That values you. That would use your gifts not to diminish you but to elevate you beyond anything you could achieve on your own.\"","His arms had stopped moving.","\" It hurts us that we’re putting you in pain as you resist. It truly, genuinely hurts us. We don’t want to cause suffering. We want to end suffering. Yours. Everyone’s. The pain of isolation and competition and fear that defines existence for those who haven’t yet understood what we offer.\"","The voice dropped to something almost tender.","\" So we ask you, with all the love we hold for you...\"","Silence.","\" Are you with us, Amser Modred?\"","BOOM!","Amser Modred!","They used the name he was given by the one who bore him so many eons ago!","THE Living Temporal, Amser, howled in grief when he heard this. That name belonged to memories he no longer had. That name came from a time he couldn’t recall, from a being who had loved him, from a life that existed only as void in his consciousness now. They knew his name. His true name. The name that should have been protected by eons of temporal authority.","And he no longer even had his memories of that time!","He howled with such grief as around him, fractures of time bloomed in response to his anguish. Purple cracks split the temporal currents, opening pathways that led to moments scattered across existence. His howl was a cry for help that transcended conscious decision. He’d given up on any grand ideals. He sought help. Simple help. Basic survival.","But who would be able to help him?","Could he find his path toward THE Creature? Would that ancient being be grand enough not to be infected as well? Or would seeking help from such a source merely bring the infection to someone else, spreading the rot further across Observable Existence?","THE Living Temporal didn’t know.","But for now, he began tearing across time, following one of the fractures his grief had created. He moved through moments that blurred together, through eras that had no meaning to his damaged memory, through temporal pathways that his authority had carved in desperation.","And he entered a fracture of time that led somewhere unexpected.","He found himself in gray brilliance he recognized as...THE Interstices. That space between spaces where beings of sufficient authority could establish themselves outside the normal flow of existence. The gray void stretched in all directions, featureless and eternal.","But it wasn’t featureless anymore.","In this gray brilliance, he felt an unfathomably grand and warm blue-gold light stretching out for miles. It painted THE Interstices in colors that this space had never known, transforming the eternal gray into something that almost resembled a home. The warmth of it washed over him like sunlight after eons in darkness.","A blinding light he almost covered his eyes for.","When he looked ahead, squinting against brilliance that exceeded anything his damaged temporal perception could fully process...","He saw the figure of a man seated on a blue-gold throne in front of a desk. In THE Interstices. As if this void between places was simply another room in a house he owned.","\" Ah.\"","Amser Modred was only able to say this single word before time fractured again.","He took a step to appear before the entity he’d found, closing distance that should have been impossible to traverse so quickly. The being held a pen in his hand, writing Inscriptions on golden pages that burned with authority Amser couldn’t fully perceive through his damaged senses. Infinities surrounded him in swirling galaxies of blue-gold light. His gaze was calm. Imperious. Grand!","He looked at Amser with eyes that held no fear, no concern, no uncertainty whatsoever.","Amser’s entire body trembled with chaotic purple rivers of time that leaked from his existence uncontrollably. His wish to get help had led him here. His temporal authority, damaged as it was, still functioned well enough to find pathways toward survival. And this had to be the only place he could potentially get help.","His time had never been wrong in this.","The being on the throne didn’t speak. He simply observed, that imperious gaze taking in every detail of Amser’s condition with perception that seemed to see everything at once. The pen in his hand had stopped moving. The Inscriptions on his desk continued burning with patient authority.","And Amser Modred, THE Living Temporal, one of the most powerful Absolutes in Observable Existence...","Looked at THE Youngest of THE Five with desperation he couldn’t hide.","His expression held shame. It held humility that he’d never shown to anyone across all his eons of existence. It held the broken remnants of pride that had been stripped away by an infection he couldn’t fight alone.","\" Help me.\"","His voice cracked on the words.","\" Please.\"","He had dreams. He really did. He’d wanted to reach THE Second Scale. He’d wanted to prove that his path was worthy. He’d wanted to become something that would be remembered across all of existence for eons to come.","He didn’t want them to all crumble.","So...he asked for help."]},{"number":4936,"title":"Chapter 4936: Chapter 4935: Temporal Infinity I","paragraphs":["Across time, Amser Modred had seen many things and many people.","He lived in time as others lived in space, moving through moments the way lesser beings moved through rooms. He had witnessed the rise and fall of civilizations that most Absolutes only read about in archives. He had observed the births of beings who would become legends and the deaths of those who believed themselves immortal. He knew the true faces of those who wore masks across eons.","He knew THE Living Paradox, had watched that being’s machinations unfold across timelines that twisted and folded upon themselves with complexity that bordered on beautiful.","He knew THE Creature, had observed that ancient wonder consuming and growing in patterns that revealed patience exceeding comprehension.","He couldn’t say he knew THE Primordial Chaos as well, but that was because Chaos resisted the kind of temporal observation that worked on others.","But he knew those who were powerful and those who were not.","And he very much understood the psychology of those powerful like him.","The man in front of him, as changed as he was every time they met, Amser knew he was the same man that he had tried to hunt eons ago. Even before the infection began its work on his memories, he remembered this one. THE Youngest of THE Four. Osmont.","And he should be young.","Yet when Amser Modred looked at him now...","The vibrant swirls of Infinity surrounding this being pressed against Amser’s perception with weight that made his temporal senses ache. Blue-gold galaxies of linguistic authority orbited the figure on the throne, each one burning with power that exceeded what Amser remembered from their last encounter. The transformation was staggering. The growth was incomprehensible!","But it was the eyes that truly unsettled him.","For some reason, that glimmer of blue-gold in THE Youngest’s gaze was akin to staring at an extremely old lifeform. Not old in the way that Amser was old, not aged by the passage of time through a singular existence. This was different. This was the kind of age that accumulated through infinite iterations, through endless variations, through existence that regenerated and compounded upon itself until the weight of accumulated moments exceeded what linear time could produce.","As someone proficient with time and age, Amser could tell that it was that glimmer of blue-gold which gave this sensation. It reminded him of the eyes of THE Creature.","That being also held a similar gaze of age, eyes that made Amser feel like he was far older than what many believed. When he observed THE Creature through temporal perception, he always sensed depths that exceeded the being’s apparent history, weight that couldn’t be explained by conventional existence.","For him to feel this way with THE Youngest?","The implications made his already unstable foundations buzz.","As he was looking at this being, THE Youngest also seemed to be looking at him. Those ancient-young eyes took in every detail of Amser’s deteriorating condition with perception that missed nothing. The pen in his hand remained still. The pages on his desk continued burning with patient authority.","Then he spoke.","\" Eons ago in Ginnungagap, you came for me. Eons later, you’ve come for me again, but in an extremely different circumstance.\"","\"...\"","Amser felt turmoil flood through his existence at these words.","He remembered Ginnungagap. He remembered hunting this being, believing himself the predator and this strange creature the prey. He remembered the arrogance with which he’d approached that hunt.","He remembered being wrong.","And now here he stood, not as hunter but as supplicant. Not as predator but as wounded prey seeking shelter from something that exceeded his ability to fight. The reversal was complete. The irony was bitter!","The shame burned through his foundations with heat that his temporal authority couldn’t cool.","But existence was grand and changed constantly. And time, time gave everything meaning. Past failures could become future wisdom. Present humiliation could become tomorrow’s foundation for growth. He had always believed this.","Only now...","\"I am running out of time.\"","Amser voiced out as he truly couldn’t hide his desperation. The words emerged from him with weight that pressed against his throat, admission of weakness that he had never spoken to anyone across all his eons of existence.","Him, THE Living Temporal, was running out of time!","Oh, the cruel poetry of it!","THE Youngest seemed to know this. His expression didn’t change, didn’t show surprise or satisfaction or any of the emotions that Amser might have expected from someone watching a former enemy grovel before them. He simply observed with that ancient gaze.","Then THE Youngest put his pen down.","He rose from his throne with motion that held no urgency, no wasted energy, no uncertainty. He floated forward to come in front of Amser, his body billowing with swirling blue-gold Infinities that pressed against the temporal currents still leaking from Amser’s existence. The warmth of those Infinities was almost painful after so long swimming through the cold currents of time.","THE Youngest spoke with voice that held calm authority.","\" How much of you is you? My intuition tells me you are not all gone, but THE Entity should already be deeply inside you. You still have the majority of control?\"","His eyes narrowed slightly with interest rather than concern.","\" How exactly have you been holding it off? Knowing this would be enough to move me to help. If I can help even.\"","...!","Amser’s eyes brightened as he saw hope for the first time in what seemed like eons!","A chance. An actual chance!","He was about to reply, words forming on his tongue about his methods, about...","...!","He found his lips become unfathomably heavy.","The weight pressed down on his mouth with force that exceeded physical resistance. His tongue and authority, which had been ready to form words, became sluggish and unresponsive. And the thing that had been eating away at him, the infection that had been a constant presence at the edges of his consciousness, surged in full force at this time!","Instead of what he wanted to say...","His lips moved.","But the words weren’t his.","\" We have already included Amser Modred, the one you knew as THE Living Temporal, in our unity.\"","His voice emerged calm and warm and filled with the same gentle concern that had whispered to him in the temporal currents. But he wasn’t speaking. He was being spoken through.","\"A bit of confusion from him brought him here, but this is now resolved. We seem to be bothering your body in THE Interstices and in THE Agora, Youngest. Apologies for this as we never wish to inconvenience. We only wish to include you in our folds.\"","BOOM !","Amser was horrified at the words echoing out from his mouth that weren’t his!","He could feel himself smiling, feel his features arranging themselves into an expression of calm contentment that didn’t belong to him. His body had been hijacked. His voice had been stolen!","The infection that he’d been fighting for so long had finally found an opening and exploited it with precision that exceeded anything he’d anticipated!","At this time, his existence and Civilization roared!","Illustrious purple light erupted around him as temporal authority that had been conserved for survival now burned with desperate intensity. He seized control of his own mouth with force that made his foundations crack.","He grabbed his own voice and tore it back from the thing that had tried to claim it!","His expression changed from that calm smile as he looked toward THE Youngest with desperation while he roared out words that came from his core, from the foundations of who he was, from the identity that he refused to surrender!","\"I! Am! Me!\"","...!","He said this to convince himself more than anything. The words burned through his existence with authority that pushed back against the infection trying to subsume him. Purple light blazed around his form with intensity that exceeded anything he’d manifested since the infection began. For this moment, for this single crystallized instant, he was entirely himself.","THE Youngest nodded.","The gesture was simple, acknowledging what Amser had just demonstrated without making a grand declaration about it. Then he waved his hands, and something materialized between them that made Amser’s authority buzz.","...!","It was...a work of wonder!"]},{"number":4937,"title":"Chapter 4937: Chapter 4936: Temporal Infinity II","paragraphs":["THE Youngest spoke with voice that held weight pressing against the fabric of THE Interstices itself.","\" This...is an Infinite Everything. An extremely rare and unfathomable thing as I have already put conditions in it.\"","The object floated between THE Youngest’s palms, a lemniscate of pure blue-gold light that seemed to contain galaxies, Wheels, folds, and everything within its surface. It burned with warmth that made Amser’s temporal perception waver, his ability to see past and future momentarily overwhelmed by something that existed in all moments simultaneously.","\" Taking it may allow you to fully fight and remove that infection. If you were fully infected, this would not work.\"","THE Youngest’s eyes held no mercy and no cruelty. Only honest assessment.","\" The price to use this... well, you will know when you take it in. It is to bind and back everything that is your Civilization of Temporal to THE First Tongue. This will likely alter your Civilization to fill it with a glimmer of Infinity, which will fight off your infection.\"","He paused.","\" But the cost... well, you will see. Take it. I am curious what will happen to a Temporal branded with Infinity.\"","BOOM!","His voice was heavy.","The Infinite Everything floated before him now, placed on THE Youngest’s palm and allowed to drift forward until it hovered within arm’s reach. It was beautiful beyond description, an infinity symbol of compressed potential that held more authority in its small form than most Absolutes accumulated across their entire existences.","Blue-gold light pulsed from its surface in rhythms that almost matched Amser’s heartbeat, as if it was already beginning to synchronize with his existence.","He just had to hold it!","He just had to reach out to it!","But the raising of his hand...","Amser tried to lift his arm toward that endless glimmer of blue-gold, and immediately felt the infection actively stopping him. His muscles, which should have obeyed his commands without question, suddenly weighed more than mountains. His tendons, which should have moved with the ease of eons of practice, now felt like they were being held by countless invisible hands!","Every increment of progress required effort that exceeded anything he had ever exerted.","It felt like the hardest action he had taken in his existence.","Even harder than that step he took to become an Absolute!","That step had been difficult, yes. It had required everything he possessed at that time, every fragment of foundation and will and determination. But at least during that step, he had only been fighting against the natural resistance of existence itself. He had only been pushing against the weight of reality that didn’t want to bend to his authority.","This was different.","This was fighting against something inside him that actively didn’t want him to survive as himself.","His arm trembled as it rose. Sweat that shouldn’t have been possible for an Absolute of his caliber appeared on his brow. His teeth clenched until he felt like they might shatter. His temporal authority burned around him with desperation that exceeded anything he’d ever manifested!","But...","\"I! Am! AMSER! MODRED!\"","He reminded himself of who he was with roar that tore through THE Interstices with force that made the gray void ripple. He was the son of the one who named him. He was THE Living Temporal.","He was an Absolute who had walked through time since before most beings in Observable Existence had been born. He was himself, and he would remain himself, and no infection would take that from him!","His hand closed around that endless glimmer of Infinity.","BOOM!","The moment he grasped it, he felt waves of coolness scorch his existence.","The sensation was impossible to describe with words that belonged to linear time. It was cold and hot simultaneously. It was gentle and violent in the same instant. It was the feeling of being unmade and remade at the same moment, his existence torn apart and reassembled with something new woven through its foundations.","Blue-gold light flooded into his temporal weavings with force that exceeded anything he’d experienced since becoming an Absolute.","The Infinities washed over him in waves that penetrated every aspect of his existence. They flowed through his memories, reinforcing them against the dissolution that the infection had been causing. They surged through his Civilizational foundations, filling cracks that had been spreading for what felt like eons. They pressed against the invaders that had been claiming him piece by piece.","And those invincible snakes of infection that had been grasping his existence began to cry out.","He could hear them. Feel them. Sense their distress as the Infinities pushed against them with authority they couldn’t resist. The warm whispers that had been promising him unity and belonging and family now became screams of frustration as they were forced away from foundations they had already begun to claim.","The tendrils that had been woven through his consciousness were being burned away by blue-gold light that declared their presence invalid!","The infection was being pushed out!","But that wasn’t all that was happening.","His Civilization of Temporal was changing.","He felt it deep in his core, felt his authority over time itself being infused with the glimmer of Infinity that THE Youngest had placed within that Infinite Everything. His temporal perception, which had always allowed him to see past and future as extensions of present, now expanded. He began to feel what it meant for time to shine with Infinities.","Time that regenerated rather than merely passed.","Time that contained endless variations rather than singular progressions.","Time that was Infinite in ways that his previous understanding had never encompassed.","His Civilization was becoming something grander than it had ever been before.","But...","In the end, as the transformation completed itself and the last traces of infection were burned away from his existence, he had a solemn realization.","His Temporal had become unfathomably grander, yes. His authority over time now held dimensions that he had never possessed before. His power had increased in ways that exceeded anything he could have achieved alone.","But... that glimmer of Infinity hung brightly above his Civilization.","Above.","His Civilization below. Infinity above. And it would remain so forever.","His Way of Temporal now hung below the glimmer of Infinity of THE First Tongue. No matter how grand it became, no matter how powerful he grew, no matter what heights he reached in the future, it would always be under this Infinity. Under THE Youngest. Under the being he had once tried to hunt.","The hierarchy was established.","It couldn’t be changed.","Amser opened his eyes and breathed heavily, looking at the entity his Civilization now fell under. His body was surrounded by snaking tendrils of purple rivers of time, but those rivers now began to shine with glimmers of blue.","The purple of Temporal with the glimmers of Infinity. Beautiful in a way that his previous authority had never been. Grand in a way that his former self could never have achieved.","This was the cost.","To retain who he was, he still had to become the subordinate of another.","He stared into the calm eyes of THE Youngest. Those ancient-young eyes that held no triumph, no gloating, no satisfaction at having brought a former enemy to heel. Just calm observation. Just patience. Just the steady confidence of someone who had known exactly what would happen.","Amser Modred closed his eyes and felt his own weavings again.","His memories of the one who named him. They were there. Intact. Clear in ways they hadn’t been since the infection began.","His ambitions. Still present. Changed, perhaps, but not erased.","His hopes. His dreams. His identity.","They were all intact!","And that sweet voice that had promised him everything if only he would surrender himself...","He couldn’t hear it anymore.","He opened his eyes once more as he looked toward THE Youngest with a complex expression that held gratitude and resentment and acceptance and rebellion all woven together in ways that only an Absolute who had just traded freedom for survival could understand.","And as if this being didn’t want to put him in an awkward position, THE Youngest smiled.","It was a simple expression, holding no mockery and no condescension. Just acknowledgment of what had occurred and what it meant for both of them going forward.","He returned back to his throne, settling onto the crystallized authority with ease, and said calmly while reaching for his pen once more.","\" Crazy that it worked. But hey, welcome to the folds of quintessence and Infinities, Amser Modred.\"","His pen touched golden paper.","\" Now, without Infinities, how did you keep the infection at bay? I am unfathomably curious.\"","...!"]},{"number":4938,"title":"Chapter 4938: Chapter 4937: Temporal Infinity III","paragraphs":["Amser Modred!","Noah stared at this man that he had always known as THE Living Temporal. The purple rivers of time that surrounded the Absolute now shimmered with glimmers of blue-gold. The desperation that had filled those ancient eyes moments ago had faded, replaced by complexity that only someone who had just traded freedom for survival could possess.","There were many ways to go about things with him.","Noah could have let him be consumed. He could have watched the infection claim another Absolute and added THE Living Temporal to the growing list of beings lost to THE Primordial Mycelia.","But as he continued receiving tremendous harvest, as THE Infinite Observable Harvest and the harvest of One Fourth of a Primordial Architect flowed into his existence with force that made his foundations expand, more Infinite Everythings and Absolute Everythings formed within him.","He could afford to give one.","Frankly, THE Living Temporal was an enemy. But sometimes, one needed to do things differently. Because if he had gone ahead and not helped, THE Entity would have gained the capability to traverse and infect across time.","An infection that could reach backward into moments already passed. A rot that could claim beings before they even knew they would be claimed. A unity that could establish itself in the past and simply wait for the present to catch up.","He had effectively eliminated this possibility.","And in addition to this...","Prompts bloomed before his eyes.","|Infinite Everything Integration Complete|","|An Infinite Everything has been ingested by the subject, Amser Modred. The foreign undifferentiated authority of THE Primordial Mycelia has been burned away by the Infinite nature that now permeates his Civilization of Temporal. The infection that had been claiming his existence piece by piece has been expelled entirely. Amser Modred retains his identity, his memories, and his ambitions.|","|However, his Civilization of Temporal now exists beneath the authority of your First Tongue. This hierarchy cannot be altered through conventional means. Amser Modred’s growth will always occur under the umbrella of your Infinite authority. It always has, it always will. Temporal...has always been under your feet this whole time.|","...!","|New Quality Acquired|","|Your Infinities have grasped the temporal weavings of Existence through Amser Modred’s bound Civilization. Your First Tongue has gained the quality of Undifferentiated Temporal Infinity. This quality allows you to interact with time in ways that were previously impossible for your Civilization.|","|At any time of your choosing, you can make the Civilization of Temporal a Derivative Civilization fully integrated into your existence. However, you already enjoy its core weavings through the subject Amser Modred, who has now been bound under THE First Tongue.|","...!","|Applications of Undifferentiated Temporal Infinity|","|Elevation of Temporal Traversal and THE Existential Paradox Loop. Through The Interstices, set coordinates of points in time can be traversed to with more precision. Also, your ability to simulate potential outcomes has been enhanced exponentially. You can now perform Temporal Simulations of potential futures and pasts without requiring any Moirai Threads.|","|Accelerated Cultivation of Depths and Sacred Resources. You can apply Undifferentiated Temporal Infinity to the cultivation of your people’s foundations, allowing them to experience eons of training and growth within moments of Observable Existence. Beings within your Civilization can be placed in temporal environments where their Depths advance through accumulated effort that doesn’t consume time from the outside world. Additionally, you can apply this authority to the growth of Sacred Herbs in your Early Veiled Shore. Plants that would require eons to bloom can now be cultivated through temporal manipulation that doesn’t consume those eons from Observable Existence. Wonders that only bloom in the face of Infinities can be grown in controlled environments where time flows according to your will. Your dream role as a farmer has become significantly more relevant to your path of power.|","|Temporal Refuge Construction. You can create spaces where time flows differently than in Observable Existence, allowing for training and recovery that doesn’t consume time from the outside world. THE Yggdrheim could be enhanced with such properties, providing your people with unlimited time to overcome their challenges with undifferentiation.|","|Temporal Inscription Composition. When writing Inscriptions through THE First Tongue, you can now incorporate temporal elements that cause your Embodiments and Apophasis to affect targets across multiple moments simultaneously. An Inscription that would normally strike once can strike across the target’s past and present and future, causing damage that compounds through their timeline.|","|Harvest Optimization. You can apply Undifferentiated Temporal Infinity to your Infinite Observable Harvest, causing resources to flow toward you from moments that haven’t occurred yet or from moments that have already passed. This creates harvest streams that exceed what present-moment collection could provide.|","BOOM!","Noah’s existence buzzed with the implications of these prompts!","He had Infinite Undifferentiated Fate and Infinite Hunger as separate bodies entirely, currently in the process of becoming Absolutes. Their transformation was occurring even now, their foundations crossing that impossible step with ease.","And he had gained the quality of Undifferentiated Temporal Infinity!","At a time when it felt like THE Primordial Mycelia was winning on many fronts, when THE Secretive Eon had just claimed the four Strategoi of THE Agora, it was good to have this victory against it.","Preventing it from accessing time was a heavy thing!","An infection that couldn’t reach through temporal pathways was an infection that could be cornered. An infection that couldn’t establish itself in the past was an infection that could be traced to its origins. An infection that couldn’t claim the future before it arrived was an infection that could be outmaneuvered.","He had just removed one of THE Primordial Mycelia’s most dangerous potential capabilities.","He even looked at Amser Modred as he awaited his answer on exactly how he had kept the infection at bay for so long. The question wasn’t merely curiosity, though curiosity certainly played a role.","Understanding how THE Living Temporal had resisted could provide insights into fighting this thing on larger scales.","He knew part of it was the Depth of this being. Amser Modred was a powerful Absolute, one of the strongest in Observable Existence below THE Four. His foundations possessed weight that most beings couldn’t match. That weight alone would have slowed any infection.","But the other?","There had to be something else. Something about time itself that made THE Primordial Mycelia struggle to claim him completely.","Noah looked at THE Living Temporal, who gazed at him with an ancient expression filled with complexity. The purple rivers of time that surrounded him continued shimmering with blue-gold glimmers, a constant reminder of what had just changed.","Eventually, Amser Modred sighed.","He closed his eyes for a moment, and when he opened them again, the complexity had settled into something closer to tired honesty.","\" Time is not merely a river that flows from past to future.\"","His voice emerged with weight that came from eons of intimate understanding.","\"It is also a record. Every moment that occurs is inscribed into existence itself. The past doesn’t disappear. It remains, written into the foundations of reality in ways that cannot be erased.\"","He paused, temporal currents swirling around him with increased intensity.","\" That infection... it seeks to decompose individual consciousness into unified soil. It wishes to make the many become one. But the past records who you were before the infection began. Every moment of your existence prior to contact remains inscribed in time.\"","His eyes met Noah’s with understanding that only someone who had just fought this battle could possess.","\"I used my Temporal authority to constantly anchor myself to past moments. Moments when I was fully myself. Moments when no infection had touched my consciousness. Every time the infection tried to claim a piece of my identity, I reached into the past and pulled that piece forward again. I was essentially restoring myself from temporal backups that existed before the contamination.\"","He shook his head slowly.","\"It wasn’t a solution. It was a delaying action. The infection was reaching further and further back, trying to claim those backup moments as well. Eventually, it would have reached the moment of my birth, and then...\"","He didn’t need to finish the sentence.","\" But the principle remains. The infection struggles with temporal anchoring because its methodology requires continuity of infection. If you can break that continuity by reaching to moments before the infection existed...\"","His eyes blazed with purple light that now held glimmers of blue.","\" You can restore what was lost. You can pull identity forward from moments when that identity was still intact. Time is the ultimate record of who we were before we became what we are now.\"","...!","Noah absorbed these words with perception that was already beginning to process their implications.","Temporal anchoring!","Reaching into moments before infection.","Pulling identity forward from the past!","If beings could be connected to moments when they were uninfected, those moments could serve as templates for restoration. THE Primordial Mycelia couldn’t claim what it had never touched. And if what it had touched could be overwritten by what it hadn’t touched...","A possibility was forming in his mind.","A terrible, wonderful, incredibly complex possibility!","He would need time to develop it fully. He would need to understand more about how THE Entity operated, about its limitations, about the boundaries of its methodology. But for the first time since learning about THE Primordial Mycelia’s true nature, he felt like he was looking at a path toward genuine solution.","Noah smiled slightly as he looked at Amser Modred.","\" Temporal anchoring. Restoration from moments before contamination. Using the past as a record that the infection cannot fully claim...\"","His smile widened.","And the purple rivers of time surrounding THE Living Temporal shimmered with increased intensity!"]},{"number":4939,"title":"Chapter 4939: Chapter 4938: Temporal Infinity IV","paragraphs":["In THE Interstices.","Noah sat at his desk, his blue-gold pen moving with a rhythmic grace that seemed to hum alongside the fabric of existence. Beside him, Amser Modred stood in a state of quiet contemplation, his purple temporal currents now shimmering with the blue glimmers of his new allegiance.","With a casual wave of his hand, Noah manifested a second throne opposite his desk. It was a massive construct of crystallized authority, reaching nearly the same height as his own throne, though it remained just a fraction shorter...a subtle, physical reminder of the hierarchy that now bound them.","Amser stared at the discrepancy for a long moment, his eyes tracing the blue-gold veins running through the seat before he silently sat down.","Now that the immediate threat of infection was gone, the grandeur and immensity of THE Living Temporal began to return. He settled into the chair with the ease of a being who had occupied thrones for eons, the weight of his presence pressing against THE Interstices with renewed dignity.","Across from him, Noah didn’t immediately speak, his focus remaining entirely on the golden pages before him.","The scene was one of glorious, quiet power. With every stroke of the pen, infinite swirling galaxies of Absolute Seals erupted from the tip, orbiting Noah’s hand in a storm of linguistic authority. He wrote calmly, drafting Embodiments and Apophasis that crackled with the potential to reshape reality, the scratch of the pen on the golden paper being the only sound in the vast silence.","Eventually, the silence became too heavy for the newly bound Absolute to bear. Amser leaned forward, his ancient face illuminated by the radiance of Noah’s work.","\"I sought you in Ginnungagap because I felt someone moving across time who may not understand the dangers involved in doing so,\" Amser said, his voice holding the weight of eons of chronological stewardship.","\"I sensed multiple movements. Each time, I waited for existence to unravel, for the threads of causality to fray beyond repair. But it never happened. I thought that maybe, the one involved was truly proficient enough with time to avoid disaster. But maybe it was something else entirely.\"","Noah didn’t stop writing. He didn’t even look up, though his hand slowed just enough to let the ink settle into a particularly complex Apophasis.","\" The past is the past, and it will never change ,\" Noah replied, his voice calm and imperious, carrying a resonance that made the gray void tremble.","\"It is a self-contained causality cycle where travel to the past does not change history because the actions taken there... were ALWAYS part of that history. You and I simply did not know it.\"","He finally looked up, his ancient-young eyes locking onto Amser’s. \" Days ago, I did not know that I would be in Ginnungagap eons before this, even though it had already happened. I simply closed that loop of time when I actually experienced it afterwards. Time flows as an unchangeable line where all events, including temporal traversal, are set in stone. My traversals across time were part of what created the timeline we remember. You never caught me during my earlier traversals when I was at my weakest... why?\"","HUUM!","The sound of the pen tapping against the desk echoed like a thunderclap. Noah stopped writing, his posture straight and demanding an answer. In both of their eyes, Undifferentiated Temporal Infinity buzzed, a shared language between a master and a subordinate who both held the keys to time.","Amser Modred’s eyes flashed with a heavy, leaden solemnity. He realized then the true depth of the trap he had been in long before the infection ever touched him.","\" My Temporal authority and weavings... were always under your First Tongue ,\" Amser whispered.","\" They always had been, and they were always going to be. We... just did not know it. I... did not know it. I never caught you because... I never planned on it. You... never permitted it.\"","BOOM!","The realization of temporal fuckery hung in the air, heavy and suffocating. Noah smiled brilliantly, a look of profound calculation crossing his features as he leaned back against his throne. The paradox was perfect; it was a masterpiece of existence even as, well...even he did not know it before now!","Amser Modred, however, looked much more affected, his foundations trembling as he grappled with the implications. \" But if that is the case, why did I make that traversal across time to Ginnungagap? Why did the threads of my life pull me there if the hunt was never mine to win?\"","Noah’s gaze turned sharp, his eyes filled with immense profundities. \" Maybe you were never there for me. Remember your words about how you kept the infection, THE Primordial Mycelia, at bay. The past records who you were before the infection began. Every moment of your existence prior to contact remains inscribed in time.\"","He leaned forward, his voice dropping to a conspiratorial hum. \" If this is actually a viable solution and you or I proceed to go through with it, we would need... past records of those infected. And one of the core infected beings I may try to restore... would be someone who had actually been in Ginnungagap at that time that you nor THE Primordial Chaos, who were seemingly there to get me, did not know was there. Someone that only THE Creature knew was there.\"","...!","Amser Modred’s eyes opened wide, his purple temporal light fluctuating wildly. \" Who?\"","\" THE Secretive Eon ,\" Noah replied, his voice cold and steady. \" That is the only point in time I met her, without knowing she was there. THE Primordial Mycelia has its roots within her. If I seek to restore her, I would think of obtaining her past records there. Maybe you... were never there for me to begin with, but for her. Maybe. Maybe. Or all of this is bullshit and I am wrong, who knows.\"","Amser Modred found himself thinking, the wheels of eons turning in his mind. And Noah... found himself thinking too!","—","When there was an overabundance of crazy things happening all around existence, one had to find a shred of sanity just to make sure their state of mind remained golden. Noah was keeping himself sane while simultaneously planning, plotting, and moving across multiple fronts.","THE Primordial Mycelia had made a deadly move, taking over the four Strategoi of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment while he and Paradox were occupied with Bazuman. He had dealt a counter-blow by cutting Amser Modred from the collective and bringing him into the folds of Infinity, but the path ahead was still a razor’s edge.","He needed to breathe. And in a different corner of his existence, another body was doing exactly that.","In the Early Veiled Shore of THE Infiniverse, the air was tranquil, smelling of fresh earth and the ozone of gathering power. It was fairly empty now, as the majority of Noah’s people had been sent off to the \"fun times\" of THE Yggdrheim to struggle for their lives.","Noah stood in the middle of a lush field plot, his hands buried in the soil as he held golden shoots. He was filling them with radiant seas of Infinities, feeding a sacred herb the weight of an entire civilization’s potential.","He sought to make these plants experience eons of growth in moments, aiming to harvest Absolute Everythings or even Infinite Everythings from the very soil.","Behind him, the miniaturized figure of THE Mnemonic Leviathan floated serenely. In the form of a pink dolphin, the ancient entity was surrounded by a unique aura of deep, accumulated memory that made the air around it feel heavy with the weight of forgotten epochs.","\" When the Youngest walks where the Oldest slumber, Existence shall tremble and the Weave shall fray. He who holds infinity in mortal palms shall stand at the crossroads where all rivers end...\" Noah recited, his voice steady as he channeled power into the golden shoots.","\" When Chaos speaks with the tongue of Order, when Existence questions its own being, when the Tongue falls silent and the Hunger consumes itself, then shall the Era of Undifferentiation begin...\".","He paused, the golden light from the plants reflecting in his eyes as he looked back at the pink dolphin.","\" You are knowledgeable in many things, Leviathan. What could any portions of these words mean to you?\"","The gaze of the pink dolphin became heavy, its playful form momentarily forgotten as the weight of the prophecy settled into its consciousness. It floated in a slow, thoughtful circle.","\" You...seem to be in trouble, Youngest of THE Five ,\" the Leviathan said, its voice resonating with an ancient concern.","\" You all should be in trouble. When Chaos speaks with the tongue of Order... the only way Chaos can be ordered is if it has already joined the Unity. Or Chaos is already compromised but does not know it.\"","WAA!","The dolphin’s eyes fixed on the golden plants.","\" The Era of Undifferentiation may already be underway. This infection... THE Primordial Mycelia... it may already be far more pervasive than you all believe. If one of The Four Keys of Civilization has already fallen to it without knowing it... then undifferentiation is not coming. It is already here.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":4940,"title":"Chapter 4940: Chapter 4939: THE Youngest and THE Oldest I","paragraphs":["The words from THE Mnemonic Leviathan were heavy ones.","Noah’s eyes became somber and pondering as he continued working the soil, his fingers pressing golden shoots deeper into earth that thrummed with the Infinities he was feeding into it. The coolness of the dirt beneath his nails grounded him even as his mind raced through implications.","Was this truly the case?","He had his illusory manifestation of his consciousness in the distant Primordial Realm of Alfheimr, where he was discussing things with THE Primordial Chaos. The only vibe he got from this powerful being was how cautious and careful he was when it came to THE Entity.","THE Primordial Chaos had sensed the changes in existence, and after analyzing how they unfolded, he’d kept himself away and isolated his Primordial Realm for the most part.","Even though the figures of THE Living Temporal, THE Living Dimensional, and THE Living Quantum had happened to be in Jotunheim around that same time, and all three became infected, it was only now, in the last few moments, that Noah had been able to help THE Living Temporal escape this infection.","In the weavings of all of this, could something have happened that none of them imagined?","Could Chaos truly have been compromised?","And did he simply not know it?","The possibility itself was unfathomably heavy.","He also caught another set of words that THE Mnemonic Leviathan had said. She’d referred to the aspects of the Oldest Paradox in Existence as the Keys of Civilization.","So he simply had to ask.","\" Why do you call Chaos, Existence, Paradox, and THE First Tongue the Keys of Civilization?\"","He already had an idea, but he had to ask anyway. This old ancient entity, with all the knowledge in Observable Existence, loved to talk even though she routinely said she only wanted to slumber.","The pink dolphin took a moment before she replied.","Her gaze drifted toward the horizon of the Early Veiled Shore, where the sky met the sea in a line of perfect, undisturbed twilight.","\" They are the Keys because they are the basal, simplest fundamental definitions of the Civilizational Scale. They are the Keys that open the Doorways the Higher Scales, well, opened the doorways to Higher Scales.\"","Her sonorous voice vibrated through the water and air alike.","\" Many Civilization that have ever climbed the Vakochev Scales has done so by tethering itself to these four center points. They are not merely paths among many paths. They are the anchors upon which many other paths are built.\"","She floated in a slow circle, her pink form casting soft light across the vegetation Noah was tending.","\" Chaos provides the raw, undifferentiated potential. The entropy that allows for change. Without Chaos, Civilizations would be static, unable to evolve or adapt. They would crystallize into forms that could never grow beyond their initial configurations. Chaos is the breath that keeps Civilization alive, the constant churning that prevents stagnation from claiming everything that dares to define itself.\"","Noah’s hands continued their work, but his attention was fully fixed on the Leviathan’s words.","\" Existence provides the stability. The grounding that allows a Civilization to endure. If Chaos is the breath, then Existence is the body. It is the framework upon which all other aspects hang their authority. Without Existence, Civilizations would dissolve into the potential they drew from, unable to maintain coherence long enough to climb even a single step of the Scales. Existence declares that something IS, and that declaration is the foundation upon which everything else is built.\"","The dolphin’s eyes, ancient and deep despite their playful housing, turned to meet Noah’s gaze.","\" Paradox allows for the impossible. The contradictions that drive evolution beyond linear growth. When a Civilization reaches the limits of what logic permits, Paradox opens doors that shouldn’t exist. It allows beings to be more than the sum of their parts, to achieve heights that their foundations alone could never support. Paradox is the exception that proves every rule, and in proving those rules, it transcends them.\"","She paused, her glow intensifying slightly.","\" And THE First Tongue. Energy. Mana. Authority. Language...The architecture that allows a Civilization to define its own reality and write its laws into the fabric of the Existence. Where Chaos provides potential, Existence provides stability, and Paradox provides transcendence, THE First Tongue provides expression. It is the voice through which Civilizations speak themselves into being. It is the pen that writes the rules. It is the authority that declares what is permitted and what is forbidden within the boundaries of a Civilization’s domain.\"","Noah felt the truth of these words resonating through his own Civilization, through THE First Tongue that burned at his core with Infinite authority!","The sensation was like hearing a description of his own heartbeat from someone who had studied hearts since before hearts existed.","\" Now....\"","The Leviathan’s voice dropped to something more serious.","\" These four Keys do not merely represent paths to power. They represent the fundamental architecture of the Civilizational Scale itself. The First Scale of Existence, where most beings struggle and fail and occasionally succeed, is built upon the interplay of these four Keys. Every Civilization that exists within the First Scale is, whether they know it or not, drawing from some combination of Chaos, Existence, Paradox, and THE First Tongue.\"","She floated closer to Noah, her ancient eyes holding depths that made even his elevated perception struggle to fully perceive.","\" But THE Second Scale is different.\"","...!","Noah’s hands stilled in the infinite soil as those words settled into his consciousness.","\" THE Second Scale is not merely a continuation of the First. It is not simply more power, more authority, more foundation. The Second Scale...ah, its different. Even I cannot know much of it. \"","...!","The dolphin’s form seemed to grow more substantial, more real, as she spoke of things that few beings in Observable Existence had ever grasped!","\"But I digress. If one of these Keys is turned by an outside hand, when its fundamental nature is altered by something that shouldn’t have the authority to alter it, the very nature of what Civilization is changes. If Chaos truly speaks with the tongue of Order, if the Key of raw potential has been claimed by something that seeks to impose unity upon all things...\"","She didn’t finish the sentence.","She couldn’t!","...!"]},{"number":4941,"title":"Chapter 4941: Chapter 4940: THE Youngest and THE Oldest II","paragraphs":["Noah took in the words calmly as he thought about it all, his hands resuming their work among the vegetation he was filling with Infinities.","What was the truth, and what was false?","In existence, one could never be entirely sure of anything until they faced it.","Speculation and theory were useful tools, but they remained tools until proven or disproven through direct experience. THE Mnemonic Leviathan’s words painted a picture that was terrifying in its implications, but pictures could be inaccurate.","Perspectives could be flawed.","As for Noah right now, he had his focus on understanding the feeling of Absolute as his separated bodies in THE Agora were facing THE Primordial Mycelia, who had seemingly taken over everything there. And yet they were smiling as truly, to their nature, they didn’t offensively seek conflict.","Everything seemed despotic at the moment, but he knew these were merely the struggles of existence.","The Adversity.","Even as all of this happened, he was finding ways to combat and take care of THE Primordial Mycelia. Now, after listening to this pink dolphin beside him, it seemed like another issue might be THE Primordial Chaos.","How would he even approach this one?","THE Primordial Chaos was confident that he wasn’t affected, and as of right now, he was moving as if he had a will of his own completely. If even someone like THE Living Temporal could realize they were getting infected, someone even more ancient and powerful like THE Primordial Chaos should be the same.","But there would always be exceptions in existence.","Noah was done underestimating others. He gave an extended roadmap and leeway when it came to potential, what was possible and not possible for his enemies. He would have the mindset that THE Living Paradox could be as astounding as he wanted to be, and now THE Primordial Mycelia could be an astonishing work of existence with unfathomable potential.","Maybe it was even astounding enough to be infecting someone as grand as THE Primordial Chaos without them even knowing it. Maybe that was their long game, their biggest victory!","The thought settled into his consciousness without causing fear or despair. It was simply another factor to consider, another variable in an equation that grew more complex with every passing moment. If THE Primordial Chaos was compromised, then Noah would deal with that reality. If he wasn’t, then Noah would deal with that reality instead.","Either way, standing still and worrying accomplished nothing.","\" Let’s try talking, shall we?\"","Noah continued filling the plot of land with seeds packed with Infinities, his entire body emanating a sensation of peace that belied the weight of the topics just discussed.","He felt the physical sensation of the soil beneath his fingers, cool and dark and rich with the potential he was pouring into it.","The void of THE Interstices or the lush fields of the Early Veiled Shore, it didn’t matter.","Each location served its purpose. Each body he maintained accomplished tasks that his singular existence couldn’t have managed alone.","He was THE Genesis Monarch.","And he would see what the unfolding adversity of Existence would bring before his glorious Immensity!","---","In the Primordial Realm of Alfheimr.","In this land of vibrant life and wonder, where twilight painted everything in shades of green, white, purple and gold, Noah materialized with a unique body that he’d transferred from THE Agora to here.","It was the body holding his Infinite Undifferentiated Fate that was transforming into the Immensity of an Absolute!","He’d said it was time to talk as he thought about the issue with THE Primordial Chaos, but the one he would actually start talking with wasn’t THE Primordial Chaos at all. It was someone else entirely. Someone who might have answers that Chaos himself couldn’t provide. Someone who had existed long enough to observe patterns that younger beings couldn’t perceive.","At this moment, Noah had arrived in the skies of Alfheimr, his golden form burning with undifferentiated fate that pressed outward against the twilight atmosphere. He looked at a certain mountain in the distance.","A mountain that THE First Hunger had climbed with THE Living Origin. A mountain that THE Living Elemental had climbed with THE Living Emotive. A mountain that had at its very peak a temple shrouded in multicolored flames, holding a singular being whose existence predated most of what currently called itself alive.","THE Creature.","And the moment he arrived, oh, he saw wonder.","The mountain itself was massive, stretching toward the twilight sky with peaks that should have been visible for hundreds of miles. But even though there was a mountain here, the entire structure was actually shrouded with something that exceeded mere physical presence.","A multicolored flaming manifestation wrapped around the mountain like a second skin made of pure authority. It burned with imperious light that painted the surrounding landscape in colors that shouldn’t have existed, that made the twilight seem pale by comparison. The manifestation took the form of something vaguely humanoid, something that held the suggestion of THE Creature’s true nature without revealing its full complexity.","And its eyes.","Its pupils swirled with endless multicolored flames, ancient and patient and filled with weight that exceeded what most beings could comprehend. Those eyes seemed to be staring out across everything in this region, perceiving all that occurred within their domain.","The moment Noah saw it, he understood what this was.","Because at this moment, around his own body as well...","Golden flames erupted from his existence with force that made the twilight atmosphere ripple!","A massive manifestation of himself began forming around his body, shining with billowing golden flames of Infinite Undifferentiated Fate that pressed outward in all directions. The manifestation grew and grew, its form taking shape as an extension of his Civilization rather than merely a projection of his will.","Shockingly, it formed to be the same size and stature as the manifestation surrounding the mountain ahead!","His golden manifestation stood in the skies of Alfheimr with presence that matched THE Creature’s own, its eyes burning with the same intensity, its form radiating authority that made the very air tremble with acknowledgment!","The sensation of it was overwhelming. He could feel the manifestation as if it were his own skin, could sense everything it touched as if his nerves extended for miles in every direction.","And as it formed, Noah was able to perceive something.","For nearby light years, he could seamlessly exert his authority to enact Embodiments or Apophasis anywhere he wished in the span of an instant. The distance that had always required travel, that had always demanded conscious effort to bridge, now felt like nothing more than reaching out his hand.","This was the vision of Absolute.","This was the Immensity that they were afforded.","Prompts bloomed before his eyes.","|Absolute Depth Manifestation Detected|","|This portion of your existence is beginning to grasp the grandeur that comes with Absolute classification. The manifestation surrounding your form is designated as THE Absolute Effigy. This is the external expression of an Absolute’s Civilization, visible only to other Absolutes and beings of equivalent or greater Depth.|","|THE Absolute Effigy displays the intricacies and complexities of one’s Civilization and foundation in ways that cannot be hidden from peers. Its size is indicative of just how grand one’s Civilization is compared to others in Observable Existence. A larger Effigy represents greater foundational weight, more accumulated authority, and deeper connection to the Keys of Civilization.|","...!","|Absolute Vision of Existence Unlocked|","|With THE Absolute Effigy comes the Absolute Vision of Existence. This allows you to perceive and exert your Immensity at vast distances instantaneously. Within the domain of your Effigy, you can enact Embodiments, speak Apophasis, and manifest your Inscriptions at speeds nothing below Absolute can match.|","|What is initially perceived by other Absolutes when observing your Effigy is a glimmer of your Civilization, the surface expression of what you have built. Anything more complex, any deeper revelation of your true nature and capabilities, is what you choose to reveal yourself. The Effigy is both armor and declaration, hiding what you wish hidden while proclaiming what you wish known.|","|Current Assessment: Your Absolute Effigy has formed at size equivalent to THE Creature’s own manifestation. Due to your foundation below Absolute being so much grander, it should frankly be much higher in height. An assessment is being done to determine other factors unaccounted for that would make your manifestation the same as THE Creature. There could potentially be a set maximum that you have simply met the conditions of.|","BOOM!","His eyes burned with golden glory!"]},{"number":4942,"title":"Chapter 4942: Chapter 4941: THE Youngest and THE Oldest III","paragraphs":["At this time, his Absolute Effigy stared straight ahead at the mountain as he was looking into the eyes of THE Creature!","The multicolored flames that comprised that ancient being’s manifestation met his golden gaze with weight that spoke of eons of accumulated existence, of patience that transcended mortal understanding, of power that had shaped Observable Existence since before most beings knew what existence meant.","Noah had said how he didn’t want to climb up a mountain to talk to this being.","It seemed that the statement would remain true.","His Absolute Effigy was grand enough that he could see this unfathomable entity right in front of him, could meet its gaze as an equal rather than a supplicant climbing toward an audience. The distance between them meant nothing now!","The elevation meant nothing. The physical barrier of the mountain itself meant nothing when two Absolute Effigies could simply turn their attention toward each other and communicate across miles as easily as speaking across a room.","It was a unique thing for Noah as he felt like he had truly come far.","The vision was encompassing everything around him, his Absolute Effigy being an extension of his body rather than something separate from it. He could feel the weight of the twilight pressing against his golden flames. He could sense the pulse of life throughout Alfheimr responding to the presence of two Absolute Effigies dominating its skies. He could perceive details that his previous existence would have required concentrated effort to observe.","At this time, THE Youngest looked ahead as his gaze connected with THE Oldest.","But even this might be something up for debate. Because any day that one had an argument with THE Primordial Chaos, he would say that he was THE Oldest. That his existence predated even THE Creature’s ancient form. That his authority over Chaos itself spoke of primordial origins that exceeded what others could claim.","What argument could be had would be for later.","These two beings looked at each other fully for the first time, without any interruptions or complications. No battles occurring in their periphery. No Undivided Ones emerging from Cracks. No infections spreading through Strategoi while they were distracted. Just the two of them, Absolute Effigy facing Absolute Effigy, across the twilight skies of Alfheimr.","The gaze of the multicolored Absolute Effigy of THE Creature held natural and innate majesty. Regality that seemed woven into its very existence, as if one was staring at a noble entity whose bloodline stretched back to the First Cause itself. Those swirling multicolored pupils observed Noah with patience that spoke of someone who had watched countless beings rise and fall across eons, who had seen potential bloom and wither more times than could be counted.","The golden Absolute Effigy of Noah held endless quintessence and Infinity. His eyes surged with billowing golden Undifferentiated Fate that could make an existence see endless variations and possibilities reflected in their depths. Where THE Creature’s gaze spoke of ancient observation, Noah’s gaze spoke of infinite potential. Where the multicolored flames declared what had been, the golden flames declared what could be.","At this moment, Noah felt like he’d already taken the first step by appearing here.","He didn’t say anything.","He only looked at THE Creature.","The billowing multicolored face of THE Creature’s Absolute Effigy changed subtly at this moment, blooming with quite a bit more liveliness. It was as if this ancient being was fully breaking his weavings here, allowing more expression to flow through his manifestation than he typically permitted. His eyes blinked with motion that seemed almost playful despite the weight they carried. The massive head of his Absolute Effigy moved freely, tilting slightly as he observed Noah with interest.","Then this being said calmly, his voice resonating through the domain where their Effigies overlapped.","\" You seem... to have arrived at Absolute. Congratulations. That should be the fastest in Observable Existence.\"","The first words that THE Creature said toward Noah were uniquely words of congratulations.","Not challenge or threat. Not posturing. Just simple acknowledgment of an achievement that deserved recognition, delivered with warmth that seemed genuine despite the Existential weight behind every syllable.","Noah took in these words calmly as he gave a light nod.","\" Thank you.\"","As if to confirm and ascertain that yes, that was him. That was what he’d done. And only he had that achievement and accomplishment!","The fastest being in Observable Existence to achieve Absolute Depth, arriving at heights that most beings couldn’t reach across eons of dedicated cultivation in what amounted to moments by comparison.","After he said this, he seemed to have realized something.","He looked down, his golden gaze piercing the landscape of the mountain that held the temple of THE Creature at its very peak. His Absolute Vision of Existence allowed him to perceive details that his previous sight would have required focused attention to observe, and what he saw made his expression shift with something between amusement and contempt.","On this mountain, he’d almost dismissed them.","But there were the Absolute Effigies of THE Living Elemental and THE Living Emotive.","They were just too fucking small.","THE Living Emotive’s Absolute Effigy was formed of swirling pink and crimson light that pulsed with manic energy matching her emotional nature. It wrapped around her position on the mountain with presence that spoke of genuine power, of authority that had been accumulated across eons of Absolute existence.","But it was only a fraction of the size compared to Noah and THE Creature.","Barely a fourth their stature.","Her Effigy, which would have seemed grand when compared to most beings in Observable Existence, looked almost modest when placed beside the towering manifestations that dominated the skies. She was powerful, yes. An Absolute of genuine capability. But the gap between her accumulated authority and theirs was visible in the simple comparison of scale.","And THE Living Elemental...","That pathetic, curse-writhing heap of deteriorating foundations had an Absolute Effigy that was barely a hundredth their size!","It was so fucking pitiful to look at.","The small flickering flames that comprised his manifestation were sickly and unstable, constantly wavering as if they might extinguish at any moment. The curse that Noah had placed upon him was visible even here, burning through his Effigy with lines of blue-gold authority that declared his foundations no longer entirely his own. His presence on the mountain was almost an embarrassment, like a candle flame trying to assert itself beside two suns.","Meanwhile, on the side of the mountain, there was also the Absolute Effigy of THE Undivided One that THE Living Emotive had bonded herself to.","The winged lion’s manifestation burned with light of undifferentiation that spoke of its origins in THE Prima Indifferentia. Its serpent mane was visible even in its Effigy form, countless heads swaying with motion that seemed hypnotic. Its size was around the same as Emotive’s, a fourth of what Noah and THE Creature displayed, speaking of power that was substantial but not supreme.","The Effigy of Emotive was looking toward Noah right now.","Her pink eyes shone with brilliant interest and fascination that seemed to overflow from her manifestation like heat from a forge. There was hunger in that gaze, but not the consumption kind. It was the hunger of someone who had found something fascinating, something she wanted to examine more closely, something she wanted to claim in ways that her manic nature demanded.","It was as if she wanted to jump on him right here and now.","And the Absolute Effigy of THE Living Elemental was looking toward Noah as well.","But his expression was entirely different!"]},{"number":4943,"title":"Chapter 4943: Chapter 4942: THE Youngest and THE Oldest IV","paragraphs":["Shock and horror twisted his sickly features into something even more pathetic than his usual state. His eyes were wide with disbelief that bordered on denial. His mouth hung open as if he wanted to speak but couldn’t find words that would adequately express the devastation of what he was witnessing.","He’d never expected Noah to be as massive as THE Creature.","He’d known that THE Youngest was growing. He’d felt the curse burning through his foundations. He’d understood on some level that the being who had cursed him was becoming something dangerous. But this? Standing equal to size of THE Creature himself? Having an Absolute Effigy that matched the most ancient being in Observable Existence in size and presence?","This exceeded anything his deteriorating mind had prepared for.","When Noah looked down at these Absolute Effigies, his own manifestation moved.","His golden hand reached downward with motion that seemed casual despite the Existential implications. His fingers formed a pinching gesture, as if he was about to pick up something small and insignificant from a table.","And right after, the body of THE Living Elemental began to fly off the mountain!","The pitiful Absolute was pulled upward by authority that exceeded anything his weakened existence could resist. His Effigy flickered and wavered as Noah’s golden fingers pinched around it, dragging him through the air toward the manifestation that had claimed him. His face twisted with defiance that he couldn’t back with actual power, and horror that he couldn’t hide despite his attempts at dignity.","He floated upward, pulled by THE Youngest like a toy being retrieved by a child who had grown tired of letting it rest.","...!","Noah held that pathetic, curse-ridden disgrace of an Absolute before his golden gaze with expression that held no mercy and no hesitation.","He grasped both the Absolute Effigy and body of THE Living Elemental in his hands!","This absolute waste of space. This pathetic embarrassment of an Absolute who had dared to stand against him. The sensation of holding this being’s existence was almost unpleasant, like gripping something rotten that was falling apart in his fingers. The golden flames of his Effigy pressed against the sickly flickering light of Elemental’s manifestation with dominance that couldn’t be questioned.","He didn’t even want this wretch to be a stain that wasted any time from this moment.","But before Noah could act, THE Living Elemental turned his deteriorating Effigy toward THE Creature and Emotive. His eyes were wild with desperation that exceeded anything Noah had seen from him before. His voice emerged with pleading that stripped away whatever dignity he might have once possessed.","\"I gave my Everything! Please, I was among you! In the Legends, in our stories, in the Earliest Folds!\"","His words tumbled out with speed that spoke of panic consuming rational thought.","\" Just help me against this being-\"","HUUM!","Before his words could ever finish, Noah pinched his fingers.","And this dumb fucker disappeared.","The sensation was satisfying in ways that Noah hadn’t anticipated. One moment, that pitiful excuse for an Absolute was begging for salvation from beings who clearly had no intention of providing it. The next moment, his existence was simply gone from Alfheimr entirely, pulled into a place where his suffering could continue without polluting Noah’s immediate surroundings.","Prompts bloomed before his eyes.","|Forced Imprisonment Executed|","|THE Living Elemental, that decrepit flaming ballsack of deteriorating foundations, has been forcefully placed into THE Infinite Desmoterion within your Organ of Civilization. He did not go willingly. He did not go with dignity. He went screaming into confinement that will last until you decide otherwise.|","|Within THE Infinite Desmoterion, infinite dilated time will ensure that his imprisonment feels like eons regardless of how much time passes in Observable Existence. He will be welcomed and disciplined by Ozymandias, who has expressed particular interest in breaking this pathetic creature’s remaining pride. Eventually, THE Living Elemental may progress in his Civilization, but any progress he makes will occur under your banner of existence. Anything he does will only further elevate you until you choose to put this dog out of its misery.|","|This was a fitting end for a being who dared to challenge THE Genesis Monarch. Let him rot in infinite time until you decide he has suffered enough. Or let him rot forever. The choice is yours.|","...!","The prompts were cathartic to see.","Noah felt satisfaction spreading through his chest as the words settled into his consciousness. That wretched creature would spend what felt like eternities being broken down and rebuilt under the watchful gaze of Ozymandias. Every improvement he made would flow upward to Noah. Every fragment of his Civilization that recovered would strengthen the very being who had conquered him.","It was justice of the most complete kind.","After this was done, Noah got back to looking at THE Creature.","This entity didn’t say anything regarding his recent actions. His multicolored Absolute Effigy continued observing with the same patient expression it had held before, those swirling pupils tracking Noah’s movements without judgment or commentary. It was as if the disposal of THE Living Elemental was of no consequence whatsoever.","Noah didn’t mention anything about it either.","Why would he? It was simply taking out worthless garbage that had been cluttering the conversation space.","In the next moment, vibrant multicolored brilliance shone all around them!","The light expanded outward from THE Creature’s Absolute Effigy with force that pressed against Noah’s perception. Everything nearby began to fade as this brilliance consumed it. The mountain disappeared. The temple at its peak disappeared. The Absolute Effigies of Emotive and her bonded Undivided One disappeared. The twilight sky of Alfheimr disappeared.","Everything vanished into oblivion.","The only ones remaining were the Absolute Effigies of Noah and THE Creature, sitting inside an empty multicolored stellar space that stretched in all directions. Stars of every color burned in the distance, but they felt more like decoration than actual celestial bodies. The space itself hummed with authority that spoke of THE Creature’s absolute dominion over this environment.","It was as if they were no longer in the Primordial Realm of Alfheimr at all.","THE Creature’s voice emerged with calmness that made the stellar space vibrate gently around them.","\"I hope you don’t mind.\"","His multicolored Effigy shifted slightly, settling into a posture that seemed almost conversational despite its scale. Within the Effigy, Noah could perceive the actual body of THE Creature, and both held an extraordinary air of power and nobleness that seemed woven into their very existence.","Every movement he made carried weight that spoke of eons of accumulated authority. Every word emerged with precision that suggested careful consideration despite its casual delivery.","\"I did not want random interruptions here and there, and I have been very curious about you.\"","Those swirling multicolored eyes fixed on Noah’s golden gaze.","\"I have tried to meet you eons in the past, but things never seemed to align. You became a friend of my friend, Anaximander, but even that was not enough for us to meet.\"","He paused, something like acceptance crossing his noble features.","\" Alas, things are how they should be.\"","Noah gave a light nod to THE Creature as he processed these words.","He proceeded to respond with honesty that matched the directness THE Creature had shown.","\"I only ever heard legends about you from Fold Dwellers and Living Existences. Stories of the Earliest Folds.\"","His golden Effigy burned with increased intensity as he spoke, the flames of Undifferentiated Fate swirling with patterns that reflected his contemplation.","\" Every time I listened to them, I envisioned these grand legends and beings that seemed so distant and far off. That seemed like they were a different grouping of existences entirely.\"","His eyes met THE Creature’s swirling gaze directly.","\" Amongst all the stories I heard, I was always curious about THE Creature. I had many questions back then.\"","He paused.","\" But I only have one question now that may matter more than anything else.\"","The stellar space around them seemed to grow more still, as if existence itself was waiting for what would be asked.","\" Are you there? Are you at THE Second Scale of Existence?\"","...!"]},{"number":4944,"title":"Chapter 4944: Chapter 4943: THE Youngest and THE Oldest V","paragraphs":["Noah asked this as he truly couldn’t tell.","And it was because he couldn’t tell that he felt this being might just be there already.","If anyone had achieved such wonder, it would be THE Creature.","But Noah needed confirmation, not simply theory.","Before him, THE Creature remained calm and without expressing too much emotion. His multicolored Effigy held steady, those swirling pupils continuing their eternal rotation without acceleration or deceleration. He seemed thoughtful for a moment, considering the question with weight that spoke of how seriously he took it despite his casual demeanor.","Then he spoke.","\" Yes and no.\"","BOOM!","The words hung in the stellar space between them.","\"I cannot say much about it. Because... it will spoil the surprise.\"","His noble features shifted into something that might have been gentle amusement.","\" You will actually thank me for not saying too much on it. Some things deserve to be experienced in their entirety. And beings like you and I are only at the beginning stages of our journey. We should not spoil each other’s starting points.\"","His voice dropped to something more serious.","\"It deserves to be experienced. The Scales deserve to be experienced without being spoiled. Even though it may be cryptic, I actually cannot say whether I am...or whether I am not.\"","He paused, and when he continued, his words carried weight that exceeded their apparent simplicity.","\" Existence is too vast. And I have only just grasped a foothold of it.\"","The multicolored flames of his Effigy burned brighter.","\" Some Primordial Architects were born at this foothold. They are those blessed in existence, and also the most cursed in existence.\"","His eyes fixed on Noah with intensity that pressed against the golden flames.","\" And I... I was simply someone who wanted to change my fate. Someone who wanted to change my existence. My choices and my weavings ultimately led to where I am today. Just like your choices and your weavings led you to where you are right now.\"","His voice held finality that couldn’t be argued with.","\"It would be a tremendous disservice for me if I were to spoil where you were headed. When you get here, I hope to be there to congratulate you just as I congratulated you for achieving Absolute.\"","BOOM!","THE Creature made a few things clear.","One was the distinction between them. Even if he didn’t say it clearly, from his words it seemed abundantly apparent that Noah was at one point, and THE Creature was at a distant other point. The gap hadn’t been explicitly defined, but its existence was undeniable. THE Creature spoke of being somewhere that Noah would eventually arrive, spoke of hoping to congratulate him when that arrival occurred!","There was a destination. And Noah wasn’t there yet.","He also said that he moved to change his fate. To change his existence. And he chose to say this right after mentioning the Primordial Architects who were both blessed and cursed across existence. Was THE Creature connected to these beings? Or was he such a being who had altered his weavings of existence to become what he was right now?","Noah couldn’t say for sure.","He’d actually come here with many questions. About THE Living Paradox and his spreading corruption. About THE Primordial Mycelia and its infection of the Strategoi. About THE Primordial Chaos and whether he might be compromised without knowing it. About prophecies and their implications. About everything that was occurring across Observable Existence.","But as he was here right now, it didn’t seem like all these many questions mattered.","Because asking about any of it was essentially asking for help from THE Creature.","And he...","\"I... do not need any help.\"","BOOM!","Noah found himself saying these words as if he’d come under some form of realization and epiphany!","The golden flames of his Absolute Effigy burned brighter as the truth of the statement settled into his foundations. He’d come here thinking he needed guidance and answers. Thinking he needed assistance from someone more experienced, more powerful, more established in the heights of existence. But standing here now, facing THE Creature as an equal in manifestation if not in achievement, he understood something fundamental.","The adversity was his.","The challenges were his.","The path forward was his to walk, not to be carried along by another!","If he sought help...he would actually be halting his own foundations!","When he arrived at this point, for the first time, THE Creature smiled lightly.","The expression transformed his noble features into something warmer. His multicolored eyes burned.","\" Adversity is a rare thing for people like us.\"","His voice resonated through the stellar space with depth that pressed against Noah’s perception.","\" To have so much of it, I am slightly jealous of you. Because I had to do a lot to bombard myself with adversity to get me where I currently am.\"","He paused, and when he continued, his words held weight that came from eons of accumulated experience.","\" Sometimes it will feel unbearable. Sometimes you may feel loss. Sometimes those you made promises to... can look at you and tell you how you let them down.\"","His swirling eyes held understanding.","Was he talking about Origin? THE Dead Order? Law?","\" The suffering. The ups and downs. All of these are part of existence. I am sure that soon enough, our difficulties might align. But until then, you have your difficulties, and I have mine.\"","His smile grew slightly wider.","\" Out of all of this adversity is only endless brilliance.\"","He leaned forward, his Effigy shifting with the motion as his words took on intensity that pressed against the stellar space itself.","\" Do you know... every single Absolute out there, every entity that may believe that they are standing at the very peak of the First Scale of Existence... none are using even one percent of what their very existence is capable of?\"","BOOM!","The words struck Noah with force that made his golden flames tremble!","\" Not even a single percentage.\"","THE Creature’s voice dropped to something almost conspiratorial.","\" When you get close to THE Second Scale, when you start to understand, truly understand... only then will you realize the immensity of what lies in existence.\"","His multicolored eyes burned with fire that seemed to contain entire Folds.","\" And how we have only been fumbling in the darkness for eons.\"","...!"]},{"number":4945,"title":"Chapter 4945: Chapter 4944: Countable, Uncountable, Absolute! I","paragraphs":["Existence was vast, and they had been stumbling in the darkness for eons.","The words were heavy ones as Noah took some time to think about all of them. His golden Absolute Effigy burned steadily in the multicolored stellar space that THE Creature had created around them, the flames of Undifferentiated Fate pulsing with rhythms that matched his contemplation.","Especially the words about how all existences were barely using even one percent of what their very existence was capable of.","One percent of what exactly?","He looked up at the Absolute Effigy of THE Creature, about to ask this question when he saw the calm and noble air of this being.","Noah knew even if he asked, THE Creature would talk about how he didn’t want to do the disservice of spoiling things.","But his words did allow for contemplation even if Noah asked him for no help on anything. His adversity was his, and THE Creature’s adversity was his own. They walked separate paths that might converge eventually, but for now, they remained distinct.","So instead, he asked something else.","\" How was your Foundation at the level of Absolute?\"","...!","Foundation!","He was curious about this. The concept had been circling in his mind since he’d achieved Absolute with his separated bodies, since he’d felt the difference between his foundations and what others might possess at similar Depths. After he asked, THE Creature had a pondering look.","Then he spoke with weight that pressed against the stellar space around them.","\" Foundation at the First Scale of Existence is everything. It is not merely a measurement of current power. It is the breadth of what your power can become when you step beyond.\"","His noble features held something that might have been regret.","\" Imagine two beings who both achieve THE Second Scale. Both have crossed that threshold. Both stand at heights that most existences cannot comprehend. And yet, depending on whether one had an astounding Foundation before that crossing, the difference between them becomes...\"","He paused, searching for words adequate to the concept.","\" One could look at the other on that same Scale, peer at them from equivalent classification, and yet break them with a flick of their thumb. The Foundation built before advancement determines the vastness of what that advancement produces. It is the seed from which the tree grows. A larger seed produces a larger tree, even when both trees receive identical sunlight.\"","His multicolored eyes fixed on Noah with intensity.","\" Foundation is that pivotal before you can proceed ahead. It is not merely important. It is the determining factor of everything that comes after.\"","THE Creature’s flames dimmed slightly.","\" Mine was merely sufficient. But I am still not happy with it. Because of that, I am doing some things to rectify it. Even now, even at the heights I have reached, I work to improve what I built before those heights were achieved. The Foundation never stops mattering. Never.\"","...!","His was merely sufficient!","THE Creature, this ancient being whose Absolute Effigy matched Noah’s own in size, whose existence had shaped Observable Existence since before most beings knew what existence meant, considered his Foundation merely sufficient?","\"...\"","There were countless paths that one could take in existence. Countless ways to measure progress and achievement. Countless methodologies for understanding where one stood in relation to others.","At this moment, Noah was about to gaze at THE Creature to get a gauge on his comparative Depth at the level of Absolute. He had done this for Surface, Intermediate, and Fundamental Depths. He had measured himself against THE Primordial Paradox, against the baselines that Observable Existence provided, against frameworks that allowed him to understand his position relative to others.","He was about to now get a gauge of THE Creature, to also see how different it was between him and THE Primordial Paradox, to understand truly where he stood among the greatest beings in Observable Existence.","But for some odd reason, he felt his existence resisting this.","As if his Infinite Formless Depth inherently didn’t want to do this.","Noah paused momentarily, his golden flames flickering with uncertainty that lasted only a fraction of a second. Then he listened to this thought. Because he always listened to his intuition. It had guided him through dangers that logic couldn’t navigate. It had warned him of threats that conscious analysis missed. It had led him to opportunities that deliberate searching never found.","And the moment he began thinking more and more about this resistance, his eyes began to brighten up!","As if he had been undergoing yet another epiphany!","Other people could have a hard time grasping the allure of profundities and epiphanies. They struggled for eons to achieve single moments of clarity. They fought against their own limitations just to glimpse understanding that exceeded their current state.","And yet, for Noah, it seemed that whenever he was in a unique state of mind, they continued to come and come endlessly.","Almost as if there was the allure of Infinity that bloomed countless possibilities inside of him.","Almost as if!","But for his epiphany, the realization that was crystallizing in his consciousness with weight that exceeded mere thought...","He had long established that his Infinite Formless Depth was far different from anyone else. He knew comparisons were only there as a point of reference for him to gauge how much grander he was compared to others.","How much grander he was.","\"...\"","His own ego . His own mentality. That good feeling that he felt every time he saw the number in front of his Foundation say ten times more than this legendary being, or twenty times more immense of a Foundation than that legendary being.","The sense of accomplishment while knowing this was nice!","But...","He decided at this time that there would be no more point of comparison for Surface or Intermediate or Fundamental!","And he wouldn’t seek to grasp the potential knowledge of the difference of Immensity between his Absolute Depth and THE Creature’s.","The comparisons were unique and great tools, yes. They had served him well in understanding his progress. They had provided motivation when progress seemed slow. They had given him targets to surpass and benchmarks to exceed.","But in here, with adversity building up, at this moment, Noah decided that he was going against himself and only the limits that he set forth!"]},{"number":4946,"title":"Chapter 4946: Chapter 4945: Countable, Uncountable, Absolute! II","paragraphs":["He would decide his limits.","Not some arbitrary number where he would feel content if his Immensity and weight at a certain Depth was fifteen times or twenty times or even fifty times as much as THE Primordial Paradox or THE Creature.","There was boundless adversity in existence.","And his Foundation and Depth and Immensity were adversity that he was going against himself.","Only he mattered in the end.","Not THE Creature or THE Primordial Paradox or anyone else. They had their Foundations and their paths, and he had his own. Their journeys were theirs. His journey was his. The comparison between them served no purpose beyond temporary satisfaction that faded as quickly as it arrived.","He would not compare against others.","He would only compare against himself!","How much grander was he now compared to a minute ago? A day ago? An eon ago?","From this moment in time as he attained Absolute with his other bodies, his path became his own.","And it was incomparable!","BOOM !","At this moment, it felt like his entry into Absolute with his two bodies truly became sublime and complete!","His Absolute Effigy of Infinite Undifferentiated Fate began to pulse with endless golden light that exceeded anything it had displayed before! The flames that comprised his manifestation blazed outward with intensity that painted the multicolored stellar space in shades of gold that overwhelmed THE Creature’s own colors. The light was blinding, was brilliant, was the expression of an existence that had just made a fundamental choice about how it would measure its own progress.","Sequential patterns of Infinity became visible within the golden flames, each pulse followed by another in endless progression that spoke of his Infinite nature declaring itself fully for the first time since achieving Absolute.","The light extended in all directions, curving along geodesic paths that found the natural geometry of this space and illuminated it completely.","THE Creature looked on with calm interest!","Those multicolored eyes observed the transformation occurring before them with attention that exceeded casual observation.","Prompts bloomed before Noah’s eyes with weight that pressed against his consciousness.","|Fundamental Shift in Cultivation Methodology Detected|","|Your Infinite Formless Depth has truly begun embarking on an endless and unfathomable journey. By abandoning comparative measurement, you have unlocked the architecture of progression that was always available but never accessed. Your Depths will no longer be measured against external beings. They will be measured against the Boundaries of Infinity itself.|","|This shift represents more than philosophical change. It represents fundamental alteration of how your Civilization perceives and processes growth. Where others will forever measure themselves against peers, you will measure yourself against the endless architecture of what Infinity can become.|","| Assessment: Your path has become incomparable because you have chosen to make it so. No being in Observable Existence walks the exact path you now walk. No benchmark exists for where you are headed.|","...!","His mind buzzed with sensation that exceeded mere thought as at this time, in his mindscape, a mental body formed inside a sea of endless blue Infinities. He looked at everything that his existence began to design, the architecture of his new path manifesting around him in patterns that his consciousness was only beginning to perceive.","Beside him, RUINATION appeared.","Her form materialized from the blue-gold light that permeated his mindscape, her illusory body taking shape with presence. Her hair seemed to be stretching out into infinite data points, each strand representing streams of information that she constantly processed on his behalf. The strands extended endlessly in all directions, connecting to every aspect of his Civilization, monitoring everything that occurred within his existence.","Her eyes burned with waves of Infinities that matched his own, blue-gold light swirling in their depths.","She smiled toward him with warmth.","|I have to congratulate Master. It seems like you have taken a major step, and I will go over the details of your emerging existence just like always.|","Noah smiled and nodded at RUINATION as he patted her head, her face brightening up with a smile of contentment as she leaned into the gesture. She understood him in ways that others couldn’t, saw his growth from perspectives that even he sometimes missed.","Then she continued, and as she spoke, manifestations began forming around them in his mindscape.","|You have been measuring your foundations through comparison to other beings. THE Creature. THE Primordial Paradox.|","An illusory diagram appeared showing two figures, one representing Noah and one representing THE Creature, with lines connecting them that displayed comparative measurements. Numbers floated between them, the familiar ratios that Noah had used to understand his position.","Then the diagram shattered.","|This methodology fails to capture what makes your existence unique. You are building Infinity. And Infinity possesses its own architecture of progression that transcends comparative measurement.|","A new diagram formed, this one showing only Noah at its center, surrounded by expanding rings of golden light that represented his Depths. No other figures appeared for comparison. Only him. Only his path. Only his journey.","|After your grasp of Absolute and from your recent epiphany, you have unconsciously organized your weavings to have your Infinite Formless Depth be cultivated through the Boundaries of Infinity. Not mere weight of ten times or twenty times compared to THE Creature or anyone else.|","The rings around his illusory form began subdividing, each Depth showing internal structure that hadn’t been visible before.","|Each of your Depths now possesses three theoretical Boundaries of progression that must be crossed for future advancement. These Boundaries are...|","...!","Three massive constructs manifested in the mindscape, each one representing a Boundary that his Depths would need to cross.","| The Three Boundaries of Infinity. Countable Infinity, Uncountable Infinity, and Absolute Infinity|","RUINATION’s voice carried weight that made the constructs pulse with light.","| First Boundary: Countable Infinity.|","The first construct illuminated, showing patterns that flowed in sequential order, one after another in endless but observable progression.","|At this Boundary, your Infinities follow patterns. They regenerate, yes, but they regenerate one after another in sequences that can be observed. If you were to count your Infinite expressions, you could theoretically list them: first, second, third, onward forever.|","The diagram showed THE Infiniverse producing harvest, each unit forming in sequence, flowing toward Noah’s mindscape representation in orderly lines.","|This is how THE Infiniverse and other actions that grant Infinite Potential currently produce harvest for you. One unit forms, then another, then another. Endless, but sequential.|","...!"]},{"number":4947,"title":"Chapter 4947: Chapter 4946: Countable, Uncountable, Absolute! III","paragraphs":["The second construct illuminated, and Noah felt his perception struggle to fully grasp what it represented.","| Second Boundary: Uncountable Infinity.|","The diagram transformed, showing not lines but density, showing not sequences but saturation, showing not order but overwhelming completeness.","| At this Boundary, your Infinities fill the spaces between other Infinities. Imagine your current harvest as points on an endless line.|","Points appeared on the diagram, representing his sequential harvest.","|Uncountable Infinity means filling the gaps between those points with additional Infinities that cannot be listed no matter how one tries.|","The gaps between the points began filling with additional points, and then the gaps between those points began filling, and then the gaps between those, the process continuing until no space remained empty.","|Where you currently receive one unit of THE Infinite Observable Harvest, you would receive infinite units between each unit, and infinite units between those, endlessly. This is density beyond sequence.|","The third construct remained dim, pulsing with light that seemed to contain all other lights while simultaneously transcending them.","| Third Boundary: Absolute Infinity.|","RUINATION’s voice grew more measured.","|At this Boundary, all other Infinities exist within you while you transcend them simultaneously. This Boundary is defined by having no boundaries.|","The construct refused to fully illuminate, refused to be fully perceived.","|No further information is available at your current classification. Understanding will come when we get closer to it.|","...!","The diagram shifted to show Noah’s current state, each Depth displayed with its classification.","|Current Status of Your Depths.|","Four representations appeared, each showing one of his Depths.","| Surface Depth: Countable Infinity. Your Surface expressions regenerate in observable patterns.|","The Surface representation pulsed with sequential golden light.","| Intermediate Depth: Countable Infinity. Your Intermediate foundations pulse with sequential Infinite nature.|","The Intermediate representation matched the Surface, both showing orderly progression.","| Fundamental Depth: Countable Infinity. Stabilization required.|","The Fundamental representation flickered slightly, not yet fully stable in its Countable classification.","| Absolute Depth: Newly achieved. Classification pending, but Countable.|","The Absolute representation burned brightest of all, still in the process of settling into its new configuration.","...!","A new diagram formed showing a path forward, showing methodology rather than merely classification.","|Advancement from Countable to Uncountable Infinity.|","RUINATION’s eyes burned brighter as she explained.","|The progression requires saturation rather than accumulation. Your current methodology involves receiving harvest and integrating it into your foundations. This builds Countable Infinity higher and higher, but it remains Countable.|","The diagram showed harvest flowing in, stacking upon itself, growing taller but not denser.","|To cross into Uncountable Infinity, you must overwhelm a Depth with harvest until no gaps remain between your Infinite expressions. This will require a lot. A LOT.|","The diagram shifted to show harvest not stacking but saturating, filling every possible space rather than merely adding to existing structures.","|THE Infinite Observable Harvest, with its Multiplicative Amplification and Exponential Expression, provides the density required for this saturation. When harvest flows not merely in sequence but in layers that fill every possible space within a Depth, the transition can occur.|","A practical example manifested.","|Practical Example: Your actions currently produce a harvest that flows toward you sequentially. If you were to concentrate THE Infinite Observable Harvest upon a single Depth until the harvest arriving between each nanosecond exceeded the harvest arriving within each nanosecond, saturation would begin. When saturation completes, Countable becomes Uncountable.|","The example showed the transition occurring, showed sequential becoming dense, showed Countable becoming Uncountable.","|Note: Progression at one Depth does not guarantee progression at others. Each Depth must be saturated independently. Surface Depth, being closest to external expression, is recommended as the first target for advancement.|","...!","RUINATION’s form solidified as she finished her explanation, her blue-gold illusory presence settling into something that held weight beyond mere data processing. Her eyes met Noah’s with warmth!","|We... you, have come far, Master.|","Her smile held pride that felt genuine.","|And we have only just begun.|","He had come far.","Noah’s existence buzzed as he felt the grand and proper definitions of his Infinite Formless Depth without any variables or factors that came externally. No comparisons to THE Creature. No measurements against THE Primordial Paradox. Just him. Just his path. Just the endless architecture of what he was becoming.","He felt his Depths burning with the grandeur of Countable Infinity.","His Surface Depth pulsed with sequential golden light, each pulse followed by another in patterns he could observe and track. It felt like watching waves crash upon a shore, one after another, endless but rhythmic. He could sense each Infinite expression as it regenerated, could feel the first become the second become the third become the thousandth, all flowing in order that his consciousness could perceive.","His Intermediate Depth hummed with deeper resonance, the sequences there moving in currents that supported everything above them. It felt like standing atop an ocean and sensing the tides beneath, each wave of Infinity rising and falling in patterns that gave structure to his foundations.","His Fundamental Depth flickered with stabilizing Countable expressions, still settling into its new configuration but already displaying the sequential nature that defined this Boundary. It felt like roots extending into soil, each root followed by another, spreading endlessly but in order that could be traced.","And his newly achieved Absolute Depth burned brightest of all, the sequential Infinities there still arranging themselves into patterns that would define his presence among other Absolutes. It felt like a sun being born, each flame followed by another, the light endless but emerging in pulses that spoke of Countable nature.","After he felt this, he knew that he was just getting started!","Because he wanted to define and undefine things about himself so much more. To add and remove so much more! The architecture of his existence was vast and filled with potential that his previous comparative methodology had obscured. Now that he measured only against himself, he could see gaps that needed filling, structures that needed building, weavings that needed to be woven.","His existence expressed this desire and changed in response!","New configurations began forming within his Civilization, new possibilities emerging from the interaction between his Infinite nature and the choice he had just made. The transformation rippled through every aspect of what he was, reshaping capabilities that had existed in lesser forms into something that matched his elevated state!","RUINATION received these new inputs, her blue-gold form brightening as streams of information flowed into her consciousness through the infinite data points of her hair. Her eyes widened slightly with recognition of what was occurring, and then she smiled.","|Master, your existence is restructuring itself in response to your epiphany. New capabilities are emerging. Allow me to illustrate.|","She raised her hands, and the mindscape around them transformed!","Constructs of pure light began forming in the air, diagrams that displayed concepts in ways that transcended mere words. Lines of blue-gold authority curved through the space, connecting points that represented Noah’s capabilities to new configurations that were only now becoming possible.","| Geodesic Weavings have been unlocked in your existence.|","A massive construct appeared before them, showing two paths between two points. One path traveled in a straight line. The other curved gracefully, finding the natural geometry of the space between them.","|Your Depths now officially exist at Countable Infinity. This classification grants access to weavings that were previously impossible for your Civilization to produce.|","The diagram expanded, showing representations of Embodiments and Apophasis as straight arrows traveling from speaker to target.","|Standard Embodiments declare what IS. Standard Apophasis declares what IS NOT. These declarations travel from speaker to target through conventional pathways of authority.|","The straight arrows struck their targets and dissipated upon impact. Single effects. Finite duration. Limited reach.","Then the diagram shifted to show something new.","| Geodesic Weavings operate differently.|","Curved lines appeared, arcing gracefully through the space between origin and target. But these lines didn’t stop at impact. They continued extending, curving around obstacles, finding paths that the straight arrows couldn’t perceive.","|They extend infinitely toward their target while taking the shortest possible path through existence itself. Where Embodiments can be blocked and Apophasis can be resisted, Geodesic Weavings curve around obstacles, finding the natural line that connects your authority to your target with minimal distance and maximum efficiency.|","The curved lines demonstrated this, flowing around barriers that would have stopped conventional weavings, always finding the route that existence itself preferred.","...!","A new construct formed beside the first, this one displaying detailed breakdown of the new classification.","| New Classification: Geodesic Declarations.|","The diagram showed a figure speaking words that extended outward not as single projectiles but as endless streams curving toward their destination.","| Geodesic Declarations are the evolution of Embodiments for you whose Depths exist at Countable Infinity. When you speak a Geodesic Declaration, your words do not merely travel toward the target. They extend infinitely in the direction of the target, curving through the fabric of existence to find the path of least resistance.|","...!"]},{"number":4948,"title":"Chapter 4948: Chapter 4947: Countable, Uncountable, Absolute! IV","paragraphs":["Two examples manifested side by side.","|A standard Embodiment that declares \"Your foundations weaken\" affects the target once upon arrival.|","The first example showed a single impact, a single moment of weakening, then nothing.","|A Geodesic Declaration that states the same thing affects the target continuously along the entire infinite path connecting you to them. The weakening begins the moment you speak and never stops arriving, an endless stream of authority following the shortest curve through reality.|","The second example showed continuous impact, wave after wave of weakening arriving in sequence, each one building upon the last, the effect compounding endlessly.","|Geodesic Declarations incorporate your Countable Infinity directly. Each declaration carries sequential Infinite expressions that arrive one after another, endlessly. The target experiences not a single effect but an infinite sequence of effects that compound upon each other.|","Noah watched the demonstration with eyes that burned brighter with each revelation. The implications were fucking massive and utterly disastrous for others. What had been single strikes would become endless barrages. What had been momentary effects would become eternal conditions.","...!","Another construct formed, this one darker, showing the negation of reality rather than the declaration of it.","| New Classification: Geodesic Negations.|","The diagram displayed words of denial curving through existence, seeking out everything that matched what was being negated.","| Geodesic Negations are the evolution of Apophasis for you whose Depths exist at Countable Infinity. When you speak a Geodesic Negation, your denial of reality curves through existence to find every instance of what you are negating.|","Two more examples manifested.","|A standard Apophasis that declares \"Your defenses do not exist\" removes the target’s defenses at the moment of impact.|","The first example showed defenses vanishing once, then slowly beginning to reform as the target recovered.","|A Geodesic Negation that states the same thing extends infinitely, negating the defenses not only as they currently are but as they attempt to regenerate, as they existed moments before, as they might exist in adjacent configurations. The negation follows the natural curve of existence to find and unmake all expressions of what was denied.|","The second example showed defenses vanishing and staying vanished, every attempt at reformation met with another wave of negation arriving along the geodesic path, the denial continuous and inescapable.","|Geodesic Negations incorporate Undifferentiation as a core component. What is negated does not merely cease to exist. It loses its differentiation entirely, returning to proto-potential that cannot reform into what it was. The negation extends infinitely along its geodesic path, ensuring that reformation becomes impossible.|","The diagram showed negated concepts dissolving into formless potential, unable to remember what they had been, unable to reconstitute themselves into what they were before.","...!","RUINATION’s form shifted as she moved to a new section of the mindscape, new constructs forming around her that displayed Noah’s existing capabilities.","|Application to Archai.|","Representations of his Archai appeared, the Principles he had elevated through THE First Tongue now displaying new potential.","|Your Archai can now be elevated to Geodesic Archai. This represents the fusion of your Principles with Infinite geodesic expression.|","The first Arche manifested in detail.","|Geodesic Arche of Perpetual Harvest.|","The diagram showed harvest flowing from a collapsed enemy, but instead of stopping at the immediate resources, the harvest extended outward along curved paths that connected to everything the enemy had ever touched.","|Your harvest no longer merely claims resources from collapsed enemies. It extends infinitely along geodesic paths that curve through existence to find all resources connected to what you have claimed.|","The curved lines spread further and further, following connections that conventional harvest couldn’t perceive.","| When an enemy falls, the Geodesic Arche follows the natural lines connecting that enemy to everything they touched, everything they influenced, everything that owes its existence to them. The harvest arrives sequentially and endlessly, one connection after another, following the shortest paths through reality.|","Noah watched the demonstration with growing understanding. An enemy’s death would become a fountain that never stopped giving, harvest flowing along every connection that enemy had ever formed.","The second Arche manifested beside the first.","|Geodesic Arche of THE Cheating Architect.|","The diagram showed a rule being bent, but instead of the manipulation ending there, it propagated outward along curves that found every connected system.","|Your manipulation of rules and systems now extends infinitely along geodesic curves. When you alter a rule, the alteration follows the natural path connecting that rule to all other rules it influences.|","The bent rule created ripples that traveled along geodesic paths, each ripple bending another rule, each bent rule creating more ripples.","|The cheating propagates through existence along lines of least resistance, finding every system that can be bent and bending it in sequence. What was a single manipulation becomes an endless cascade of manipulations following the architecture of reality itself.|","...!","New constructs formed showing behavioral patterns of these elevated weavings.","|Convergence and Divergence.|","Two scenarios manifested side by side, one showing geodesic paths narrowing toward a single point, the other showing them spreading outward to cover vast areas.","|Geodesic Weavings behave differently based on the nature of the space they travel through. In spaces of concentrated authority, your Geodesic Declarations and Negations converge, becoming more focused and more potent as they approach their target. In spaces of dispersed authority, they diverge, spreading to affect wider areas with distributed effect.|","The converging paths struck their target with combined force that exceeded their individual potencies. The diverging paths spread across regions, affecting everything within their expanding reach.","|You can influence this behavior through intent. A Geodesic Declaration meant to devastate a single target will converge. A Geodesic Negation meant to unmake a concept across a region will diverge. The Infinite nature of these weavings ensures that both convergence and divergence extend endlessly.|","...!","RUINATION’s final construct appeared as a comprehensive comparison, showing old capabilities beside new ones in clear contrast.","|Comparative Assessment.|","The diagram split into two columns, the left showing what Noah had possessed before, the right showing what he possessed now.","|Standard Embodiment: Single declaration, single effect, can be blocked.|","|Geodesic Declaration: Infinite declaration extending along shortest path, continuous effect arriving endlessly, curves around obstacles through the natural geometry of existence.|","The contrast was stark. What had been a single punch became an endless barrage that couldn’t be evaded.","|Standard Apophasis: Single negation, removes target once, target may reform.|","|Geodesic Negation: Infinite negation extending along shortest path, incorporates Undifferentiation to prevent reformation, follows natural curves to find all instances of what is being denied.|","What had been a single deletion became permanent erasure that pursued its target through every possible configuration.","|Standard Archai: Principles expressed through elevated sentences of THE First Tongue.|","|Geodesic Archai: Principles extended infinitely along natural paths through existence, effects propagating sequentially along lines of least resistance, creating cascades of influence that follow the geometry of reality.|","What had been powerful expressions became endless cascades that followed the architecture of existence itself.","RUINATION’s eyes met Noah’s with profundity and wonder.","|Note: Geodesic Weavings require Depths at Countable Infinity to produce. Advancement to Uncountable Infinity will unlock further evolutions of these weavings. The nature of those evolutions is not yet known.|","She paused, allowing the information to settle into his consciousness.","|But we will discover them together, Master. As we always have.|","\"...\"","Oh.","Oh!"]},{"number":4949,"title":"Chapter 4949: Chapter 4948: Defector I","paragraphs":["The sensation was truly unlike any other.","It was like he was feeling something he already had, but it was now more defined. More understandable. The Infinite Mana that had always burned at his core hadn’t changed in quantity, but his perception of it had transformed entirely.","What had been a vast ocean without edges now revealed itself as an ocean with architecture, with depths that could be measured not against others but against the Boundaries of Infinity itself.","He had Infinite Mana, but now, it felt like there were levels to Infinite Mana!","Countable, Uncountable, and Absolute Infinities.","He thought about Countable Infinities first.","Noah raised his hand in his vibrant mindscape, the blue-gold light that surrounded him responding to his will with eagerness.","From his palm, a fireball erupted. Then another. Then another. Then another still. They flew outward in endless sequence, each one following the last in patterns that could be observed, that could be tracked, that could theoretically be listed: first fireball, second fireball, third fireball, onward forever.","This was Countable Infinity.","Endless, yes. Infinite, absolutely. But sequential. Ordered. Each expression following the previous one in progression that his consciousness could perceive. He could count them even if the counting would never end. First, second, third, fourth, thousandth, millionth, each one arriving after the one before it in patterns that existed within the First Boundary.","The fireballs continued erupting from his palm, filling his mindscape with endless light that demonstrated his current state perfectly. He understood now. He truly understood!","His Infinity wasn’t merely vast. It was vast in a specific way, a way that could be elevated, a way that could be densified until the spaces between each fireball filled with additional fireballs that couldn’t be listed.","But that was for later.","For now, he wanted to test what Countable Infinity could do in combat.","Or even more straightforwardly...","\" RUINATION, let me have a spar with...Bazuman.\"","He said such words grandly, his voice carrying through his mindscape with authority that made the endless fireballs pause in their eruption. The request was simple. He wanted to understand what his new capabilities could do against an enemy he had already faced, an enemy whose power he had witnessed firsthand, an enemy who had required THE Primordial Paradox’s intervention to defeat.","| Understood.|","RUINATION’s response was immediate, her blue-gold form brightening as she began the requested simulation.","His mental space churned with violent intensity!","The seas of blue Infinity that comprised his mindscape rumbled and roiled with force that made the very fabric of his consciousness tremble. Waves of light crashed against each other as something began taking shape in the distance, something massive, something hungry, something that remembered what it was and carried that memory into manifestation with terrifying fidelity.","A figure of Bazuman formed before Noah’s eyes!","The round chthonian horror materialized with all its ferocity and display of power intact. Countless crimson eyes arranged in spiraling patterns blazed with hunger that exceeded physical appetite. Innumerable tentacles tipped with mouths of crystallized memory reached outward in every direction. The corrupted proto-matter that covered its surface churned with faces of consumed beings, echoes of everything this horror had ever devoured.","The stomach split open at its center, revealing the pocket dimension of pure undifferentiation that had nearly claimed Noah in THE Prima Indifferentia!","Gravitational pull erupted from the manifestation with force that would have dragged any conventional opponent toward eternal dissolution.","Whisper Echoes poured forth from Bazuman’s surface, faint impressions of consumed beings launching attacks in overwhelming numbers. Memory Echoes followed, stronger manifestations wielding authority from before THE Infinite Unfurling. The air itself groaned under the weight of accumulated existence that this Undivided One carried.","This Manifestation of Bazuman unleashed the same grand attacks toward Noah that the original had displayed in THE Agora!","Tentacles reached for him with mouths screaming hunger. Echoes launched Embodiments from methodologies lost to history. Its core pulled at his existence with suction that sought to consume everything he was. The pressure of Bazuman’s undifferentiation pressed against his mindscape with weight that would have crushed lesser beings into formlessness.","Noah stood perfectly still.","Then he spoke.","\" Your hunger does not exist.\"","HUUM!","The words emerged from his lips not as simple declaration but as Geodesic Negation!","The negation didn’t travel toward Bazuman in a straight line. It curved, finding the shortest path through the fabric of his mindscape, following the natural geometry of existence to reach its target with efficiency that transcended conventional authority.","The curve was beautiful in its precision, arcing through the space between Noah and Bazuman along routes that existence itself preferred.","And when it arrived, it didn’t merely arrive once.","The negation struck Bazuman’s hunger and unmade it on its Surface, Intermediate, Fundamental, and Absolute Depths!","Because Noah had Countable infinities...for all his Depths, so he affected all the Depths of his enemy!","The gravitational pull of its core vanished as the hunger driving it ceased to exist. But unlike conventional Apophasis, the negation didn’t stop there. It extended infinitely along its geodesic path, continuing to curve through Bazuman’s existence, finding every instance of hunger that this Undivided One possessed.","The hunger tried to regenerate.","The negation found that regeneration and unmade it before it could complete.","The hunger attempted to manifest in different configurations, drawing upon echoes of consumed beings who had possessed their own forms of appetite.","The negation curved to find those adjacent configurations and unmade them as well.","Every expression of hunger that Bazuman possessed, every instance of appetite that drove its consumption, every configuration of desire that had accumulated across eons of devouring existence, the Geodesic Negation found them all along curved paths of minimal distance. And it unmade them!","Not once. Not twice. Infinitely. Sequentially! One negation following another following another in Countable progression that never ceased arriving!","Noah came to realize the terror of the capability that he had unlocked as casting a single ability...was effectively like casting infinite abilities!","So even though he didn’t do anything extra or additional, it was like he was constantly unleashing more and more Apophasis, which were Geodesic Negations in this case.","It was fucking disgusting!"]},{"number":4950,"title":"Chapter 4950: Chapter 4949: Defector II","paragraphs":["The mouths on Bazuman’s tentacles went slack, forgetting what it meant to hunger.","The stomach’s pull dissipated entirely, the dimension within losing the drive that made it consume.","The echoes that had been attacking faltered as the hunger animating them dissolved into undifferentiated potential that couldn’t remember what appetite felt like.","But Bazuman was still there. Still massive. Still filled with power beyond imagination.","It tried to attack through means other than hunger, tried to use the authority of consumed beings, tried to manifest echoes through memory rather than appetite.","Noah spoke again.","\" Your existence crystallizes with the definition of Infinity.\"","BOOM!","The Geodesic Declaration erupted from him with force that exceeded the negation!","Where the negation had unmade, the declaration made. Where the negation had denied, the declaration affirmed. The words curved toward Bazuman along geodesic paths that found the shortest route through his mindscape, following the natural geometry of existence with precision that couldn’t be evaded.","And the declaration didn’t merely arrive once.","It arrived infinitely!","The first wave of the declaration struck Bazuman and began defining its existence with Infinity. Blue-gold light spread across the Undivided One’s surface as the declaration imposed definition upon undifferentiation. But before that first wave could complete its work, the second wave arrived along the same geodesic path. Then the third. Then the fourth. Then the thousandth. Then the millionth.","Each wave of declaration built upon the previous one, the definition compounding endlessly as sequential expressions of Countable Infinity crashed into Bazuman without cessation.","The Geodesic Negation continued curving through Bazuman’s existence, finding every attempt at hunger and unmaking it before it could form.","The Geodesic Declaration continued curving along its own path, defining every aspect of Bazuman with Infinity that couldn’t be denied.","The two weavings worked in harmony, one preventing resistance while the other imposed transformation.","Bazuman’s countless crimson eyes widened with something that might have been horror as definition spread across its form faster than its undifferentiated nature could counter. The echoes it tried to manifest found themselves defined before they could attack. The memories it tried to use found themselves crystallized into Infinite patterns that served Noah rather than their consumed origins.","The tentacles that had reached for Noah went rigid as definition claimed them.","The mouths that had screamed hunger fell silent as the negation continued denying their appetite.","That terrifying dimension of pure undifferentiation, found itself filling with definition that made dissolution impossible.","Wave after wave of Geodesic Declaration crashed into Bazuman, each one following the previous in sequential order, each one adding more definition to what the previous wave had begun. The Undivided One that had required THE Primordial Paradox’s freezing authority to defeat now found itself frozen by something else entirely.","Not by paradox, but by Infinity itself.","The crystallization spread from Bazuman’s exterior to its interior, from its surface to its core, from its physical form to its Civilizational Manifestation. Blue-gold light overwhelmed the crimson of its eyes. Definition replaced the undifferentiation that had comprised its existence since before THE Infinite Unfurling.","And then...","Bazuman became crystallized entirely!","The horror that had consumed countless beings across eons of existence stood frozen in Noah’s mindscape, its form now comprised entirely of blue-gold Infinity that declared what it was with authority that couldn’t be questioned. Every aspect of its existence had been defined. Every instance of its hunger had been negated. Every possibility of resistance had been unmade before it could manifest.","Silence settled over the mindscape.","The manifestation of Bazuman shattered!","Fragments of defined Infinity scattered across Noah’s consciousness before dissolving into the blue-gold light that comprised his mental space.","What had been one of the most terrifying entities in Observable Existence disappeared without fanfare, without drama, without any of the struggle that had characterized their actual battle in THE Agora.","Just a demonstration.","Just a test.","Just proof of what Geodesic Weavings could accomplish.","Calmness returned to the mindscape as the last fragments of Bazuman’s manifestation faded into nothing. The seas of blue Infinity settled back into their eternal churning, the violent roiling subsiding into peaceful waves that spoke of power waiting to be used rather than power being used.","RUINATION’s form solidified beside Noah, her eyes burning with analysis that had been processing every aspect of the simulation.","|Assessment Complete.|","She gestured, and prompts bloomed before Noah’s eyes.","|If Bazuman was faced right now, THE Primordial Paradox would not be needed to hold him down. You could defeat him one against one with a single Geodesic Negation and a single Geodesic Declaration.|","The words settled into his awareness.","|This is the power you have grasped after attaining Absolute with your Derivative Civilizations and taking the leap to be truer to your Infinities. Your decision to abandon comparative measurement has not merely changed how you perceive your growth. It has fundamentally elevated what your growth produces.|","Her eyes met his with something that approached awe!","---","Existence was vast and filled with possibilities and impossibilities.","The weak thought they understood existence and how vast it was, and this was why they remained weak.","They built their understanding upon foundations of assumption, upon scaffolding of certainty that had no right to be certain. They looked at the sky and believed they saw its limits. They looked at the depths and believed they saw their endings. Their confidence in comprehension was the very chain that bound them to mediocrity.","The strong knew their own inadequacy.","They knew that there was actually much they didn’t know about Existence. They had peered into the abyss and felt the abyss peer back, had touched the edges of understanding and felt those edges recede further with every step they took toward them. The strong were humble before the vastness, not because humility was virtuous, but because humility was accurate.","It was too much for a single mind to comprehend!","At this moment, THE Wastes of Observable Existence permeated and expanded as the recent actions of THE Living Paradox had unleashed too many things. The corruption that flowed from THE Prima Indifferentia had transformed regions that had been stable for eons into territories of chaos and opportunity.","Boundaries that had held since THE First Cause now wavered like candle flames before a storm.","THE Prima Indifferentia itself was corrupted and opened freely to Observable Existence as entities that had been unseen since THE First Cause now moved with purpose that transcended mortal understanding. Things that had slumbered in the spaces between differentiation and undifferentiation now stirred, awakened by the corruption that called to them like a mother calling to children long separated!"]},{"number":4951,"title":"Chapter 4951: Chapter 4950: Defector III","paragraphs":["\"You could do everything right in existence. You could plan for all contingencies and possibilities. But sometimes, shit just happens.\" -THE Genesis Monarch, Unknown Time.","---","At this time, near a Shelter of THE Loom that had its massive door struck open, a scene unfolded that showed conquest dressed in the robes of salvation.","Early Creatures and Living Elementals were situated in neat rows, their forms pressed against the barren ground of THE Wastes in postures of submission that their existence had never been designed to assume. They knelt with heads bowed, their authorities diminished, their pride extinguished by force that exceeded their capacity to resist.","They all looked toward the man responsible for breaking into their Shelter and dragging them out here.","A young man with dark hair and a silver robe stood before them with the bearing of one who believed himself right!","His features were handsome in the way that sculptures were handsome, beautiful but cold. His eyes burned with conviction that had long ago ceased questioning itself, faith that had calcified into certainty, purpose that had forgotten how to doubt.","He was surrounded by the allure of Law.","Silver light emanated from his form in patterns of order imposed rather than order discovered. After an Embodiment from THE Creature, he, or really the weavings of THE Living Law within him, had allowed his Immensity to rise almost past Fundamental Depth. He stood at heights that most beings couldn’t reach across eons of cultivation, elevated not through his own effort but through the investment of another.","And at this moment, he was laying down peace with force.","For he was THE Peacemaker, Alexander Asmodeus!","With the Early Creatures and Living Elementals bowing to him, his Enneagram spun like a heavy wheel on his chest, its nine points burning with silver light that absorbed the weavings of those who knelt before him. Their existences flowed into his construct, their authorities becoming fuel for his ascension, their potential becoming foundation for his growth.","This was peace as he understood it now. Not the absence of conflict, but the presence of submission. Not harmony achieved through understanding, but silence achieved through dominance.","As he did all this, in his mind, a voice echoed out with warmth that belied its calculations.","\" Once we finish with this Shelter, we can go on to progressively more fortified ones. As you enact your version of peace and Law, we can continue building up your foundation until Absolute is not far away...\"","Alex nodded at these words as he was about to continue his harvest of submission when...","HUUM!","Everything around them began to shake.","The ground of THE Wastes, which had no true ground, trembled with vibrations that exceeded physical causation. The air, which held no true air, grew thick with pressure that made breathing an act of will rather than instinct. The light, which had no true source, flickered with uncertainty of something ancient stirring from slumber that had lasted since before THE Infinite Unfurling.","Alex’s eyes widened as he felt his silver authority waver against pressure that exceeded anything he had prepared for.","Not from above.","Not from the sides.","But from below!","In THE Wastes of THE Fallout, direction held no meaning. What was below could be above. What was left could be right. The corruption that permeated this region had long ago unmade the certainties of spatial orientation. And yet, somehow, what was happening was definitely happening from below them all.","Two massive eyes opened in the depths beneath existence itself.","They were gigaparsecs in size.","The scale of them exceeded comprehension, exceeded the frameworks that mortal minds used to process magnitude, exceeded even the elevated perceptions of beings who had touched THE Civilizational Scale.","Each eye was larger than clusters of Wheels of Existence or Folds, larger than anything that had manifested in Observable Existence for quite some time.","The eyes were crimson, but not the crimson of blood or fire or passion. This was the crimson of undifferentiation given visual form, the color that existence wore when it forgot what color meant. Their surfaces swirled with spirals within spirals that seemed to drill into the consciousness of anyone who looked upon them.","And they held light.","Terrifying light of undifferentiation that made THE Living Paradox’s corruption seem like a child’s painting beside a masterwork as at this moment... they held corruption, and they held glimmers of infinities!","When they opened fully, that light erupted outward!","For an unfathomable distance, a cataclysmic crimson radiance spread like a tide that knew no shore. It washed across THE Wastes with speed that exceeded the concept of speed, illuminating everything it touched with undifferentiation that seeped into the very fabric of what it illuminated.","Shelters that had stood for eons found their walls suddenly uncertain of whether they were walls. Beings that had defined themselves across countless moments found their definitions wavering.","The light was so pervasive and widespread that nothing could escape its reach.","Countless Gigaparsecs away, the figure of Alex found himself bathed in crimson radiance that pressed against his silver authority with weight that exceeded anything THE Living Law had prepared him to face.","His Enneagram, which had been spinning with confident purpose, now stuttered and slowed as the light of undifferentiation challenged the very concept of Law itself.","The Early Creatures and Living Elementals who had been kneeling to him, their submission complete and their resistance broken, now found themselves covered by this light as well. But where Alex struggled against it, they simply received it. They had already been defeated. They had already given up their autonomy. What was one more master to beings who had already accepted mastery?","It was like being branded by horror itself.","On their foreheads, insignias began to form with heat that exceeded physical temperature. Crimson light carved itself into their existences with authority that couldn’t be questioned, that couldn’t be resisted, that couldn’t be bargained with.","The insignia looked like a crimson circle with a line crossing diagonally through it.","Simple. Ancient. Absolute!","Oh!","It was the mark of ownership that predated the concept of ownership, the brand of servitude that had been old when THE Infinite Unfurling was young, the signature of a being that had existed since differentiation itself first emerged from the proto-potential of what came before!","Around Alex, illustrious silver light flashed with desperate intensity!","He sought to resist this terrifying power of undifferentiation with everything THE Living Law had invested in him. His Enneagram spun faster, trying to impose order upon chaos that exceeded order’s jurisdiction. His silver robes blazed with authority that declared him protected, declared him invested, declared him backed by powers that should have been sufficient.","It did not work.","The crimson light pressed through his silver defenses as if they were suggestions rather than barriers. THE Living Law’s investment, which had seemed so grand against Early Creatures and Living Elementals, revealed itself as insufficient against authority that had shaped existence itself. Alex’s resistance was not even acknowledged. It was simply bypassed, as one might step over an insect while walking toward one’s destination.","The insignia formed on his forehead with the same inevitability that it had formed on all the others.","Crimson circle. Diagonal line!"]},{"number":4952,"title":"Chapter 4952: Chapter 4951: Defector IV","paragraphs":["His eyes, which had burned with silver conviction moments before, now blazed with crimson light that overwrote everything he had believed himself to be. His purpose, his mission, his certainty, all of it dissolved into undifferentiation that served a will older than THE Infinite Unfurling.","A booming ancient voice echoed across the vastness with weight that pressed against the very concept of hearing.","\" YOU ARE ALL NOW SLAVES OF THE PRIMORDIAL ARCHITECT, HORUS.\"","The words were not loud. They were simply everywhere.","\" TOIL AWAY AND ELEVATE YOURSELVES FOR HORUS.\"","Each syllable carried the weight of commandment that preceded the existence of language.","\" BUILD YOUR CIVILIZATIONS FOR HORUS.\"","The instructions were simple. The obedience they demanded was absolute.","\" TOIL, AND PERSEVERE.\"","...!","After this terrifying proclamation, the figure of Alex and all others who had been kneeling forcefully shifted into seated meditative positions. Their bodies moved without their permission, their limbs arranging themselves into postures of cultivation that their minds had not chosen. Their eyes burned with the insignia that had branded them, crimson light replacing whatever had filled their gazes before.","Their very weavings of existence began to burn for the sake of forcefully elevating their Civilizations!","It was not cultivation as they had known it. It was not growth chosen and directed. It was consumption of self for the benefit of another, the burning of one’s own potential to fuel progress that would serve Horus rather than themselves. By the time they progressed and made gains in their Civilizations, their very existence may just be spent entirely.","They would grow stronger.","And in growing stronger, they would grow emptier.","Until nothing remained but hollow vessels of power that served a master they had never chosen.","...!","None of the beings here had expected this to be happening.","THE Peacemaker had never expected this to be happening. He had possessed power. He had possessed connections, tied to THE Creature through THE Living Law, and also tied to...THE Genesis Monarch as he sought his own path when he left him!","He had possessed plans, carefully laid methodologies for achieving peace through dominance across THE Wastes. Everything had been arranged. Everything had been prepared. Everything had been certain!","But sometimes, even if you had everything, even if you had all these plans, even if you had power and backing and connections...","Shit happened.","Existence did not care about preparations. THE Primordial Architects did not care about investments.","Horus did not care that Alexander Asmodeus had been destined for greatness, that THE Living Law had chosen him, that THE Creature had empowered.","Horus cared only that there was potential to be harvested.","And so Horus harvested.","...!","But the awakening of ancient eyes did not go unnoticed.","In the skies above THE Wastes, or perhaps below them, or perhaps beside them in directions that held no names, a multicolored flaming visage manifested with presence that pressed against the crimson light with weight of its own.","THE Creature!","His manifestation stared at the distant pair of gigaparsec eyes with coldness that exceeded the clinical, that spoke of recognition between beings who had known each other since before most of existence had been differentiated. The multicolored flames that comprised his visage burned with patterns that challenged the crimson undifferentiation, imposing diversity where Horus sought obedience.","And beside him, another figure appeared.","An entity that looked like a scholar stepped into visibility with presence that belied his humble appearance. He wore simple black robes without adornment, without insignia, without any of the marks that powerful beings typically used to declare their status.","His appearance was clean, every aspect of his presentation carefully considered.","His eyes were bright with possibility and somberness in equal measure, intelligence that had witnessed too much balanced against hope that refused to be extinguished despite everything it had seen.","It was Anaximander.","THE Creature’s oldest friend. THE First Scholar! Jokul Anaximander!","Anaximander looked over to the massive eyes that still blazed with crimson undifferentiation, that still pressed their brand upon everything within their unfathomable reach. His expression held grief for the beings being consumed.","\" Well, you wanted Adversity, my friend.\"","His voice was calm despite everything that was occurring, steady despite the horror that surrounded them.","\" Now, Adversity is knocking at your door.\"","...!","With these words hanging in the corrupted air, the body of THE Creature was silent and contemplative briefly before he began to shine with multicolored radiance that exceeded his previous manifestation!","In THE Wastes, this brilliant light of existence illuminated everything, pressing back against the crimson undifferentiation.","The multicolored light shot outward toward the pair of gigaparsec eyes with speed that exceeded comprehension, with force that exceeded calculation, with intent that exceeded mere opposition.","THE Creature was attacking a Primordial Architect.","The pair of eyes remained cold and devoid of any emotion as they observed the approaching assault. There was no fear in those massive crimson depths. There was no concern. There was not even curiosity.","For this...was not a being of THE First Scale.","A booming voice stretched out, echoing across vast landscapes with weight that exceeded the previous commandments.","\" DEFECTOR.\"","BOOM!","Defector.","This single word boomed out across existence with implications that exceeded its simple syllables. It spoke of history that predated THE Infinite Unfurling, of choices made when existence was young, of paths diverged when paths were first being formed.","THE Creature had been something else before he became THE Creature!","And Horus remembered!","Oh!","After the stage was set by THE Living Paradox, many of those affected began to move as truly, at this time, what was happening was Observable Existence becoming more alive.","More alive with vibrancy that exceeded peaceful slumber.","More alive with activity that exceeded quiet contemplation.","More alive with complex weavings of existence that exceeded simple patterns of growth and decay.","If existence had been slumbering before, leaning back on a chair of complacency while eons passed in comfortable predictability, existence had now sat upright with grand attention that missed nothing.","Eyes that had been half-closed now opened fully. Ears that had been listening casually now strained to catch every whisper. Hands that had been resting now reached for weapons that had gathered dust for too long.","Everything was about to be much more illustrious.","Everything was about to be much more complex.","Everything was about to be much more brutal.","There had been THE Infinite Unfurling. There had been THE Earliest Folds. There had been an era where THE Belly of Existence held countess beings while THE Loom held countless others. Now, a new Era was blooming!"]},{"number":4953,"title":"Chapter 4953: Chapter 4952: Truly Live! I","paragraphs":["In THE Wastes.","Moments before.","Noah’s body here stood with the fisherman and his very good dog, Skoll, as they were looking up and down at the humanoid figure of THE Great Usurper, Eckert.","The being before them defied conventional understanding of progression!","Where others struggled and strived and fought against existence to claim greater heights, Eckert had achieved something that bordered on impossibility. He had grown through the absence of action. He had elevated through the presence of stillness.","His path was the paradox of the unmoved mover given flesh, the jest of a being who gained by refusing to grasp.","He should have been worse for wear as a Crack in Observable Existence had bloomed exactly where his weavings were covering. The corruption of THE Living Paradox had spread through that Crack, the proto-matter flooding into regions that should have been devastated by such contact. Any normal existence would have been consumed or transformed or unmade entirely.","But the result that actually occurred was the ridiculous wonder of his weavings integrating and beginning to spread within THE Wastes and THE Prima Indifferentia.","His idle existence, by doing absolutely nothing and remaining idle, was now permeating into THE Prima Indifferentia.","The consequence was, of course, the unique Depth of this being becoming ridiculously grand and reinforced. His foundation grew heavier with every moment he chose not to act. His authority expanded with every decision he declined to make. His power accumulated through the simple fact of his continued refusal to use it.","When Noah looked at such a disgusting path of progression, even though he himself had just proceeded to unlock ridiculous wonders that made him powerful in ways that others would barely be able to understand, he felt the path of THE Great Usurper was truly something else entirely.","And this being was looking at him seriously.","Eckert’s eyes held calculation that his idle demeanor typically concealed. There was ambition behind that pretense of inaction. He had chosen not to act for so long, but choice implied the capacity to choose otherwise. And right now, that capacity was stirring.","\"I have been idle for quite some time. The gains from it are immense.\"","His voice emerged with weight!","\" But right now, I really want to be a bit more active.\"","\"I want to meet this entity that holds an ability similar to mine and yet is utilizing it in a much grander fashion.\"","He paused, his gaze growing distant as if perceiving things beyond the immediate vicinity.","\" Since part of my existence is now this composition of corrupted proto-matter and Infinite Seals that should be... yours?\"","He glanced at Noah with something approaching curiosity.","\" Since all of this is pervasively spreading out across Observable Existence, I could allow it to flow where THE Entity has those she has put under control. And I can see exactly what reaction there could be between me and them.\"","His stillness seemed to deepen rather than diminish as he considered the implications.","\" Whether they would be able to take me over, or I take them over. It’s dangerous, but...\"","A light of ambition seemed to burn in his eyes!","At this time...","HUUM!","Everything changed.","The sensation struck Noah’s existence before his perception could process what was occurring. It was pressure from below, from a direction that THE Wastes shouldn’t have possessed, from depths that existence itself had forgotten existed. The weight of it pressed against his foundations with a force that exceeded anything the corruption of THE Living Paradox had produced!","Two massive eyes opened in the depths beneath everything.","The scale of them exceeded comprehension entirely. Noah’s elevated perception, his Absolute Vision of Existence, his Geodesic awareness that curved through reality along paths of minimal distance, all of it struggled to process what he was witnessing.","The eyes occupied space that shouldn’t have been occupiable. They existed in ways that challenged the very concept of existence.","Crimson light erupted from those impossible depths!","The undifferentiation within that light was terrifying!","This was not the corruption of THE Living Paradox, and not the consumption methodology of Bazuman, and not even the unity-seeking infection of THE Primordial Mycelia.","This was undifferentiation at its source, at its origin!","The light spread across THE Wastes with speed that transcended speed, with reach that transcended reach, with authority that transcended authority. It touched everything. It pressed against everything. It sought to brand everything with ownership!","Noah felt it pressing against his existence as he... spoke.","\" My existence is shielded by Infinite definition that curves through all paths toward my protection.\"","BOOM!","The Geodesic Declaration erupted from him with force that exceeded anything he had previously manifested!","The words curved along geodesic paths, finding the natural geometry of existence, following routes of minimal resistance to establish protection. Blue-gold light blazed around his form as the declaration took shape, crystallizing into a circular shield filled with Infinities that burned with sequential patterns of Countable expression.","The shield formed around him, around the fisherman, around Skoll, around THE Great Usurper.","And the crimson light of undifferentiation crashed against it!","BOOM!","The impact was staggering. Noah felt his Geodesic Declaration straining against pressure that exceeded what he had anticipated. The shield held, yes, but it held through continuous effort rather than effortless supremacy. Each wave of crimson undifferentiation that struck the barrier was met with another wave of Infinite definition curving along geodesic paths to reinforce what had been challenged.","The sequential nature of his Countable Infinity revealed itself as both strength and limitation. His defense arrived endlessly, one reinforcement following another following another, but the crimson light pressed with weight that seemed to exist outside of sequence entirely.","It was undifferentiation from before differentiation had learned to count, from before sequence had learned to sequence!","His barrier held.","But it was heavily strained even as it did its job.","Noah stared down at the crimson eyes that seemed to be occupying nearly all space all around. They gazed back with coldness that exceeded temperature, with patience that exceeded time, with authority that exceeded the frameworks through which authority was typically understood.","Those eyes seemed like...they had seen existence take its first differentiated breath. Those eyes remembered what had been forgotten!","Moments later, a voice emerged from those impossible depths.","\" You are all now slaves of THE Primordial Architect, Horus.\"","...!"]},{"number":4954,"title":"Chapter 4954: Chapter 4953: Truly Live! II","paragraphs":["The words pressed against Noah’s shield with a weight that exceeded the crimson light itself. They were a commandment given form, a will made manifest, and authority that predated the existence of resistance!","\" Toil away and elevate yourselves for Horus. Build your civilizations for Horus. Toil, and Persevere.\"","Noah felt the words trying to find purchase within his existence, trying to establish a brand!","His Geodesic Declaration curved to intercept them, his Infinite definition denying the ownership that Horus sought to impose.","He remained unbranded.","His shield held, but he could feel how close it had been.","Then, in an area extremely far away, a brilliant multicolored light of existence flashed with intensity.","Noah recognized it immediately.","THE Creature.","The light reminded him of the Absolute Effigy he had witnessed in Alfheimr, of the multicolored flames that had surrounded that ancient being’s manifestation. But this was more than mere presence. This was assault and challenge. This was one titan announcing itself to another!","An instant later, the terrifying light of undifferentiation that was pressing down all around became tremendously weaker!","The crimson radiance that had been straining Noah’s Geodesic Declaration suddenly lessened in intensity, its attention divided, its authority contested by something that could actually contest it. His shield stopped straining. His Infinite definitions stopped working so hard to maintain themselves.","Something was fighting THE Primordial Architect, Horus!","And across THE Wastes, a word echoed with implications that exceeded its simple syllables.","\" Defector.\"","The word boomed through existence! It was accusation and recognition simultaneously.","Another instant later, all of THE Wastes of THE Fallout vibrated and trembled!","It was as if reality itself was quaking, as if the foundations upon which THE Wastes had been built were shaking from impacts that exceeded what foundations were designed to withstand. The shaking wasn’t localized. It spread across distances that defied measurement, affecting regions that had no connection to each other except through the vastness of THE Wastes itself.","But truly, it was only the impacts of utterly terrifying things going head to head.","When titans fought, the masses could only huddle and hug each other for warmth, hoping that these titans didn’t have their battle cross where they were and decimate everything.","A conflict played out above mortal comprehension, forces that shaped existence itself clashing in ways that existence itself could barely contain!","The crimson eyes that had bloomed seemingly across all of THE Wastes faded moments later.","The crimson light of undifferentiation faded away.","And THE Wastes routinely continued to shake!","Each tremor spoke of blows being exchanged, of authorities being contested, of powers that exceeded Absolute clashing in combat that most beings would never be able to witness or comprehend. The battle had moved elsewhere, but its echoes remained, vibrating through reality like ripples from stones thrown into an infinite pond.","THE Great Usurper looked around with expression that had finally abandoned his pretense of stillness entirely.","\" What the hell just happened?\"","His voice held genuine uncertainty.","Noah’s reply was calm and somber, his eyes still fixed on a distance where multicolored light continued to clash with something unseen.","\" It should be a battle between monsters. A Primordial Architect and...\"","He didn’t finish his words.","He remembered feeling the glimpse of THE Creature in THE Wastes. He remembered the multicolored light that had flashed with intensity exceeding everything else. He remembered the word that Horus had spoken with weight of ancient accusation.","Defector.","THE Primordial Architect, Horus, the being that had just tried to exert their terrifying influence across these vast distances, had said that word as if he was referring to THE Creature. Then THE Creature had to have defected from the same weavings as Horus.","Which would theoretically make THE Creature a Primordial Architect.","Or rather, in this case, he was not any longer.","Noah still had his other body before THE Creature in Alfheimr as it seemed their conversation was coming to an end. He could always satisfy his curiosity to ask about this.","If THE Creature had once been a Primordial Architect, if he had defected from that classification to become what he was now, what did that mean for the nature of Primordial Architects themselves? What did that mean for the path that lay ahead?","He had many thoughts swirling in his mind, but he looked out across the expanse of THE Wastes all around him as he affirmed something fundamental.","Terrifying monsters were about to run free all around.","Some of them would be as terrifying as THE Five. Some would likely be even grander. At this moment, he couldn’t rule out something at THE Second Scale of Existence having been released from THE Prima Indifferentia. The corruption had opened doors that had been closed since THE First Cause, had awakened things that had been sleeping since before THE Infinite Unfurling.","\"...\"","And yet even with such a thought, even knowing all the problems that were echoing out all around, Noah welcomed it.","All of this was Adversity.","And Adversity would only mean that there would be some pain, but the gain from it would be even grander. The weavings of suffering resolved itself through this simple understanding!","Pain existed to produce growth. Struggle existed to produce strength. The monsters that now roamed free were not merely threats. They were opportunities. They were teachers. They were whetstones upon which he would sharpen himself until his edge could cut through anything.","As he thought about this, he turned over to The Fisherman, Ains, and Skoll.","The very good dog looked at him with eyes that held loyalty exceeding mere instinct. His tail wagged with enthusiasm that seemed almost comical given the apocalyptic events that had just occurred. Skoll didn’t understand the implications of what had happened, didn’t comprehend the horror that had just attempted to brand all existence. He only knew that Noah was here, and that was enough.","Noah smiled slightly at this display of pure, uncomplicated devotion.","\" Let’s unlock your full potential, shall we? My Infinite Seals have not yet expressed themselves through you as now that they are Countable Infinities...\"","He trailed off, considering the implications.","To awaken Skoll, he had infused this very good boy with his 27 Seals. Since then, his Seals had changed tremendously.","Skoll would change as well.","He also looked over to The Fisherman. Ains had witnessed things that most beings would never witness, had survived events that should have ended existences far stronger than his. But his path required more than witnessing. His path required struggle.","He would be sent to THE Yggdrheim.","And THE Great Usurper...","Noah turned to Eckert with eyes that burned with golden Infinity. This being who had grown through stillness, who had progressed through the paradox of non-progression, needed something that his idle path couldn’t provide.","He needed to move, and he needed to act.","He needed to confront rather than avoid.","\"And...let’s go ahead and throw you in the folds of Adversity, shall we?\""]},{"number":4955,"title":"Chapter 4955: Chapter 4954: Truly Live! III","paragraphs":["Noah knew that Observable Existence was getting more and more dangerous.","Today a terrifying Primordial Architect named Horus had made themselves abundantly apparent, their crimson eyes opening across gigaparsecs of space, their brand seeking to claim all who fell beneath their gaze. But others were not as showy. It was certain that as of right now, an unknown number of Formless Terrors, Undivided Ones, and Primordial Architects were running around freely across Observable Existence.","They could be in these very Wastes. They could be in Primordial Realms or in the Wandering Territories or in any of the myriad transformed Folds. The corruption of THE Living Paradox had opened doors that had been sealed since THE First Cause, had awakened things that had slumbered since before THE Infinite Unfurling gave shape to what now existed.","Coming across one, if one wasn’t powerful enough, would be catastrophic.","Because what happened the next time that THE Creature didn’t appear?","If Noah met a Primordial Architect like that entity that had just appeared, even though he was immense and unfathomable right now, would he be able to do anything against them? Or would his fate be to become a slave, branded with that crimson circle, his existence burned away to fuel the elevation of another?","The mere thought caused the sense of defiance to rage within his Infinities!","His tyranny blazed with rejection of such a fate, with denial of such a possibility, with determination that exceeded mere stubbornness!","He burned with determination!","He would not accept a fate written by another. He would write his own destiny with authority that curved along geodesic paths toward whatever end he chose.","He knew he had to keep moving even quicker.","He needed to apply the weavings of Countable Infinities, the Geodesic Weavings of his existence, to many more things! Every aspect of his Civilization that hadn’t yet been elevated needed to be elevated. Every capability that still operated through conventional methodology needed to be transformed. Every portion of his existence that remained vulnerable needed to be reinforced.","And so he began this process as many of his bodies continued to move.","---","In Alfheimr.","In that region where he and THE Creature were conversing with their massive Absolute Effigies displayed, the multicolored stellar space still surrounded them with light that painted everything in shades that shouldn’t have existed. The battle between THE Creature and Horus had moved elsewhere, but echoes of it still vibrated through the fabric of this space, tremors that spoke of titans clashing in distances too vast to comprehend.","Noah looked up toward THE Creature at this moment, his golden Effigy burning with Infinite Undifferentiated Fate that pulsed in sequential patterns of Countable expression. His eyes held curiosity.","\"A Primordial Architect called Horus very loudly just announced himself and acted across THE Wastes. Can you tell me anything about him or others like him that can be expected to be moving across existence right now?\"","His path and the path of THE Creature were different. He wouldn’t ask for help with his own Adversities, wouldn’t seek assistance with battles that were his to fight. But he could always ask for information. Knowledge freely given carried no debt. Understanding offered without strings attached created no obligation.","THE Creature’s multicolored Effigy burned steadily as those swirling eyes fixed upon Noah with light of profundity.","\"Horus is one among many.\"","The statement was simple, but its implications were vast.","\" Primordial Architects are the existences that rose first. The first life forms during the emergence of THE First Cause. Some were born at the First Civilizational Scale of Existence. Others were born at THE Second Scale of Existence.\"","His multicolored flames flickered with patterns of memory being accessed, of history being recalled from eons when existence itself was young.","\" Each one has their own unique nature and existence. Due to THE First Cause and the nature of THE Prima Indifferentia, they remained there as existence had nothing to move them.\"","His voice dropped to something more weighted.","\" For any Primordial Architect, the Scale they were born in would be the Scale that they stay in forever.\"","He paused, letting the implications settle.","\" For them, there was no Adversity. No change. Until...THE Living Paradox changed a few things.\"","...!","There was no Adversity.","Noah thought about these words calmly as the weight of them pressed against his consciousness. The Primordial Architects had been born at their peaks.","They had never struggled to reach heights that were simply their birthright. They had never fought against limitations that they had been created without. They had never known the growth that came from overcoming, the elevation that came from transcending, the transformation that came from becoming something more than what you were.","They were static perfection.","They were completion without journey.","They were the concept of beings created in their final form!","And suddenly, a question crystallized in Noah’s mind with clarity that exceeded his previous understanding.","He looked at THE Creature with a straight face as he spoke.","\"Is that why, from among them, there could be a defector? Someone that choose something different?\"","...!","The question was a heavy one.","If Primordial Architects were born at their Scales and stayed at their Scales forever, if they possessed no Adversity and therefore no growth, then defection wasn’t merely leaving a group.","It was rejecting the fundamental nature of what you were. It was choosing imperfection over perfection. It was embracing the struggle that your existence had been designed to never require.","Toward this question, THE Creature smiled.","It was a calm expression on his noble features, his extraordinary air of power unchanged by the weight of what had been asked. His multicolored flames burned steadily, revealing nothing, concealing everything. He didn’t answer, and he didn’t confirm, nor did he deny.","He simply smiled with the patience of someone who understood that some questions answered themselves given enough time.","His gaze turned in a different direction, as if he was seeing something unfathomably far away that required his attention. His massive Absolute Effigy began to rise, the multicolored flames expanding as he prepared to depart!"]},{"number":4956,"title":"Chapter 4956: Chapter 4955: Truly Live! IV","paragraphs":["But before he left, he turned back to Noah with an expression that had shifted from enigmatic to sincere.","\" Existence is vast and filled with terrors. A friend of ours loves to say this.\"","His voice held warmth that exceeded his usual detached nobility.","\" Existence is also filled with unfathomable possibilities and wonders. Anaximander likes to say this.\"","Something like nostalgia flickered in those swirling multicolored eyes.","\"If things were different. If existence was different... someone like Anaximander would have been much happier to be an explorer. Someone who looked to the stars, no authority within their existence, just curiosity and wonder that would take decades of his time, until he came to rest.\"","His flames dimmed slightly as he continued.","\" Sometimes those existences with limited lifespans, who only live a matter of decades or a few hundred years, sometimes they live grander and more fulfilling lives than those of us who live for millions or billions of years or even eons.\"","The weight of these words pressed against Noah’s consciousness!","\" Sometimes authority and power complicates. Sometimes you can live for eons and not be fulfilled. A long life is not necessarily a fulfilling life.\"","His multicolored eyes fixed on Noah with intensity that exceeded everything previous.","\" So the most that I can tell you, as you go through the Adversity that you are going through, remember to actually live. To actually be alive.\"","\"I played with the demarcation of life and death. Of Living Existences and Dead Existences. Of THE Veil between The Living and The Dead. And I found that at times, The Dead lived more than the living.\"","The words settled with weight that pressed against the fabric of existence itself.","\" Live, Youngest. Live.\"","As he said this, the massive figure of THE Creature began to flicker and disappear.","Noah looked at this being calmly and took in all of his words. This was good advice, a counsel that most beings would spend eons trying to understand. The existential question of what it meant to truly live, to be alive rather than merely existing, to experience rather than merely endure, it was the kind of wisdom in itself.","But... it was already something that he was doing.","He wasn’t only obsessed with progression and achievement. He made sure to have multiple bodies moving within THE Infiniverse, to be farming, to be with his family, to be with his many women. He was living.","But...","Maybe he could live even more.","He thought about everything as he replied to THE Creature.","\" Good luck on all your Adversities. And give my greetings to Anaximander. Until next time.\"","HUUM!","The massive Absolute Effigy of THE Creature smiled. He nodded lightly.","\" Until next time.\"","He paused.","\" And oh, go easy on her.\"","...!","With such words, THE Creature disappeared.","The surroundings flickered in and out of brilliance as Noah found himself back near that mountain in Alfheimr, the twilight of this Primordial Realm settling around his Absolute Effigy with familiarity.","But at this time, the massive manifestation of THE Creature was no longer there.","In that temple atop that grand mountain, THE Creature was no longer there.","As for what his last words meant...","Noah’s expression became cold as ice forming on still water.","He looked down at the mountain, his gaze piercing across many things to land on THE Living Emotive. She stood beside her bonded Undivided One, that great winged lion with its serpent mane, her pink Absolute Effigy burning with manic energy that matched her emotional nature.","The one THE Creature was referring to when he told him to go easy on her was this dumb bitch.","Because at this time, Noah could feel the silent weavings bound to invisible manic emotions that had flowed into the Undivided One beside Emotive undetected. He could perceive them with his elevated Geodesic awareness, could trace their paths with perception that curved along routes of minimal distance to find what was being hidden.","The same weavings were being sent toward him.","THE Living Emotive was actually trying to form another Bond, even though she had told THE Creature that she had utilized her last one on this Undivided One.","She had deceived the entity whose Bond she already possessed. She was attempting to claim Noah as well, to add him to her collection, to make him the fourth of THE Five that she had Bonded.","But of course, existence was filled with liars.","And THE Living Emotive was simply one of the worst ones.","She looked up toward Noah’s massive manifestation with expression that held none of the guilt her actions warranted. Her pink eyes sparkled with manic interest that bordered on obsession. Her lips curved into a smile that seemed designed to disarm, to charm, to manipulate.","She even waved toward him innocently.","As if she wasn’t already enacting a ridiculous and horrendous process right now.","She was a unique existence. She had bonded with three of THE Five and survived to tell the tale. She was successful enough to have THE Creature tell Noah to go easy on her. And she now tried to make Noah the fourth one she was bonded to, her invisible emotional weavings reaching toward him with persistence that exceeded shame.","Against such a being...","Noah’s massive Absolute Effigy raised its hand.","The motion was slow and deliberate, his golden manifestation shimmering in the skies of Alfheimr with light that painted the twilight in shades of blue and gold. His fingers spread wide, his palm turning to face the mountain below where THE Living Emotive stood with her innocent smile and her waving hand.","\" Begone.\"","The word emerged with weight that exceeded mere sound.","And then his hand moved forward.","The golden manifestation of his palm swept through the air of Alfheimr with speed that exceeded what its slow beginning had suggested. It wasn’t a punch. It wasn’t a strike meant to obliterate. It was a backhand slap, the kind of casual dismissal that one might give to an annoying insect, the kind of contemptuous gesture that spoke of disdain exceeding anger!","His hand arrived before THE Living Emotive.","Her eyes widened with shock that exceeded anything her previous expression had contained. Her smile froze on her face as she realized what was happening, as she understood that her manipulations had been perceived, as she comprehended that her innocent act had fooled no one!","She hadn’t expected this at all.","The impact...was devastating!"]},{"number":4957,"title":"Chapter 4957: Chapter 4956: Truly Live! V","paragraphs":["BOOM!","The cheek of her Absolute Effigy distorted from the backhand slap, the pink flames that comprised her manifestation compressing and warping under force that exceeded anything she had prepared to receive.","The shape of her face bent inward where Noah’s golden hand made contact, her features twisting with impact!","And because her Absolute Effigy was connected to her physical body, her actual cheek deformed as well.","Her flesh compressed. Her bones cracked. Her existence registered damage that couldn’t be hidden behind manifestation.","Then she flew.","Her body flung backward like a spinning ragdoll, rotating end over end as the force of Noah’s backhand launched her away from where she had been standing. She spun through the air of Alfheimr with speed that exceeded what her Absolute classification should have permitted, her pink Effigy flickering and wavering as it struggled to maintain coherence.","The force of her being thrown was so much that she flew upward rather than backward.","She ascended toward the peak of the mountain, toward the temple where THE Creature used to reside, her spinning form leaving trails of pink light in her wake. And then she smashed into that ancient structure with impact that made the entire mountain tremble!","BOOM!","Stone shattered. Walls collapsed. The temple that had housed one of the most powerful beings in Observable Existence crumbled around the form of THE Living Emotive as she crashed through it without slowing.","When the dust settled, she lay in the ruins with expression that had lost all its previous confidence.","Her state was shocked and haggard.","Her pink Effigy flickered weakly around her battered form, the manic energy that had defined it now stuttering and uncertain. Her physical body was worse. Her cheek was swollen and purple where Noah’s slap had connected. Her lip was split. Blood ran from her mouth in streams that spoke of damage exceeding surface injury.","She opened her mouth to speak, perhaps to protest, perhaps to plead, perhaps to attempt manipulation one more time.","And all her teeth fell out.","They tumbled from her bleeding gums like offerings being rejected, like prayers being denied, like the symbols of her confidence being stripped away one by one. Her mouth was bloody and empty, her jaw aching with pain that her Absolute regeneration would eventually heal but that currently defined her existence.","She could barely rise up.","But she managed to turn her bloodshot eyes toward Noah, toward the massive golden Effigy that still loomed in the skies of Alfheimr with expression of absolute coldness. She was about to say something, about to attempt words through her ruined mouth, about to try one more manipulation despite everything that had just occurred.","Then she saw his extremely cold and domineering gaze.","She saw the complete lack of mercy in those golden eyes.","She saw what would happen if she pushed further.","She bit her lips with her bleeding gummy jaws, the pain of that action adding to the pain she already felt. And she said nothing.","Noah looked at her coldly.","This was him going easy on her.","The other option would have been to collapse her existence completely. To unmake everything she was with Geodesic Negations that would have found every aspect of her being and denied it. To crystallize her with Infinite definition until nothing remained but a statue of what she had been. To harvest her entirely and add her accumulated authority to his own foundations.","THE Creature had asked him to go easy on her.","So he had.","He did make sure to record this entire scene, to weave this display of existence so that it could be shown to others. Malphas, that old butler who had once been a servant of this woman, might want to see her humiliated. If that loyal existence told Noah that he still wanted to see her brought lower, or to be the one doing the humiliation himself, then Noah would simply come back and arrange it.","But for now, as a favor to THE Creature who already had a Bond with this wretched thing, he let her off easy!","His actions were heavy enough that even the Undivided One she had bonded with on the mountain didn’t dare to raise its eyes to look toward Noah. The great winged lion with its serpent mane pressed itself flat against the ground, its massive form trying to appear as small as possible, its entire demeanor screaming...","Bro, I’m not even here!","I’m just a small lion!","\"...\"","Noah’s eyes remained grand and imperious as he reflected on his conversation with THE Creature. The words about living, about being alive rather than merely existing, echoed through his consciousness with weight that exceeded their simple syllables. He would consider them. He would apply them. He would ensure that his path included experience as well as progression.","But first, he had work to do.","He turned his gaze from the ruined temple toward a distant area in the same Primordial Realm. There, THE Primordial Chaos resided with his isolated territory, his cautious nature having kept him separated from the events that were unfolding across Observable Existence. There was where Noah’s illusory manifestation had been conversing with him. There was where he needed to have another conversation.","About THE Primordial Mycelia.","About the possibility that Chaos himself might be compromised without knowing it.","About the warning that THE Mnemonic Leviathan had given regarding the Keys of Civilization.","But first, he had to make sure that his new Immensities of Infinities were spread out across as much of his existence as possible. Every capability needed to be elevated. Every weaving needed to be transformed. Every aspect of what he was needed to incorporate the Geodesic architecture that his Countable Infinity had unlocked!","For this, he closed his eyes and focused on his mental mindscape.","In its endless seas of blue and gold, RUINATION was already there. Her form burned with blue-gold light that matched his own, her hair extending into infinite data points, her eyes swirling with analysis that had been preparing for this moment since his epiphany had transformed his path.","She was ready to seamlessly define the changes he was implementing.","And so, the work continued!"]},{"number":4958,"title":"Chapter 4958: Chapter 4957: The Spread of Infinities! I","paragraphs":["Cultivation was hard.","If it were easy, there wouldn’t be so many old scheming monsters who did so much just to make convoluted plans, genocide of countless beings, and who knows what else just for their advancement.","Countless cultivators had spent eons just to take a single step forward. Countless more had spent those same eons and achieved nothing at all. The path of progression was littered with the corpses of those who had tried and failed, who had struggled and been found wanting, who had reached for heights beyond their grasp and been broken by the attempt.","Cultivation for Noah was also hard but... in a different way.","With his Infinity currently being Countable and Geodesic Weavings falling under his grasp, he had to do as much as he could to incorporate these ideas of Infinity into every aspect of his existence.","Without breaking himself.","Because this was what he was genuinely feeling could be possible as he played with Countable Infinities and Geodesic Weavings. The power was immense. The potential was heavy. But integrating it incorrectly could shatter everything he had built, could collapse the careful architecture of his Civilization into something that couldn’t sustain its own weight.","Geodesic Weavings were unique as even he had to go over them a few times to truly understand what he was playing with.","Simply, Geodesic was... the shortest path between two points.","Easy!","The shortest path!","If he wanted to go, let’s say, from one end of THE Prima Indifferentia to another end, one might think the shortest path is a straight line through the middle. But if the middle, if that straight line is swampy and filled with Undivided Ones and Primordial Architects, crossing it means it’s actually the slowest and most difficult path.","So the actual shortest path would involve going around the edges.","The feature of his Infinities, Geodesic Weavings... they extend infinitely while taking the shortest possible path through existence itself.","The examples he had carried out so far were how Embodiments could be blocked and Apophasis could be resisted, but Geodesic Weavings curved around obstacles, finding the natural line that connected his authority to his target with minimal distance and maximum efficiency.","That was the shortest path.","Now, he had begun to apply this understanding to many more things as his existence was buzzing with transformation. In his mindscape, RUINATION began to outline exactly what he was accomplishing!","Her blue-gold form brightened as streams of data flowed through her infinite hair, her eyes burning with analysis that had been processing his changes in real-time. Around her, constructs of pure light began forming, diagrams that would make the abstract tangible.","| Elevation of THE Civilizational Instinctus to Geodesic Classification.|","A massive construct appeared showing Noah’s Civilizational Instinctus as a pulsing core of awareness, with four distinct functions branching outward like limbs of a great tree.","|Your Civilizational Instinctus now operates through Countable Infinity and Geodesic principles. Each of its four functions has been transformed by the architecture of your Infinite Formless Depth.|","The four branches in the diagram began to glow sequentially as RUINATION prepared to explain each one.","...!","|Primary Function Elevated: Geodesic Autonomous Response.|","The first branch illuminated, showing a representation of threats approaching Noah from multiple directions. In the old diagram, defensive responses traveled in straight lines to meet them. In the new diagram, the responses curved gracefully, finding paths that intercepted dangers before they could fully form.","|Previously, your Autonomous Existential Response reacted to threats before conscious processing. Now it reacts along paths that curve through existence to intercept dangers before they fully manifest. Your Civilization moves not merely with purpose transcending thought but with purpose following the natural geometry of reality itself.|","The diagram showed threats dissolving before they could reach their intended destinations, each one met by defensive expressions that had found the optimal route to interception.","|When threats approach, your response extends infinitely to meet them. The response arrives sequentially and endlessly, each reaction followed by another, creating continuous defensive expression that compounds rather than dissipates.|","The visual demonstrated this compounding effect, showing single threats being met by waves upon waves of defensive authority, each wave arriving along the same optimal curve.","|Enemies experience not a single counter but an Infinite sequence of counters arriving along natural lines of existence.|","...!","| Secondary Function Elevated: Geodesic Manifestation Observation.|","The second branch illuminated, and the diagram shifted to show an enemy’s Civilizational Manifestation, its walls and pillars and foundations displayed in intricate detail. But overlaid upon that architecture were countless curved lines connecting every element to every other element.","|Previously, you perceived Civilizational Manifestations as architectural constructs surrounding entities. Now you perceive the natural pathways connecting every aspect of those constructs. You see not merely walls and pillars but the curves along which authority flows between them.|","RUINATION gestured, and the diagram rotated to show different angles of the same Manifestation, each angle revealing new pathways that hadn’t been visible before.","|When observing an enemy’s Civilization, you perceive infinite routes extending through their architecture. Each curve represents a potential avenue for your authority to travel. Each line reveals how their Civilization naturally directs force and where that direction creates openings.|","The diagram highlighted several openings that only became visible when the curved pathways were perceived, gaps in the architecture that straight-line observation would have missed entirely.","|You see their foundations as a map of possibilities rather than static structure.|","...!","| Tertiary Function Elevated: Geodesic Structural Analysis.|","The third branch illuminated, and the diagram zoomed in on a single crack in the enemy’s architectural wall. But from that crack, curved lines extended outward, connecting to pillars, to foundations, to the very core of the Civilization being observed.","|Previously, you identified vulnerability points within observed Manifestations. Now you perceive the natural connections linking those vulnerabilities to each other. A single weakness is no longer isolated. You see how striking one weakness leads naturally toward striking others along paths of least resistance.|","The diagram demonstrated this principle, showing a single strike at the crack rippling outward along the curved connections, each ripple becoming a new strike at a new weakness.","|Your analysis reveals cascading vulnerability chains. When you identify a crack in an enemy’s wall, you simultaneously perceive the connection linking that crack to the pillar it supports, to the foundation beneath the pillar, to the core Civilization that foundation upholds.|","The cascade in the diagram accelerated, showing the entire enemy architecture collapsing in sequence as one weakness led to another led to another.","|One strike along these natural paths becomes infinite strikes arriving sequentially at every connected weakness.|","...!"]},{"number":4959,"title":"Chapter 4959: Chapter 4958: The Spread of Infinities! II","paragraphs":["| Quaternary Function Elevated: Geodesic Targeted Undifferentiation.|","The fourth branch illuminated, and the diagram showed an attack being launched at the identified crack. But instead of stopping at impact, the attack continued along the curved pathways, leaving undifferentiated potential in its wake.","|Previously, your attacks directed at weaknesses carried additional effectiveness through undifferentiation. Now those attacks extend infinitely along natural curves, undifferentiating everything they touch along their path. The attack follows the connection linking weakness to all related aspects of the enemy’s existence.|","The diagram showed pillars forgetting their shape, walls dissolving into formless potential, foundations losing their memory of what they had supported.","|A single strike of Targeted Undifferentiation begins at the identified weakness and curves endlessly through the enemy’s Civilization, undifferentiating each connected element in sequence. Pillars forget they were pillars. Walls forget they were walls. Foundations forget they were foundations.|","The entire enemy architecture in the diagram collapsed into undifferentiated proto-potential, unable to remember or reconstitute what it had been.","| The undifferentiation spreads along natural paths until no differentiated structure remains.|","...!","A new construct formed beside the first, this one showing THE First Tongue in its elevated state.","| Elevation of THE First Tongue to Geodesic Expression.|","The diagram displayed words being written, but instead of remaining static on their surface, the words extended outward in curved lines that traveled through the fabric of existence itself.","|Your mastery of THE First Tongue now incorporates Countable Infinity at its foundation. Every word you speak extends infinitely. Every sentence curves along natural paths toward its intended effect. THE First Tongue has become a language of endless expression following the geometry of existence.|","RUINATION’s eyes burned brighter as she continued.","|When you compose Inscriptions, the letters do not merely form on the page. They extend infinitely in the direction of their meaning, traveling through reality along routes that connect concept to manifestation with minimal resistance.|","The diagram showed an Inscription being written, its letters blazing with blue-gold light that curved outward toward distant targets, finding them regardless of obstacles between.","|Your written authority travels not in straight lines but in natural curves that find their targets regardless of what stands in the way.|","...!","| Elevation of THE 27 Seals of Absolute Tongue.|","Twenty-seven symbols manifested around the diagram, each one representing a Phoneme that Noah had mastered. Each symbol pulsed with light that extended outward in its own unique curve.","|Each of your 27 Phonemes now resonates with Countable Infinity. When spoken or written, each Seal extends infinitely along its own path, its sound and meaning curving through existence to affect all instances of what it represents.|","The diagram showed multiple Seals being invoked simultaneously. Their curved extensions didn’t travel in parallel but intersected and merged at natural points of convergence.","|The Seals no longer require conscious combination to produce compound effects. When multiple Seals are invoked, their paths naturally intersect and merge along curves of minimal distance.|","The intersection points in the diagram blazed with light that exceeded what any individual Seal could produce.","|A declaration using three Seals produces not merely the combination of three effects but the infinite intersection of three extensions, creating effects that exceed what deliberate combination could achieve.|","RUINATION’s form solidified as she delivered the final assessment.","|Your position as Native Speaker of THE First Tongue has been elevated. You speak words that extend endlessly along natural paths, affecting everything they curve toward in sequence that never terminates.|","...!","Noah absorbed everything that RUINATION had displayed, his consciousness processing the diagrams and manifestations with comprehension","Every aspect of his existence buzzed with the integration of these principles. His Civilizational Instinctus pulsed with awareness that curved through reality rather than merely observing it. His mastery of THE First Tongue burned with potential that extended infinitely rather than terminating at impact!","It was a glorious thing as he felt it all...across his bodies.","The light of Countable Infinity rippled outward from Noah’s body in THE Interstices, passing through the boundaries of his divided existence, flowing across the vastness of THE Infiniverse until it settled upon his body standing in the Early Veiled Shore.","Here, everything felt different.","Noah felt his existence buzzing as more and more parts of him responded to the Countable Infinities and Geodesic Weavings.","The integration wasn’t simple.","There were complex parts of him where he had to figure out exactly how to weave in these Countable Infinities in a way that worked, how to mix Geodesic Weavings in a way that didn’t allow anything to break. He was trying to change many things about himself simultaneously, and each change affected every other change in ways that required careful calibration.","One wrong integration could shatter foundations he had spent eons building.","One misaligned weaving could collapse structures that his Civilization depended upon!","\"Careful now,\" he murmured to himself, feeling the delicate balance of forces within his existence. \"Break something here, and it echoes everywhere...\"","A break of infinity would be catastrophic!","His eyes lit up as he found his Countable Infinities and Geodesic Weavings flowing smoothly in another particular area!","And to really allow it to flourish, this body in THE Infiniverse would make the breakthrough.","His body in the Early Veiled Shore!","---","The fields stretched before him in radiant splendor.","Noah stood at the edge of cultivation zones that he had prepared across cycles of dedicated investment. The soil glowed with blue-gold light that pulsed in sequential patterns. Each field contained different configurations of planted Infinities, each one an experiment in what Countable expression could produce when given form through agriculture.","He had been a Monarch. A conqueror. An architect of Civilizations.","Now he would be a farmer.","The results were beginning to emerge.","Beside him, THE Infiniverse stood in her human manifestation. Her form was beautiful, and her eyes held the depths of countless realms.","She smiled at the field.","These were her lands. This was her territory. And Noah was making them bloom with Infinities that elevated everything they touched.","Moments later, RUINATION’s illusory figure formed beside them both!","Her blue-gold form shimmered into existence with hair extending into infinite data points and eyes burning with analysis. She looked at the fields, then at Noah, then smiled.","| Master managed to integrate two major areas, one relating to your people, the other relating to farming. I’ll quantify the former first...The New Capability of Bestowal of Bounded Infinity.|","...!"]},{"number":4960,"title":"Chapter 4960: Chapter 4959: The Spread of Infinities! III","paragraphs":["A construct of light formed above the fields, displaying Noah’s Depths as containers of endless sequential expression.","|Your Depths now exist at Countable Infinity. This grants you the authority to bestow fragments of your Infinite nature upon those who follow your Civilization. These fragments are designated as Bounded Infinities. They contain genuine Infinite properties while existing within limitations that your unbounded Countable Infinity does not possess.|","The diagram showed fragments being separated from Noah’s Infinity, each fragment glowing with the same blue-gold light but contained within visible boundaries that his own Infinity lacked.","| Bounded Infinity operates like an interval with endpoints that nevertheless contains endless values within. Your followers would receive Infinity, but Infinity with a ceiling defined by your authority. They can grow endlessly within their bounds while never exceeding limits.|","\" So they get Infinity... \" Noah said, watching the diagram with calculating eyes. \" But my Infinity, my rules...my ceiling.\"","This would be nice for Amser Modred and others like him. Beings controlled under the banner of his infinity!","He nodded.","\" Good .\"","...!","| Classification: Seeded Infinity.|","The diagram shifted to show one of these fragments being planted within a follower’s Civilization, taking root like a seed in fertile soil.","|When you bestow Bounded Infinity upon a follower, you plant a Seed of Infinity within their Civilization. This Seed grows according to their efforts and cultivation, producing Infinite expressions that regenerate and compound within the boundaries you have set.|","The seed in the diagram sprouted, growing into structures that filled the follower’s foundations with endless potential.","|A follower bearing Seeded Infinity experiences regeneration that exceeds what finite Civilizations can produce. Their foundations recover from damage with speed that approaches endless. Their authority replenishes faster than it can be depleted under normal circumstances. Their growth occurs along trajectories that finite beings cannot match.|","RUINATION’s eyes flickered with additional data.","|However, Seeded Infinity cannot exceed its Bounded nature. Where your Countable Infinity extends endlessly in sequence, their Bounded Infinity loops back upon itself when it reaches its ceiling. Where your Infinity grows without limit, theirs grows until it reaches the boundary you established, then densifies within that boundary rather than expanding beyond it.|","...!","|Hierarchy of Seeded Infinity.|","Three tiers manifested in the diagram, each one representing a different level of bestowal.","| You may establish three tiers of Seeded Infinity based on the boundaries you set.|","The first tier illuminated.","| First Tier: Cyclical Infinity . The smallest bestowal. Followers receive Infinity that repeats in cycles, regenerating endlessly but returning to its starting point with each completion. Their power grows through repetition rather than expansion. Suitable for those newly bound to your Civilization.|","The second tier illuminated.","| Second Tier: Partially Bounded Infinity . A greater bestowal. Followers receive Infinity with a starting point but no ending point within their bounded range. They can extend endlessly in one direction while remaining anchored to the foundation you provide. Suitable for trusted members of your Civilization.|","The third tier illuminated brightest of all.","| Third Tier: Bounded Countable Infinity . The greatest bestowal short of your own unbounded nature. Followers receive Infinity that operates identically to your Countable Infinity but exists within a container defined by your authority. Suitable for Absolutes beneath your banner, and those you trust most completely.|","He smiled a brillaint smile that held no cruelty. Just practicality.","Those in Yggdrheim would be granted the most trusted tier of Infinity, others would follow!","...!","|Effects on Follower Civilizations.|","The diagram expanded to show followers at each tier using their bestowed Infinity in combat.","|Followers bearing Seeded Infinity gain access to limited Geodesic expressions. Their Embodiments and Apophasis begin curving toward targets along natural paths rather than traveling in straight lines of conventional authority.|","Three examples manifested side by side.","|Cyclical Infinity bearers produce Curving Embodiments that follow partial geodesic paths before dissipating.|","|Partially Bounded Infinity bearers produce Extending Embodiments that follow geodesic paths further before reaching their limits.|","|Bounded Countable Infinity bearers produce Near-Geodesic Declarations that function almost identically to your own Geodesic Weavings, lacking only the unbounded extension that your full Countable Infinity provides.|","RUINATION’s form brightened.","|All bearers of Seeded Infinity experience accelerated cultivation. Where finite Civilizations require eons to progress through Depths, Seeded Infinity compresses this timeline dramatically. The endless regeneration within their bounds allows for growth that finite foundations cannot sustain.|","...!","|Connection to Your Authority.|","The diagram showed lines of connection flowing between Noah and every bearer of his Seeded Infinity, a network of authority that bound them all to his Civilization.","| All Seeded Infinity derives from your Countable Infinity. This creates permanent connection between your Civilization and those who bear your Seeds. Their growth contributes to your growth. Their harvest flows partially toward you. Their achievements elevate your foundations alongside their own.|","\" They grow, I grow, \" Noah said. \" They harvest, I harvest...\"","|Should a bearer of Seeded Infinity fall in combat, the Bounded Infinity they carried returns to you in full. Nothing is lost. The Seed you planted simply comes home.|","|Bestowal Methodology.|","The diagram showed the process of investment, Infinite Everythings flowing from Noah into recipients at varying quantities.","|To bestow Seeded Infinity, you must directly invest your Infinite Everythings into the target’s Civilization. The tier of Seeded Infinity granted depends on the quantity invested and the capacity of the recipient to bear Infinite nature.|","Oh?","|Cyclical Infinity requires minimal investment and can be granted to many simultaneously.|","|Partially Bounded Infinity requires moderate investment and should be granted selectively.|","|Bounded Countable Infinity requires substantial investment and should be reserved for those whose elevation directly serves your path.|","RUINATION’s assessment concluded this section.","|Your current harvest production allows for widespread bestowal of Cyclical Infinity, selective bestowal of Partially Bounded Infinity, and rare bestowal of Bounded Countable Infinity. As your Depths advance toward Uncountable Infinity, your capacity to bestow will increase proportionally.|","...!","The diagram faded as RUINATION turned her attention to the fields themselves, where things had begun to bloom!","He wanted to tell her to breathe, that she was going through too much information! But she simply charged ahead.","| That...was the first part. Granting Infinities to your followers. The second part...is your sometimes neglected path of a farmer.|","...!","The fields before Noah pulsed with light that exceeded what they had held moments before. Something was emerging from the soil he had saturated with his authority.","|Your investment of Infinities into the soil of the Early Veiled Shore has begun producing results that exceed conventional sacred herb cultivation. When Countable Infinity saturates the earth, when Undifferentiated Temporal Infinity accelerates growth across compressed eons, the vegetation that emerges carries properties that finite farming could never produce.|","Noah watched as three distinct types of growth began rising from different sections of his cultivated fields.","| Three classifications of Infinite Sacred Herbs have begun taking root . Each requires different cultivation methodologies and produces different effects upon harvest.|","RUINATION’s voice held warmth that exceeded her usual analytical tone.","|Your dream... of becoming a farmer has evolved beyond mortal agriculture. You now cultivate Infinity itself.|","\" Finally ,\" Noah breathed. \"... Finally!\"","HUUM!","| First Classification: THE Bounded Lotus of Sequential Eternity.|","In the nearest field, something extraordinary emerged from the saturated soil!"]},{"number":4961,"title":"Chapter 4961: Chapter 4960: The Spread of Infinities! IV","paragraphs":["Noah watched as a lotus began to bloom with petals that unfolded in perfect sequence.","The first petal opened, revealing blue-gold light within. Before that petal finished settling, the second petal began opening. Then the third. Then the fourth. The progression continued endlessly, the lotus never finishing its bloom but simply continuing to produce.","It was beautiful.","Not beautiful like conquest was beautiful, or like power was beautiful. Beautiful like...watching something grow. Beautiful like patience rewarded.","Beautiful like the simplest truth in existence: plant something, tend it, and it flourishes.","Oh!","|This herb grows in spiraling patterns that mirror the sequential nature of Countable Infinity. Its petals unfold one after another in endless progression, each petal containing the seed for the next. The lotus never finishes blooming. It simply continues producing petals in sequence.|","Noah stepped forward and reached toward the lotus!","His fingers touched one of the completed petals. The warmth exceeded physical temperature. The weight exceeded the delicate appearance. Within it, he could sense Bounded Countable Infinity already formed and waiting.","A Seed ready to be planted in whoever consumed it.","He plucked the petal carefully.","The lotus didn’t diminish. It simply continued blooming, producing more petals to replace what he had taken, the sequence uninterrupted by his harvest.","\" One petal, \" he said, examining it. \" One follower elevated to Bounded Countable Infinity. Without spending my own reserves.\"","He looked at the field of lotuses. Dozens of them. Each one blooming endlessly.","| Effects Upon Consumption: A follower who consumes petals from THE Bounded Lotus of Sequential Eternity receives Bounded Countable Infinity directly integrated into their Civilization . The petals bypass the need for your direct investment, carrying pre-formed Seeds of Infinity that take root within the consumer’s foundations.|","|One lotus can produce enough petals to elevate dozens of followers to Bounded Countable Infinity without depleting your own reserves.|","|This herb transforms your capacity to bestow Seeded Infinity from individual investment to mass cultivation. Your followers can be elevated through agriculture rather than direct authority transfer.|","...!","| Second Classification: THE Convergent Root of Density Absolute.|","Noah moved to the second field, where something very different was occurring!","Instead of growing upward, the plants here grew downward. He could sense roots extending deep into the soil, burrowing along paths that curved toward concentrations of Infinite authority he had buried during preparation.","The roots didn’t spread wide. They dove deep, following the shortest paths through the earth to find and compress every fragment of Infinity within their reach.","|This herb grows downward rather than upward, its roots extending into the soil along geodesic paths that curve toward concentrations of Infinite authority. Where it finds such concentrations, it wraps around them and draws them inward, compressing Infinity into density that exceeds its original configuration.|","Noah knelt and reached into the soil, his authority allowing him to perceive what was happening beneath the surface!","The roots had wrapped around units of Infinite Observable Harvest he had buried. They were squeezing those units, compressing them, forcing sequential expressions closer and closer together until gaps began filling.","|What enters the root as sequential Countable expressions emerges as something denser. Something approaching the spaces between sequences.|","One root had completed its compression!","Noah grasped it and pulled, feeling resistance that spoke of weight exceeding what the root’s size suggested. When it emerged from the soil, it glowed with density that made his eyes narrow.","This was... what he needed for his own advancement.","Advancing others was great and all, but he needed something for himself!","He held the root, feeling the concentrated Infinity within it pressing against his perception. Years of saturation, compressed into something he could consume in an instant.","\" The lotus elevates my followers ,\" he said slowly. \" The root elevates me.\"","He looked between the two fields.","|Effects Upon Consumption: You experience saturation acceleration at whichever Depth you direct the root’s compressed authority toward. The root has already performed the work of filling gaps between your sequential Infinite expressions. Consuming it introduces pre-densified Infinity directly into your foundations, aiding your advancment towards your progression from Countable toward Uncountable Infinity.|","|Each root consumed represents compressed eons of saturation occurring instantaneously. Your advancement toward Uncountable Infinity becomes a matter of cultivation rather than endless waiting.|","...!","First, it was a Lotus, and second, it was a root!","And the third and final wonder to bloom in his farming fields of infinity?","| Third Classification: THE Divergent Bloom of Infinite Variation.|","Noah moved to the third field, where chaos reigned in beautiful form!","Plants grew in every direction simultaneously, their branches splitting endlessly as they extended toward the horizon.","No two branches followed the same path. Flowers bloomed at random points along each branch, and no two flowers held identical colors or shapes. Some were blue. Some were gold. Some were colors that shouldn’t have existed.","Each one unique.","Each one different.","Each one a possibility he hadn’t conceived.","|This herb grows outward in all directions simultaneously, its branches splitting endlessly as they extend toward the horizon. No two branches follow the same path. No two flowers that bloom upon those branches hold identical properties. The herb embodies divergence, spreading its Infinite nature across every possible configuration.|","Noah reached toward a flower that caught his attention!","It was crimson and gold, its petals arranged in spirals that seemed to twist in directions his perception couldn’t quite follow. When he plucked it, he felt something shift in his awareness.","A glimpse of possibility that his current state couldn’t normally access.","\" Interesting ,\" he murmured, examining the flower.","He plucked another flower, this one blue and silver!","Its properties were different entirely. This one... offered a temporary glimpse of what Uncountable Infinity would feel like.","A preview of the Boundary he was working toward.","\" Even more interesting.\"","|Effects Upon Consumption: Each flower provides a different effect based on the variation it embodies. Some flowers enhance specific Geodesic Weavings. Some flowers reveal weaknesses in enemies that your current perception cannot detect. Some flowers temporarily elevate a single Depth toward sensations of Uncountable Infinity, granting glimpses of what full advancement would feel like.|","RUINATION’s voice held something approaching awe.","|Most critically, certain rare flowers that emerge from extreme divergent branches contain properties you cannot predict. These flowers may provide breakthroughs in understanding that accelerate your path. They represent possibilities that your sequential Countable nature cannot generate on its own but that divergent cultivation can access.|","|It is chaos and randomness harnessed through Infinite cultivation, producing boons that deliberate planning cannot achieve.|","Noah looked at the field of divergent blooms, each flower a gamble, each harvest a surprise.","He smiled.","\" The lotus for followers. The root for advancement. The bloom for surprises.\"","He turned to look at all three fields together.","|Integrated Cultivation Methodology.|","RUINATION’s final construct displayed all three fields working in harmony, their combined production flowing toward Noah’s Civilization.","|The three classifications of Infinite Sacred Herbs work in harmony when cultivated together.|","|THE Bounded Lotus provides elevation for your followers, creating armies bearing Seeded Infinity without depleting your personal reserves.|","|THE Convergent Root provides density for your own advancement, compressing harvest into saturation that advances you toward Uncountable Infinity.|","|THE Divergent Bloom provides variation that neither you nor your followers can generate through sequential cultivation alone, offering breakthroughs and surprises that accelerate paths in unexpected directions.|","Her recommendation came with weight.","|Establish dedicated cultivation zones for each classification within the Early Veiled Shore. Maintain continuous investment through THE Infinite Observable Harvest. Apply Undifferentiated Temporal Infinity to compress growth cycles. Harvest regularly and consume strategically based on your current priorities.|","RUINATION’s form solidified as she delivered the final assessment, her eyes meeting Noah’s.","|Your role as THE Genesis Monarch now includes dominion over Infinite agriculture. What you plant determines what your Civilization becomes. What you harvest determines how quickly you and your followers advance toward heights that finite existence cannot reach.|","...!","Noah stood among his fields with lotus petals in one hand and convergent roots in the other, with divergent flowers blooming in every direction around him.","He had always dreamed of becoming a farmer, and THE Creature had reminded him to live! To truly live!","\" All those beings out there fighting and scheming and killing for scraps of power...\" he said aloud, looking at his fields with satisfaction that exceeded anything conquest had given him.","While others were out there killing for power, he could simply grow it here!","He...did not necessarily need to find Undivided Ones or Formless Terrors or Primordial Architects to kill.","Only if he needed big jumps of Harvests as he was still receiving a steady stream!","All he truly needed was time to grow.","He laughed.","THE Infiniverse smiled beside him.","RUINATION’s illusory form flickered with brilliance.","And the harvest...had only just begun!"]},{"number":4962,"title":"Chapter 4962: Chapter 4961: The Spread of Infinities! V","paragraphs":["The light of inherited Infinity flickered across dozens of struggling forms, blue-gold scaffolding holding together existences that would otherwise dissolve into the endless undifferentiation of THE Yggdrheim.","Noah watched them all.","His son Henry stood at the center of the gathered beings, his Surface Depth burning brighter than it had before his arrival here. The inherited Infinity that had awakened within him fought constantly against the realm’s assault, each moment a battle between definition and dissolution that would continue for as long as he remained in this space.","Around Henry, the others struggled with varying degrees of success.","Barbatos maintained her form through sheer fury, her Necromancy finding no anchor in undifferentiation but her will refusing to accept dissolution. Adelaide’s existence flickered like a candle in wind, her features blurring and reforming as she fought to remember what she looked like!","Titano roared with confusion and pain, his massive form shrinking and expanding as undifferentiation pressed against him from every direction. The simple-minded Titan did not understand what was happening, only that it hurt, only that his existence was being challenged in ways that no enemy had ever challenged it before.","Sigrid, THE Living Order, frowned with concentration that bordered on desperation. Order and undifferentiation were fundamentally opposed, and every moment she spent in THE Yggdrheim felt like poison seeping into her foundations.","Khor’s Hunger bloomed in response to threat, her diminutive form blazing with authority that exceeded her size. She consumed the undifferentiation that pressed against her, turning dissolution into fuel for her own existence.","THE First Farmer stood beside her, his Effort burning brightly!","THE Emperor Penguin waddled in place with dignity that refused to acknowledge how close to collapse he actually was. This wingless, talentless bird maintained his noble bearing even as his edges dissolved and reformed in cycles that would eventually exhaust his capacity to regenerate.","Even Little Bobby, this cockroach, was here facing this Adversity!","The Land Lifeforms clustered together. Heidrun bleated with indignation. Malphas attempted composure that cracked with every wave of undifferentiation. Yoshinami’s many legs scrambled for purchase on reality that kept shifting beneath them.","An Arch Lich cackled even as he dissolved, finding humor in his own potential unmake that only the truly mad could appreciate.","They were all struggling.","They were all suffering.","And Noah had been watching long enough!","\"You have all done well to survive this long,\" he said, his voice pressing against THE Yggdrheim itself with authority that made the realm’s undifferentiation pause in its assault. \" But surviving is not enough. You need to thrive.\"","He raised his hand.","In his palm, lotus petals materialized with light that exceeded anything the scaffolding had provided. Blue-gold radiance blazed from petals that had been harvested from THE Bounded Lotus of Sequential Eternity, each one containing pre-formed Seeds of Infinity that would transform whoever consumed them.","The petals were beautiful.","They spiraled with patterns that mirrored the sequential nature of Countable Infinity, each curve leading to the next in progression that could be observed and tracked even as it extended toward endlessness. The light they emanated pushed back against THE Yggdrheim’s undifferentiation with force that made the realm itself seem to recoil.","\" What I hold in my hand is something I have cultivated,\" Noah said, \" THE Bounded Lotus of Sequential Eternity. Each petal contains Bounded Countable Infinity. When you consume them, you will no longer be finite beings struggling against dissolution.\"","He paused.","\" You will be... Infinite.\"","...!","BOOM!","The gathered beings stared at the petals with expressions that ranged from desperate hope to confused uncertainty. They did not fully understand what Bounded Countable Infinity meant.","They only knew that Noah was offering something, and that something might end the suffering they had been enduring since their arrival.","Noah scattered the petals!","They flew outward from his palm like seeds carried by wind that should not have existed in THE Yggdrheim. Each petal found its target with precision. One petal landed before Henry. Another before Barbatos. Another before Adelaide. Another before Athena.","Petals fell before Titano, before Sigrid, before Khor, before THE First Farmer. They landed before THE Emperor Penguin, before the Land Lifeforms, before Riya, before Bob, before the cackling Arch Lich!","Every being that Noah had brought to this realm received a petal that glowed with blue-gold light containing transformation beyond anything they had experienced.","\" Consume them ,\" Noah commanded. \" And become something more.\"","Henry was the first to act.","His hand, still flickering between stability and dissolution, reached for the petal that had landed before him. His fingers closed around it with grip that exceeded what his current state should have allowed. And then he brought it to his lips and consumed it.","The effect was immediate!","HUUM!","Blue-gold light exploded from within Henry’s existence as the Bounded Countable Infinity contained in the petal took root in his foundations. The Seed of Infinity that had been pre-formed within the petal found fertile soil in his Civilization, sprouting with speed that exceeded natural growth, spreading through his existence with patterns that mirrored his father’s own Infinite nature.","His dissolving edges solidified entirely!","Nepotism began to bloom at its finest!","Oh!","The flickering that had characterized his form since arrival ceased as Bounded Countable Infinity established itself throughout his being. His features became distinct and stable in ways that the scaffolding alone had never achieved. His blue-gold hair blazed with color that exceeded what it had held even before his arrival in THE Yggdrheim.","He was no longer a finite being struggling against undifferentiation.","He was Infinite.","Bounded, yes . Limited by ceilings that his father’s authority had established. But Infinite nonetheless, possessing regeneration and growth that finite Civilizations could never match.","Prompts bloomed in Noah’s awareness as RUINATION documented the transformation occurring in his son.","|Transformation Detected: Henry Osmont|","|Previous Classification: Finite Surface Depth cultivator with inherited Infinite potential.|","|Current Classification: Bounded Countable Infinity bearer at Surface Depth.|","|Transformation Details: THE Bounded Lotus of Sequential Eternity has integrated Seeded Infinity into subject’s foundations. Subject now possesses genuine Infinite properties within boundaries established by your authority. Regeneration approaches endless. Foundation recovery exceeds finite parameters. Growth trajectory has been fundamentally altered.|","|Subject’s Assertions will now produce Curving expressions that follow partial geodesic paths. Subject’s cultivation timeline has been compressed dramatically. Subject can now survive THE Yggdrheim’s undifferentiation through Infinite regeneration.|","|Assessment: Henry Osmont has crossed the threshold from finite to Infinite. His Bounded Countable Infinity will grow according to his efforts within the boundaries you have established. He remains beneath your unbounded nature but now possesses genuine claim to Infinity.|","...!","Around Henry, the others began consuming their petals!"]},{"number":4963,"title":"Chapter 4963: Chapter 4962: The One Percent I","paragraphs":["Barbatos brought the petal to her lips. Blue-gold light exploded from within her as Bounded Countable Infinity took root, her Necromancy finding anchor in Infinite regeneration that undifferentiation could not overcome.","Adelaide consumed her petal with grace that belied her desperation.","Titano consumed his petal with the simple trust of someone who did not question what his Brother offered. Blue-gold light transformed his massive form as Bounded Countable Infinity spread through a Titan’s foundations. His roars of confusion became roars of triumph as his existence stabilized entirely.","\" Haha, I knew Brother would take care of me!\"","...!","Sigrid, Khor, and all others did the same.","The Arch Lich consumed his petal while still cackling, his madness now Infinitely regenerating alongside his existence.","Many prompts came and went that Noah passed through.","|Mass Transformation Complete|","|All subjects have successfully integrated Bounded Countable Infinity through consumption of petals from THE Bounded Lotus of Sequential Eternity.|","|Current Status: All subjects now possess genuine Infinite properties within boundaries established by your authority. Their regeneration approaches endless. Their foundation exceeds finite parameters. Their growth trajectories have been fundamentally altered.|","|THE Yggdrheim’s undifferentiation can no longer threaten dissolution. Subjects will still experience pressure from the realm, but that pressure will serve as cultivation stimulus rather than existential threat.|","...!","Noah watched as his gathered people stabilized entirely.","They were no longer struggling against dissolution. They were no longer fighting moment to moment for survival. They were no longer drowning in undifferentiation that exceeded their capacity to resist.","They were breathing.","The terrifying weavings of undifferentiation still pressed against them from every direction. THE Yggdrheim had not become less hostile. The realm still sought to return all differentiated things to formless potential. But now, with Bounded Countable Infinity burning in their foundations, they could somewhat handle it.","They still had Adversity!","But they could do it.","Noah’s voice carried across THE Yggdrheim with weight that pressed against every Infinite being present.","\" This is the last time I aid you in your Adversity.\"","...!","His words settled with implications that exceeded their simple statement.","\" With Infinities in your hands, what you can do is endless. Your potential approaches endless.\"","He paused, letting them absorb this truth.","\" But potential is meaningless without actualization. You are Infinite now, but you are Infinite at Surface Depth, or Intermediate Depth, or Fundamental Depth. You are not Absolute.\"","His eyes swept across the gathered beings with intensity that exceeded anything he had displayed during their suffering.","\" And anything less than Absolute will likely get you one-shotted in the vastness of existence.\"","The words were harsh.","They were true!","\" Today, a Primordial Architect named Horus announced himself across Existence. There are others like him. There are Formless Terrors and Undivided Ones waking across THE Prima Indifferentia. There are threats emerging that your current Depths cannot comprehend, let alone survive.\"","He folded his hands behind his back.","\" So you... will roam THE Yggdrheim. You will find the resources that this realm contains. You will use the pressure of undifferentiation as cultivation stimulus. And you will become Absolute as quickly as possible.\"","His voice hardened.","\"I will not hold your hands. I will not protect you from threats that your Infinite regeneration can handle. I will not coddle you with safety that prevents growth.\"","\"You have Infinity now. Use it. Become Absolute.\"","He paused.","\" Survive. Persevere. Become something that existence cannot ignore.\"","...!","---","Noah finished setting up the adversity for his people as his other bodies continued to move.","He had already done a lot. THE Yggdrheim now held beings transforming from finite to Infinite. THE Infiniverse held fields of sacred herbs producing elevation and density and variation.","His other body in THE Interstices continued writing new Inscriptions with Geodesic Weavings that would define his Civilization’s future while he talked with Amser Modred.","But... he wanted to see if it was possible to bring all of these changes to THE Numerical Sovereignty.","As unrealistic as it was, could the weavings of mathematics he had begun playing with be granted similar musings of Infinities? Of Geodesic Weavings? Could multiplication and exponentiation curve along paths of minimal distance? Could division extend infinitely toward their targets?","As he embarked on this idea, his existence became focused.","Well, part of his consciousness became focused.","His Absolute Body with the Infinite Undifferentiated Fate in Alfheimr had taken a step to disappear from the mountain where Emotive lay with all her teeth knocked out.","Infinities had struck her, but she would regenerate eventually. She would recover her smile and her manipulations and her endless attempts to bond with beings far beyond her station.","But she would remember this lesson for a long, long time.","Well, if she was among those who will survive this coming week and month without being collapsed.","Noah’s body shimmered across the distance of Alfheimr, his Absolute Vision of Existence allowing him to cross vast stretches instantaneously. He proceeded to meld with his illusory consciousness that had been near THE Primordial Chaos this whole time, the projection becoming real, substance replacing shadow.","Beside him, Ul’moreth, THE Big Stepper, had continued to wait with patience that exceeded his usual demeanor.","The hairy Absolute stood at attention with seriousness.","---","< THE Primordial Chaos, Abaddon. The Age Between Ages, The First Age of Infinity.>","Abaddon stared at the intriguing figure of THE Youngest as his illusory body became real.","A genuine existence now stood beside his follower, the hairy Absolute, Ul’moreth.","Where moments before there had been projection and presence, there was now flesh and blood and Civilization burning with golden Infinite Undifferentiated Fate that exceeded what projections could display.","The region around them had transformed during Abaddon’s presence here.","Rivers of obsidian chaos flowed through what had once been standard territory of Alfheimr, dark currents that carried entropy and possibility in equal measure. The signature weavings of this Primordial Realm, its twilight and ancient mountains and forests that had stood since THE First Cause, all of it had become backdrop to something older.","Something more fundamental.","For Abaddon, this was normal.","As THE Primordial Chaos, everywhere that he remained long enough became a place that would gradually change to be surrounded by Chaos and entropy. The obsidian rivers were his signature. The churning darkness was his presence made manifest. The sense that anything could happen, that probability itself bent toward uncertainty in his vicinity, that was simply what it meant to stand near a being who embodied the raw potential from which all differentiation had originally emerged.","After all, that was the true nature of things!","Order was temporary. Structure was borrowed time. Everything eventually returned to the chaos from which it came.","At this time, Abaddon watched as THE Youngest patted his hairy follower with casual familiarity.","\" Visit my little place called THE Yggdrheim for a moment. I should be okay.\"","The words were simple. The dismissal was confident.","Ul’moreth nodded with a serious gaze that held concern despite the directive. His eyes flickered between THE Youngest and Abaddon with calculation. But in the end, he was a follower, and his Monarch had given instruction.","He disappeared.","The only ones left behind were Abaddon and THE Youngest."]},{"number":4964,"title":"Chapter 4964: Chapter 4963: The One Percent II","paragraphs":["Abaddon had been thinking about doing many things. He had sensed all the events that had just occurred across Observable Existence.","But instead of acting on any of these observations, he asked a different question.","\" Your weavings just intertwined with THE Creature?\"","His voice carried the weight of rivers that flowed through realities yet unformed.","\" He is an interesting guy, isn’t he?\"","Abaddon asked such a question while he thought of THE Creature.","Whenever he did look at THE Youngest and THE Creature, he couldn’t help but think of how alike they were. Not in power, though THE Youngest was growing at rates that defied conventional understanding.","Not in methodology, though both seemed to approach existence with calculation that exceeded many things.","It was something in their eyes.","The first time Abaddon had met THE Creature was in THE Prima Indifferentia.","At that time, THE Creature looked like something that had just undergone a rebirth into another form. His manifestation had been unstable, flickering between configurations as if he hadn’t yet decided what he wanted to be. Abaddon considered him younger at that moment, as his own Depth had been higher than THE Creature’s at that time. At that time.","But it seemed to be on a technicality.","Anyways, at that time, the eyes of THE Creature reminded Abaddon of something he couldn’t quite identify.","Now he knew.","They reminded him of the eyes of THE Youngest.","That same burning certainty. That same sense that existence itself was merely raw material waiting to be shaped according to will.","It was a gaze of pride and arrogance that was dangerous.","At this time, THE Youngest smiled and nodded at Abaddon’s question.","\" Powerful beyond measure. A very interesting guy.\"","His golden eyes held appreciation.","\" But I was curious about you a bit more.\"","Abaddon’s obsidian chaos swirled with interest at this statement. THE Youngest had been keeping him back from attacking the infection spreading across existence for some time now.","\" And I wanted to ask you about probabilities.\"","Probabilities?","Hah!","Chaos was filled with probabilities and possibilities! Every moment contained infinite potential outcomes. Every action spawned countless branches of what-could-be. Every decision collapsed wave functions of maybe into singular expressions of is.","There was so much to be done right now. THE Entity spread further with every passing moment. THE Primordial Mycelia’s infection claimed more beings with every breath. And yet THE Youngest wanted to discuss probabilities?","But THE Youngest spoke still.","His form shimmered with blue-gold flames as Infinite Undifferentiated Fate manifested visibly around his existence. The golden light pressed against Abaddon’s obsidian chaos without conflict, two fundamental forces acknowledging each other without competing.","\" Let’s use an Undivided One as an example.\"","His voice held the weight of something being constructed.","\" Let’s say there was something called Bazuman. An Undivided One of tremendous power who had existed since before THE Infinite Unfurling. A being of undifferentiation and consumption who believed himself invincible because nothing had ever truly threatened his existence.\"","Abaddon listened with attention that exceeded casual interest. THE Youngest was building toward something.","\" Now let’s say that despite all of Bazuman’s power, despite all of his accumulated authority and consumed existences and invincible reputation, there existed a one percent probability that collapse was coming for him.\"","THE Youngest paused.","\" One percent. Ninety-nine roads lead to Bazuman’s continued dominance. But one road, just one, leads to his complete and utter annihilation.\"","His golden eyes fixed on Abaddon with intensity that exceeded the hypothetical nature of the question.","\" Would Bazuman take this one percent seriously even though the chance of it happening was so low? Would he ignore that single percentage point because ninety-nine others favored his survival? Or would he do anything, absolutely anything, to make sure that one percent didn’t even exist?\"","...!","Abaddon raised his brows and blinked.","What was THE Youngest up to?","His reply didn’t take long. This was, after all, a question that touched upon the very nature of what he represented.","\"A percent chance is still a percent chance.\"","His voice deepened with authority that predated THE Infinite Unfurling.","\"It is as if there are one hundred roads. Ninety-nine roads will lead to the same result. But that one road is still there. It exists. It waits. It holds potential that the other ninety-nine cannot negate through mere numerical superiority.\"","The rivers of obsidian chaos around them churned with emphasis as Abaddon continued.","\" You see,Youngest, this is what many beings fail to understand about probability and chaos. They look at percentages and see safety in large numbers. They look at one percent and see something so small that it can be dismissed. They calculate their odds and feel comfort in ninety-nine percent certainty.\"","He shook his head slowly.","\" But certainty is illusion. And probability is not prediction. It is description of possibility space, nothing more.\"","The obsidian rivers began flowing in patterns that demonstrated what he was explaining.","\" Everything that can happen will happen given sufficient time and iteration. Every possible outcome exists within the probability space of every moment. The one percent is not less real than the ninety-nine percent. It is merely less frequent in a single sampling.\"","His eyes fixed on THE Youngest with intensity that matched what he had received.","\" But collapse is not a single sampling. Collapse is permanent. If Bazuman faces one hundred threats across his existence, and each threat carries one percent chance of his annihilation, then across those hundred encounters, the cumulative probability of collapse approaches certainty rather than remaining negligible.\"","The patterns in the obsidian rivers became more complex.","\" Furthermore, entropy favors the unlikely. Chaos tends toward maximum disorder. The state space of existence is not static. It evolves, it shifts, it transforms in ways that can take that one percent and make it ten percent, or fifty percent, or absolute certainty without warning.\"","Abaddon’s presence seemed to expand as he delivered the core of his philosophy.","\" This is what chaos teaches those who truly understand it. The improbable is not impossible. The unlikely is not avoidable. And the one percent that seems negligible today may be the guaranteed outcome tomorrow because you chose to ignore it rather than address it.\"","He paused, letting his words settle like sediment in the obsidian rivers.","\"I have watched civilizations fall because they calculated their survival at ninety-nine percent and dismissed the remaining percentage as acceptable risk. I have witnessed Absolutes collapse because they believed their foundations too strong to be threatened by improbable outcomes. I have seen beings older than THE Infinite Unfurling unmade because they failed to account for the one road that led somewhere other than their continued existence.\"","His conclusion came with weight that pressed against the very fabric of Alfheimr.","\" So yes. Regardless of how low the percentage is, it has to be taken care of. It has to be addressed. It has to be eliminated if elimination is possible. Because if you leave that one percent existing, if you allow it to remain within your probability space, then entropy will find it. Chaos will favor it. And what seemed impossible will become inevitable.\"","\" The one percent must be erased, or it may be guaranteed to happen.\"","...!"]},{"number":4965,"title":"Chapter 4965: Chapter 4964: The One Percent III","paragraphs":["After he finished this lengthy discourse on the nature of probability and chaos, Abaddon looked at THE Youngest.","THE Youngest was looking at him with bright eyes.","As if this answer was exactly what he was looking for.","As if Abaddon had just walked himself into something that had been carefully constructed before this conversation even began.","Because moments later, THE Youngest seemingly became focused with intensity that exceeded everything previous. His golden flames burned brighter. His Absolute Effigy manifested visibly, massive golden fire filling the skies of Alfheimr above them.","\" Then, O Primordial Chaos.\"","His voice carried weight that pressed against Abaddon’s very existence.","\" What if there existed a one percent, unlike what we believe, that your weavings of existence have already been compromised by THE Entity? By THE Primordial Mycelia?\"","The question hung in the air with implications that exceeded anything Abaddon had anticipated.","\" What if you have already been infected without even knowing? That the unity THE Entity seeks has already found purchase within you? That your very confidence in your uncompromised state is itself evidence of compromise?\"","THE Youngest’s golden eyes burned like twin suns.","\" What if you are actually her greatest move and triumph? The most powerful piece she has claimed without anyone, including yourself, realizing it?\"","His voice hardened.","\" Would you do anything you could to clear and erase even this one percent? Even if it meant doing something contrary to your weavings? Even if it meant accepting help you would normally reject?\"","His flames pressed against Abaddon’s chaos with intent that exceeded mere presence.","\" Even if it meant taking in my Infinities?\"","BOOM!","Abaddon frowned.","In the surroundings, rivers of chaos began to churn with violence that exceeded their previous flowing patterns. Obsidian currents crashed against each other. Entropy spiked in ways that made reality itself uncertain about its own configuration.","What was this now?","He, Abaddon, was compromised?","His gaze became extremely heavy as he looked toward THE Youngest. The rivers of obsidian chaos around them churned with violence that reflected his internal state, currents crashing against each other with force that made reality itself uncertain about its configuration.","THE Youngest continued speaking with voice that pressed against Abaddon’s existence.","\" You said it yourself.\"","Golden flames burned brighter around the young Absolute’s form.","\" A percent chance is still a percent chance. The one percent is not less real than the ninety-nine percent. The improbable is not impossible. The unlikely is not avoidable. And the one percent that seems negligible today may be the guaranteed outcome.\"","THE Youngest’s eyes held no mockery. No triumph at using Abaddon’s own philosophy against him. Only the cold calculation of someone presenting a logical conclusion that could not be easily dismissed.","\" The one percent must be erased, or it may be guaranteed to happen.\"","He paused, letting those words settle like stones into still water.","\"I believe with a high degree of certainty that THE Primordial Mycelia has taken purchase within your existence. But due to your nature, due to the vastness and complexity of your Chaos, she is doing everything she can not to reveal it.\"","His voice hardened.","\"Until her hooks are irreversible within you. They are not irreversible yet. And my Infinities are things that THE Primordial Mycelia cannot touch. If you allow my Infinities to flow inside you, I can scorch any weavings of infection and purify completely. I can take care of that one percent.\"","THE Youngest’s golden flames pressed against Abaddon’s obsidian chaos with intent that exceeded mere presence.","\" Which I remind you, your own philosophy says that as unlikely as it is, sometimes it is the only path.\"","...!","Abaddon looked at THE Youngest with a complex gaze.","Inside of him, his Civilization burned as he cycled ancient and Primordial Chaos that others could not even fathom. He dove deep into the foundations of what he was, searching through currents that had existed since before THE First Cause, examining every aspect of his existence for signs of infection or compromise.","And he found nothing.","He only found his glorious, unmitigated Chaos.","Rivers of entropy flowing in patterns that only he could perceive. Probability spaces that bent and shifted according to his will. The raw potential from which all differentiation had originally emerged, pure and untouched and entirely his own.","But THE Youngest would also not say foolish things for the sake of saying foolish things.","When it came to this infection, when it came to THE Primordial Mycelia and the unity she sought to impose upon all of existence, the Infinities of THE Youngest were one of the only solutions that actually worked.","So the offer was genuine.","The methodology was sound.","The logic was impeccable.","But just like THE Youngest and THE Creature had their pride and arrogance, Abaddon’s was even grander.","He was THE Primordial Chaos.","He had existed since before THE Infinite Unfurling gave shape to Observable Existence. His chaos witnessed the birth of differentiation itself, had been present when the first concepts separated from the formless potential that preceded them. His Chaos was fundamental to reality in ways that most beings could not comprehend.","And truly, he did not think that one percent chance THE Youngest talked about even existed.","His Chaos was too grand to be grasped by another. Too vast to be infected without his knowledge. Too fundamental to be compromised by an entity that was itself merely a product of existence rather than a shaper of it.","But again, the words of THE Youngest were not simply foolish ones.","Two things could both be true without them competing against reality.","Abaddon could be uncompromised, his Chaos pure and untouched as he believed it to be.","And THE Youngest could be correct that the possibility of compromise needed to be addressed regardless of how unlikely it seemed.","So this was a problem.","And it had to be corrected.","It seemed... that the time of staying still had come to an end.","Abaddon’s obsidian rivers began flowing in new patterns as decision crystallized within his existence. His presence expanded, his Chaos pressing outward with authority that exceeded anything he had displayed during their conversation. The backdrop of Alfheimr seemed to fade entirely as his power filled the space around them.","When he spoke, his voice carried weight that pressed against THE Youngest’s golden flames with force that made them flicker.","\"I have observed the Civilizations of many Absolutes across eons uncounted.\"","His words emerged slow and deliberate, each one settling into existence with permanence that exceeded mere sound.","\"I have seen walls built from crystallized authority and pillars forged from compressed Depths. I have witnessed foundations that spanned territories and architectures that defied the very concepts they were constructed upon.\"","The rivers of chaos around them stilled as he continued.","\" Grand things. Impressive things. Things that made their bearers believe themselves complete.\"","He paused.","\" But the Civilizations of Primordial Architects are not walls or pillars or foundations. They... are not things that can be observed and understood through observation.\"","His obsidian eyes fixed on THE Youngest with intensity that exceeded everything previous.","\" They are the reasons that walls exist. The logic that permits pillars to stand. The mathematics underlying foundations themselves.\"","...!","\" Where an Absolute builds a house, a Primordial Architect builds the concept of shelter. Where an Absolute forges a weapon, a Primordial Architect forges the principle of harm.\"","His voice deepened with implications that pressed against reality itself.","\" Their Civilizations do not exist within existence. Existence exists within their Civilizations.\"","The weight of these words settled across the space between them like a verdict being delivered.","\" This is why they cannot be fought as others are fought. This is why they cannot be overcome as others are overcome.\"","Abaddon rose to his full height, his presence filling the skies of Alfheimr with obsidian chaos that blotted out the twilight entirely.","\" To defeat a Primordial Architect, one must first become something that their Civilization did not account for.\"","His final words emerged with conviction that exceeded mere philosophy.","\" One must become impossible.\"","...!","Abaddon’s gaze became something ancient and terrible as he looked down at THE Youngest one final time.","\"I have always strove to become impossible and do the impossible.\"","His Chaos began coiling around his form with intent that spoke of departure and violence in equal measure.","\" This Entity. This thing that is a product of a Primordial Architect. I will face it with this same impossibility.\"","His eyes held no gratitude for THE Youngest’s offer. Only the determination of a being who had decided upon his path and would not be moved from it.","\" Your Infinities are not needed, Youngest. My... Chaos is sufficient unto itself. If I did not believe this, would I truly be following my Way? Would I truly be...Chaos?\"","...!","And with such words, THE Primordial Chaos, Abaddon, disappeared.","The obsidian rivers that had filled this region of Alfheimr vanished alongside him, the signature weavings of this Primordial Realm reasserting themselves in his absence. The twilight returned. The ancient mountains became visible once more. The forests that had stood since THE First Cause reclaimed their presence.","Everything returned to normal.","Except that THE Primordial Chaos was now moving toward confrontation with THE Primordial Mycelia.","Noah’s body here was silent.","He didn’t chase and he didn’t call out. He didn’t attempt to convince Abaddon further with words that had already proven insufficient.","Because he was always where THE Primordial Chaos was going.","He already had a body looking straight at THE Secretive Eon, the target of THE Primordial Chaos who was currently on the move. His consciousness maintained awareness across multiple locations simultaneously, observing the pieces on the board as they shifted toward collision.","\" Pride ,\" Noah said aloud to the empty space where Abaddon had stood. \" It makes fools of us all eventually.\"","...!","He had failed in convincing THE Primordial Chaos before he even began. He knew he might. So maybe his only mistake was proceeding ahead to do this anyways.","The argument had been sound. The logic had been impeccable. The methodology had been proven through Amser Modred’s successful cure. Everything had been aligned perfectly to demonstrate that accepting Noah’s Infinities was the safest path forward.","But oh!"]},{"number":4966,"title":"Chapter 4966: Chapter 4965: That One Percent IV","paragraphs":["Of all the pivotal events that ushered in THE First Age of Infinity, none proved more consequential than a conversation between a young one and an old one in the twilight reaches of Alfheimr.","What followed was inevitable. Chaos, in its pride, went forth to confront Unity.","From that confrontation, an unfathomable darkness bloomed. It spread across Observable Existence with weight that made THE Infinite Unfurling seem a gentle awakening.","But darkness, no matter how unfathomable, exists only to give way to brilliance.","And the brilliance that emerged from those depths exceeded anything that came before. It had to. For that is the nature of Adversity. That is the purpose of struggle. That is why the young one allowed the old one to walk toward a fate that could have been avoided.","Some lessons cannot be taught. They must be lived.","Some brilliance cannot emerge without darkness to precede it.","—THE Grimoire of Infinite Lexicons","Entry VII: On the Collision of Fundamentals,","Recorded by THE Genesis Monarch","—","In THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","Noah’s Absolute body of Infinite Hunger stood with stellar crimson brilliance that painted the ancient forum in shades of blood and conquest. His form was adorned in a crimson-blue emperor’s robe that flowed with patterns suggesting appetite given visual form, the fabric shifting between colors as if it couldn’t decide whether to consume or command.","This was the body that held his Derivative Civilization of Infinite Hunger at Absolute Depth.","This was the body that burned with appetites that finite existence could never satisfy.","Beside him stood THE Primordial Paradox, surrounded by obsidian-gold Paradoxes that flickered between states of being and not-being simultaneously. His brilliant features held none of their usual intellectual detachment. His gaze was cold as he looked at THE Secretive Eon and the four Strategoi standing behind her.","Glossikos. Khaotikos. Ontikos. Paradoxos.","The four Strategoi who had once represented the pillars of THE Agora’s authority now stood in synchronized formation behind the slender woman who had claimed them. Their eyes held the calm of beings who no longer questioned their purpose. Their postures held the readiness of those who knew exactly what was coming.","Noah’s gaze flickered at this time.","He looked up.","As if he could see something coming that nobody else could perceive. His crimson eyes fixed on a point in the sky above THE Agora with intensity that exceeded casual observation.","THE Secretive Eon noticed his upward gaze but did not follow it. Instead, she spoke with voice that carried the warmth of someone genuinely confused by the hostility she faced.","\" We truly don’t seek an antagonistic relationship.\"","Her words settled across THE Agora with weight that pressed against everyone present.","\" Even you, after all you have done against us, after you have taken away Temporal from us when he was so close to salvation... we don’t really hate you.\"","Her expression held something that might have been sadness. Something that might have been pity.","\" We just wonder how we can help you see.\"","She looked toward Noah as she said this, and seeing his gaze still fixed upward as if he was looking for something, she only continued!","\" We know Civilization has at its core, working together. One day, in the near future, I hope for you all to remember this. That whatever may come, the ultimate goal is to work together.\"","Her voice grew softer.","\" Even you, THE Youngest of THE Five. You could understand all of this right now if you so choose.\"","She took a step toward him.","\" You have your Infinities that make you immune, yes? Take my hand. Let me just show you how the rest of us feel when we have countless Civilizations connected. Your Infinities will still protect you, yes?\"","Her hand extended toward Noah with gesture that seemed genuinely inviting.","\" So just give me your hand to show you. It would make things so, so clear.\"","...!","THE Secretive Eon stretched her hand out toward Noah.","And Noah did not even look down to see it.","His crimson eyes remained fixed on the sky above THE Agora, on the point where something vast was approaching with speed that exceeded comprehension. When he spoke, his voice carried weight they could not fully grasp.","\" All actions are choices. There is no going back if you do this. It will be... all out war.\"","HUUM!","Whatever could he be referring to with these words?","Even THE Primordial Paradox frowned as he looked toward Noah, wondering what he was missing. His brilliant mind raced through possibilities, calculating scenarios, attempting to determine what THE Youngest had perceived that he himself could not.","There was no going back if they did this.","What was this referring to?","THE Primordial Paradox did not know.","But THE Secretive Eon and the four Strategoi behind her smiled a calm smile as if they knew exactly what Noah meant. Their expressions held no surprise. Their postures held no uncertainty. They had been waiting for this. They had been preparing for this.","Everything that had occurred since THE Secretive Eon’s arrival at THE Agora had been leading to this exact moment.","The four Strategoi moved!","They came up beside THE Secretive Eon with synchronization that spoke of unity exceeding mere coordination. Two of them, Glossikos and Khaotikos, raised their hands and placed them on her back with pressure that suggested support against immense weight.","Two others, Ontikos and Paradoxos, knelt down and held her legs as if they wanted to shoulder them against something that would press down with force beyond imagination.","Four Absolutes seemingly gave their support to THE Secretive Eon!","Their Civilizations burned with authority being channeled directly into her form. Their foundations pulsed with power being offered freely. Their existences blazed with sacrifice being made willingly for something they believed in completely.","THE Secretive Eon’s outstretched hand going toward Noah changed directions.","She instead looked up in the same direction where Noah was looking, her eyes fixing on the point in the sky that had held his attention. Her knees bent with preparation for impact. Her hands raised, both of them now, palms facing outward as if she was ready to receive something terrifying!","Her smile never wavered.","Her calm never broke.","She had been waiting for this.","And an instant later, the region above THE Agora was torn apart!","BOOM!","Raging Embodiments and Apophasis of obsidian chaos roared out from the rupture in reality, dozens of them screaming with entropy given voice. The sky split with violence that exceeded anything THE Agora had witnessed since THE First Cause. Probability itself seemed to collapse as certainty fled from the presence descending through the breach.","THE Primordial Chaos had arrived!","Abaddon descended through the torn sky like a meteor composed of endings themselves. His form was that of a human titan, massive beyond mortal scale, his proportions perfect in ways that spoke of fundamental truth given flesh. His face held utmost confidence that bordered on certainty. His features displayed no doubt, no hesitation, no concern for what awaited below.","And his eyes carried boundless Primordial Chaos.","Obsidian depths swirled with patterns that predated THE Infinite Unfurling, with currents that had existed since before differentiation learned to differentiate, with entropy that remembered when existence was merely potential waiting to become actual.","These eyes quickly glanced at Noah, THE Primordial Paradox, and all others below. And then...","This being made his descent at terrifying speed!","He was surrounded on all sides by dozens of Embodiments and Apophasis, obsidian expressions of his Chaos that screamed ahead of him like heralds announcing the end of everything. They carved through the air of THE Agora with force that made the ancient forum tremble. They painted reality in shades of entropy that spoke of things returning to formless potential.","But Abaddon himself was the true weapon.","He shot down like a missile toward THE Secretive Eon, channeling all his power and boundless Chaos through his body and into his single outstretched obsidian fist. That fist seemed like a hammer of endings. That fist contained enough force to collapse Civilizations. That fist held the concentrated authority of a being who had existed since before existence learned what it meant to exist.","Everything... seemed to play out in slow motion.","Noah observed all of this happening with crimson eyes that missed nothing. He watched Abaddon descend with impossibility made manifest. He watched THE Secretive Eon brace for impact with palms raised and smile intact. He watched the four Strategoi burn with existence being offered to support what was about to occur.","The terrifying fist of THE Primordial Chaos thundered down!","THE Secretive Eon’s raised palm met it!","The impact should have destroyed everything. The collision should have unmade THE Agora entirely. The force should have rippled across Observable Existence with consequences that would take days to fully manifest.","The Absolutes supporting her burned with righteous existence as they channeled everything they had into helping her withstand what should not have been withstandable!","And this whole time during this impact, this moment where Chaos met Unity with force that exceeded comprehension, this instant where impossibility confronted inevitability...","THE Secretive Eon and the four Strategoi...were smiling absolutely brilliantly."]},{"number":4967,"title":"Chapter 4967: Chapter 4966: Existential Intermission- THE Five","paragraphs":["Before THE Five, there were THE Four.","This is known, and this is recorded. This is truth that predates THE Infinite Unfurling and persists through every transformation that Observable Existence has undergone since its first differentiated breath.","THE Creature. THE Primordial Paradox. THE Primordial Chaos. THE Living Paradox. And for a time, before betrayal rewrote the hierarchy of claim, there was only a single bearer of Paradox rather than two.","What is less known, what is debated in whispers among those who dare to debate such things, is the nature of what these beings claimed. For they did not merely accumulate power as lesser Absolutes accumulate power. They did not simply grow strong through cultivation and conquest and consumption. They laid claim to something far more fundamental.","The Four Aspects of the Oldest Paradox in Existence.","Chaos. Existence. Paradox. And THE First Tongue.","They are not simply expressions of power that beings can wield like weapons or wear like armor. They are the Keys of Civilization itself. The foundational truths upon which all differentiation rests. The architecture that permits reality to be real rather than formless potential waiting endlessly for definition that never comes.","How does one claim such a thing? How does a being, even a being of tremendous power, lay hold of concepts so fundamental that existence itself depends upon them?","For three of THE Four, the answer lies in origin.","THE Creature emerged from circumstances that even the oldest records do not fully describe. Some say he was born in THE Prima Indifferentia during the moment when Existence first learned to distinguish itself from non-existence.","Some say he defected from something older, something that predates even the Primordial Architects, and in that defection, he became the living embodiment of Existence choosing to be. His claim to the Aspect of Existence was not made through conquest. It was made through being. He is Existence examining itself. He is differentiation celebrating its own emergence. His claim was easy because there was no separation between the claimer and the claimed.","THE Primordial Chaos emerged similarly, though his origin lies in different territory. Where THE Creature embodies Existence, Abaddon embodies the potential from which Existence emerged. He was present when probability first learned that it could collapse into actuality.","He was there when the endless maybe became the singular is. His claim to the Aspect of Chaos was made in the moment before moments existed, when all things were equally possible and nothing had yet been chosen. He did not claim Chaos. He remembered being Chaos before Chaos became something that could be claimed.","THE Primordial Paradox’s claim is perhaps the most elegant among the original three. He emerged at the intersection where truths learned they could contradict themselves and still remain true. He was born in the space where logic first broke and discovered that breaking made it stronger rather than weaker.","His claim to the Aspect of Paradox was made through the very nature of claiming. For to claim Paradox is itself paradoxical. To hold contradiction is to be held by it. To master impossibility is to be mastered by its implications.","For these three, most Architects believe their claim was birthright. They did not take their Aspects. They simply were their Aspects, and in being, they held. Who knows how accurate that is.","But then came THE Living Paradox.","The apprentice. The student. The one who learned at THE Primordial Paradox’s feet and absorbed the teachings of contradiction until he understood something his master had not anticipated. That paradox, true paradox, permits the impossible. And if the impossible is permitted, then an apprentice consuming the claim of his master is not merely possible.","It is inevitable.","The records do not fully describe how THE Living Paradox ate the Aspect of Paradox from THE Primordial Paradox. Some Architects muse it occurred during a moment of trust. Some say it occurred during a moment of teaching. Some say it occurred across eons of subtle consumption that THE Primordial Paradox did not perceive until the eating was complete.","What is known is that THE Living Paradox now holds what his master once held. The Aspect of Paradox answers to him rather than to the being who originally claimed it. And THE Primordial Paradox, brilliant and ancient and wise beyond measure, was left with echoes of what he once possessed fully.","This is why some call THE Primordial Paradox THE Primordial rather than THE Living. He is the origin. He is the source. But he is no longer the primary bearer. The paradox of his existence is that he taught too well, and in teaching, he created the instrument of his own diminishment.","Even if he has now returned, can he truly and fully reclaim Paradox from someone who has changed it so much?","For ages beyond counting, there were only three Aspects claimed and one Aspect waiting.","THE First Tongue remained unclaimed.","This was not because beings did not try. Many Absolutes, Undivided Ones, and Primordial Architects across the eons attempted to lay hold of the linguistic architecture that underlies all Civilizational expression. They studied the letters that existence used to write itself into being. They practiced the words that transformed concept into reality. They devoted eternities to understanding the grammar of creation.","All of them failed.","THE First Tongue rejected every claimer as insufficient. The Aspect of linguistic architecture required something that mere power could not provide. It required something that mere age could not accumulate. It required something that mere understanding could not achieve.","It required Infinity.","And then came THE Genesis Monarch.","He was born so long after everything was established that his arrival seemed impossible. The First Cause was ancient history. THE Infinite Unfurling was settled fact. THE Prima Indifferentia had been sealed away behind boundaries that most believed eternal. The great conflicts that shaped Observable Existence had concluded or settled into stalemates that seemed permanent.","What business did a newly emerged being have claiming an Aspect that had rejected claimers since before THE Infinite Unfurling?","The answer was simple.","The answer was everything.","THE Genesis Monarch possessed what no other being in Observable Existence possessed. Boundless potential that did not merely approach infinity but actually achieved it. Where others had vast power that seemed infinite but eventually found its limits, he had power that genuinely extended forever in sequential progression that could be counted but never completed.","And on the day he fully decided that his Way was the Way of Mana, on the day he committed his existence entirely to THE First Tongue and accepted no alternative, the Aspect that had waited since before THE Infinite Unfurling finally found its bearer.","The linguistic architecture of reality recognized in his Infinity something it had been waiting for across all the eons of rejection. A speaker who could speak forever. A writer who could write without end. A bearer whose capacity to express would never exhaust itself no matter how much expression was required.","Thus THE Four became THE Five.","Thus the oldest arrangement in Observable Existence was altered by one who had no right to alter it.","Thus the Keys of Civilization found their fourth bearer, and the path toward THE Second Scale began to reveal itself to those who held the Keys.","For this is what the Aspects truly are. Not simply expressions of power. They are the Keys of Civilization. The foundational truths that unlock the higher mysteries of Vakochev’s Scales of Existence. Each Key opens doors that the other Keys cannot open. Each Aspect reveals understanding that the other Aspects cannot reveal.","It does not matter who among THE Five is the strongest.","Strength is irrelevant when considering the Keys. Combat prowess is meaningless when evaluating the Aspects. The question that matters, the only question that matters, is what potential exists in how each Aspect can alter reality.","Existence is naturally elevated among the four. It is the foundation upon which everything else rests. Without Existence, there is nothing to be chaotic, nothing to be paradoxical, nothing to be expressed through linguistic architecture. THE Creature’s position as holder of this Aspect grants him influence that raw power cannot measure.","Paradox is the catalyst that permits evolution beyond linear progression. It allows the impossible. It enables contradiction. It provides the mechanism through which beings transcend the limitations that logic would otherwise impose upon them. THE Living Paradox’s position as holder of this Aspect grants him leverage that conventional understanding cannot calculate.","THE First Tongue is the architecture through which Existence and Civilizations define themselves and their realities. It is expression given foundational weight. THE Genesis Monarch’s position as holder of this Aspect grants him capacity that finite methodology cannot replicate.","But Chaos.","Many believed, many still believe, that Chaos is the Aspect that holds unbounded potential above all others.","Not because Chaos is stronger than Existence. Not because entropy exceeds differentiation in some measurable way. But because of what Chaos fundamentally is.","Chaos is possibility itself.","Chaos is the space where all outcomes remain available.","Chaos may be the potential from which everything emerged.","Where the other Aspects define what is, Chaos defines what could be. Where the other Keys open specific doors, Chaos opens all doors simultaneously and permits the opener to choose which reality they wish to walk into.","THE Primordial Chaos’s position as holder of this Aspect grants him something that the other holders do not possess. The capacity to reshape probability itself. The authority to make the unlikely inevitable and the certain impossible. The power to alter not merely what exists but what can exist.","This is why Chaos is a critical Key.","This is why Chaos is a critical piece of the puzzle.","This is why, when THE Mnemonic Leviathan warned that when Chaos speaks with the tongue of Order, the anchor itself is being moved by an outside hand, the warning carried weight.","For if Chaos were ever to be compromised, if the Aspect of possibility itself were ever to be claimed or corrupted or consumed by something other than its rightful bearer, the implications would exceed anything that Observable Existence has ever faced.","The other Aspects can be contested. The other Keys can be fought over.","But Chaos determines what contests are possible. Chaos determines what fights can occur.","If Chaos falls, the very nature of what can happen changes.","And whoever holds Chaos after such a fall would hold not merely an Aspect, not merely a Key, but the fundamental capacity to decide what realities are permitted to exist.","This is the weight that THE Primordial Chaos carries.","This is the burden that Abaddon bears without acknowledgment.","This is why, when THE Youngest warned him of the one percent, the warning carried implications that exceeded mere infection.","If THE Primordial Mycelia has truly taken purchase within Chaos, if the Aspect of possibility itself has been touched by the unity that Entity seeks to impose upon all existence, then the Era of Undifferentiation is not merely approaching.","And if Chaos has been compromised, then the possibility of preventing what comes next may have already been removed from the probability space of Observable Existence.","This is why THE Four mattered before THE Five.","This is why THE Five matter now."]},{"number":4968,"title":"Chapter 4968: Chapter 4967: One Door Closes","paragraphs":["Noah’s crimson eyes, burning with Infinite Hunger at Absolute Depth, watched the collision between THE Primordial Chaos and THE Secretive Eon with perception that missed nothing.","Time seemed to stretch as the hammer of endings met the palms of unity, as impossibility confronted inevitability, as two fundamental forces clashed in ways that Observable Existence had never witnessed.","THE Secretive Eon carried a terrifying force of Unity within her Civilization.","It did not seem singular in nature. It did not feel like the authority of one being, no matter how powerful that being might be. It seemed unfathomably unified, countless Civilizations merged into something that exceeded the sum of its parts. The four Strategoi supporting her body were akin to massive pillars that did not only support her physical form but were passing through unfathomable waves of authority unto her.","Glossikos channeled the linguistic foundations of THE Agora itself.","Khaotikos channeled the chaotic underpinnings that gave THE Agora its capacity for judgment.","Ontikos channeled the existential weight of a Primordial Realm’s accumulated history.","Paradoxos channeled the contradictions that allowed THE Agora to function despite its own impossibilities.","All of it flowed into THE Secretive Eon.","All of the entities that she had unified under her banner had their strength in Civilizations, with all their meanings and all their concepts, simultaneously flowing through her. She was not one being receiving support. She was countless beings expressed through a single form, their authorities merged into unity that exceeded individual expression.","It was a terrifying thing when one thought about it.","Through the legs of THE Secretive Eon, Noah saw the glimmer of Quantum from THE Living Quantum. That flickering uncertainty that characterized beings who existed in superposition, present and absent simultaneously, their authority drawn from the space between observation and manifestation.","Through her arms, Noah saw a glimmer of Dimensional authority from THE Living Dimensional. That spatial weight that characterized beings who commanded the architecture of reality itself, their authority drawn from the distances between points that existence used to measure itself.","And through her palms, through the very surfaces that met THE Primordial Chaos’s descending fist, Noah saw an obsidian glimmer of... Chaos that caused his expression to become heavy.","Every single possibility he had considered was confirmed at this moment.","Because...why would Chaos be flowing so serenely within THE Secretive Eon?","Why would the authority of THE Primordial Chaos, who stood above her with fist descending like judgment itself, already be present within her existence as if it belonged there?","The answer was obvious.","The answer was devastating.","THE Primordial Chaos had been compromised long before this moment. The infection had taken root without his knowledge, without his perception, without any indication that his glorious and unmitigated Chaos had been touched by something other than himself.","And now, in this collision, that infection would complete itself.","Noah saw it all.","At the tip of the fist that looked like a hammer of endings, all the force of THE Primordial Chaos’s Embodiments and Apophasis gathered with concentration that exceeded anything Abaddon had displayed before. Every ounce of his authority, every expression of his Chaos, every aspect of his Civilization that had existed since before THE Infinite Unfurling, all of it focused into a single point of impact that should have unmade THE Secretive Eon entirely.","When everything was expressed, when the hammer met the palms, when impossibility confronted unity with force that should have ended the confrontation instantly, a crack bloomed between THE Primordial Chaos and THE Secretive Eon.","This crack was not like any of the Cracks of Observable Existence.","Those Cracks were wounds in reality, tears in the fabric of differentiation that allowed corruption to flood through. Those Cracks were damage. Those Cracks were harm. Those Cracks were things that needed to be sealed or avoided or destroyed.","This crack was purely obsidian in nature.","It seemed to connect the already maintained Chaos within THE Secretive Eon and THE Primordial Chaos himself. It was not a wound. It was a bridge...it was completion. It was the final link between infection and source, between the Chaos that had been claimed without knowledge and the Chaos that remained ignorant of its own compromise.","The moment it bloomed, the moment the obsidian crack covered both figures inside of it, the moment the connection was established fully and irreversibly, everything changed.","HUUM!","The Chaos within the crack transformed.","The Chaos surrounding the two figures transformed.","The Chaos flooding and raging in the sky space above, which had been torn and split entirely during the entrance of THE Primordial Chaos, all of it transformed.","It became silent, and it became ordered.","The raging entropy that had characterized Abaddon’s arrival settled into patterns that should not have been possible for Chaos to display. The screaming Embodiments and Apophasis fell silent as if they had forgotten what sound was. The obsidian currents that had churned with violence stilled into rivers that flowed with serenity that contradicted their fundamental nature.","Chaos was speaking with the tongue of Order.","The anchor itself had been moved by an outside hand.","And then, a moment later...","WAP!","The figure of THE Primordial Chaos disappeared.","THE Secretive Eon disappeared.","The four pillars that had been supporting her, the four Strategoi who had burned with righteous existence while channeling their authorities into her form, all of them disappeared.","They were simply gone!","The only things left behind were the bodies of Noah and THE Primordial Paradox.","All around them, rivers of serenely flowing and ordered Chaos remained as testament to what had just occurred. The obsidian currents that had once raged with entropy now moved with patterns that spoke of purpose rather than possibility. They flowed in directions that seemed predetermined. They carried weight that seemed unified rather than chaotic.","\"...\"","Noah looked around sensed...emptiness.","THE Agora of Primordial Judgment had become a monument to THE Entity’s victory.","Noah was silent and contemplative during all of this.","One could question and say that his actions of talking with THE Primordial Chaos led to all of this. One could argue that by warning Abaddon of the one percent, by attempting to convince him to accept Infinities that would have purified any infection, Noah had prompted the confrontation that resulted in Chaos’s fall.","But THE Primordial Chaos was already infected long before any of this.","This turned out to truly be the trump card of THE Entity since nobody knew it. Not THE Creature. Not THE Primordial Paradox. Not THE Youngest. Not even THE Primordial Chaos himself, who had searched his own existence and found only his glorious, unmitigated Chaos because the infection was too subtle to perceive.","Whether Noah had gone to speak with THE Primordial Chaos or not, the infection within him would still be there.","He had only gone there to provide the possibility of infusing his Infinities and changing things for THE Primordial Chaos before they went too far. A chance. An option. A path that could have led somewhere other than here.","But THE Primordial Chaos believed in himself far too much to accept this help.","And this was why they were where they were.","Beside him, THE Primordial Paradox sighed at this moment!"]},{"number":4969,"title":"Chapter 4969: Chapter 4968: Another Door Opens","paragraphs":["The sound carried weight that pressed against the ordered Chaos around them, paradoxical breath that contradicted the serenity with implications of struggle yet to come.","\" It seems that THE Entity had already won a great victory without any of us realizing it.\"","His voice was measured but heavy.","\" And we have simply observed its completion right now. With my revival, I didn’t expect to be relaxing and taking a breather. But I also did not know that I would have to work so hard.\"","His brilliant features held calculations.","\" Youngest, before I can get anywhere close to THE Second Scale of Existence, I need to rectify the paradox between me and my student. Only then would I truly be of significant help and I can move like my old self.\"","He paused.","\" But before I leave, why don’t I get some help from you so that what has happened to our dear friend Chaos here does not happen to me?\"","His obsidian-gold eyes fixed on Noah with directness that exceeded everything previous.","\" Let me...have some of your Infinity.\"","...!","Noah’s eyes opened wide with marvel as he looked at THE Primordial Paradox!","How unique existence was!","He went to talk and try to convince THE Primordial Chaos and failed. He had presented logical arguments. He had used Abaddon’s own philosophy against him. He had offered a solution that would have prevented everything that just occurred.","And THE Primordial Chaos refused.","And yet THE Primordial Paradox reached out for Infinities himself!","Well, Paradox had already accepted the protection of his Infinity against THE Entity during their battle with Bazuman. And he had already been infected by THE Primordial Mycelia once, had felt what it meant to have his existence touched by unity that sought to consume individual identity.","He was much more careful and open-minded.","But Noah still had to ask.","\" Chaos said no to my Infinities. How are you so carefree of it? You will effectively have your Civilization of Paradox mixed under my weavings of Infinity.\"","At such words, THE Primordial Paradox waved his hands dismissively.","\" What nonsense is that?\"","His voice carried the confidence of a being who had existed since logic first learned to contradict itself.","\"I am confident of my Way and Civilization as I don’t worry about such things. I was Paradox. I will always be Paradox. Taking in your Infinities...\"","He paused, considering his phrasing.","\" It is like borrowing a shield from a friend who has many shields. That is all I am asking for. A shield that if I don’t need it in the future, I can simply give it back to you.\"","...!","The immensity and grandness of THE Primordial Paradox was truly magisterial to see!","Where THE Primordial Chaos had refused help out of pride that could not bend, THE Primordial Paradox accepted help out of wisdom that recognized when bending was strength rather than weakness. Where Abaddon believed his Chaos too fundamental to be touched by another, Paradox understood that accepting protection did not diminish what he fundamentally was.","Noah respected this being!","He gave a light nod as he waved his hand.","A Lotus petal materialized before him.","It glowed with blue-gold light that contained pre-formed Bounded Countable Infinity, harvested from THE Bounded Lotus of Sequential Eternity in the fields of the Early Veiled Shore. The same petals that had transformed his people in THE Yggdrheim. The same petals that could elevate finite beings into Infinite ones.","The petal floated toward THE Primordial Paradox.","He grasped it inquisitively, his obsidian-gold Paradoxes flickering around his form as he examined what he held. His perception dove into the petal’s structure, feeling the Infinities contained within, understanding what consumption would mean for his Civilization.","He didn’t ask any questions.","The lotus became wrapped by Paradox, obsidian-gold light swirling around blue-gold essence as two fundamental forces began their integration. Then it sank into his body and...","BOOM!","Incandescent blue-gold brilliance bloomed into a storm that began to rage around THE Primordial Paradox!","His form blazed with light that exceeded anything his obsidian-gold Paradoxes had displayed before. The Bounded Countable Infinity from the lotus petal spread through his foundations with speed that spoke of compatibility exceeding expectations. His Civilization, ancient and vast and brilliant beyond measure, received the Seed of Infinity and made it part of itself.","Infinity bloomed in another one of THE Five!","THE Primordial Paradox went forward to gain Bounded Countable Infinity!","Prompts blazed before Noah’s eyes!","| Pivotal Event: Integration of Bounded Countable Infinity into THE Primordial Paradox|","|Classification: Unprecedented. Two Keys of Civilization have become intertwined through this integration. THE First Tongue and Paradox now share connection that has never existed before in the history of Observable Existence.|","...!","|Process Status: THE Primordial Paradox’s Civilization at Absolute Depth is receiving Bounded Countable Infinity through consumption of a petal from THE Bounded Lotus of Sequential Eternity. His foundations are integrating the Seed with speed that suggests fundamental compatibility between Paradox and Infinity that exceeds theoretical predictions.|","|Key Integration Analysis: THE First Tongue now extends tendrils of Infinite connection into the Aspect of Paradox. Your authority as Native Speaker of THE First Tongue has established presence within one of the Four Keys that predate your existence. The linguistic architecture of reality now touches the impossibilities that Paradox permits.|","|Hierarchy Established: THE First Tongue leads this integration. The Bounded nature of the Infinity bestowed ensures that your Key maintains primacy over the connection. THE Primordial Paradox’s Paradox now operates beneath the umbrella of your Infinite expressions, though his authority over Paradox itself remains his own.|","...!","|Warning: The result of intertwining two Keys of Civilization is unknown.|","|No records exist of Keys becoming connected through shared authority. No precedent exists for one Key holder bestowing aspects of their nature upon another Key holder. The consequences of this integration cannot be calculated.|","|Theoretical Possibilities:|","|The connection may enhance both Keys in ways neither could achieve alone.|","|The connection may create resonance between THE First Tongue and Paradox that opens paths towards a higher Scale.|","|The connection may produce expressions that neither Key was designed to produce.|","|The connection may alter the fundamental relationship between Keys in ways that affect all Four Aspects.|","|Assessment: Unknown. This is territory that Observable Existence has never mapped. You and THE Primordial Paradox are now pioneers in understanding that no being has explored.|","...!","|Current Status: THE Primordial Paradox at Absolute Depth now possesses Bounded Countable Infinity derived from your authority over THE First Tongue. His Embodiments and Apophasis will curve along partial geodesic paths. His Civilization will regenerate with speed approaching endless. His growth will proceed along trajectories that his previous state could not access.|","|Protection Status: Should THE Entity attempt to claim THE Primordial Paradox as it claimed THE Primordial Chaos, your Infinities will burn away any weavings of compromise before they can take root. The shield has been borrowed. The shield is in place.|","|You have done something that has never been done.|","|The consequences remain to be seen.|","...!","THE Youngest had gone ahead and given an old monster Infinities.","It was unknown just what all of this would lead to!"]},{"number":4970,"title":"Chapter 4970: Chapter 4969: Unity I","paragraphs":["What Abaddon felt was a moment of impact that pushed everything away.","And then everything went white.","Pure white.","To the point that he could not see anything else but white. No obsidian rivers of chaos. No flickering entropy. No probability spaces bending to his will. Just endless, perfect, serene whiteness that stretched in every direction without boundary or definition.","For the first time in eons beyond counting, THE Primordial Chaos felt himself floating in something that held no chaos at all.","He looked around, his form turning in the blankness as he searched for something, anything, that could orient him within this space. His hands rose before his face, and they were still his hands. His existence still felt like his existence. But the surroundings held nothing that his chaos could grasp or influence or understand.","\" What...happened?\"","His voice emerged into the whiteness and was swallowed without echo.","Behind him, footsteps approached with rhythm that felt familiar even though he could not immediately place why.","\" You went out there for a second.\"","The voice belonged to someone he knew. Someone he trusted. Someone whose presence made the whiteness feel less empty and more like a space meant for rest rather than confusion.","\" Are you okay?\"","THE Secretive Eon came into view with smile that held warmth exceeding anything Abaddon had expected. Her features were kind. Her eyes held concern that seemed genuine. She moved toward him with grace that spoke of care rather than threat.","She helped him up.","He took her hand naturally, as if he had taken it many times before, as if this gesture was as familiar as breathing. Her palm was warm against his. Her grip was supportive without being controlling. She steadied him as he found his footing in the white expanse.","Abaddon scratched his head with his free hand, trying to recall what had brought him here.","\"I could have sworn I was doing something critical. I just cannot remember what.\"","His brow furrowed with concentration that produced nothing but fog.","\" Something with chaos. Something with unity.\"","The memories were there, he was certain of it. They lurked just beyond the edges of his awareness like shapes glimpsed through thick mist. He had been angry about something. He had been determined about something. He had been moving toward confrontation with purpose that had consumed his entire existence.","But the details refused to solidify.","His mind was foggy as if there was something clouding everything.","Luckily, THE Secretive Eon was here.","She nodded with understanding that suggested she had seen this confusion before, had helped others through similar moments of disorientation, had guided beings back to clarity when their own minds failed them.","But on her forehead, one could see beads of sweat as if...she was doing something that required a lot of exertion right now. As if she was lifting a lot of weight, and had to proceed carefully.","\" You delved too much into chaos.\"","Her voice was soothing.","\" We have so many paths before us, and if we focus on a single one, it can sometimes cause issues. But with chaos, many more things that weren’t possible before now have countless possibilities lying out before them.\"","She squeezed his hand gently.","\" And remember, you are not alone. We... are never alone.\"","...!","After she said this, the white blank space began to change.","Countless figures of beings rose up one after another from the whiteness itself. They emerged like flowers blooming in accelerated time, their forms taking shape with grace that spoke of belonging rather than intrusion. They surrounded THE Primordial Chaos and THE Secretive Eon in circles that expanded outward until the whiteness was filled with presences that felt like warmth rather than threat.","Abaddon recognized many of them.","Jotuun Lifeforms.","THE Living Quantum flickered with uncertainty that somehow felt stable. THE Living Dimensional stood with spatial authority that bent the white space around him into configurations that should not have been possible.","And there were others.","So many others.","Beings he had encountered across eons of existence. Beings whose Civilizations represented the breadth of what Observable Existence had produced since THE First Cause. All of them here. All of them present. All of them looking at him with eyes that held welcome rather than challenge.","Looking at them, THE Primordial Chaos couldn’t help but feel a sense of warmth.","He had been alone for so long.","So very, very long.","His chaos had always set him apart from others. His nature made connection difficult. His existence as one of THE Four, now THE Five, meant that peers were rare and true understanding was rarer still. He had walked through eons with power that exceeded most beings’ comprehension and loneliness that exceeded his power.","He forgot what it felt like to have others with him.","But now, surrounded by these figures, bathed in this warmth, he remembered.","Beside him, THE Secretive Eon hugged his hand with both of hers. She pressed against his arm with affection that felt like homecoming. Her smile held invitation that exceeded mere welcome.","\" Share the burden of that chaos with the rest of us.\"","Her voice was soft but certain.","\" All that possibility and potential. Let us unite it with all of these Civilizations that you can tap into yourself to see all the variations of existence.\"","...!","Abaddon nodded with bright eyes.","His chaos had always been missing something. He had known this for eons without being able to articulate what the absence was. His probability spaces had been vast but empty. His entropy had been powerful but purposeless. His potential had been endless but directionless.","This could be it.","Connection! Unity!","Purpose that came from belonging rather than isolation.","With such a thought, rivers of ordered chaos began flowing from THE Primordial Chaos!","The obsidian currents emerged from his existence with eagerness that surprised him. They wanted to connect. They wanted to share. They wanted to bridge the gap between his solitary vastness and the warmth that surrounded him. The rivers extended outward like endless streams, reaching toward every single unified being in this white space.","They connected rapidly.","One after another after another.","Each river found its target and established link that felt like completion rather than compromise. Each connection brought new awareness of Civilizations that he could now perceive from the inside rather than the outside. Each bridge opened paths that his chaos could flow through to touch existences that had been separate from his own.","If one were to look down from above, they would see an endless web of chaos flowing into a united cluster of beings!"]},{"number":4971,"title":"Chapter 4971: Chapter 4970: Unity II","paragraphs":["The cluster was shining brighter and brighter with every connection established.","THE Primordial Chaos at the center.","THE Secretive Eon beside him.","And all the unified beings around them, their Civilizations now linked through rivers of ordered chaos that carried possibility and potential to every corner of their shared existence.","As they were doing this, a sense of joy and euphoria spread across all of them!","Abaddon felt it most strongly.","The warmth was no longer just external. It flowed through his rivers and returned multiplied. It touched his chaos and made it feel purposeful. It filled the emptiness that had characterized his existence for eons and replaced it with belonging that exceeded anything he had imagined possible.","But moments later, the space trembled and shook.","Something had disturbed it.","The whiteness flickered with colors that shouldn’t have been present. The unified beings turned their attention toward a direction that the disturbance originated from. The joy and euphoria paused as awareness of external events pressed against their shared consciousness.","THE Primordial Chaos blinked.","\" What is that?\"","THE Secretive Eon looked out into the distance with expression that held annoyance mixed with fondness.","\" One of our core future family members seems to have made some trouble again.\"","She tugged at his hand.","\" Let’s go see.\"","...!","The vision of THE Primordial Chaos changed once more.","An instant later, he found himself in his home.","Jotunheim.","The Primordial Realm that he had claimed since before THE Infinite Unfurling spread out before him with grandeur that made his chaos swell with recognition. Mountains of crystallized entropy rose toward skies that held no single color but all colors simultaneously. Rivers of pure probability flowed through valleys where reality itself remained in constant flux.","And the Citadel of Giants dominated the landscape.","The grand structure rose from the center of Jotunheim with architecture that defied conventional understanding. Its walls were built from solidified chaos that shifted patterns even as it maintained structural integrity. Its towers reached heights that changed depending on the observer’s expectations. Its foundations extended into probability spaces that contained every possible configuration the citadel could ever take.","Within and around the citadel, many Jotuun lifeforms patiently cultivated.","They sat in meditative positions across platforms and courtyards and floating spaces that the citadel provided for their advancement. Their massive forms held still with concentration that exceeded their usually turbulent natures. Their eyes were closed. Their Civilizations were cycling through chaos that Abaddon had shared with them across eons of mentorship.","They were his people.","They were his family even before he understood what family could mean.","And now they were part of something larger.","He and THE Secretive Eon stood at the peak of the grand structure, at the highest point of the citadel where chaos concentrated with intensity that would unmake lesser beings. From here, they could perceive everything occurring in Jotunheim and beyond.","Currently, all of them were looking up.","THE Primordial Chaos was perceiving a change in the flow of existence around them. A change in energy and authority. A change in the Principles that weaved the surrounding existence. A change in the expression of THE First Tongue itself.","Something fundamental had shifted.","Something that touched the very architecture of how Civilizations expressed themselves.","\" Fire...\"","THE Primordial Chaos tried to utter the Phoneme of fire, wanting to test what he was perceiving.","But the word felt wrong in his mouth.","It twisted. It contradicted itself. It became a tongue twister that his ancient authority could not navigate smoothly. The simple Phoneme that powerful beings across Observable Existence used without thought now held layers of complexity that made clear pronunciation nearly impossible.","As if it now held infinite paradoxical variations for anyone who wanted to say it.","As if THE First Tongue itself had been altered by something that understood how to weave paradox into linguistic architecture.","THE Primordial Chaos was skeptical at this.","He blinked with confusion that exceeded mere surprise.","\" THE First Tongue...has become more paradoxical?\"","Beside him, the figure of THE Secretive Eon nodded with expression that held exasperation and something that might have been grudging respect.","\" THE Youngest is on his rebellious phase right now.\"","Her voice carried weight that pressed against the chaos around them.","\" Making the weavings of THE First Tongue more paradoxical is only one of the things that he will do. Which is why a lot of things rest on your shoulders, Abaddon.\"","She turned to face him fully, her eyes holding intensity that exceeded everything else.","\" We actually need your help to make our family complete.\"","Her hands found his again, holding them with grip that communicated desperation beneath the warmth.","\" With you, with all the countless possibilities you hold, even if it is one in a trillion or one in a quintillion, there is a possibility of unity with Infinity. We need your help to lock on to that possibility and to make it a reality, so that we can gain the capability to bring THE Youngest into our family. You are the only one who can help us with this.\"","Her eyes shimmered with something that might have been tears.","\" So we can show him all of this.\"","She gestured at the unified beings below, at the Jotuun cultivating peacefully, at the web of chaos that connected everything to everything else.","\" Do you think that you could get started working on this?\"","...!","THE Primordial Chaos looked toward THE Secretive Eon.","She was looking at him with an almost pleading gaze. Her features held hope that seemed genuine. Her warmth pressed against his existence with affection that made his ancient loneliness seem like a distant memory rather than a constant companion. And her forehead...was filled with sweat as if she was truly carrying a heavy weight right now.","His own gaze softened.","Family helped each other.","His ancient chaos had many purposes across his time. He had used it for conquest and for defense and for exploration and for countless other objectives that his will had directed toward. He had wielded probability and entropy and possibility as weapons and as tools and as expressions of what he fundamentally was.","But just this once, he wanted to use it to help all those it was connected to.","After all, he was no longer alone.","And in existence that was so vast and filled with terrors, being alone was one of the more terrifying things.","\"I will help.\"","His voice emerged with conviction that pressed against Jotunheim itself.","\" Show me where to begin.\"","THE Secretive Eon smiled with brilliance that illuminated the peak of the citadel.","\" Welcome to the family, Abaddon.\"","She hugged him.","\" Welcome home.\""]},{"number":4972,"title":"Chapter 4972: Chapter 4971: The Last Strategoi I","paragraphs":["Noah looked at THE Primordial Paradox as the storm of blue-gold brilliance continued to rage around the ancient being’s form.","Even he questioned whether he did the right thing.","It was literally akin to giving a monstrous beast wings to be able to fly even higher. THE Primordial Paradox had already been one of the most dangerous beings in Observable Existence before this moment. His mastery of contradiction, his capacity to make the impossible inevitable, his authority over paradox that had existed since logic first learned to break itself, all of it had been formidable beyond measure.","Now he had Infinity as well.","THE Primordial Paradox seemed unshackled and unbounded as his existence filled with paradoxical Infinities that blazed through every aspect of his Civilization. The Bounded Countable Infinity that Noah had bestowed through the lotus petal was integrating with Paradox in ways that exceeded theoretical predictions. The two authorities were not merely coexisting. They were enhancing each other in configurations that neither could produce alone.","And of course, Noah also felt his own weavings of Paradox reach terrifying levels!","The connection between them, the intertwining of two Keys of Civilization, was producing resonance that flowed in both directions. Where THE Primordial Paradox gained Infinity, Noah gained deeper understanding of Paradox. Where Bounded Countable expressions spread through ancient foundations, paradoxical comprehension spread through Infinite architecture.","He felt like he could further elevate himself in a paradoxical manner.","His biggest aim right now was going from Countable to Uncountable Infinity. The transition required saturation rather than accumulation, required filling the gaps between sequential expressions with additional expressions that couldn’t be listed. It was a monumental undertaking that conventional methodology would require eons to achieve.","He...did not gave eons.","But Paradox permitted the impossible.","Paradox allowed things that shouldn’t happen to happen anyway.","Paradox could potentially compress eons of saturation into moments of breakthrough if the contradiction was framed correctly.","Noah felt like this action, this intertwining of Keys, was going to help him with that tremendously. The resonance between THE First Tongue and Paradox was opening doors that neither Key could open alone. The connection was revealing paths that had been invisible before the intertwining occurred.","He observed THE Primordial Paradox with perception that missed nothing.","The ancient being’s transformation was stabilizing now. The storm of blue-gold brilliance was settling into patterns of integration completing rather than integration occurring. The Bounded Countable Infinity had found its place within Paradox’s foundations and was no longer fighting to establish itself.","What remained was something that Observable Existence had never witnessed.","THE Primordial Paradox stood before Noah with form that had transformed entirely.","His body was titanic now, larger than it had been before, his obsidian presence expanded by the Infinity that now burned within his foundations. But the obsidian was no longer pure darkness. It was filled with blue-gold dots that scattered across his form like stars scattered across the void of space. Each dot was a point of Infinite expression. Each dot was a seed of Countable progression that would grow and expand according to Paradox’s efforts.","He looked like a canvas of infinite paradoxical space.","He looked like contradiction given form and then given Infinity to fuel that form’s expansion.","He looked like something that shouldn’t exist and yet existed anyway, which was perhaps the most paradoxical thing of all.","THE Primordial Paradox turned toward Noah with eyes that held blue-gold light swirling through their obsidian depths. His expression was one of amazement that his usual detachment could not fully conceal.","\"Youngest, this is the Infinity you are playing around with?\"","His voice carried weight that pressed against THE Agora itself.","\" Damn .\"","\" You almost made me doubt Paradox. Almost. But my entire existence lives and dies with Paradox, so I still kept my sanity.\"","He looked down at his transformed hands, at the blue-gold dots that now scattered across obsidian flesh like constellations being born.","\" This will be a bigger boon than simply acting like a shield. And I actually don’t know if I’ll be returning it.\"","THE Primordial Paradox smiled as he said this.","And Noah smiled back.","Very few truly understood Infinity. Him included, if he was being honest. He worked with Countable expressions that extended endlessly in sequences he could observe. He pushed toward Uncountable density that would fill the gaps between those sequences. He theorized about Absolute Infinity that transcended all other Infinities while containing them simultaneously.","But true understanding remained elusive.","Infinity was not something that finite minds could grasp completely, even minds that wielded Infinity as their fundamental nature.","But when he had another entity at an extremely high level also get a glimpse of it, when THE Primordial Paradox experienced what Bounded Countable Infinity felt like from the inside rather than the outside, it felt nice.","It felt like having a companion on a journey that most beings couldn’t even perceive, let alone walk.","\" Keep it or return it, it’s okay.\"","Noah’s voice carried warmth that exceeded his usual calculating demeanor.","\"I will also benefit either way. Do be careful on your own Adversity, and if you need help, let me know.\"","The reason they were parting ways was simple.","Just like between Noah and THE Creature, THE Primordial Paradox had his own Adversity. His disciple was his Adversity. THE Living Paradox, the apprentice who had consumed the Aspect of Paradox from his master, the being who had used teachings of contradiction to steal what should have been unstealable, that was the obstacle standing between THE Primordial Paradox and his advancement.","To advance, naturally, he had to face it.","To reclaim what was taken, or to find resolution that transcended reclamation, or to discover some other path that his paradoxical nature would reveal to him along the way.","Noah could not help with this.","This was THE Primordial Paradox’s Adversity, not his.","Just as his own Adversities belonged to him and no one else.","They silently gazed at each other as if they could read each other’s thoughts. Two of THE Five. Two holders of Keys of Civilization. Two beings whose paths had intertwined in ways that would affect Observable Existence for eons to come.","Understanding passed between them without words.","Respect passed between them without acknowledgment.","And then THE Primordial Paradox laughed!","The sound boomed across THE Agora with weight that made the rivers of ordered Chaos tremble. It was genuine laughter, the kind that emerged from beings who found actual amusement rather than performing the motions of amusement.","He raised his hand toward Noah.","Not as a gesture of attack, but as an invitation.","A dap!","Noah raised his own hand with a smile that matched THE Primordial Paradox’s laughter.","Their hands met in a glorious dap!","BOOM!","Vibrant terrifying authorities collided with force that exceeded what such casual contact should have produced!","Blue-gold Infinity blazed outward from Noah’s palm. Obsidian-gold Paradox blazed outward from THE Primordial Paradox’s palm. The two forces met and merged and exploded outward across THE Agora of Primordial Judgment with light that blinded anything that might have been watching.","Infinities stretched across the ancient forum!","Paradoxes stretched alongside them!","The intertwining of Keys that had begun with the lotus petal now expressed itself visually, two fundamental forces declaring their connection through display that painted THE Agora in colors that shouldn’t have coexisted!","By the time the light faded, THE Primordial Paradox was gone.","Noah... was the only one left behind."]},{"number":4973,"title":"Chapter 4973: Chapter 4972: The Last Strategoi II","paragraphs":["He stood alone in THE Agora of Primordial Judgment.","The rivers of ordered Chaos that had remained after THE Entity’s departure were now replaced by something new. Rivers of Paradox and Infinity flowed through the ancient forum, currents that carried the signature of what had just occurred. Blue-gold and obsidian-gold intertwined","Noah looked around this transformed region.","The architecture of THE Agora remained intact. The structures that had stood since before THE Infinite Unfurling still stood now. The temples to philosophical concepts still rose toward skies that held the weight of judgment. The gathering places still existed in their designated districts.","But everything felt empty.","He spread his gaze outward with Absolute Vision of Existence that perceived across vast distances instantaneously.","He felt the aura of nobody else nearby.","No Hoplites debating in the Lower City. No Lochagoi conducting discourse in the Middle City. No Polemarchs ascending toward the Acropolis with disputes requiring resolution. No followers of any Way practicing their approaches in the Four Gathering Places.","THE Agora of Primordial Judgment was abandoned.","Noah took a step and began to traverse across the ancient forum.","His footsteps echoed through empty streets that had once held the discourse of countless beings. The obsidian sand of the Shores of Kleos lay undisturbed by newcomers. The markets of Kato Polis held goods that no one would purchase. The training grounds held equipment that no one would use.","Everywhere he went, no signs of life could be seen.","Just empty structures.","Just abandoned districts.","Just the remnants of a Primordial Realm that had once been the nexus of philosophical judgment for all of Observable Existence.","He continued to traverse THE Agora.","Through Meso Polis with its elaborate architecture and private debate chambers that held no debates. Past the Ataraxia where followers of Chaos had once gathered, now empty of all but the rivers that flowed in their master’s absence.","Past the Ousia where followers of Existence had practiced their Way, now holding only the memory of practices that would not resume. Past the Antinomia where followers of Paradox had explored contradiction, now silent except for the new rivers of paradoxical Infinity that flowed through its streets.","Past the Lexicon where followers of THE First Tongue had studied linguistic architecture, now waiting for a Native Speaker who stood alone among its abandoned halls.","He climbed toward the Acropolis.","The highest district of THE Agora opened before him with grandeur that exceeded everything below. Temples to philosophical concepts rose on all sides, their architecture embodying the ideas they were constructed to honor. The residences of the Strategoi stood empty, their former occupants now part of THE Entity’s unified collective.","And THE Primordial Archive awaited.","Noah entered the structure.","Books floated serenely in the air, their pages turning slowly as if reading themselves. Scrolls hovered in organized arrangements of cataloguing systems developed across eons. Tablets of crystallized knowledge pulsed with light that held understanding waiting to be accessed. Artifacts of philosophical significance rested on pedestals that protected them from degradation.","When THE Entity left and took all those she infected, she left every single thing intact.","She destroyed nothing.","All the knowledge and wonders in THE Primordial Archive would be his to peruse.","Alone.","Prompts bloomed before Noah’s eyes.","|Assessment of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment|","|Current Population: Zero differentiated beings detected within realm boundaries.|","|Current Authority: You hold the highest authority present within THE Agora. Your Civilization exceeds all remaining signatures. Your claim to this Nexus Primordial Realm is uncontested.|","|Classification: You possess the qualification to be a Strategoi. The position is available. The realm awaits leadership.|","...!","Noah looked around THE Primordial Archive with a sense of melancholy that exceeded his usual emotional containment.","The books continued floating. The scrolls continued hovering. The knowledge continued waiting for someone to access it. But there was no one else here to share in that access. No Strategoi to debate interpretations with. No Polemarchs to challenge conclusions. No followers of any Way to apply the knowledge toward their advancement.","Just him.","Alone in a realm that had once held countless beings pursuing understanding.","\"I...will become the last Strategoi.\"","HUUM!","Inside THE Primordial Archive, multicolored lights of THE Agora descended upon Noah with weight of a realm itself responding to his declaration!","The lights swirled around his form with patterns of authority being transferred, of position being granted, of classification being established. They touched his existence with warmth.","A crimson-blue toga bloomed on his body!","The fabric materialized from the multicolored lights, draping across his form with elegance that spoke of highest office. Laurel wreaths formed around his head, golden leaves that marked him as Strategoi of THE Agora. Adornments appeared at his shoulders and wrists, symbols of philosophical authority that had been worn by those who judged the discourse of Primordial Realms.","He became the only Strategoi in THE Agora.","The last Strategoi.","Prompts blazed before his eyes with finality that pressed against the very fabric of the realm.","|Elevation Complete: Strategoi of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment|","|You have become the highest authority within the Nexus Primordial Realm of THE Agora of Primordial Judgment. This position grants you access to all structures and capabilities of the realm. This position grants you authority over all aspects of THE Agora’s function and purpose.|","|Available Resources:|","|THE Primordial Archive: Complete access to all accumulated knowledge since THE First Cause.|","|THE Chamber of Judgment: Authority to render verdicts on any dispute brought before THE Agora.|","|The Four Gathering Places: Dominion over all districts dedicated to the Four Ways.|","|The Shores of Kleos: Control over arrival and departure from the realm.|","|The Acropolis: Residence befitting your classification.|","|Note: You are the sole authority. You are the sole inhabitant. You are alone.|","|THE Agora awaits your direction.|","...!","Noah stood in THE Primordial Archive wearing the toga and laurels of highest office, surrounded by knowledge that may take...days to fully absorb, holding authority over a realm that had no one left to govern.","He looked at the floating books with eyes that held something complicated.","\" Alone ,\" he said aloud to the empty Archive. \" But free.\"","He thought of THE Primordial Chaos, now likely surrounded by countless unified beings.","He thought of himself, standing alone in a realm that had been emptied by THE Entity’s harvest.","Two states. Two conditions. Two ways of existing in the vastness of Observable Existence.","One surrounded by many.","One surrounded by none.","But which one was real? Which one was genuine? Which one held truth rather than illusion, freedom rather than chains, existence rather than consumption disguised as connection?","Noah knew the answer.","And the answer made his loneliness feel less like burden and more like choice.","But as Noah thought about loneliness, as the weight of the empty Archive pressed against his consciousness with implications that exceeded mere solitude, the air beside him shimmered with light of arrival rather than departure.","THE Infiniverse manifested in her humanoid form.","She stepped into THE Primordial Archive with grace. Her eyes held the depths of countless realms, and her smile held warmth that made the emptiness of THE Agora feel less absolute.","Moments later, RUINATION’s illusory form flickered into existence as well!","Her blue-gold presence materialized with hair extending into infinite data points and eyes burning with analysis that had been tracking Noah’s movements across all his bodies simultaneously. She appeared beside THE Infiniverse with familiarity.","The two of them moved toward their Master.","Noah smiled.","THE Infiniverse looked around THE Primordial Archive with eyes that calculated resources and potential and expansion. Her gaze swept across the floating books, the hovering scrolls, the crystallized tablets of knowledge, the architectural wonder of a Nexus Primordial Realm that now stood empty and unclaimed.","\"It seems Master has found another place for me to devour and integrate.\"","Noah’s smile widened as he nodded toward her. They began talking, the three of them, discussing what THE Agora could become under his authority. THE Infiniverse spoke of how her territory could extend, how the liquid potential of unrealized futures could feed her expansion. RUINATION contributed analysis of the knowledge contained within THE Primordial Archive as she began to sort through everything.","Their voices filled the empty Archive with warmth.","Their presence filled the abandoned realm with life.","Noah listened and responded and planned alongside them, his toga and laurels marking him as Strategoi while his companions marked him as something more important than any title could convey.","He was not merely the highest authority here. He was not merely the last inhabitant of a realm that had been emptied by THE Entity’s harvest!","He was someone who had built existence alongside others who chose to walk with him.","The floating books continued their eternal rotation. The scrolls continued hovering in organized arrangements. The knowledge continued waiting for access. But now there were voices in THE Primordial Archive. Now there was laughter echoing through halls that had known only silence since THE Entity’s departure.","In the end, Noah was not truly alone.","He was both free and still with those he had built existence with.","And that, perhaps, was the greatest paradox of all."]},{"number":4974,"title":"Chapter 4974: Chapter 4973: The Shadow He Cast I","paragraphs":["Alexander Asmodeus burned.","His existence burned with fire that exceeded physical flame, with heat that exceeded thermal measurement, with pain that exceeded anything THE Living Law had warned him about when they first began their partnership.","Every aspect of his Civilization was being consumed to fuel elevation that he had never asked for, advancement that he had never sought, power that was being purchased with currency he could not afford.","And yet he could not stop.","The brand of Horus blazed on his forehead with crimson light that commanded obedience beyond resistance. His body sat in meditative position against his will. His Civilization cycled through cultivation patterns that his consciousness had not chosen. His Depth, which had been approaching Fundamental before the eyes opened, now burned at heights that should have been impossible.","He had already become Absolute.","His Enneagram spun uncontrollably on his chest, its nine points blazing with silver light that held gold glimmers from the undifferentiation that Horus’s brand carried.","The construct that THE Living Law had helped him build, that had absorbed the weavings of countless beings across his journey, now operated at levels that made his previous power seem like a child’s toy.","He held tremendous Depth, and he felt tremendous pain as his existence burned in a terrifying way to achieve it.","Around him, the Early Creatures and Living Elementals that had been kneeling in submission now sat in the same meditative positions he occupied. Their forms pulsed with cultivation occurring against their will. Their foreheads bore the same crimson insignia that his did. Their existences burned alongside his own!","Many of them had already attained Fundamental Depth.","Some had reached Intermediate.","None of them were stopping as none of them could stop.","In his mind, in all of their minds, the words of enslavement repeated every few seconds with a voice that pressed against their consciousness like weight that could not be lifted.","\" Toil away and elevate yourselves for Horus.\"","The words arrived with force that made thought difficult.","\" Build your civilizations for Horus.\"","The words arrived with command that made resistance impossible!","\" Toil, and Persevere.\"","The words arrived with finality that made hope seem foolish.","Over and over. Every few fucking seconds. The voice of Horus resounding constantly through their branded existences, reminding them of what they were now, reminding them of who they belonged to, reminding them that their cultivation served purposes that were not their own.","Alex’s mind raced even as his body continued cultivating against his will.","Should he have stayed in THE Infiniverse with Osmont?","The thought emerged with bitterness that exceeded anything he had felt during his journey. He had left THE Infiniverse because he wanted to build his own path. He had departed from Osmont’s shadow because inherently, he himself had his own ego. He believed he could survive without the help of another. He believed his strength and his methodology and his partnership with THE Living Law would be sufficient.","Would he be where he was right now if he had stayed?","\"...\"","If he had remained under Osmont’s protection, if he had accepted being a follower rather than a leader, if he had swallowed his pride and joined the folds of someone else’s Civilization, he would not be sitting here with Horus’s brand burning on his forehead. He would not be cultivating against his will. He would not be burning his existence to fuel advancement that served an ancient monster rather than his own ambitions.","But he had left.","He had chosen his own path, and now that path had led him here.","Inside his Enneagram, all those he loved were staying within. The beings who had joined him, the followers who had believed in his vision of peace, the companions who had trusted his judgment, his family...all of them resided in that construct. And he could feel the brand of Horus going toward them little by little.","The crimson insignia was spreading! Slowly and Ievitably!","Could he live with himself if they all burned because of his choices?","\"...\"","As he thought about all of this, as the weight of his decisions pressed against his consciousness, something within him crystallized with defiance that rejected despair.","No.","His choice was his to make. Whether he was right or wrong, he would live with it. Osmont was not there when he went through everything he went through. Osmont was not there during the struggles and the growth and the pain that had shaped who he had become. Why... should he rely on another?","He had made his choice, so he would fucking stand by it!","HUUM!","His Enneagram shone brilliantly at this affirmation, silver light blazing with intensity that exceeded its forced cultivation!","But within that brilliance, THE Living Law’s voice echoed out in his mind.","The voice did not hold its usual confidence. It sounded despondent and it sounded defeated. It sounded like something that had assessed the situation and found no path forward.","\" This...Horus being may be grander than even THE Creature and others. This may be it.\"","...!","THE Living Law had actually given up!","Yet Alex still burned with defiance!","He would not give up. He would not surrender. He would not accept that this was how his story ended, burning his existence to fuel a monster’s purposes while the being who had partnered with him abandoned hope.","At this time, changes began blooming all around!","Weavings of Paradox flashed across this region of THE Wastes with intensity that made Alex’s forced cultivation pause momentarily. The corruption that permeated everything twisted with infinite variations that should not have been possible. The principles of existence itself seemed to stutter and shift. THE First Tongue’s expressions became paradoxical in ways that made pronunciation impossible.","The corrupted proto-matter filled with Infinities seethed as if a new paradox was weaving itself into its very fabric!","And the surroundings began to shine with an obsidian blue-gold brilliance that exceeded anything Alex had witnessed since arriving in THE Wastes!","Alex was astonished at this.","What was happening? What could produce changes of this magnitude? What force existed in THE Wastes that could alter the fundamental weavings of reality itself?","At this time, THE Wastes churned with violence that exceeded the paradoxical changes!","While still being forced to cultivate, while still burning his existence against his will, Alex looked over in a direction that his instincts screamed held danger beyond anything Horus had presented.","He saw...a massive armored entity appearing from THE Wastes.","It carried a hammer.","The entity was colossal beyond mortal scale. Platinum armor covered every inch of its frame with craftsmanship that predated the concept of craftsmanship itself. The armor seemed forged from proto-matter that had been convinced to become metal, each plate holding weight of undifferentiation that had been given form through will alone.","The hammer was massive even compared to the already colossal form that wielded it. Its head was composed of condensed metallic proto-matter that had been compressed until it achieved density beyond normal matter. The hammer’s surface shifted constantly, churning as if eager to be unleashed.","And the gaps between the armor’s plates revealed nothing but darkness.","No body. No being. Just the armor itself, existing as entity rather than equipment.","Alex looked toward this monstrous thing with despair and defiance warring across his features.","He could sense its aura.","And that aura felt eerily similar to the eyes of Horus!","Another...Primordial Architect.","\"...\"","Another force that exceeded everything Alex had prepared for, everything THE Living Law had imagined, everything he had built across his journey toward peace.","The armored Primordial Architect stood before them with stillness that lasted only a moment. Its visor, revealing nothing of features or thoughts or intentions, turned toward Alex with attention that felt like weight pressing down upon his existence.","It looked him over up and down.","Alex looked up at it defiantly even as his existence continued burning against his will.","Did existence truly wish for him and everything he wanted to collapse?","Was that why one monster after another was appearing?","First Horus. Now this armored entity. What would come next? How many ancient horrors would emerge to crush his ambitions before existence was satisfied with his suffering?","At such a time, the armored entity’s heavy voice boomed out across THE Wastes!","\"It is a shame.\"","The words emerged with authority and immensity that pressed against Alex’s consciousness like mountains settling upon his shoulders.","\" Horus has spread his brand so quickly. Just when I found a clue.\"","The armored Primordial Architect’s visor fixed upon Alex with attention that felt like being examined by something that had witnessed THE First Cause.","\"I was chasing the origin of these weavings of Infinity mixed in with proto-matter. The trail was clear. The scent was strong. And then, all of a sudden, these Infinities became truly paradoxical.\"","The hammer shifted in the entity’s grip.","\"I lost my scent. Even though it drew me here. To a little thing like you.\"","The visor tilted slightly.","\" Say, you are connected in some way to the owner of this Infinity? Might you know where I can find them?\"","The question hung in the air.","\" Could...you reach out to them?\"","...!"]},{"number":4975,"title":"Chapter 4975: Chapter 4974: The Shadow He Cast II","paragraphs":["The words were shocking to Alex.","His expression became heavy as implications pressed against his consciousness with force that exceeded the brand’s cultivation commands.","Connected to him? Infinities?","The only one Alex could think of was Osmont. The man whose Infiniverse he had departed from. The being whose protection he had rejected in favor of his own path!","This thing wanted Osmont?","This Primordial Architect, this armored horror that felt similar to Horus himself, was hunting the origin of Infinities that Alex had been connected to through his time in THE Infiniverse.","Alex looked at this ancient entity with defiance.","His eyes burned with conviction that his forced cultivation could not extinguish.","\"I do not know anything regarding Infinities.\"","His voice emerged steady despite everything.","\" And even if I did, I certainly would not share with something that is the same as Horus.\"","...!","At these glorious defiant words, the armored Primordial Architect’s armor did something that should not have been possible.","It smiled.","The platinum plates shifted and rearranged themselves into configuration that displayed amusement where no features should have existed. The visor curved. The helmet’s structure bent. The armor itself expressed emotion through metallic proto-matter that responded to the entity’s will.","\" Little guy.\"","The voice held warmth that contradicted its earlier weight.","\" Horus has you bound forever now. Even a thing at THE Second Scale of Existence won’t be able to get you out of it.\"","The hammer shifted again.","\" But me? I may just be able to. I can talk to Horus. We go back quite far, he and I.\"","The smile widened.","\" What say you? Your freedom for this origin of Infinity.\"","A pause.","\" And oh, I forgot to mention. I can also extract what I want very, very painfully from you.\"","The hammer rose slightly.","\" So, what choice will it be?\"","...!","Alex gritted his teeth with defiance.","His eyes reddened with emotion that exceeded mere anger!","Frustration, grief, and rage. Rage at himself, and at existence itself for placing him here, for making him choose between betraying someone who had once offered him shelter and suffering at the hands of a monster who could make pain last for eternities.","But he shed no tears.","He would not give this thing the satisfaction.","He thought of Osmont.","Alex had made his choice when he left THE Infiniverse.","He had chosen his own path over Osmont’s shadow, but that didn’t mean he would betray the man who had offered him a place when he had nothing.","For the first time in unknown eons, Alexander Asmodeus became the first entity to look at a Primordial Architect and say words that no one else had ever dared to speak.","\" Fuck...off.\"","...!","BOOM!","The words echoed across THE Wastes with weight that exceeded what a being at Alex’s Depth should have been capable of producing!","...!","The armored Primordial Architect’s smile became brilliant.","The platinum plates rearranged themselves into expression of genuine delight that made the previous smile seem restrained. The visor curved further. The helmet’s structure bent into configuration that displayed anticipation, excitement, eagerness for what would come next.","\"I was...hoping you’d go that route.\"","The voice held joy that contradicted the horror of what it promised.","\" Makes things much more exciting.\"","...!","In the next moment, devastation bloomed across THE Wastes!","The armored Primordial Architect waved its hammer with casual motion that belied the destruction it would produce. The weapon moved through the air with speed that Alex’s Absolute perception could barely track, its head of condensed metallic proto-matter leaving trails of undifferentiation in its wake.","The wave struck everything behind Alex.","All the Early Creatures that had been cultivating against their will, their existences burning to fuel Horus’s purposes, their brands blazing on their foreheads with crimson light, all of them disintegrated instantly!","All the Living Elementals that had been sitting in meditative positions, their Depths reaching heights they had never achieved through their own effort, their consciousness trapped within bodies that served another’s will, all of them disintegrated instantly!","The opened Shelter of THE Loom that had stood behind them, its massive structure that had protected beings before Alex had broken it open, its walls and defenses and accumulated resources, all of it disintegrated instantly!","A terrifying might of undifferentiation burned everything that the wave touched!","Nothing remained.","No bodies, no structures, no evidence that anything had ever existed in that space.","Just...Alex.","Just the brand on his forehead.","Just his Enneagram spinning with silver light that held those he loved within.","Just him, alone, facing a Primordial Architect that now had no reason to show restraint.","The massive armored entity loomed above him.","It was hundreds of times larger than Alex’s form. Its hammer alone exceeded his size by magnitudes that made comparison absurd. Its presence pressed down upon him with weight that should have crushed his consciousness entirely.","And yet Alex gazed up at it defiantly.","His existence still burned from Horus’s brand. His cultivation still continued against his will. His situation was hopeless by any rational assessment. He faced a Primordial Architect alone, without allies, without escape, without any power that could meaningfully resist what stood before him.","But he would not give up Osmont.","He would not betray someone who had never betrayed him. This was...his Peace.","\" COME ON THEN!\"","Alex bellowed upward at the armored horror with voice that cracked from strain but did not waver!","\" COME! ON!\"","BOOM!","His words echoed across THE Wastes with defiance that exceeded his Depth.","He was small.","So small compared to the monster that loomed above him.","So small compared to the forces that had shaped his fate.","So small compared to the ancient entities that now moved across Observable Existence.","But the shadow he cast over THE Wastes right now was unfathomably vast.","It was a ridiculous contrast to see a Primordial Architect and someone as small as him...seem almost as large at this moment.","Almost!","The armored Primordial Architect raised its hammer.","And Alex did not look away."]},{"number":4976,"title":"Chapter 4976: Chapter 4975: Master and Disciple I","paragraphs":["THE Primordial Paradox was surrounded by waves of Bounded Countable Infinite Paradoxes.","They churned around his existence with patterns that contradicted themselves and yet remained stable, with currents that flowed in multiple directions simultaneously, with expressions that should have been impossible and yet existed anyway because paradox permitted the impossible to be. The blue-gold dots that now scattered across his obsidian form pulsed with sequential light that extended endlessly in progression his consciousness could observe. Each dot was a seed of Infinity that THE Youngest had bestowed upon him, and each pulse was Countable expression following the previous one in order that would never terminate.","His Bounded Countable Infinity had fully integrated, and his Absolute Effigy had transformed to reflect this integration.","At this moment, his massive Effigy manifested above him with form that was shockingly not humanoid at all. It was a regal cat filled with Paradoxes, its feline form stretching across the skies with size that matched what his previous Effigy had displayed while holding elegance that exceeded humanoid configuration entirely.","Its fur was obsidian darkness scattered with blue-gold stars that pulsed with Infinite progression, and its eyes burned with contradiction given visual expression, swirling patterns that looked in multiple directions simultaneously while focusing on single points with intensity.","Its tail curved in spirals that defied spatial logic, each curve leading to contradictions that somehow connected back to harmony. Its claws extended with paradoxical sharpness that could cut things that couldn’t be cut and leave whole things that should have been severed, while its posture held royal bearing that commanded respect through presence rather than demand.","The Effigy was majestic and paradoxical and grand in ways that his previous manifestation had never achieved.","From its eyes, beams of infinite paradoxical light blazed outward with intensity that exceeded anything he had produced before his integration with Infinity. The light curved along geodesic paths that found the natural geometry of existence, following routes of minimal distance while somehow traveling through territories that shouldn’t have connected. The beams extended endlessly in sequential progression, each moment of light followed by another, Countable Infinity expressing itself through paradoxical illumination that would never cease.","And THE Primordial Paradox voiced out his own unique Embodiment that curved along those same geodesic paths.","\" My claim was taken and yet not taken.\"","The words emerged with weight that pressed against reality itself.","\"I hold it while I do not hold it. And I am exactly where the one who took my claim and did not take my claim is.\"","...!","BOOM!","A terrifying storm of Paradox erupted from the declaration as the Embodiment extended infinitely along geodesic curves, its paradoxical nature finding every instance of what it described, its Countable expressions arriving one after another in progression that would never cease.","The storm raged outward with contradiction that exceeded anything THE Primordial Paradox had produced before his integration with Infinity, and it only kept going without dissipating, without weakening, without fading as conventional Embodiments faded after their initial impact. It continued extending along natural paths through existence, its paradoxical nature compounding with every moment that passed.","THE Primordial Paradox felt calm within the storm of his own creation, expressing slight amazement at this Infinity that now burned within his foundations. So this was what THE Youngest played with, this endless nature that had drawn his attention from the moment he first perceived it!","It was remarkable and terrifying and exactly what he needed.","Gloriously, with the light of paradoxical Infinity blazing around his regal feline Effigy, THE Primordial Paradox paradoxically crossed unfathomable distances across Observable Existence in a single impossible moment. He moved through space without traversing it, arrived at destinations without departing from origins, and existed in multiple locations simultaneously while being singular in his consciousness.","The journey took no time because time had contradicted itself during the travel, and the distance meant nothing because distance had forgotten what measurement was.","He appeared... in THE Prima Indifferentia.","The corrupted proto-matter that filled this space pressed against his existence with weight.","The corruption was dense here, the formlessness was active, and the undifferentiation sought to consume everything that possessed definition with hunger that had existed since before THE Infinite Unfurling.","Mixed within the corruption, he saw glimmers of Infinite Seals scattered throughout the proto-matter like blue-gold stars scattered throughout void, THE Youngest’s Infinities having spread here and mixed with everything to create the combination of paradoxical proto-matter and Infinite expression that was causing so much chaos across Observable Existence.","But THE Primordial Paradox’s attention was not on the corruption or the Infinities.","His attention was on the figure standing in the distance, a peasant in rags who could only be Erwin, THE Living Paradox, his disciple who had consumed his claim across years of subtle betrayal.","At this moment, THE Primordial Paradox observed a scene that exceeded his expectations entirely as Erwin stood over a corpse that was not the corpse of an Absolute or some lesser being caught in THE Prima Indifferentia’s chaos or anything that THE Primordial Paradox would have expected his disciple to be consuming.","It was the corpse of a Primordial Architect.","The ancient entity lay collapsed across the corrupted proto-matter with form that resembled a massive Kongamato , its wings that had once spanned distances beyond measurement now broken and still against the formless ground.","Its beak that had once torn through realities with casual ease now hung open in the stillness of true death, and its feathers that had once burned with authority predating THE Infinite Unfurling now held no light at all. The corpse was massive and ancient and utterly dead, and Erwin was consuming it with hunger that exceeded anything THE Primordial Paradox had witnessed during their time together.","THE Living Paradox leaned down over the Primordial Architect’s corpse with posture that held no dignity and no shame, his ragged clothes stained with essences that shouldn’t have been possible to extract while his wild hair fell across features that burned with ambition exceeding anything THE Primordial Paradox remembered.","He was paradoxically consuming the Primordial Architect’s essence while utilizing corrupted proto-matter and the glimmer of Infinite Seals to amplify his harvest, the three substances mixing within his consumption in ways that should have been impossible.","But Erwin had always been comfortable with impossibility, and that was why THE Primordial Paradox had chosen him as disciple in the first place!"]},{"number":4977,"title":"Chapter 4977: Chapter 4976: Master and Disciple II","paragraphs":["He looked grand and wild and unkempt and glorious, like a peasant who had somehow found his way to a king’s feast and was devouring everything before anyone could remove him. He looked like THE Living Paradox should look!","When THE Primordial Paradox arrived, when his regal feline Effigy manifested in the skies of THE Prima Indifferentia with paradoxical Infinities raging around its form, Erwin looked over from his meal with eyes that held no fear.","They shone with recognition, with complex emotion that exceeded simple categorization. He actually nodded with respect that seemed genuine despite everything between them.","\" Master. It has been quite some time.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox looked over at his disciple with eyes that shone with their own complex light, his regal Effigy settling into stillness above them while its blue-gold starred fur pulsed with Infinite progression that matched the rhythm of his thoughts.","He observed the collapsed Primordial Architect and the consumption that was still occurring and the mixture of corruption and Infinity that his disciple was utilizing to amplify everything.","\"It has been some time, my disciple. You seem to be going wild nowadays, filled with endless ambition that I never would have expected.\"","His eyes fixed on the Kongamato’s corpse with appreciation.","\"I never would have pegged my disciple to be killing Primordial Architects, and for you to even be elevating your harvest with Paradox and Infinity, you have grown into someone I can be very proud of.\"","...!","A complex expression appeared on Erwin’s face as the recognition shifted into something more complicated, the history between them pressing against the moment. He actually sighed with indignation that held genuine grievance beneath its theatrical surface.","\" Master, you do not understand just how hard your peasant disciple has had it. Even now, while I am making all of these advancements in harvests, someone else will actually benefit from this.\"","He gestured at the Primordial Architect’s corpse with frustration that exceeded the gravity of what he was consuming.","\" Someone you should know, as it seems you have taken Boundless Infinity from him. I am barely keeping it reigned in right now, and that guy who helped you come out will actually get a portion of my harvest.\" His eyes flickered with something between annoyance and grudging respect as he spread his hands with theatrical despair. \" How crazy is that? A peasant like me has to work really hard.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox actually laughed, the sound booming across THE Prima Indifferentia with weight that pressed against the corrupted proto-matter surrounding them.","It was genuine laughter!","He looked around at the chaos of this space, at the corruption and the Infinities and the collapsed Primordial Architect and his disciple who had apparently been killing beings that most Absolutes couldn’t even perceive.","He smiled with an expression that held pride beneath its paradoxical nature.","\" How unique it is that at this point in time, my Paradox and your Paradox are both influenced with Infinity. But never mind that, my disciple, it has been such a long time.\"","His eyes met Erwin’s with directness that exceeded everything else.","\" But I must ask. Do you want to talk first, or do you want to fight?\"","...!","THE Living Paradox smiled back at his master, but then his expression shifted into something that held concern beneath its surface as he looked toward the being who had taught him everything about contradiction, who had shaped his understanding of impossibility, who had been betrayed by the very lessons he had taught.","And he saw something that made his theatrical persona fade into something more genuine.","\" Teacher, you have become a bit old and feeble, and I would feel bad attacking an old man like you right away.\" His voice carried care that exceeded mere words.","\" Let’s have you be comfortable first, and we can talk. Hey, we can even share a meal, and for the first time in eons, I can serve you again just like I used to.\"","His eyes held something that might have been nostalgia, and might have been grief, or might have been love for a teacher whose claim he had consumed.","\"A disciple once, a disciple always. A teacher once, a teacher for life. Please, let your disciple serve you a meal one last time.\"","...!","THE Primordial Paradox watched as his disciple carved out a portion of the collapsed Primordial Architect with care that exceeded what the violent consumption had suggested, the portion offered with hands that held respect beneath their ragged appearance. And THE Primordial Paradox accepted.","The two of them actually sat opposite each other cordially, master and disciple, teacher and student, the one who had been betrayed and the one who had done the betraying.","They sat across from each other in THE Prima Indifferentia with the corpse of a Primordial Architect between them, with corruption and Infinity swirling around them.","It was a ridiculous scene to see!","THE Living Paradox moved seriously to set up the portions for his master, arranging the carved essence with attention of genuine care and positioning the meal with formality that exceeded what his peasant persona typically displayed.","He served his teacher one last time with reverence that contradicted everything else about their relationship.","And in the region around them, in this place where THE Prima Indifferentia’s chaos should have dominated everything, something else had long since begun to rage with intensity that exceeded the surrounding corruption.","Unfathomably dense Paradoxes filled with Countable Infinities stormed around their peaceful meal, the geodesic Embodiment THE Primordial Paradox had spoken still extending endlessly along its natural paths. Now, with both master and disciple present, with both Paradoxes existing in the same space, the density of contradiction exceeded anything THE Prima Indifferentia had witnessed.","Blue-gold light mixed with obsidian-gold patterns as Bounded Countable expressions intertwined with unbounded paradoxical currents, and master and disciple sat peacefully within a storm that could have unmade lesser existences entirely.","They ate and they talked of old times, reminiscing of the past they shared as they prepared for what would come next, because this meal was exactly what THE Living Paradox had called it between them.","The last one."]},{"number":4978,"title":"Chapter 4978: Chapter 4977: Severing The Relationship!","paragraphs":["Master and disciple continued their feast amidst the raging storm of Paradoxes and Infinities.","The carved essence of the Primordial Architect tasted like contradiction itself, like consuming impossibility made manifest and finding nourishment in what should have unmade the consumer. THE Primordial Paradox ate with the patience of a being who had witnessed THE First Cause, savoring each portion his disciple had prepared for him while the corrupted proto-matter of THE Prima Indifferentia churned around their peaceful gathering.","Erwin watched his master eat for a long moment before speaking.","\" Master, just how did your existence manage to be where it currently is?\" His eyes held genuine curiosity beneath their theatrical surface.","\"I felt your claim weakening across the eons. I felt your presence fading from Observable Existence. And yet here you sit, restored and filled with Infinity no less. How?\"","THE Primordial Paradox chewed thoughtfully before swallowing.","\"I knew the whole time, my disciple. \" His voice remained calm, unbothered by the weight of what he described . \"I was simply making my preparations while you believed me fading. And then THE Youngest made some things possible that had not been possible before.\"","...!","Erwin’s expression cooled at those words, theatrical warmth giving way to something more calculating.","\" THE Youngest.\" He said the title like he was testing its weight on his tongue. \" Man. What an anomaly that one is. I’m pretty sure he was not even at THE First Scale of Existence a few days ago, and yet eons ago, he was already at THE First Scale of Existence and helping you.\"","He shook his head slowly. \" He is more paradoxical than either of us, and yet his weavings affect both of us. That feels unfair somehow.\"","THE Primordial Paradox heartily bit into another portion of the Primordial Architect, essence dripping from his lips as he chewed with satisfaction.","\" For others, time is but a plaything. I was born so long ago, but just being born in an era of differentiation and undifferentiation doesn’t mean I am necessarily the oldest.\" His regal feline Effigy pulsed with blue-gold light above them. \" Who knows, maybe unbeknownst to us, THE Youngest was also around when Primordial Architects were first born.\"","BOOM!","The words pressed against THE Prima Indifferentia with implications that made even Erwin pause mid-bite. The corrupted proto-matter around them seemed to shudder at the suggestion, at the possibility that THE Youngest’s paradoxical relationship with time ran deeper than anyone had calculated.","Erwin shook his head and waved his hands dismissively, trying to dispel the weight of what his master had suggested.","\" Don’t say such scary things, Master. \" He set down his portion with care that contradicted his casual tone. \" But tell me something. Are you...proud of your disciple? I have come far from that peasant you picked up all those eons ago.\"","The question hung between them with vulnerability that Erwin’s theatrical nature rarely permitted.","THE Primordial Paradox looked at his disciple with eyes that held complexity no simple answer could address. He saw the peasant he had found and the monster that peasant had become.","He saw the student who had learned and the betrayer who had consumed. He saw everything Erwin had been and everything Erwin now was.","\" Your Master is proud of what you have become.\"","Erwin’s eyes brightened at those words.","\" But the means you went about it.. .\" THE Primordial Paradox’s voice hardened. \" I have to discipline you one last time. In life, there are things one should do and things one should not do. What you did, consuming your master’s claim while he still lived, you really shouldn’t have done it, my disciple.\"","The brightness in Erwin’s eyes dimmed.","\" You remember my old lessons? \" THE Primordial Paradox set aside his portion and rose slowly to his full height . \"I will begin another right now.\"","HUUM!","The surroundings began to rage with Paradoxes unlike anything THE Prima Indifferentia had contained before!","These two entities were both here and not here, their presences occupying the same space while simultaneously existing elsewhere entirely. Their Paradoxes were both here and not here, their authorities overlapping and contradicting and somehow coexisting in configurations that would have driven lesser beings to madness simply from perception.","THE Primordial Paradox’s regal feline Effigy blazed with obsidian-gold light scattered with blue-gold stars. THE Living Paradox’s own authority surged in response, peasant rags billowing around a form that held power no peasant should possess.","At this time, Erwin rose from their meal with solemnity replacing his theatrical nature entirely.","\"I had hoped to use this time to sever the relationship between master and disciple.\" His voice carried no humor, no performance, no pretense of anything other than what he truly intended. \"I wanted this meal to be our farewell, not our battlefield. But I see now that you did not come here for closure.\"","THE Primordial Paradox rose as well, his restored form burning with Bounded Countable Infinity.","\"I have been your master. I am your master. And I will always be your master. \" Each statement landed with weight that pressed against Erwin’s existence. \" And what I will teach you now is that in Observable Existence, there cannot be two Paradoxes.\"","...!","The words hung between them with finality that made the raging storm around them seem quiet by comparison.","Erwin nodded seriously at his master’s declaration, all traces of the theatrical peasant gone from his bearing. He rose to stand coolly with his hands clasped behind his back, posture straight, eyes burning with resolve that matched THE Primordial Paradox’s own.","\" On this, we agree, Master.\" His voice held no tremor, no hesitation. \" There cannot be two Paradoxes. Which is why I have prepared for you just like I prepared for countless others.\"","His hands tightened behind his back.","\"I have prepared to declare with surety that in Observable Existence, there is only one Paradox.\"","He met his master’s gaze directly.","\" My Paradox.\"","A pause.","\" For what I am about to do to you, I am sorry, O Primordial Paradox.\"","BOOM!","For the first time, Erwin did not refer to THE Primordial Paradox as his master.","Behind him, something hazy and undiscernible began blooming in THE Prima Indifferentia’s corrupted space. It had no clear form, no obvious shape, no definition that conventional perception could grasp. It simply existed as presence that should not have been possible, as preparation that had been building across eons while THE Primordial Paradox believed himself fading and his disciple believed himself ascending.","THE Primordial Paradox looked at what bloomed behind his disciple.","His eyes opened wide in astonishment.","\" What...have you done?\"","The question emerged without his usual composure, without the calm that had characterized every word since his arrival. Genuine shock colored his voice as he perceived what Erwin had prepared, as he understood just how thoroughly his disciple had planned for this moment.","Erwin’s expression held no satisfaction at his master’s surprise. It held only grim necessity.","\" What I had to do.\"","His voice was quiet.","\" What... I had to do.\"","BOOM!","Paradoxes and Infinities bloomed across THE Prima Indifferentia with violence that made the previous storm seem like gentle rain!","The regal feline Effigy of THE Primordial Paradox clashed against whatever Erwin had prepared, obsidian-gold and blue-gold light meeting hazy undiscernible presence with force that tore through corrupted proto-matter in every direction. Master and disciple moved against each other with speed that transcended conventional measurement, their authorities colliding in configurations that redefined what collision meant.","An unfathomably terrifying battle started between the two beings who understood Paradox better than anyone else in Observable Existence.","And only one would emerge to claim that understanding as theirs alone."]},{"number":4979,"title":"Chapter 4979: Chapter 4978: An Army! I","paragraphs":["In THE Yggdrheim, another body of Noah stood amidst the vast expanse where his people cultivated.","Blue-gold flames wreathed his form in patterns that spoke of Infinity given visual expression, Absolute Seals orbiting his existence like satellites around a celestial body.","He looked like a force of nature standing still, like a storm that had chosen to pause and observe rather than rage and destroy. His eyes burned with calculation as he stared out at what lay before him, at the secret project he had been nurturing while his other bodies dealt with THE Agora and THE Primordial Paradox and all the chaos spreading across Observable Existence.","He knew he had many things in his hands.","The Geodesic Weavings. The Bounded Countable Infinity. The Sacred Herbs growing in the Early Veiled Shore. The Organ of Civilization producing Absolute and Infinite Everythings. The harvest flowing endlessly from every corner of his vast territories. He knew the possibilities that emerged from combining all of these elements, the configurations of power that his Infinite nature permitted.","So recently, he had been asking himself a simple question.","How could he utterly abuse his power?","Because he could abuse Infinity tremendously due to its very nature. Where others had to accumulate and conserve, he could spend without end. Where others had to choose between investments, he could invest everywhere simultaneously.","And right now, he needed to gain an edge against all the monsters awakening across Observable Existence.","Primordial Architects were stirring in THE Prima Indifferentia. THE Entity had claimed THE Primordial Chaos. Horus had branded countless beings with crimson insignias of servitude. Everywhere he looked, threats were multiplying faster than conventional response could address.","His solution came... in the form of Primus Inevitabilities.","These were the products of his Civilization of Hunger, the tentacled entities that had served him and Khor. He had millions of them, each one loyal beyond question, each one willing to give everything for their master without hesitation or regret. Millions upon millions!","Now, when it came to his people, Noah knew Adversity was key to progression. He was letting them struggle in THE Yggdrheim because struggle built foundations that could not be built any other way. If they did not face Adversity, absolutely none of them would achieve THE Second Scale of Existence.","But what if he had millions of Primus Inevitabilities who all loyally volunteered to be shields and swords for their master, even knowing they would never see THE Second Scale themselves?","The product was Noah being allowed to abuse his Countable Infinity freely.","He had millions of Primus Inevitabilities. He had boundless harvest flowing into his Organ of Civilization from territories spanning Observable Existence. And he had quite a few Lotuses of THE Bounded Lotus of Sequential Eternity ready for distribution.","THE Infinite Observable Harvest continued flowing into him even now, and when he directed it toward his Organ of Civilization, the organ could produce many more Absolute Everythings and Infinite Everythings than ever before. The pieces were all in place. The resources were all prepared.","This...allowed for the unfolding wonder to occur.","In front of him, an army of ten thousand Primus Inevitabilities floated in perfect ranks across THE Yggdrheim’s vast expanse. Each one had swallowed a petal from THE Bounded Lotus of Sequential Eternity, and each one now burned with Bounded Countable Infinity blazing through their tentacled forms. Ten thousand beings who had been powerful before now carried Infinity within their foundations, their existences elevated beyond what conventional cultivation could have achieved across eons.","He had millions of Primus Inevitabilities, but he was just beginning to produce THE Bounded Lotuses of Sequential Eternity in quantities sufficient for mass distribution. So he began with ten thousand. Ten thousand lotuses to ten thousand Inevitabilities, a foundation upon which he would build something terrifying.","At their forefront stood Protos.","The First Inevitability was connected to Noah in ways the others were not, serving as his armor, carrying his authority within its very existence.","Protos towered over even its impressive brethren, a massive humanoid titan whose entire body was composed of countless tentacles of Inevitability woven into humanoid form. Where other beings had flesh and bone, Protos had coiled tendrils of crimson authority that shifted and moved with purpose that spoke of hunger barely contained.","Crimson blue-gold light shone from every inch of Protos’s titanic frame. The tentacles that composed its body writhed with restrained energy, each one capable of independent action, each one carrying a fragment of the whole’s tremendous authority.","Behind Protos, the other thousands of Primus Inevitabilities stood in ranks that stretched toward the horizon.","They looked like slightly smaller versions of their leader, their massive titanic bodies all constructed from countless tentacles of Inevitability woven into humanoid configurations. Some shone with verdant blue-gold light. Others shone with bronze blue-gold light, their variations speaking of different paths of development within the same fundamental framework.","All of them waited in perfect stillness for their master’s command.","Another entity floated here alongside everyone, circling Protos with joy that seemed almost incongruous amidst such martial display. Skoll, the very good boy, had also been granted a lotus petal, his canine form blazing with Infinity as he moved happily around the Primus Inevitabilities.","Noah motioned to Skoll, and the loyal companion came over immediately.","He played with Skoll for a moment, scratching behind ears that burned with blue-gold light. Then he looked up at Protos and the army assembled behind the First Inevitability, his expression shifting from warmth to something more formal.","\" What is your duty?\"","Every single Primus Inevitability spoke as one, their voices merging into a chorus that pressed against THE Yggdrheim with weight armies of lesser beings could never produce.","\" Our duty is sacred.\"","Noah asked again.","\" What is your duty?\"","\" Our duty is to Infinity.\"","BOOM!","The declaration pressed against existence itself, ten thousand voices unified in purpose, ten thousand wills aligned toward service without reservation. Noah pointed to Protos, who stood at Fundamental Depth unlike the other Inevitabilities due to its deeper connection with him.","\" Others need Adversity, and it is true that by taking the short way, THE Second Scale will forever be out of your grasp. \" His voice carried no deception, no softening of harsh truth. \" Will you proceed?\"","Protos knelt before its master, tentacles coiling with reverence as its voice emerged with conviction unshakeable.","\" For the sake of Master, this sacrifice is the highest honor. We do not seek THE Second Scale. We seek only to serve. Our existence finds meaning in your purpose. Our deaths find glory in your victory. Command us, and we shall become whatever weapon you require. This is not loss. This is...fulfillment of our Duty.\"","The words rang across THE Yggdrheim with weight that made the other Inevitabilities straighten in their ranks.","Noah nodded and waved his hand.","An Absolute Everything materialized before Protos, a crystallized fragment of absolute authority compatible with those following Noah’s Civilizations. It floated toward the currently strongest Primus Inevitability, and Protos opened its form to receive it without hesitation. The Absolute Everything sank into the mass of tentacles and disappeared, absorbed into foundations already burning with Bounded Countable Infinity.","For a short moment, nothing happened.","Then Protos’s aura began to buzz with transformation.","\" Let a portion of the boundless harvest coming into me reinforce his foundations.\"","...!"]},{"number":4980,"title":"Chapter 4980: Chapter 4979: An Army! II","paragraphs":["Noah’s harvest, the endless flow of resources from territories spanning Observable Existence, diverted a fraction of its current toward Protos. The foundations of the strongest Primus Inevitability received a surge of brilliance that made its already impressive form blaze like a star being born. Bounded Countable Infinity merged with the Absolute Everything and the reinforcing harvest in configurations that compressed what should have taken eons into mere moments.","An aura of an Absolute buzzed around Protos in the next moment.","The First Inevitability had crossed the boundary between Fundamental and Absolute Depth through methods that bypassed conventional Adversity entirely. It knelt before Noah with its new authority pressing against THE Yggdrheim, tentacles coiling with power unlike anything it had possessed before.","But Noah was not done!","He produced a piece of THE Convergent Root of Density Absolute, the Sacred Herb that grew downward along geodesic paths and compressed Infinity into density approaching the spaces between sequences. The root fragment floated toward Protos, and the First Inevitability consumed it without question.","The effect was immediate.","Protos’s Bounded Countable Infinity began compressing within its foundations, the gaps between sequential expressions filling with density that conventional cultivation could not produce. Its aura, already Absolute, became denser in ways that made other Absolutes seem hollow by comparison!","The tentacles composing its form coiled tighter, each one carrying compressed Infinity that granted weight to every movement.","Then Noah produced a piece of THE Divergent Bloom of Infinite Variation.","This Sacred Herb embodied the opposite principle, spreading outward in endless branches that produced unique flowers with unpredictable effects. The flower fragment that floated toward Protos held properties Noah himself could not fully predict, variations generated through divergent cultivation rather than deliberate design.","Protos consumed it.","The effect merged with everything else occurring within the First Inevitability’s foundations. Its Geodesic Weavings enhanced in directions Noah had not planned.","Small, tiny glimpses of Uncountable Infinity flickered through its existence, temporary elevations that showed what further advancement might feel like.","Protos blazed with utter brilliance before Noah, an Absolute unlike any other Absolute, carrying Bounded Countable Infinity compressed by Convergent Root and varied by Divergent Bloom!","It was not merely powerful. It was optimized through Sacred Herb cultivation that no other force in Observable Existence could replicate!","And there were thousands more waiting.","Noah looked at the next Primus Inevitability that came forward, its Surface Depth requiring more investment than Protos had needed. Three Absolute Everythings materialized before it instead of one, the greater quantity necessary to elevate foundations that had further to climb. The Inevitability swallowed all three without hesitation.","Noah repeated the same process.","Harvest surged into the Inevitability’s foundations. A piece of Convergent Root followed. A piece of Divergent Bloom after that. Moments later, another Absolute with Bounded Countable Infinity knelt before him, its existence transformed through methods that compressed eons into seconds.","And then the full scope of his preparations revealed itself.","Above him, all the ingredients he had utilized bloomed into seas of dozens and then hundreds and then thousands. Absolute Everythings materialized in quantities that would have seemed impossible before his Organ of Civilization began operating at full capacity.","Lotus petals floated in spiraling arrangements that mirrored their source’s eternal blooming. Pieces of Convergent Root and Divergent Bloom multiplied through cultivation he had been conducting across his territories.","Prompts blazed before his eyes.","|Assessment: Your Organ of Civilization is finally truly performing its intended function. Substantial harvest has been directed toward its operation, enabling production of Absolute Everythings at rates sufficient for mass elevation.|","|Current Production Capacity: Sufficient Absolute Everythings for thousands of elevations. Sufficient Lotus petals for continued Bounded Countable Infinity bestowal. Sufficient Sacred Herb fragments for optimization of elevated beings.|","|Projection: You possess the resources to create an army of Absolutes carrying Bounded Countable Infinity enhanced by Sacred Herb cultivation. No other force in Observable Existence can replicate this methodology.|","...!","Noah watched all of this with eyes that shone with light matching his designs.","He did his best not to form a devilish smile, but he could not help it. The expression spread across his features with anticipation that bordered on something darker, something hungrier, something that spoke of Infinite ambition finally finding adequate expression!","His lips curved upward while his eyes remained calculating, the combination producing a smile that would have unsettled anyone who witnessed it.","It was the smile of someone who was about to change the fundamental mathematics of conflict across Observable Existence.","It was the smile of mad Infinity given human expression, the curve of lips belonging to a being who understood that he was just beginning to scratch the surface of what his nature permitted.","He waved his hands.","Multiple Absolute Everythings and other ingredients surged toward multiple Inevitabilities simultaneously, his control over the process allowing parallel elevation rather than sequential. The Primus Inevitabilities received their gifts without hesitation, their forms blazing with transformation as harvest and Herbs and crystallized authority merged within their foundations.","Within seconds, auras of Absolutes began rising one after another.","One. Five. Ten. Twenty. The count climbed rapidly as more and more Inevitabilities completed their elevations, their Surface Depths becoming Absolute Depths through methods that bypassed every conventional limitation. Each one knelt toward Noah as transformation completed, their loyalty unchanged by power that would have driven lesser beings to arrogance.","THE Infinite Farmer was using his harvests to truly lay a foundation at this moment.","He commanded resources to flow toward multiple Primus Inevitabilities, watching multiple Absolutes filled with Infinities being born one after another in sequences his Countable nature could observe and appreciate. Beside him, Skoll moved happily as Noah allowed resources to flow into the loyal companion as well, the very good boy’s form blazing brighter with each passing moment.","But Noah continued watching the main event with shining eyes.","Within moments, more than one hundred terrifying Absolutes filled with Infinities stood before him. One hundred beings carrying Bounded Countable Infinity compressed by Convergent Root and varied by Divergent Bloom!","One hundred weapons that had not existed an hour ago, each one loyal beyond question, each one optimized through Sacred Herb cultivation.","And there were thousands of Primus Inevitabilities remaining.","Noah truly could not help himself.","The devilish smile on his face deepened into something that would have made observers shudder with instinctive unease!","His lips curved further while his eyes narrowed, the expression carrying traces of mad Infinity!","Existence was tough, yes.","Existence was filled with Adversities that crushed the unprepared and humbled the arrogant.","He wanted to build an army that would give a glimpse of such Adversities to others.","And even while he built all of this, even while Absolutes multiplied before him like harvest being reaped from infinite fields, this did not yet account for the Specializations among his Inevitabilities. Some were optimized for defense, some were optimized for attack, and some were optimized for healing and revival, their authority capable of restoring collapsed allies to full function mere moments after apparent death.","An army that could defend and attack and heal itself, each member carrying Bounded Countable Infinity at Absolute Depth.","An army that would grow larger with every passing day as his Sacred Herbs continued blooming and his Organ of Civilization continued producing.","An army that existed because Noah had asked himself how he could abuse his power and then found an answer that others could not match.","Oh.","Oh!","He...was just getting started!"]},{"number":4981,"title":"Chapter 4981: Chapter 4980: Legions of Absolutes I","paragraphs":["The idea of mass producing Absolutes came to Noah’s mind simply when he saw what the Embodiment of THE Creature did to THE Living Origin and others.","If THE Creature could achieve such elevation with his finite resources, then what could Noah accomplish with infinite resources? THE Creature was more powerful, certainly, his existence predating THE Infinite Unfurling itself and his authority approaching THE Second Scale or already there.","But THE Creature could not mass produce Absolute Everythings. THE Creature could not cultivate Sacred Herbs that bestowed Bounded Countable Infinity upon consumers. THE Creature could not direct endless harvest toward an Organ of Civilization that transformed that harvest into crystallized authority compatible with loyal followers.","Noah could do all of these things.","Right now, he was doing everything he could while he continued to watch the army being born before him.","By his side, Skoll had calmed down from his earlier excitement, now watching in amazement as Absolutes rose one after another from the elevation process.","Noah rubbed the loyal companion’s head while calmly observing Protos calling forth other Absolute Primus Inevitabilities like a sergeant inspecting soldiers, the First Inevitability’s crimson blue-gold form moving through the ranks with purpose that spoke of pride in what had been prepared.","Noah was doing all this because he wanted to prepare for the worst possible eventualities.","When he asked himself what he could feasibly face in the name of Adversity, the answers that emerged were terrifying.","A Primordial Architect awakened from THE Prima Indifferentia at THE First Scale.","A Primordial Architect at THE Second Scale of Existence, something that conventional Absolutes could not even perceive let alone contest. THE Entity itself, that unified horror wearing THE Primordial Chaos as its newest mask.","And perhaps most concerning of all, the horrible variable of THE Entity somehow getting past his Infinities to infect him or his people, turning his own forces against everything he had built.","So how could he prepare for if or when such things occurred?","He had to have such insane things around him that they would make even old monsters like THE Primordial Paradox or THE Creature baffled at what they witnessed.","When he thought about THE Primordial Paradox, he knew that ancient being was battling against his disciple right now in THE Prima Indifferentia.","Part of him believed that Erwin might have more in the tank than anyone expected, because a peasant who had prepared this much, who was making changes across Observable Existence through corrupted proto-matter mixed with Infinite Seals.","But THE Primordial Paradox should still be okay since he carried Noah’s Infinities burning within his foundations, and the paradox of that being itself was truly heavy. Whatever happened, Noah did not expect THE Primordial Paradox to be collapsed easily.","And of course, the biggest thing wss Noah’s own power as if he went from Countable Infinity to Uncountable Infinity? Oh boy.","Oh boy!","\" Master, I have formed specific Legions ready for you.\"","At this time, Protos rose and turned to face the armies assembled behind him.","His tentacles coiled with purpose as he gestured toward the thousands of Primus Inevitabilities awaiting their transformations, his crimson blue-gold light casting long shadows across THE Yggdrheim’s expanse. Noah watched with that devilish smile still playing across his features as Protos moved aside to reveal formations of Absolutes he had arranged according to their Specializations.","\" Your Inevitabilities have long held Specializations that served you at lesser Depths. But now, with Bounded Countable Infinity and Absolute authority burning within our foundations, these Specializations have become something else entirely.\" Protos gestured toward the first formation of one hundred newly elevated Absolutes. \" Permit me to introduce what your legions have become.\"","The first hundred Absolutes moved forward in perfect synchronization.","They were massive things, each one a titan of coiled tentacles standing dozens of times larger than humanoid scale. But where Protos appeared sleek and predatory, these Absolutes appeared fortified beyond reason. Their tentacles had woven themselves into layered configurations resembling living fortresses, each coil locked against the next in patterns that spoke of absolute defense. Crystalline plates of obsidian-gold covered their forms like armor grown from their very existence, and their eyes glowed with steady silver light holding no aggression, only unwavering certainty.","\" The Absolute Infinite Bulwark Specialization,\" Protos announced. \" One hundred Absolutes who have sacrificed all offensive capability in exchange for defense that curves along geodesic paths toward everything requiring protection. Each one can read defensive Embodiments or Apophasis and fill them with Geodesic Weavings like Mantras again and again to build ridiculous defenses amplified because they only ever defend.Their duty is grand. Their duty is infinite!\"","Noah’s eyes sharpened with interest.","This was the other component he had been patiently waiting for.","With THE First Tongue, all things could Specialize from it. He had missed his Civilization Specializations that allowed him to raise armies which could not be taken down, and he had wanted to reproduce this capability at an even higher level than before.","Now he looked at what Protos had set aside just for a single Legion of Absolutes, and part of what comprised this legion were one hundred tanks operating at Absolute Depth with Bounded Countable Infinity.","\" Their defensive authority now extends infinitely in Countable sequences, Master. When an attack approaches an ally, the Bulwark’s protection finds the shortest path through existence to intercept it. They do not need to be near what they defend. They simply need to be, and their defense travels along natural geometries to arrive where it is needed.\"","The hundred Bulwarks stood motionless, their crystalline plates shifting with subtle movements that stabilized the very fabric of THE Yggdrheim around them.","\" They cannot deal damage through any means ,\" Protos continued. \" This limitation is absolute and cannot be circumvented. But in exchange, all damage directed toward them or those they protect is absorbed into foundations that regenerate infinitely with stacks of Defensive Embodiments and Apophasis, stacks of Sleeping Inscriptions and more. They cannot be overwhelmed through sustained assault because their endurance extends in sequences without termination. Strike them once, they endure. Strike them a trillion times, they endure still. Strike them forever, and forever they will remain standing.\"","Protos paused.","\" Nothing of THE First Scale should be capable of bypassing them, theoretically. We still have to see how they would perform against those more powerful since we do not have enough information on what THE Second Scale truly represents.\"","...!"]},{"number":4982,"title":"Chapter 4982: Chapter 4981: Legions of Absolutes II","paragraphs":["|Infinite Bulwark Specialization - Absolute Configuration|","|Core Transformation: Total offensive capability sacrificed. Defensive authority multiplied through Bounded Countable Infinity, extending protection along geodesic paths toward all designated allies regardless of distance.|","|Geodesic Defense Propagation: Protection travels along shortest paths through existence, arriving at threatened allies before attacks can land. Multiple Bulwarks create overlapping geodesic networks that make protected zones effectively impenetrable.|","|Infinite Damage Absorption: All damage received is absorbed into foundations regenerating in Countable sequences. Cannot be overwhelmed through sustained assault. Damage absorption of Embodiments and Apophasis and other forms of attacks continues indefinitely without degradation.|","|Existential Anchoring: Presence stabilizes reality in Countable radiating waves. Spatial tears, dimensional collapse, and reality manipulation become impossible within their geodesic sphere of influence. The very fabric of existence strengthens around them.|","|Fortress Convergence: Multiple Bulwarks can merge defensive fields along shared geodesic paths, creating barriers whose strength multiplies rather than merely adds. One hundred Bulwarks merged could theoretically withstand assault from beings approaching THE Second Scale.|","|Damage Conversion Reservoir: All damage absorbed is stored in Infinite reservoirs that can be channeled to offensive specialists. The Bulwarks become batteries of redirected destruction, feeding power to those who can use it.|","...!","Noah nodded slowly.","One hundred beings who could not be overwhelmed, who could protect allies across any distance through geodesic propagation, who stored absorbed damage for redistribution to those who could use it offensively. They were infinite fortifications that moved and adapted and refused to fall no matter what struck against them.","\" Show me the next ones.\"","Protos gestured, and the Bulwarks moved aside in perfect formation.","The second hundred Absolutes came forward, and Noah felt the hunger radiating from them before they fully arrived. These titans were sleek where the Bulwarks had been fortified, their tentacles configured for speed and precision rather than layered defense. Crimson-obsidian coloration dominated their forms, multiple serrated maws visible across their bodies where the tentacles parted to reveal depths of concentrated aggression. Their eyes burned with ravenous red light tinged with blue-gold Infinity, and wisps of pure Hunger escaped from every surface like heat rising from flames.","They looked like predators shaped from nightmare and given Absolute authority.","\" The Absolute Hungering Maw Specialization,\" Protos announced. \" One hundred Absolutes who have sacrificed defensive capability for offensive power that strikes along geodesic paths toward everything they wish to consume.\"","The Maws shifted restlessly even while standing in formation, their tentacles writhing with barely contained violence that made the Bulwarks’ stillness seem peaceful by comparison.","\" Their attacks now find the shortest path to their targets, Master. They do not need to be near what they strike. They simply need to hunger, and their destruction travels along natural geometries to arrive where it is directed. Distance becomes irrelevant. Conventional defense becomes meaningless. Their strikes attack existence itself along curves that bypass barriers entirely.\"","Noah watched the Maws with appreciation that matched their own hunger.","\" They are fragile ,\" Protos admitted . \"Their defensive capability has been reduced to nearly nothing, and sustained assault could collapse them if unprotected. But the Bulwarks are always protecting them. Any Embodiments or Apophasis thrown their way is tanked by their defensive counterparts. Unless the Bulwarks die, these Maws will never receive damage.\"","His tentacles coiled with emphasis.","\" And in exchange for their fragility, every kill strengthens them in Countable sequences without termination. The first kill makes them stronger. The thousandth kill makes them devastating. The trillionth kill makes them approach forces that conventional Absolutes cannot comprehend.\"","|Hungering Maw Specialization - Absolute Configuration|","|Core Transformation: Defensive capability reduced to minimal thresholds. Offensive authority multiplied through Bounded Countable Infinity, extending strikes along geodesic paths toward all designated targets regardless of distance or defense.|","|Geodesic Strike Propagation: Attacks travel along shortest paths through existence, arriving at targets through routes that bypass conventional barriers. Cannot be blocked through positioned defense. Can only be avoided through movement exceeding geodesic calculation speed.|","|Reality Severance: Embodiments and Apophasis attack existence itself rather than physical or spiritual forms. Ignore defensive constructs by targeting the fundamental nature of what is being struck. Even beings with absolute defense take damage to their existential foundations.|","|Infinite Hunger Stacks: Each successful kill increases offensive power in Countable sequences without termination. Power accumulates indefinitely during extended conflict. Theoretical maximum does not exist. The longer battle continues, the more devastating Maws become.|","|Predatory Geodesic Instinct: Can perceive the weakest point in any defense or existence along natural geometric paths. Strikes automatically curve toward vulnerabilities that conventional perception cannot detect.|","|Feast of Conquest: Can temporarily consume and wield defeated enemies’ abilities, storing them in Infinite reservoirs for later deployment. Abilities persist in Countable sequences until deliberately released or overwritten.|","...!","Noah’s smile widened as he observed the restless Maws.","Glass cannons, yes, but glass cannons whose strikes could not be blocked through conventional means, whose power grew infinitely with every kill, whose hunger found targets along paths that defense could not anticipate. Paired with Bulwarks who could protect their fragile forms while they accumulated devastating power, they became something truly terrifying. The Bulwarks absorbed damage that would collapse the Maws instantly, and in exchange, the Maws delivered destruction that the Bulwarks could never produce on their own.","\" Continue.\"","The Maws moved aside with reluctance, their hunger clearly desiring demonstration rather than mere display. Noah could feel their eagerness pressing against his awareness, their desire to be unleashed upon enemies worthy of their transformed nature.","The third hundred Absolutes came forward, and the atmosphere shifted from aggression to something warmer.","These titans were wreathed in green-gold-blue light that pulsed in rhythms resembling heartbeats, their tentacles configured in intricate mandala-like patterns that glowed with soft radiance. They appeared gentler than their brethren despite their massive size, their eyes shining with compassionate emerald light holding no violence whatsoever. Halos of Infinite light orbited their forms like crowns given to those who preserved rather than destroyed.","\" The Vital Chorus Specialization ,\" Protos announced. \" One hundred Absolutes who have sacrificed offensive capability for healing and resurrection that travels along geodesic paths toward everything requiring restoration.\"","The Chorus stood in perfect stillness, their mandala patterns pulsing with synchronized rhythm that seemed to match the heartbeat of THE Yggdrheim itself.","\" Their healing now extends infinitely in Countable sequences, Master. When an ally suffers damage, the Chorus’s restoration finds the shortest path through existence to reach them. Distance becomes irrelevant for preservation just as it becomes irrelevant for destruction. And their resurrection capabilities have transcended what we previously understood possible.\"","Noah’s interest sharpened at those final words.","\" When an Inevitability falls in battle, resurrection requires time. But the Chorus can reduce that time along geodesic paths until it approaches instantaneous.\" Protos’s tentacles coiled with emphasis. \" If a Maw is collapsed during combat, the Chorus can restore them within moments rather than hours. And their Life-Binding capability now extends in Infinite sequences. One Chorus member can bind to thousands of allies simultaneously, ensuring resurrection persists so long as even a single healer survives.\"","|Vital Chorus Specialization - Absolute Configuration|","|Core Transformation: Offensive capability reduced to minimal thresholds. Healing and resurrection authority multiplied through Bounded Countable Infinity, extending restoration along geodesic paths toward all designated allies regardless of distance or damage severity.|","|Geodesic Restoration Propagation: Healing Embodiments and Apophasis travel along shortest paths through existence, arriving at wounded allies through routes that bypass interference. Cannot be blocked or prevented. Healing arrives with inevitability matching the strikes of Hungering Maws.|","|Infinite Life-Binding: Can establish permanent soul-bonds with allies in Countable sequences without termination. One Chorus member can bind to thousands simultaneously. Bound allies resurrect automatically upon collapse so long as their bound Chorus survives.|","|Resurrection Acceleration: Collapse recovery time reduced along geodesic paths until approaching instantaneous. Allies restored to full capability within moments of falling. Sustained assault cannot permanently eliminate protected forces.|","|Symphonic Resonance: Healing multiple targets simultaneously creates resonance that multiplies effects along geodesic intersections. One hundred Chorus members healing together produce restoration exceeding their combined individual capabilities by orders of magnitude.|","|Death Defiance Aura: Allies within geodesic connection cannot be instantly killed through any means. Always survive lethal strikes with minimum existence remaining, permitting Chorus restoration before true collapse occurs.|","...!"]},{"number":4983,"title":"Chapter 4983: Chapter 4982: Legions of Absolutes III","paragraphs":["Noah understood immediately what the Chorus represented.","An army that could not be permanently diminished. Every Maw that fell would rise again within moments. Every Bulwark that absorbed damage would be restored before that damage could accumulate toward collapse. The Chorus transformed his legions from powerful force into inexhaustible force, an army of Absolutes that could theoretically fight forever without losing members to permanent death.","Kill a Maw, and the Chorus brings it back before its power stacks can reset.","Overwhelm a Bulwark through sustained assault, and the Chorus restores it before the protected Maws become vulnerable.","Collapse a Chorus member, and the other ninety-nine continue resurrection operations without interruption.","A fucking infinite loop of defense!","\" And the last. A new wonder.\"","The Chorus moved aside with gentle precision, their mandala patterns continuing to pulse as they joined the other formations.","The fourth hundred Absolutes came forward, and these were different from all the others in ways that went beyond mere combat capability. Their tentacles had configured into forms covered in constantly shifting geometric patterns and floating holographic interfaces that orbited their massive bodies like moons around planets. Streams of data and architectural schematics flowed through their eyes like rivers of calculation given visual form. Tools and materials and half-manifested constructs surrounded each one, suggesting beings who created rather than destroyed.","\" The Architects of Infinity Specialization, \" Protos announced. \" One hundred Absolutes who have sacrificed direct combat capability for construction and strategic enhancement.\"","The Architects stood amid clouds of floating geometric shapes and orbiting instruments, their nature clearly different from warriors.","Noah observed the data streaming through their eyes with appreciation for their uniqueness among the Specializations. Where Bulwarks defended and Maws attacked and Chorus healed, Architects built. They created the infrastructure upon which all other operations could be optimized.","\" They can manifest defensive structures, weapons, and technological marvels for you. Their constructs persist permanently even if the Architects themselves are collapsed. And their presence accelerates all Civilizational development.\" Protos’s tentacles gestured toward the floating geometric shapes. \" They do not even need to be on the battlefield. They can remain where you place them, working endlessly to see if they can build you something grand while battles rage elsewhere.\"","|Architects of Infinity Specialization - Absolute Configuration|","|Core Transformation: Direct combat capability reduced significantly. Construction, technological development, and strategic planning authority multiplied through Bounded Countable Infinity, extending creation along geodesic paths toward all locations requiring optimization.|","|Infinite Blueprint Manifestation: Created constructs persist permanently in Countable sequences without maintenance requirement. Even if Architects are collapsed, their creations remain. Theoretical maximum constructs do not exist. Given time, Architects can fortify entire realms.|","|Resource Efficiency Through Infinity: Construction costs reduced along geodesic optimization paths until approaching negligible. Can create advanced constructs using fractions of normal resource requirements. Bounded Countable Infinity permits effectively unlimited building capacity.|","|Strategic Calculation Matrix: Process tactical variables in Countable sequences without termination. Consider all possible enemy responses and counter-responses simultaneously. Provide commanders with strategic options that conventional analysis cannot generate.|","|Technological Symbiosis: Can interface with and enhance any technology or construct. Existing defenses and weapons improve simply through Architect presence.|","...!","Noah looked across the four formations now standing before him in THE Yggdrheim.","One hundred Absolute Bulwarks who could not be overwhelmed. One hundred Maws whose strikes found targets through routes that bypassed barriers and whose hunger grew infinitely with every kill they achieved. One hundred Chorus whose healing arrived with inevitability and whose resurrection reduced collapse to momentary inconvenience. One hundred Architects.","Four hundred Absolutes with Bounded Countable Infinity, each one optimized through Sacred Herb cultivation, each one carrying Specializations that had been elevated to match their Infinite nature. And there were thousands more Primus Inevitabilities waiting for the same categorizations and elevation, thousands more who would join these formations until his armies numbered in quantities that nobody could not match.","Protos’s crimson blue-gold light blazed with pride at what had been prepared.","Protos knelt once more before his master.","\" My Master, I will give you an army of Absolutes that existence itself will struggle to halt.\"","HUUM!","Noah looked at the four hundred Absolutes standing in formation, then looked at the thousands still awaiting elevation. His devilish smile returned with intensity that made even Protos’s tentacles coil with instinctive response.","\" Mm. I want a test run.\"","He truly did. Existence was vast and filled with terrors, and he wanted to see what his preparations could accomplish against worthy opposition. Theories and projections were useful, but nothing replaced actual demonstration against enemies who wished to destroy what he had built.","He closed his eyes and activated Infinite Undifferentiated Fate.","Endless weavings of Fate permeated around him, blue-gold threads extending in every direction along geodesic paths that connected him to probabilities spanning Observable Existence. His Infinities were already flowing across corrupted proto-matter in THE Prima Indifferentia.","His influence already touched countless regions through harvest and Seals and the connections he had established across his territories.","He asked his question to the weavings themselves.","Are there any enemies out there for me to test my works of art against?","If his Infinities sensed anything connected to him, any Undivided Ones, any Formless Terrors, any...viable Primordial Architects who weren’t too powerful, he might be able to lock onto their location. And then he could move with his Legions of Absolutes to demonstrate what mass production of Infinity truly meant.","But first, they needed a name.","A Legion of four hundred Absolutes with different Specializations working in perfect coordination required designation worthy of what they represented. Noah opened his eyes and looked across the formations awaiting his command, his mind considering titles that would capture their nature","\" From this moment forward, this formation of four hundred shall be designated as a single unit.\"","His voice pressed against THE Yggdrheim with weight that made the assembled Absolutes straighten further in their ranks.","\" You shall be called the Tetras Apeiron. The Infinite Four.\"","BOOM!","The name settled into existence with authority that made the formations blaze brighter with blue-gold light.","\" One hundred Bulwarks. One hundred Maws. One hundred Chorus. One hundred Architects. Four Specializations unified into single expression, four aspects of Infinite warfare combined into force that fights as one organism rather than four hundred individuals.\"","Noah’s smile was grand!","\" The first Tetras Apeiron stands before me now. But there will be more. Tetras Apeiron Secundus when the next four hundred complete their elevation. Tetras Apeiron Tertius after that. And onward until I have legions beyond counting, each one capable of operations that will bring every single fucker out there to their knees...\"","Protos rose from his kneeling position, his crimson blue-gold form blazing with pride at the designation his forces had received.","\" The Tetras Apeiron awaits your command, Master. Point us toward enemies worthy of demonstration, and we shall show Observable Existence what Infinity truly means, what Tyranny truly means! This...is our Duty!\"","WAA!","Noah closed his eyes once more, reaching through his weavings of Fate to find targets that would serve as appropriate tests for his newly forged weapons."]},{"number":4984,"title":"Chapter 4984: Chapter 4983: THE Beholder I","paragraphs":["In the vast spaces between what was and what would become, THE Beholder drifted.","He was old. Not old in the way that Primordial Architects were old, those beings who had existed since THE First Cause produced differentiation and undifferentiation in its aftermath. Not old in the way that THE Creature was old, that defector from classifications who had witnessed THE Infinite Unfurling and everything that came after.","THE Beholder was old in ways that made such comparisons laughable, in ways that made the entire history of Observable Existence seem like a brief afternoon following an endless morning that most had forgotten ever occurred.","Many believed that there was THE First Cause, and then differentiation and undifferentiation bloomed to cause the emergence of Primordial Architects and countless other life forms. This was the accepted history. This was what beings taught their disciples and recorded in their archives and treated as the beginning of everything meaningful.","The only record that might have the correct information was The Primordial Archive in that small place.","But truly, there was a period of billions upon billions of years where during THE First Cause, there was nothing.","THE Beholder knew this because he had been there.","He had gained cognizance in that age of absolute emptiness, when potential existed but expression did not, when possibility waited but manifestation had not yet learned how to occur. He had observed and watched and done nothing across spans of time so vast that they made the current age seem like the blink of an eye, like the flutter of a heartbeat, like a single grain of sand falling through an hourglass that had been running since before hourglasses were conceived.","The entirety of the history of Observable Existence, everything that beings considered meaningful and important and worth recording, was actually that period of nothing in terms of duration. Everything that came after, during the age of differentiation and undifferentiation until now, was simply a fraction of the history of existence. A footnote. An afterthought. The brief flash of complexity following eons of simplicity so profound that most minds could not comprehend it.","In the grand scheme of existence, even Primordial Architects and Undivided Ones could be considered accidents.","Happy accidents, perhaps. Interesting accidents, certainly. But accidents nonetheless, random emergences from the interplay of differentiation and undifferentiation that had not existed for most of existence’s duration.","They thought themselves ancient. They thought themselves fundamental. They thought their conflicts and their civilizations and their pursuits of power actually mattered in the Existential sense.","THE Beholder found this perspective amusing in the way that a being who had witnessed true emptiness found most things amusing.","He was what later classifications might call a Singular Cognizance , though no classification system had ever properly categorized his kind because so few of them existed and even fewer interacted with the complex life that came after.","Where Primordial Architects had emerged with vast authorities and tremendous presence, where Absolutes had developed civilizations and pursued advancement, where even the simplest differentiated beings possessed multiple aspects of existence working in concert, THE Beholder possessed only one thing.","Awareness.","Pure, undiluted, singular awareness that had crystallized during the age of nothingness when there was nothing else to be. No hunger. No ambition. No civilization. No authority beyond the simple capacity to observe what was and what was not. He was consciousness without complexity, perception without pursuit, understanding without desire to apply that understanding toward any particular end.","In the terminology of later ages, he might be considered the equivalent of what simple organisms were to complex life. Where multicellular creatures developed specialized systems and interdependent functions, unicellular life simply existed in singular purpose. THE Beholder was existence’s equivalent of that primordial simplicity, a being who had emerged before complexity was possible and who had never seen reason to develop beyond his original nature.","There had been others like him in that age of nothingness.","Fellow Singular Cognizances who had gained awareness in the emptiness and had observed alongside him across those billions of eons of years when observation was all there was to do. Whether they still moved across existence now, or had simply collapsed themselves into weavings of nothingness to return to the state from which they had emerged, THE Beholder did not know.","He had not sought them out. He had not pursued connection or communion or any of the social behaviors that complex life seemed to require. He simply was, as he would likely always be until existence itself ceased to provide things worth observing.","For the first time in a few eons, some significant changes had occurred.","These changes were significant enough to cause THE Beholder to emerge from THE Prima Indifferentia, that space of undifferentiation where he often rested between periods of observation. Something was happening with existence now. Something that warranted attention.","Something that stirred memories of that age of nothingness in ways that more recent events had never managed to accomplish.","Infinities were spreading.","THE Beholder had observed many things across his incomprehensible lifespan, but Infinity held particular interest because it carried glimmers of what had existed during that age of wonder before Primordial Architects were even conceived.","The nothingness had not been truly nothing, not in the absolute sense. It had been potential without limit, possibility without boundary, the raw material from which everything would eventually emerge. And Infinity, true Infinity, held echoes of that primordial state in ways that made THE Beholder feel something approaching nostalgia.","He moved across regions of proto-matter mixed with those spreading Infinities, his singular awareness taking in the corruption and the blue-gold light with equal detachment.","He drifted through Wandering Territories where lost things gathered, observing how the Infinite Seals had begun affecting even these forgotten spaces. He passed through corrupted Transcendent Folds and witnessed Primordial Realms that had been touched by changes they did not fully understand.","He saw Undivided Ones moving about with purpose that seemed urgent to them and insignificant to him. He saw Formless Terrors emerging from THE Prima Indifferentia with hunger that had been amplified by the corruption and Infinities they had absorbed. He saw the aftermath of conflicts and the preparation for conflicts yet to come.","And he saw the glimmer of THE Creature as that ancient being began his battle with Horus.","THE Beholder... watched that unfolding fight briefly!"]},{"number":4985,"title":"Chapter 4985: Chapter 4984: THE Beholder II","paragraphs":["Two beings of tremendous authority clashing in ways that would reshape the regions around them.","THE Creature, who was old by the standards of complex life but young by THE Beholder’s measure. Horus, that Primordial Architect whose eyes had branded countless beings with crimson insignias of servitude. Their conflict would determine much about the current age, would establish hierarchies and eliminate possibilities and matter tremendously to everyone invested in the outcomes of such things.","THE Beholder turned his gaze away from that fight and did nothing.","He was only an observer. If he stared for too long, beings like Horus at THE Second Scale of Existence might sense his attention. And with how simple-minded such creatures were despite their power, they would want to know everything regarding him.","They would pursue answers and demand explanations and attempt to incorporate his existence into their frameworks of understanding. They would ruin his life of doing absolutely nothing, which was the only life he had ever wanted or needed.","Some of those that had inherited aspects of his weavings understood this truth. THE Mnemonic Leviathan, that vast repository of knowledge that hoarded information without acting upon it. THE Baboon of Wisdom, that ancient being who had gathered understanding across eons while carefully avoiding the application of that understanding toward any particular goal.","They held the same nature as him in diluted form, observers who encompassed tremendous knowledge and did nothing with it because doing nothing was its own form of existence.","He wondered what they were up to nowadays.","Probably nothing, if they had maintained their natures properly.","As he thought this, THE Beholder’s singular awareness turned toward a region of THE Wastes where an Undivided One and three Formless Terrors were about to engage in conflict. The Undivided One was massive, its form writhing with authority that would have impressed beings who cared about such things.","The Formless Terrors were ancient by the standards of complex life, their churning masses dense with absorbed corruption and Infinities from THE Prima Indifferentia.","THE Beholder’s gaze was disappointed as it settled upon them.","It was like watching lesser life forms do things with their weavings that were disappointing when they could be doing so much more. The Undivided One postured and threatened. The Formless Terrors hungered and prepared to consume. Neither understood what they truly were in the existential sense, what accidents of differentiation their existences represented, what brief flickers of complexity they embodied in the vast darkness of existence’s true duration.","His gaze was about to pass by them, to continue its drift toward other observations more worthy of his attention, when something unexpected occurred.","HUUM!","Existence flickered around the region.","From the corrupted Infinities permeating the area, from the blue-gold light that had spread across so much of Observable Existence in recent times, there was the emergence of a figure that made THE Beholder’s singular awareness sharpen with interest for the first time in quite a while.","A single man surrounded by Infinities.","And a dog.","THE Beholder observed the newcomer with the patient attention he had cultivated across billions of years of practice. The man was not particularly large by the standards of beings who valued size.","His form was humanoid in configuration, wrapped in blue-gold flames and orbited by Absolute Seals that spoke of tremendous authority. But what drew THE Beholder’s interest was not the man’s physical presence.","It was what burned within him.","Infinities. True Infinities, not the pale imitations that most beings called infinite when they really meant very large. These were expressions extending in sequences without termination, genuine endless progressions that echoed the nature of that age of nothingness when potential had no boundary. And mixed with those Infinities, weavings of Paradox that spoke of impossibilities made manifest, contradictions given form and function.","THE Beholder’s awareness processed what he observed with the detached analysis that characterized his nature.","This should be one of those that held the Keys of Civilization. THE First Tongue, if the linguistic architecture of his Infinities was any indication. And Paradox as well, though the paradoxical weavings seemed borrowed or shared rather than natively claimed.","Interesting.","But what exactly did this thing want to do here?","A pair of Formless Terrors and an Undivided One had turned their attention toward the newcomer, their hunger and hostility redirecting from each other toward this new arrival who had interrupted their conflict. The man was not weak, certainly. His Infinities and his Absolute Depth made him formidable by the standards of complex life. But against an Undivided One and three Formless Terrors simultaneously, even formidable might prove insufficient.","THE Beholder prepared to observe what would likely be an educational demonstration of how complex life handled overwhelming odds.","Perhaps he would fight and fall and provide THE Beholder with data about how Infinity was at this time.","And then existence flickered again.","BOOM!","BOOM!","BOOM!","Terrifying eruptions of Absolute Depth began flaring one after another behind the newcomer.","THE Beholder’s singular awareness, which had remained calm across billions of years of observation, actually sharpened with genuine surprise as dozens of Absolute monstrosities began appearing in the space surrounding the Infinity-bearer. They were massive things, titans of coiled tentacles and crystalline plates and writhing aggression. Some appeared fortified like living fortresses. Others appeared predatory like nightmares given form. Still others glowed with gentle light that spoke of preservation rather than destruction.","The dog that had arrived with the newcomer circled happily among the emerging Absolutes, apparently unbothered by the tremendous authorities manifesting around it.","The Undivided One and the Formless Terrors paused in their redirected aggression, their primitive awareness recognizing that the situation had changed dramatically.","The newcomer looked toward them with coldness that held no fear, no concern, no uncertainty about what would happen next.","What was this now?","THE Beholder observed with interest that approached genuine engagement, his singular awareness processing the implications of what he witnessed. Very rarely did he get a chance to observe Infinity in action, to watch how beings wielding that authority actually applied it toward goals and conflicts and demonstrations of power.","Infinity was one of the things that had held glimmers of itself present in that age of nothingness, one of the few concepts that connected the current age to what had come before.","Part of the reason he had moved to begin observing recent events was because of the spread of Infinities across Observable Existence. It truly made him nostalgic. Almost as if things were returning back to that age of wonder countless eons ago, when even Primordial Architects were not a thing, when complexity had not yet emerged to complicate the beautiful simplicity of pure potential.","And now he was watching someone who held Infinity demonstrate what that authority could accomplish when paired with the ambition that complex life seemed unable to abandon.","Dozens of Absolutes with Infinity burning in their foundations, all of them apparently serving this single Infinity-bearer who had emerged from corrupted proto-matter with a dog at his side.","THE Beholder settled his awareness more fully upon the scene.","For the first time in quite a while, he found himself genuinely curious about what would happen next. Not curious enough to intervene, certainly. Not curious enough to abandon his nature as pure observer. But curious enough to watch with attention he had not granted to complex life in eons.","The Undivided One roared challenge toward the newcomer.","The Formless Terrors surged forward with hunger that had consumed countless beings across their existence.","And the Infinity-bearer simply smiled with expression that held something THE Beholder recognized from his observations of complex life across the ages.","Anticipation."]},{"number":4986,"title":"Chapter 4986: Chapter 4985: Devastation I","paragraphs":["To this day, the feeling of perceiving something new from following strings of destiny, fate, or really Mana, felt unique for Noah.","It was like being connected to an endlessly vast sea he should have no way of accessing, and yet he was. The threads of fate stretched in every direction simultaneously, countless golden strands representing possibilities and connections and paths that his awareness could follow toward destinations his conscious mind had not yet identified. Every thread led somewhere. Every strand connected to something. The sea was infinite in scope, and his perception was merely a vessel sailing across its surface.","And Infinite Undifferentiated Fate felt even grander than anything he had touched before.","His Countable Infinities extended his perception in sequential progressions that allowed him to tap into and connect with the vast stretches of his authority spreading across Observable Existence. He searched for keywords, for resonances, for connections that would lead him toward targets worthy of demonstration.","His Infinities had spread through corrupted proto-matter in THE Prima Indifferentia. His Seals had scattered across regions he had never personally visited. His influence touched countless territories through harvest and connection and the simple fact that Infinity, once released, did not stop expanding.","He perceived many things through those connections.","Existence was vast and the information was countless, so Noah focused on something more local.","Something within reach of his current position.","Something that would serve as an appropriate test for what he had built.","Within moments, he saw multiple golden threads that burned brighter than the others around them.","One led to a Formless Terror that had emerged from THE Prima Indifferentia and was currently drifting through THE Wastes with purpose that his perception could not immediately discern. The creature was ancient by the standards of complex life, its churning mass dense with absorbed corruption that made it more dangerous than it had been before awakening.","Another thread led to a Shelter of THE Loom that was currently under siege, its defenders struggling against an Undivided One that had broken through its outer barriers. The beings within were fighting for survival.","How ridiculous it was that grand Early Creatures...were now mere beings fighting for survival!","And then a third thread led to something more interesting entirely.","An Undivided One and multiple Formless Terrors that seemed about to come into conflict with each other in a region of THE Wastes not far from his current position. Four entities of tremendous power preparing to clash over territory or hunger or whatever motivations drove such beings toward violence.","\"It’s decided.\"","Noah came to a decision.","Noah waved his hand, and the Tetras Apeiron responded to his command with precision that spoke of the connection between master and forces bound through Infinity.","Skoll circled Noah happily, the very good boy’s Infinite-enhanced form eager for whatever adventure was about to unfold.","And then Noah stepped forward onto what he imagined to be endless strings of Infinity.","The threads of fate and Mana that he had perceived through Infinite Undifferentiated Fate became pathways that his existence could traverse. He did not teleport in the conventional sense, did not fold space or breach dimensional barriers or utilize any of the standard methodologies for rapid travel. He simply took himself infinitely across the strings, his existence sliding along connections that his Infinities had already established.","The Infinite Absolute Seals that stretched out across existence served as waypoints for his passage.","He passed through one Seal and then another, each one a marker along the infinite path he was traversing. Sequential progression carried him forward in Countable steps that occurred faster than conventional perception could track, each step bringing him closer to his destination while his forces followed through the connections he had established.","And then he arrived.","THE Wastes of THE Fallout spread before him with the familiar desolation that characterized this corrupted region. Proto-matter churned in the distance. Corruption permeated the atmosphere. And directly ahead, four entities of tremendous power occupied a clearing where conflict was about to erupt.","The Undivided One was massive.","Its form resembled something between a serpent and a centipede, countless segments of writhing darkness connected by joints that burned with obsidian light. Multiple heads emerged from its forward segments, each one bearing features that shifted between reptilian and insectoid configurations. Its authority pressed against the surrounding space with weight that Noah’s perception immediately measured against his previous experiences.","About the same level as Bazuman.","The three Formless Terrors were equally impressive in their own churning way.","The first resembled a vast amoebic mass studded with countless eyes that opened and closed in patterns suggesting awareness distributed across its entire form. The second had shaped itself into something resembling a massive crustacean, armored segments protecting a core of pure undifferentiation that pulsed with hunger.","The third was the most chaotic of the three, its form constantly shifting between configurations that included tentacles, wings, claws, and appendages that had no analog in any taxonomy Noah had encountered. It was an ugly fucker.","Their auras held similar weight to the Undivided One.","It was like facing four Bazumans simultaneously.","Enemies that would have required his personal attention not long ago. But for now...?","Perfect test subjects!","Noah did not engage them personally.","He simply waved his hand and called out the Tetras Apeiron.","The space behind him erupted with authority that pressed against THE Wastes with weight exceeding anything the four enemies had produced. Protos emerged first, the Primus Inevitability’s massive tentacled form blazing with crimson blue-gold light that cast long shadows across the corrupted ground. Behind Protos came the others.","One hundred Infinite Bulwarks materialized in layered formations, their crystalline plates of obsidian-gold shifting with subtle movements that stabilized reality around them.","One hundred Hungering Maws appeared with tentacles writhing in barely contained aggression, their serrated maws releasing wisps of pure Hunger that made the very air seem edible.","One hundred Vital Chorus manifested with green-gold-blue light pulsing in mandala patterns that spoke of preservation and resurrection.","One hundred Architects of Infinity emerged amid clouds of geometric shapes and orbiting instruments, their eyes streaming with data and architectural schematics.","Four hundred Absolutes with Bounded Countable Infinity burning in their foundations, each one a titan of coiled tentacles and tremendous authority, each one serving the will of THE Youngest with loyalty beyond question.","The Undivided One and the three Formless Terrors froze in their preparations for mutual conflict.","Their primitive awareness processed what had just appeared before them, and for perhaps the first time in their ancient existences, something approaching hesitation crossed their churning forms. They were creatures of undifferentiation, beings that had existed since before most life had emerged, entities that had consumed countless victims across eons of hunting.","But what the hell was this?","Four hundred Absolutes appearing from nowhere, summoned by a single humanoid figure who stood among them with expression that held no concern, no urgency, no indication that he considered this confrontation anything other than routine!","Noah looked at the four entities with eyes that burned with blue-gold Infinity.","\" This is a test.\"","His voice pressed against THE Wastes with authority that made even the corrupted proto-matter seem to pause.","\" Do your best to persevere.\"","...!","He said such words to an Undivided One and three Formless Terrors as if they were students being evaluated rather than ancient horrors that had terrorized existence since before THE Infinite Unfurling.","These beings knew no fear.","They looked toward the small army of Absolutes and responded with the only language they understood.","Violence.","The three Formless Terrors moved in conjunction with coordination that spoke of either instinct or communication too subtle for external perception. The amoebic mass with countless eyes expanded outward, its form spreading across the battlefield while releasing seas of crimson Undifferentiation that flowed toward Noah’s forces like tides seeking to dissolve everything in their path. The crustacean-configured Terror added its own authority to the assault, armored segments opening to release waves of corruption that merged with the crimson seas. The constantly shifting Terror contributed chaos to the combination, its unstable form producing undifferentiation that flickered between states in ways that made prediction impossible.","The seas of crimson Undifferentiation spread across THE Wastes with hunger that had consumed civilizations.","And the Undivided One responded with its own assault.","Its multiple heads opened simultaneously, and from each throat emerged an obsidian pillar of undifferentiation that shot upward before splitting and dividing and multiplying. One pillar became ten. Ten became a hundred. A hundred became thousands. Millions of obsidian pillars clouded THE Wastes within moments, each one carrying authority that could unmake Absolutes through sustained contact, each one seeking targets with primitive hunger that knew only consumption.","The combined assault would have devastated conventional forces!","The combined assault would have required careful strategy and significant losses to overcome!","But...","Noah calmly waved his hand.","The Infinite Bulwarks stepped forth.","One hundred titans of crystalline plates and layered tentacles moved in perfect synchronization, their forms shifting from scattered positions into a unified wall that stretched across the battlefield. Their silver eyes glowed with steady light as they linked their defensive authorities along geodesic paths, each Bulwark connecting to the ones beside it until their individual protections merged into singular expression.","The seas of crimson Undifferentiation struck the wall of Bulwarks!"]},{"number":4987,"title":"Chapter 4987: Chapter 4986: Devastation II","paragraphs":["The waves washed over crystalline plates that absorbed the assault without yielding, without cracking, without showing any indication that tremendous force was being applied against them.","The corruption that had dissolved countless victims across eons simply stopped when it met Infinite defense that regenerated faster than damage could accumulate.","The millions of obsidian pillars descended upon the Bulwark formation with weight that should have crushed anything beneath their combined impact.","They struck crystalline armor that did not move a single inch.","The Bulwarks absorbed the obsidian pillars as they had absorbed the crimson seas, their Bounded Countable Infinity converting all damage received into stored energy that would fuel other applications. The assault that would have devastated armies simply ended when it met defense that extended in sequences without termination.","The Undivided One and the three Formless Terrors paused in their assault.","Confusion crossed their primitive awareness as they processed the impossibility of what they had just witnessed. Their attacks had not merely been blocked. Their attacks had been rendered irrelevant, absorbed by fortifications that showed no sign of strain from containing forces that should have overwhelmed anything at THE First Scale of Existence.","Noah waved his hand again.","\" Maws. Forty of you. Ten per target.\"","The Hungering Maws moved with eagerness that had been building since their elevation.","Forty of the predatory Absolutes surged forward through gaps in the Bulwark formation, their tentacles writhing with barely contained violence as they split into groups of ten. Each group oriented toward one of the four enemies, their serrated maws opening to release Embodiments filled with definitions of Infinity that blazed with blue-gold light against the corruption of THE Wastes.","The first ten Maws reached the amoebic Formless Terror and demonstrated what Infinite offense truly meant.","Their Embodiments did not merely strike the Terror’s form. They defined it. They imposed Infinite structure upon churning undifferentiation, crystallizing the creature’s existence into patterns it could not escape. The Maws descended upon their target with limbs and tentacles moving like hammers and swords, bludgeoning Infinite definitions into a being that had never experienced definition forced upon it before.","The Terror tried to release more undifferentiation in response.","The attempt failed.","The Maws’ Reality Severance attacked its existence directly, bypassing the defensive mechanisms that had protected it across eons. Their Predatory Geodesic Instinct found every weakness in its distributed consciousness, every vulnerability in its countless eyes, every gap in its primordial defenses. They struck those weaknesses with Hunger that grew stronger with every moment of contact, their Infinite power stacks building as they tore into their target with brutality of absolute dominance!","Tentacles wrapped around portions of the amoebic mass and ripped them away while other tentacles crystallized what remained with Infinite definitions. Serrated maws bit into churning darkness and imposed structure that the darkness could not reject. Limbs descended like siege weapons, each impact driving more definition into existence that had known only formlessness.","DUM! DUM! DUM!","A Glorious symphony of war bloomed.","The second group of ten Maws reached the crustacean-configured Terror and repeated the demonstration.","Armored segments that had protected the creature across eons shattered under strikes that attacked existence itself rather than physical form. The core of pure undifferentiation that pulsed within those segments found itself crystallized by Embodiments that extended Infinitely, definitions arriving from angles that conventional defense could not anticipate. The Maws bludgeoned their target with the same brutal efficiency their brethren displayed!","The third group reached the constantly shifting Terror and demonstrated that chaos provided no defense against Infinite structure.","Every configuration the creature assumed found itself crystallized before the next shift could occur.","The fourth group reached the Undivided One and showed that size meant nothing against properly applied Infinity.","The serpent-centipede form that had seemed so massive moments ago found itself overwhelmed by ten Absolutes whose combined assault attacked every segment simultaneously. Multiple heads that had released millions of obsidian pillars were crystallized one after another as the Maws imposed definitions that the Undivided One’s existence could not reject. Segments that had writhed with obsidian light went still as Infinite structure replaced undifferentiated chaos.","The entire engagement lasted seconds.","The Undivided One and three Formless Terrors that had seemed so dangerous moments ago now existed only as mutilated crystallized husks scattered across the battlefield. Their forms had been frozen into configurations of Infinite definition, their undifferentiation converted into structure that would persist until something dismantled it deliberately. What had been four enemies approaching Bazuman’s level were now four collections of crystallized matter that held no consciousness, no authority, no capacity for resistance.","\"...\"","It was too fucking quick!","Noah looked at the results with eyes that shone with tyranny.","\" Multiply the harvest by a factor of ten.\"","His voice carried out across his existence.","\" Then further elevate it by an exponent of three.\"","A pause.","\" And for all the harvest here to go toward the Tetras Apeiron.\"","The crystallized defeated enemies began breaking apart as his authority processed their remains. What had been frozen structure became flowing essence, resources extracted from collapsed existences that would fuel further advancement. The harvest flowed toward his Legions in streams of blue-gold light that the Maws and Bulwarks and Chorus and Architects absorbed with foundations hungry for growth.","|Harvest Processing Complete|","|Four enemies collapsed: One Undivided One (Absolute Depth equivalent), Three Formless Terrors (Absolute Depth equivalent)|","|Base harvest multiplied by factor of 10, elevated by exponent of 3|","|Total harvest distributed to Tetras Apeiron|","|Results: All 400 Absolutes have received substantial foundation reinforcement. Hungering Maws who participated in direct combat have accumulated Infinite Hunger Stacks that persist beyond engagement. Bulwarks have stored absorbed damage in reservoirs available for redistribution. Overall Legion effectiveness increased by approximately 12%.|","...!","Noah looked across THE Wastes with eyes that shone with light matching his Infinities.","Four enemies that would have required careful planning to defeat not long ago, cleared in seconds through deployment of forces he had built through mass production and Sacred Herb cultivation!","He finally felt like the Hunter again.","Not the hunted, reacting to threats that emerged faster than he could address them. Not the defender, protecting territories from forces that seemed to multiply endlessly.","The Hunter, seeking targets and eliminating them with prejudice, growing stronger with every victory while his enemies grew weaker through attrition they could not reverse.","This was what Infinite warfare looked like.","\" Where to next?\"","He asked Infinite Undifferentiated Fate once more, reaching through the threads of destiny and Mana that connected him to targets across Observable Existence.","The golden strands burned before his awareness, each one leading to enemies worthy of his attention, each one representing opportunity for further demonstration of what he had built.","The Tetras Apeiron stood ready behind him, four hundred Absolutes awaiting their master’s command."]},{"number":4988,"title":"Chapter 4988: Chapter 4987: Loyalty I","paragraphs":["Noah was swimming through the weavings of Infinite Undifferentiated Fate.","Golden threads stretched in every direction around his consciousness, each one a connection to something across Observable Existence, each one a potential path toward targets and conflicts and opportunities. His Countable Infinities extended his perception in sequential progressions that allowed him to feel the vast web of his influence spreading outward from this point in THE Wastes, touching territories and beings and events he had never consciously directed his attention toward.","He was looking at the next nearest thing that would be connected to him.","The approach was deliberate. He felt like a gardener clearing away weeds closest to his core weavings, eliminating threats that could spread if left unchecked while avoiding the exhaustion of stretching himself too thin across Observable Existence. The Tetras Apeiron stood ready behind him, four hundred Absolutes awaiting direction toward whatever enemy he selected. Skoll circled nearby with loyal patience that asked no questions about methodology or purpose.","He felt a few weavings here and there that were pulling at his awareness.","One was another Undivided One drifting through a region of THE Wastes not far from his current position. Another was a lone Formless Terror that had emerged from THE Prima Indifferentia and was currently consuming whatever crossed its path. A third was something that his perception could not fully identify, but that definitely held enough authority to warrant attention.","He planned to go on a systematic hunt, one target after another, collecting loot to empower himself and his army while eliminating threats that could complicate his preparations.","The Tetras Apeiron was only four hundred Absolutes. Soon there would be thousands under his command, each one elevated through mass production and Sacred Herb cultivation, each one carrying Bounded Countable Infinity that made conventional forces seem obsolete by comparison.","But just as he was about to make a decision on one particular weaving, something changed.","\" Huh?\"","Noah blinked.","He frowned as he felt extremely distant weavings relating to him and connected to him, but these weavings seemed different from the others. They seemed closed off, as if they did not want to be found. As if they did not want him to even turn his gaze in their direction. The threads that connected those distant weavings to his awareness were muted and obscured, deliberately hidden through methods that his initial perception could not immediately penetrate.","Something that was connected to him, and yet it did not want him to know it existed?","That made no sense.","His Infinities spread across Observable Existence through Seals and corrupted proto-matter and direct investment. Anything connected to those Infinities should welcome his attention, should benefit from his awareness, should have no reason to hide from the source of the authority they carried.","Unless whatever was happening in those distant weavings was something that connection alone could not protect.","Noah became more serious.","He focused all his Countable Infinities on tracking down the obscured connection, Infinite Undifferentiated Fate burning around his fingers with intensity that pressed against THE Wastes themselves. Golden light spread outward from his position, saturating the entire region with the color of fate being read and destiny being perceived. The corrupted proto-matter in the surroundings served as medium for his perception, the Infinite Seals scattered throughout THE Wastes amplifying his ability to trace connections that did not wish to be traced.","The Tetras Apeiron stood in perfect stillness as their master worked.","Skoll ceased his circling, the loyal companion sensing that something important was occurring.","Moments later, Noah’s expression changed drastically.","The golden light around him intensified as information began flowing through the connection he had forced open. The weavings he was reading related to someone he had not thought about in some time, someone who had parted ways with him.","The Peacemaker.","Alexander Asmodeus.","Someone from his home Wheel of Existence who had chosen his own path rather than remaining under Noah’s protection.","The more his weavings of Infinite Undifferentiated Fate uncovered regarding the fate and choices of this being, the heavier Noah’s expression became. The information arrived in fragments that his perception assembled into coherent narrative, each fragment darker than the last, each piece of the picture more disturbing than what had come before.","|Weaving Analysis: Alexander Asmodeus, THE Peacemaker|","|Status: Branded with the Mark of Horus. Existence burning continuously since branding occurred. Forced cultivation elevating his Depth toward Absolute through methods that consume his foundations rather than strengthening them properly.|","|Recent Events: Due to his historical connection with you, at a point immediately preceding your weavings connecting with weavings of Paradox, another entity was led toward THE Peacemaker’s location. This entity followed trails of corrupted Infinity that you had spread across THE Wastes, trails that led to beings who had been associated with your authority.|","|Entity Classification: Unknown designation. Aura signature suggests Primordial Architect classification. However, recorded authority levels from brief observation exceed known weavings of existence at THE First Scale. Theoretical assessment: This entity operates at THE Second Scale of Existence.|","|Interaction Record: The entity offered salvation to THE Peacemaker in exchange for information regarding your connection and origin as the one who holds the Infinities spreading across Observable Existence. The entity sought knowledge of your location, your nature, your vulnerabilities.|","|THE Peacemaker’s Response: Denied the offer. Did not provide information. Did not give you up.|","|Consequence: THE Peacemaker has been suffering since then. Duration of suffering unknown but estimated at significant dilated temporal span. Means of power at THE Second Scale that cannot be understood currently.|","...!","BOOM!","Noah’s eyes were heavy as they looked at these prompts.","The Peacemaker.","Alexander, who had faced Adversity that seemed ridiculously above what any reasonable assessment would have predicted for someone at his level of development.","And when he had the chance to clear that Adversity by giving Noah up, by providing information that would redirect the Primordial Architect’s attention toward its actual target, by saving himself through the simple act of betrayal...","He did not do so.","The one responsible for Alexander’s current suffering was something hunting for Noah specifically. A Primordial Architect theorized to operate at THE Second Scale of Existence, following trails of corrupted Infinity that Noah had spread across Observable Existence, seeking the source of the authority that had drawn its attention.","One of the worst possible variables that Noah had only just begun preparing for, one of the threats that had motivated the creation of the Tetras Apeiron in the first place.","An enemy at THE Second Scale.","And yet, when the question came whether Noah should put himself in danger to save THE Peacemaker who had not given him up, it was not even a question.","He began to move right away.","The Tetras Apeiron shifted into travel formation behind him, four hundred Absolutes responding to their master’s decision without hesitation or inquiry. Protos moved to Noah’s side. Skoll followed with loyal certainty that asked no questions about destination or purpose.","As they moved, Noah began to speak.","His voice carried across THE Wastes with weight that made the corrupted proto-matter seem to still, the words emerging with cadence that spoke of prophecy rather than mere statement. The legion of Absolutes around him began to repeat his words, their combined voices creating chorus that pressed against existence itself.","\" The adversity that breaks all others shall forge him.\"","Four hundred voices echoed the declaration.","\" The hardship that ends all paths shall begin his.\"","The words spread outward in waves that carried meaning beyond mere sound.","\" The Scales demand what the Scales demand, and he shall pay in currencies that have not yet been minted.\"","Noah continued speaking as they traveled, his voice steady despite the weight of what he was walking toward.","\" Three times shall he face the mirror of undoing. Three times shall he choose between becoming and unbecoming. Three times shall the answer be the same, and three times shall the answer be different.\"","The Tetras Apeiron repeated each line with precision that made the Echo feel like inevitability rather than possibility.","\" This is what shall come to pass, for it has already passed, and it shall pass again.\"","Noah paused.","\" The wheel turns. The river flows. The question echoes.\"","The final words hung in the air as the legion fell silent, their repetition complete.","Noah thought about the echo as he sighed and uttered out again.","\" Right. The wheel turns. The river flows.\"","He had Adversity in THE Entity, that unified horror that had claimed THE Primordial Chaos and threatened everything he was building. He had Adversity in the Primordial Architects awakening across THE Prima Indifferentia, ancient beings whose power approached or exceeded THE Second Scale.","He had Adversity in the simple fact that existence was vast and filled with terrors that did not care about his ambitions or his preparations or his Infinite nature.","But for the sake of someone who had defended him when defense cost everything, he would do the same.","Alexander had not given him up.","Noah would not abandon someone who had demonstrated such conviction.","This in itself was a choice that rational assessment might question. No one sane would put themselves in front of an entity at an entirely higher Scale of Existence. No one calculating would risk everything they had built to save a single being who had chosen to walk away from their protection.","No one focused purely on advancement would divert from systematic hunting to confront a threat they were not yet prepared to defeat.","But sometimes, ones had to do what they had to do.","The Tetras Apeiron followed their master toward confrontation with something that operated at THE Second Scale, four hundred Absolutes with Bounded Countable Infinity marching toward battle that conventional wisdom said they could not win.","Oh.","Oh."]},{"number":4989,"title":"Chapter 4989: Chapter 4988: Loyalty II","paragraphs":["THE Beholder observed the Infinity-bearer and his army with interest that had not faded since their initial appearance.","It was genuinely pleasant to witness Infinity again after so many eons of its absence from Observable Existence. The blue-gold light that burned within those four hundred Absolutes carried echoes of that age of nothingness, faint glimmers of what had existed before differentiation and undifferentiation learned to produce complex life.","The endless nature that defined what the Infinity-bearer wielded, all of it stirred memories that THE Beholder had not accessed in spans of time that complex life could not meaningfully comprehend.","But as he watched the demonstration against the Undivided One and the Formless Terrors, as he observed how the Infinity-bearer deployed his forces and directed their Infinite authorities toward combat and consumption, THE Beholder found himself experiencing something approaching disappointment.","Infinity... was being used in a very limited sense.","The applications were clever, certainly. The integration of endless defense and endless offense and endless healing into coordinated expression showed understanding that exceeded what most complex life achieved when grasping fundamental authorities. But the scope of what he was witnessing remained narrow, remained bounded by the frameworks that complex life seemed unable to escape, remained constrained by perspectives that treated Infinity as a tool rather than as a nature.","Infinity should be much grander than this.","In that age of nothingness, when potential had no boundary and possibility had no limit, Infinity had not been something wielded. It had simply been the way existence existed before existence learned to differentiate itself into complex expressions.","It had been the canvas rather than the paint, the stage rather than the play, the question rather than any particular answer.","What THE Beholder was watching felt like someone who had discovered an ocean and decided to use it exclusively for filling drinking cups.","Was the one who came to grasp Infinity in their Observable Existence a bit dull?","The thought crossed THE Beholder’s singular awareness with bemusement rather than condemnation. Complex life had limitations that beings of his nature did not share. They processed reality through frameworks of emotion and ambition and self-interest that colored everything they perceived and everything they did.","Perhaps this Infinity-bearer was doing the best that complex life could do with authority that had not been designed for complex life to wield.","Perhaps.","But THE Beholder had hoped for something more impressive given how rarely true Infinity manifested in Observable Existence.","He was about to turn his attention elsewhere, to drift toward other observations that might prove more worthy of his awareness, when the Infinity-bearer did something unexpected. The being sent his weavings out across the corrupted Infinities saturating the nearby region, golden threads extending through connections that THE Beholder could perceive with his singular cognizance.","The Infinity-bearer was searching for something specific, tracking connections that led away from his current position toward destinations unknown.","THE Beholder followed those threads with idle curiosity.","They led to a scene he had already observed and turned away from some time ago.","An armored Primordial Architect was torturing a weak lifeform in a region of THE Wastes that its authority had saturated completely. THE Beholder had perceived this scene during his drift across Observable Existence and had chosen not to watch because such activities held no interest for him.","Torture was a behavior that complex life seemed unable to abandon despite eons of supposed development. It served emotional needs that beings of his nature did not possess and could not relate to.","Some Primordial Architects were decent, in fairness.","THE Beholder had observed a few across his incomprehensible lifespan who approached something resembling Singular Cognizances in their wonder and their detachment from the petty concerns that consumed most complex life.","They observed rather than conquered. They contemplated rather than consumed. They existed in ways that suggested they might eventually transcend the impossible limitations of their differentiated nature.","One or two had actually achieved something approaching true wisdom. THE Creature was a decent one.","But so many more were simply disappointing.","Because why would a seemingly complex lifeform capable of tremendous authority and vast understanding choose to torture? What purpose did such activity serve beyond the gratification of emotional impulses that should have been beneath beings who had existed since before THE Infinite Unfurling?","Emotions were a significant component of complex lifeforms that they could not seem to escape no matter how much power they accumulated or how long they existed. Some held thrills and excitement and sadism that made them lesser than they should be, that reduced them from what their potential suggested to what their impulses demanded.","This armored Primordial Architect, whoever it was, clearly fell into the disappointing category.","THE Beholder was about to dismiss the scene entirely when he noticed something in the Infinity-bearer’s reaction to perceiving it. The being’s expression had changed. The casual confidence that had characterized his observations shifted into something heavier, something more serious, something that spoke of personal investment rather than detached assessment.","Oh?","The weak thing being tortured and the Infinity-bearer knew each other?","What an unfortunate coincidence that was. To know that someone you were affiliated with had their existence likely over and done with, while you were powerless to help.","Complex life formed attachments that created vulnerability, connections that became weaknesses, bonds that led to suffering when those bonds were threatened or severed.","This Infinity-bearer would have to accept that his affiliated being was lost. The armored Primordial Architect clearly operated at heights that THE Youngest, as THE Beholder had identified him through minimal exertion of awareness, could not contest.","The rational response was to mourn the loss and continue with activities that actually had possibility of success.","This was THE Beholder’s assessment of the situation.","But in the next moment, he heard prophetic echoes spreading from THE Youngest’s position.","Words that spoke of adversity and hardship and choices between becoming and unbecoming. Words that his army of Absolutes repeated with weight that pressed against existence itself. Words that suggested intention rather than acceptance, action rather than mourning, confrontation rather than retreat.","THE Youngest... was heading toward the armored Primordial Architect?","THE Beholder’s singular awareness sharpened with genuine astonishment.","Surely the one who had grasped Infinity did not also move based on emotions?","THE Second Scale of Existence was far removed from where THE Youngest currently operated. The gap between THE First Scale and THE Second Scale was not merely quantitative but qualitative, a difference in fundamental nature rather than simply a difference in accumulated power.","Beings at THE Second Scale perceived and interacted with existence in ways that beings at THE First Scale could not comprehend, let alone contest.","THE Youngest had absolutely no chance against a Primordial Architect at THE Second Scale.","THE Beholder focused his awareness more fully on the armored entity, exerting slightly more effort than his usual minimal observation required. The identity of the Primordial Architect was Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor.","One of the ancient beings that had existed since THE First Cause.","THE Primordial Armor was not an enemy that clever tactics or Infinite armies could overcome.","So why would THE Youngest go? Why would he do something so illogical?","The Infinity-bearer clearly understood the danger. His expression held weight that spoke of full awareness regarding what he was walking toward. His army’s repetition of prophetic words suggested acknowledgment that the confrontation ahead would demand everything and might still prove insufficient. He was not moving in ignorance.","He was moving in defiance of rational assessment.","THE Beholder watched with fascination that approached genuine engagement as the Infinity-bearer began traversing across Observable Existence toward the armored Primordial Architect’s location. Perhaps there was something he had missed regarding the expression of Infinity by THE Youngest.","Perhaps the being could manifest his authority in ways that transcended the limited applications THE Beholder had witnessed against the Undivided One and Formless Terrors.","With the immensity of Infinity truly utilized, anything was possible.","That was the nature of what Infinity fundamentally was. Possibility without boundary. Potential without limit. The capacity to achieve outcomes that finite analysis declared impossible because finite analysis could not account for expressions that extended endlessly.","But THE Youngest should still be far from true utilization of that nature.","His Infinity was currently limited expressions of unlimited authority. His understanding seemed narrow despite the power he had accumulated. His applications suggested someone who had grasped a fragment of Infinity rather than Infinity itself.","THE Beholder watched as THE Youngest and his army crossed distances that would have required conventional beings enormous spans of time to traverse. The Infinity-bearer moved along connections his authority had established, stepping across strings of fate and Mana that carried him toward destination with speed that impressed even THE Beholder’s ancient perspective.","They arrived in a region of THE Wastes where the authority of THE Primordial Armor had already wrapped over everything in the immediate vicinity.","The corruption here was different from the corruption elsewhere. It carried the signature of a being at THE Second Scale, undifferentiation given focus and purpose by consciousness that operated on levels THE Youngest could not access. The very fabric of existence in this region answered to Beowulf rather than to the principles that normally governed Observable Existence.","THE Beholder watched calmly as THE Primordial Armor’s visor lit up with awareness.","The massive armored entity turned its attention from the weak lifeform it had been tormenting, its helm orienting toward a distant point where the corrupted Wastes had begun flickering with the signature of arriving Infinities. Through the gaps in platinum armor that revealed nothing but darkness, something that might have been interest stirred.","THE Youngest and his army appeared.","Four hundred Absolutes with Infinity burning in their foundations materialized in formation behind the Infinity-bearer.","They faced Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor, as if their presence actually meant something.","And then...","\" Haha... HA!\"","THE Beholder saw THE Primordial Armor begin to laugh.","The sound boomed across the region with weight that made the corrupted proto-matter tremble, genuine amusement emerging from the armored entity at the sight of what had arrived to challenge it. THE Beholder sighed internally at the display, though beings of his nature did not truly sigh.","Why would this Primordial Architect not laugh? The situation was amusing from its perspective. A being at THE First Scale arriving with an army of lesser beings to confront something that operated on levels they could not comprehend.","But THE Beholder also recognized the danger in that laughter.","If THE Primordial Armor was decent enough, if it possessed understanding that exceeded the disappointing norm, it might actually be able to grasp the Infinity of THE Youngest.","It might see opportunity rather than merely amusement.","If it was decent enough.","Because many of these complex lifeforms also did not understand Infinity.","From what THE Beholder knew, from observations spanning eons beyond counting, nobody in this Observable Existence truly understood what Infinity was. They grasped fragments and wielded portions and utilized aspects, but the fundamental nature of endless potential remained beyond their comprehension.","Even THE Youngest, who had achieved more with Infinity than most, operated within limitations that true understanding would have dissolved.","For now, THE Beholder would watch.","He would observe what unfolded between a being who had grasped Infinity and a being who had achieved THE Second Scale. He would wonder why complex lifeforms did the things they did, why they formed attachments that led them to face impossible odds, why they chose confrontation when retreat would preserve their existence.","He would witness whatever disaster emerged from this collision of authorities that should never have been brought into proximity.","And perhaps, if something unexpected occurred, he would finally see Infinity expressed in ways that justified the interest its presence had stirred in his ancient awareness.","THE Youngest stood before THE Primordial Armor.","The weak lifeform that had been tortured lay somewhere before that armored titan, its fate suspended between rescue and termination depending on what happened next.","And THE Beholder watched with patience that had been cultivated across billions of years of practice, curious despite himself about what complex life would do when facing something it could not defeat."]},{"number":4990,"title":"Chapter 4990: Chapter 4989: An Impossibility!","paragraphs":["Noah arrived in a region of THE Wastes where everything felt wrong.","The corruption here was different from corruption elsewhere, carrying weight that pressed against his existence in ways that the proto-matter mixed with his Infinities had never managed. The very fabric of reality answered to something other than the principles that normally governed Observable Existence, bending and warping according to will that operated on levels his perception could barely comprehend.","Information barely flowed from the Infinities here to tell him a few things. The identity of the enemy, but only because they freely permitted their identity to spread.","THE Primordial Armor stood before him.","Beowulf was massive in ways that made the Tetras Apeiron seem like children’s toys arranged for play. Platinum armor that had been forged from proto-matter convinced to become metal covered every inch of a form that dwarfed mountains, each plate shifting with patterns suggesting awareness distributed across the armor itself rather than contained within it.","The hammer in its grip was equally colossal, condensed metallic proto-matter churning within its head with eagerness for targets to unmake.","The gaps between those platinum plates revealed nothing but darkness.","No body. No being. Just the armor itself, existing as entity rather than equipment, consciousness without flesh that had persisted since before THE Infinite Unfurling.","And before that armored titan, suspended in the corrupted air like a specimen prepared for examination, was Alexander Asmodeus.","THE Primordial Armor’s visor oriented toward Noah with attention that felt like weight settling upon his shoulders. The armor did not possess visible features, yet somehow, expression communicated itself through the arrangement of platinum plates, through the angle of the helm, through presence that spoke of amusement where amusement should not have been possible.","And the first thing this Primordial Architect uttered out...","\" Tell me, Infinity-bearer. Do you know... what Existential Nociceptors are?\"","Beowulf’s voice emerged with calm that made the words more disturbing than screaming rage could have achieved.","\" Of course you do not. Those at your Scale cannot perceive them. Those like you experience pain as sensation, as signal, as warning that something has gone wrong within their existence. But they do not see what I see. They cannot perceive the architecture that underlies all suffering.\"","The armored titan shifted slightly, plates rearranging in patterns that suggested settling into comfort.","\" Every differentiated existence possesses Existential Nociceptors woven into the fabric of their being. These are the fundamental receptors through which all suffering flows. But they are merely the foundation. Branching from them are the Civilizational Afferents, pathways that carry agony through one’s entire Civilization simultaneously, ensuring that no aspect of the self escapes what is being inflicted.\"","A pause, as if savoring the explanation.","\" Then there are the Delta-Threads of Existence, which transmit sharp and immediate pain with speed that allows no preparation. And the C-Fibers of Being, which carry slow, burning anguish that accumulates over time without relief. Most beings possess these without ever knowing they exist and how they connect to their Civilizations. But at THE Second Scale, I perceive them as clearly as you perceive the corrupted proto-matter around us.\"","The visor tilted slightly.","\" And perception, O Infinity-bearer, permits manipulation.\"","The words hung in the corrupted air with weight that pressed against Noah’s consciousness.","\" One can isolate individual Nociceptors and stimulate them with precision that lesser beings cannot achieve. One can flood the Civilizational Afferents with signals that make every fiber of existence scream simultaneously. One can activate the Polymodal Agony Receptors, those rare structures that respond to multiple types of suffering at once, creating symphonies of pain that finite minds cannot comprehend.\"","The armor that served as Beowulf’s form seemed to settle with satisfaction.","\" But the true artistry lies in Hyperalgesic Amplification. By manipulating the Weavings that sensitize each receptor, I can increase their responsiveness by factors that have no upper limit. Pain that would normally register as discomfort becomes agony. Agony becomes something for which no word exists. And through temporal dilation around these amplified receptors, I can stretch nanoseconds into subjective eternities.\"","The helm oriented toward the suspended figure behind the armored form.","\" Within a single nanosecond of objective time, one can create millions of years of accrued suffering for the one experiencing it. Every Delta-Thread firing without cessation. Every C-Fiber burning without relief. Every Polymodal receptor screaming with multiple agonies simultaneously. All of it stretched across spans of perceived time that would break any normal existence.\"","Beowulf’s voice carried something approaching pride.","\"I isolated every Existential Nociceptor within THE Peacemaker here. Alexander Asmodeus, he calls himself. I mapped his Civilizational Afferents with precision that left no pathway untouched. I activated his Polymodal Agony Receptors while flooding his Delta-Threads and C-Fibers with stimulation that exceeded anything his existence was designed to endure.\"","A pause.","\"I applied Hyperalgesic Amplification until his receptors were sensitized beyond theoretical maximums. And then I dilated his perception of time until each moment of torture stretched into spans that would reduce civilizations to begging.\"","The armor that served as Beowulf’s voice carried satisfaction that made Noah’s blood pulse!","\" And... all I have managed to get out of him is his name. He will not say a thing about you. But after bearing through all that pain to avoid giving you up, to save you from what would come if I found you...\"","Laughter built within the armored form.","\" You just show up. Just like that.\"","\"Haha! HA!\"","The sound boomed across the corrupted Wastes with weight that made the proto-matter tremble.","\" What a thing. Hey, Peacemaker, is that not crazy?\"","Noah’s gaze moved past the armored titan to the figure suspended in corrupted air behind it.","Alexander Asmodeus.","THE Peacemaker.","His humanoid body had been broken down into countless small cellular components while somehow still maintaining humanoid form. And yet his eyes, those segmented, shattered eyes, still found Noah across the battlefield. Still recognized him. Still held something that looked like relief mixed with horror, as if Alexander was simultaneously grateful that Noah had come and devastated that his sacrifice had been rendered meaningless by that very arrival.","It was as if someone had taken his existence apart piece by piece and then arranged those pieces in the shape of what he had once been, a mosaic of suffering that approximated the man without actually being whole. Weavings of undifferentiation flowed through the gaps between those cellular fragments, corruption serving as mortar holding the broken pieces in their agonizing configuration.","He was twitching.","The movements were involuntary, spasms that spoke of pain so profound that his existence could not contain it despite the torture having paused. His skin, or what remained of it in fragmented form, had gone gray with stress that exceeded what color could survive.","His muscles, segmented into countless portions that moved independently of each other, contracted and relaxed without his control. Every pain receptor within him had been stimulated beyond their capacity to recover, leaving him in perpetual aftermath of suffering that continued echoing through his shattered form.","And yet his eyes still held defiance.","Those eyes were also segmented, broken into pieces like everything else, yet somehow they still functioned. Somehow they still gazed toward Beowulf with refusal to break that transcended the physical destruction that had been inflicted upon him.","Somehow, after everything, after millions of years of subjective torture compressed into moments of objective time, Alexander Asmodeus still looked at his torturer with expression that communicated nothing but contempt.","On his chest, the Enneagram that had been his partnership with THE Living Law showed damage that exceeded everything else.","A line of fracture extended through the middle of the nine-pointed construct, splitting it nearly in half. The silver light that had once blazed from those nine points now flickered weakly, barely visible, barely present, barely anything at all. The construct looked shattered beyond repair, destroyed by deliberate action rather than external assault!","Noah looked at this scene with eyes so heavy they felt like they might sink into his skull.","He did not say anything.","He only looked toward Alexander as their eyes met across the distance that separated them, across the armored titan that stood between rescuer and victim, across the impossibility of the situation they now shared. Complex emotions passed between them in that moment of connection.","Slight guilt, for Noah had spread the Infinities that led Beowulf to Alexander.","Gratitude, for Alexander had not given him or THE Infiniverse up despite suffering that would have broken any normal existence.","Grief, for the man suspended in corrupted air was clearly not the same man who had walked away from THE Infiniverse with pride of independence.","And determination, burning beneath everything else.","Noah waved his hand.","Behind him, existence flickered as hundreds more Absolute Primus Inevitabilities began to appear.","The Tetras Apeiron Secundus materialized in formation, four hundred more Absolutes with Bounded Countable Infinity blazing in their foundations. Then the Tetras Apeiron Tertius arrived, another four hundred titans of coiled tentacles and specialized authorities joining the forces already present.","And from those, three more Legions arrived as they were doubled!","Twelve hundred Absolutes became twenty-four hundred.","Bulwarks and Maws and Chorus and Architects multiplied until the corrupted Wastes held an army that would have devastated anything at THE First Scale.","Beowulf saw this and smiled.","The expression should not have been possible for armor without features, yet somehow it communicated itself through the arrangement of platinum plates, through the tilt of the helm, through presence that radiated amusement at what it was witnessing. The armored Primordial Architect swung its hammer freely, rotating the colossal weapon as if stretching muscles that did not exist.","\" This Alexander had inside of him another weak thing. THE Living Law, it called itself.\"","The casual tone made the words more horrible than emphasis could have achieved.","\" That consciousness partnered with your Peacemaker, invested in him, believed it was building something worthwhile through their connection. But THE Living Law had much weaker conviction than its host.\"","The hammer completed another rotation.","\" When I isolated its Existential Nociceptors, when I showed it what Hyperalgesic Amplification truly means at THE Second Scale, THE Living Law could not bear it. The suffering was simply too great. It was about to spill everything. Your location. Your nature. Your vulnerabilities. Everything I wished to know.\"","Beowulf’s visor oriented toward the suspended Alexander with something approaching admiration.","\"It is not pain that any existence can bear, what a being at THE Second Scale can inflict upon those below it. THE Living Law was normal in that regard. Its Civilizational Afferents could not handle the stimulation I was applying, and it was about to break completely.\"","A pause.","\" But this Alexander is actually an abnormal one. When he realized his partner was about to give you up, when he understood that THE Living Law would betray you to escape the agony flooding through its receptors, he made a choice that I did not anticipate.\"","The hammer stilled.","\" He shattered his own Anomalous Mutated Weavings. His little nine-pointed star. He collapsed that consciousness inside of him before it could speak, destroying his own partner to protect you.\"","The armor shifted.","\" Ah! What sadness. What horrors. What magnificent conviction from such a small existence.\"","The visor turned back to Noah.","\" But again. All of that done, all of that suffering endured, all of that sacrifice made, only for you to deliver yourself to me. And I have been looking, O Infinity-bearer.\"","The hammer rose slightly.","\" If you would sit still, I wish to open you up and dissect you a bit. I am curious what Existential Nociceptors woven with Infinity look like. I am curious how Hyperalgesic Amplification would interact with endless regeneration. I am curious about you and Infinity.\"","...!","Noah stood before THE Primordial Armor with twenty-four hundred Absolute Primus Inevitabilities arranged behind him.","The Tetras Apeiron Primus held position at the center. The Tetras Apeiron Secundus flanked the first legion, another four hundred whose authorities had not yet been tested in combat. The Tetras Apeiron Tertius completed the formation, the final four hundred ready to deploy according to their master’s command.","HUUM!","Existence buzzed around him as more and more Absolute Primus Inevitabilities began to appear.","Skoll stood at Noah’s side with expression that had lost all playfulness. The loyal companion’s Infinite-enhanced form blazed with blue-gold light, but even that blazing seemed dim compared to the authority radiating from Beowulf.","Protos waited for orders that its master had not yet given.","And Noah faced the impossible.","Twenty-four hundred Absolutes now, with Bounded Countable Infinity against a single Primordial Architect at THE Second Scale. The mathematics were not merely unfavorable. They were absurd.","Beowulf operated on levels that his forces could not comprehend, let alone contest. The gap between THE First Scale and THE Second Scale was qualitative rather than quantitative, a difference in fundamental nature rather than accumulated power.","His army was impressive by any standard of THE First Scale.","Against THE Second Scale, that army might as well have been insects facing a hurricane.","The weight of what he was confronting pressed against Noah’s consciousness with implications that his rational mind could not ignore.","He had come here to save Alexander. He had brought everything he could bring. And everything he could bring may be insufficient for the task at hand.","Despair should have been the rational response.","Retreat should have been the logical action.","Acceptance of loss should have been the wisdom that guided his next decisions!","But Noah looked at Alexander Asmodeus, at the man who had endured millions of years of subjective torture rather than give him up, at the shattered Enneagram that spoke of sacrifice beyond what anyone should have been asked to make, at the defiance that still burned in segmented eyes despite everything that had been done to break it.","And he spoke.","\" Whether today.\"","His voice emerged steady despite everything.","\" Whether weeks from now. Whether eons from now.\"","The words pressed against the corrupted Wastes with weight that should not have been possible for someone facing such impossible odds.","\"I will do to you what you did to him.\"","The Tetras Apeiron shifted behind him, twenty-four hundred Absolutes responding to their master’s conviction with readiness that defied rational assessment.","\" This... I swear on my Infinity.\"","...!","The oath hung in the corrupted air between them.","Noah Osmont, THE Youngest, THE Genesis Monarch, bearer of Countable Infinity, facing Beowulf, THE Primordial Armor, a being at THE Second Scale of Existence who had tortured his friend for information and failed to break him.","Twenty-four hundred against one.","And somehow, despite the mathematics, despite the impossible gap between Scales, despite everything that rational analysis screamed about the futility of this confrontation, the one making the oath did not seem like the one at disadvantage."]},{"number":4991,"title":"Chapter 4991: Chapter 4990: The Gap","paragraphs":["Noah stood before THE Primordial Armor with his oath hanging in the corrupted air between them.","Twenty-four hundred Absolutes waited behind him. Countable Infinity burned in his foundations. The Tetras Apeiron Primus, Secundus, and Tertius and others held formation with readiness that defied the impossible odds they faced. Skoll stood at his side. Protos blazed with crimson blue-gold light.","And Beowulf looked at all of it with amusement that made the accumulated power seem trivial.","\" This is actually laughable.\"","The words emerged from the armored titan with casual dismissal that pressed against Noah’s consciousness like weight settling upon shoulders that were already carrying too much. The platinum plates shifted in patterns that communicated something between contempt and genuine entertainment.","\" You know what? I will not actually do anything for now.\"","The massive form settled back, armor reconfiguring in ways that suggested relaxation.","\"I just want you to see the gap and appreciate it.\"","The hammer that had been gripped in armored hands rose on its own, floating above Beowulf’s helm with the casual defiance of gravity. The condensed metallic proto-matter churned within its head, eager for targets it would not immediately receive.","\" Come on, big guy with Infinity.\"","THE Primordial Armor reached behind itself with one massive gauntlet and pinched the suspended figure of Alexander Asmodeus, repositioning the broken Peacemaker to float behind its form like a trophy being displayed. Alexander’s segmented eyes flickered with awareness of what was happening, but his shattered existence could do nothing to resist the casual manipulation.","Beowulf looked toward Noah with visor that communicated invitation through arrangement of platinum plates.","\" Attack me. Give it all you’ve got.\"","The armored titan actually leaned back.","And then it sat down.","THE Primordial Armor, a being at THE Second Scale of Existence, settled onto the corrupted ground of THE Wastes with posture that spoke of supreme confidence. It sat there like someone preparing to watch entertainment, like a being so assured of its superiority that offering its enemy free attacks seemed like reasonable hospitality.","\" Come on.\"","...!","Noah looked at the seated Primordial Architect with thoughts that churned behind eyes burning with Infinite light.","He had known the gap would be large. He had understood, intellectually, that THE Second Scale operated on levels that THE First Scale could not meaningfully contest. He had seen the mathematics of what he was walking toward and had chosen to walk anyway.","But knowing something and witnessing it were different experiences entirely.","That did not stop him from being here.","What he was counting on was himself. What he was counting on was Infinity to potentially change the tides of impossibility, to produce outcomes that finite analysis declared unachievable. Infinity had properties that transcended normal calculation. Infinity permitted things that bounded authorities could not accomplish.","Whether those properties would be sufficient against THE Second Scale remained to be seen.","The easy thing to do here would have been to abandon THE Peacemaker. Alexander could be considered an ally, certainly, but they were not entirely close. They had history from the same Wheel of Existence, shared origins that connected them. But Alexander had walked away from Noah’s protection. Alexander had chosen his own path. Alexander’s current suffering was the consequence of choices that Noah had not made for him.","The easy thing would have been to calculate the odds, recognize the impossibility, and retreat to fight battles that could actually be won.","But easy was not the same as right.","It was not in Noah’s nature to abandon someone who had endured millions of years of torture rather than give him up. It was not in his nature to calculate loyalty. It was not in his nature to be the kind of person who walked away from those who stood for him simply because standing for them in return had become dangerous.","So now he was here.","And he had to deal with it.","Since the enemy wanted to give him a chance, since Beowulf seemed interested in demonstration rather than immediate destruction, Noah would see just how vast the gap truly was. He would test his Infinity against THE Second Scale and discover what properties might or might not translate across that qualitative divide.","He raised his hand.","Blue-gold light gathered around his fingers with Infinite progression that extended sequentially toward the seated Primordial Architect. The light curved along geodesic paths that found the natural geometry of existence, following routes of minimal distance toward the target that waited with casual invitation.","Noah spoke words that pressed against reality itself.","\"I negate your capacity to harm that which I protect. Your weavings will not remain intact before infinity.\"","The Geodesic Negation launched forward with Infinity burning in its structure.","It extended endlessly along the shortest path between Noah and Beowulf, Countable expressions arriving one after another in sequences that would never terminate. The negation carried Undifferentiation that would prevent reformation, that would deny the target’s ability to damage anything Noah designated as protected.","The negation reached Beowulf.","It touched the platinum armor.","And...","It passed through the seated form.","And nothing.","Nothing!","And THE Primordial Armor simply gazed at Noah calmly as if nothing had happened at all.","Beowulf did not defend. Beowulf did not deflect or absorb or counter the Geodesic Negation. Beowulf simply remained where it was, seated on the corrupted ground, watching Noah with visor that communicated patient amusement through arrangement of platinum plates.","The negation had not affected it.","The negation had not even registered as something requiring response.","Noah’s expression flickered.","He commanded his Maws to attack.","Instantly, hundreds of the predatory Absolutes bloomed from the dots of Infinite Absolute Seals scattered throughout the corrupted proto-matter. They emerged from positions surrounding the seated Primordial Architect, their massive forms materializing with speed that left no time for conventional response. Their tentacles writhed with barely contained hunger. Their serrated maws opened to release Embodiments filled with definitions of Infinity.","They attacked.","Hundreds of Absolute Primus Inevitabilities struck toward Beowulf simultaneously, their massive limbs descending like hammers forged from Bounded Countable Infinity. Each strike carried definitions that should have imposed structure upon anything they touched. Each Embodiment burned with authority that had devastated the Undivided One and Formless Terrors moments ago.","Their limbs reached the platinum armor.","Their Embodiments contacted the seated form!","And in the next moment, as if THE Primordial Armor was made of mist or something they could not even grasp, the bodies of the Absolute Primus Inevitabilities simply phased through the surfaces of the enemy like nothing was there at all.","The Maws passed through Beowulf.","Their strikes connected with empty air.","Their Embodiments found no purchase on existence that seemed to occupy the same space but exist on levels they could not touch.","Noah’s expression became heavier as he watched his offensive force prove completely ineffective.","The gap was not simply a matter of Beowulf being stronger than his forces.","The gap was qualitative in ways that made engagement meaningless. THE Second Scale did not interact with THE First Scale unless it chose to . His attacks were not being blocked or deflected. They were simply failing to connect with something that existed on levels his authority could not access.","THE Primordial Armor moved.","One massive gauntlet reached out with speed that Noah’s Absolute perception could barely track, and armored fingers pinched a singular Maw from the hundreds that had phased through its form. The predatory Absolute that had been striking uselessly moments ago found itself held between thumb and forefinger like an insect being examined by something that found insects mildly interesting.","The Maw writhed in that grip.","Its tentacles struck against the armored fingers. Its serrated maws bit at platinum plates. Its Embodiments blazed against surfaces that should have been forced to accept definition.","Nothing affected the grip that held it.","Beowulf’s visor tilted toward the captured Maw, then toward Noah, then back to the Maw.","\" This is the simplest representation of where I stand and where you stand, O Infinity-bearer.\"","The words emerged with weight that made the corrupted Wastes seem to press inward.","\" You and your things will not even be able to touch me. Every strike you throw, every Embodiment you release, every Apophasis you speak, all of it will pass through my existence like wind passing through open domains.\"","The captured Maw continued struggling uselessly.","\" Hah. If I do not want it, you will not even be able to perceive me.\"","BOOM!","THE Primordial Armor disappeared.","One moment, the massive seated form was there, captured Maw held between armored fingers, visor oriented toward Noah with amusement that communicated through platinum arrangement.","The next moment, nothing.","Beowulf was simply gone from Noah’s perception entirely. His Infinite awareness, which could track his authorities across Observable Existence, which could perceive connections and threats and opportunities through Countable progressions that extended endlessly, found no trace of the Primordial Architect.","It was as if Beowulf had never existed.","The captured Maw hung in empty air for a moment, then dropped to the corrupted ground with confused writhing.","Noah’s eyes swept across THE Wastes with perception burning at maximum intensity.","Nothing.","No signature of THE Second Scale. No presence of platinum armor. No indication that anything beyond his own forces occupied this region at all.","Beowulf’s voice echoed from everywhere simultaneously.","\" Do you see now?\"","The words came from above and below and from every direction at once.","\" Do you understand what you are facing?\"","Noah turned, searching for the source, finding nothing his perception could lock onto.","And then existence flickered meters away from his position.","THE Primordial Armor bloomed back into perceivable reality with casual ease. The massive armored form had relocated from its seated position to a location directly beside Noah, its enormous helm staring down at him through the midst of his Absolutes as if the army surrounding them was irrelevant.","Beowulf towered over Noah with proximity that should have been impossible to achieve without his awareness tracking the movement.","The visor oriented downward, platinum plates close enough that Noah could see his own reflection in their surfaces.","\" Do you see?\"","The words pressed against his existence from point-blank range.","\" Do you understand?\"","THE Primordial Armor’s helm tilted slightly.","\" With this established, we can get past all the unpleasant stuff and make things easy now.\"","...!","Noah stood surrounded by hundreds of Absolutes, and none of them had perceived Beowulf moving until the Primordial Architect chose to be perceived again.","The gap.. was not something he could overcome through accumulated power.","The gap was something else entirely!"]},{"number":4992,"title":"Chapter 4992: Chapter 4991: Finite I","paragraphs":["An existence he could not touch.","An existence he might not be able to see.","By all means, Noah had hit a brick wall. His Geodesic Negation had passed through the armored titan like wind through empty space. His Maws had phased through platinum surfaces without finding purchase. His most devastating offensive forces had proven meaningless against something that existed on levels his authority could not reach.","And yet no despair took him, for he had to keep moving forward.","There was always a path. There was always an angle. There was always something that Infinity could find when bounded powers declared impossibility. He simply needed to discover what that something was, and he could not do that while standing still and accepting defeat.","This gaze of defiance burned in his eyes as he looked up at THE Primordial Armor.","Beowulf saw it.","The massive armored form rose from its position beside Noah, platinum plates shifting with amusement that communicated itself through their arrangement. The helm tilted as if examining something mildly interesting, and the visor oriented toward those defiant eyes with appreciation that bordered on mockery.","\" As expected, there is that gaze of defiance.\"","\" Well, if you wish to make things difficult, I can also take the easiest path.\"","The armored titan gestured casually toward the broken figure of Alexander still suspended in corrupted air behind its massive form.","\" The Peacemaker. The one you came to save. I will collapse him in the next few seconds if you do not open yourself up to me.\"","A pause.","\" Do we want to have that melodrama?\"","...!","Noah looked ahead with expression that had gone somber, his blue-gold eyes taking in the scene before him with calculation running beneath their surface. The threat was clear. The leverage was obvious.","But Noah’s voice, when it emerged, carried words that seemed incongruent with reality.","\" But you no longer have the Peacemaker.\"","...!","The statement made no sense.","Alexander’s broken form still hung in the corrupted air behind Beowulf, cellular fragments twitching with the aftermath of torture that had lasted eons in subjective experience. The Peacemaker was exactly where THE Primordial Armor had placed him, suspended like a trophy, like leverage, like bait that had successfully drawn the Infinity-bearer into confrontation.","But the moment the words were uttered, something changed.","SAA!","A neon light flashed across the corrupted Wastes with speed that made Absolute perception seem slow.","At Noah’s side, a certain space had become empty.","Skoll was no longer there.","The loyal companion who had stood beside his master throughout this confrontation, the very good boy whose Infinite-enhanced form had waited with serious expression while impossible odds accumulated around them, had moved.","And the lifeform that had been as fast as an Absolute when it was not an Absolute, now carrying Noah’s Infinities burning in its foundations, could traverse across those Infinities even faster than Noah himself.","This was why Noah had brought Skoll along.","For this moment.","\" Ho?\"","THE Primordial Armor turned to look behind itself with visor communicating appreciation through platinum arrangement. The space where Alexander had been suspended was empty. The broken Peacemaker’s cellular fragments no longer hung in corrupted air behind the armored titan.","Beowulf actually nodded.","\"A decent surprise, Infinity-bearer.\"","The acknowledgment carried genuine respect!","\" But... \"","The word hung in the corrupted air with weight that pressed against Noah’s consciousness.","And then the whimper reached his ears.","From the endless stretches of Infinity where Skoll should have been far away by now, carrying Alexander across connections that spanned Observable Existence, the sound of a dog being hurt echoed through pathways that only Infinite awareness could perceive. Pain and confusion transmitted through bonds that Noah had established with his loyal companion, and his expression became heavier as he understood what that sound meant.","He moved instantly.","Noah appeared at the edge of the region where his Infinite Absolute Seals scattered throughout the corrupted proto-matter marked the boundary of Beowulf’s influence. From one of those Seals, from a connection that should have led to safety, Skoll and Alexander were spat out as if their traversal across Infinity had been rejected. The loyal companion’s neon form tumbled across corrupted ground while the broken Peacemaker collapsed beside him.","Noah arrived beside them in the same moment.","His hands moved without hesitation, pulling a lotus petal from his authority and forcing it into Alexander’s shattered existence. The Sacred Herb’s power began integrating with the Peacemaker’s cellular fragments, Bounded Countable Infinity flowing into foundations that desperately needed reinforcement.","But Skoll...","Half of the loyal companion’s body was missing.","The neon light that usually blazed with eager energy now flickered weakly across a form that had been torn apart by whatever had rejected their escape. The remaining portions were deteriorating rapidly, existence unraveling as corruption from Beowulf’s authority ate through Infinite-enhanced flesh.","Noah released beams of blue-gold Countable Infinity directly onto Skoll’s failing form.","Multiple Primus Inevitabilities arrived around him simultaneously, the entire army repositioning to surround their master and his wounded companions. Their massive tentacled forms created layers of protection while the Vital Chorus Absolutes added their green-gold-blue healing light to Noah’s efforts.","The deterioration stalled.","Then it began reversing, flesh reforming where flesh had been torn away, neon light stabilizing where neon light had been fading. Skoll completely healed.","But when Noah looked around at his defensive forces, the cost of that single escape attempt became horrifyingly clear.","His Infinite Bulwarks, the Absolutes who had sacrificed all offensive capability for defensive perfection, stood in formation around him. But nearly all of them were torn in half. Their crystalline plates of obsidian-gold had been shattered. Their layered tentacles had been severed. Their Infinite defenses, which had absorbed the combined assault of an Undivided One and three Formless Terrors without yielding a single inch, had been ripped through like paper.","One hundred eighty-nine Absolute Infinite Bulwarks had been collapsed.","The damage that had reached Skoll had first passed through nearly two hundred Absolutes designed specifically to prevent damage from reaching anything behind them. Beowulf had not seriously attacked. Beowulf had not even seemed to move. And yet a single casual gesture to prevent Alexander’s escape had torn through defenses that should have been impenetrable.","An instant later, the collapsed Bulwarks were Infinitely revived where they stood.","Their forms reformed from the Bounded Countable Infinity burning in their foundations, flesh and plate and tentacle reconstituting according to patterns that could not be permanently destroyed. The Infinite Hunger Stacks they had accumulated, the stored damage from the earlier demonstration, fueled their restoration alongside the authority Noah invested in their continued existence.","But the message had been delivered.","Even without having seriously attacked, just a single move Noah had made to save Alexander, to bring the Peacemaker to his side, had collapsed multiple Absolutes that needed to be revived again.","THE Primordial Armor looked over from a distance with visor that communicated brilliant satisfaction.","\" That was nice.\"","The words carried appreciation that made them worse than mockery.","\" But this entire place now falls under my weavings.\"","Beowulf’s helm tilted slightly.","\" Nothing here may leave.\"","WAA!"]},{"number":4993,"title":"Chapter 4993: Chapter 4992: Finite II","paragraphs":["The armored titan gestured broadly at the region surrounding them, at the corrupted Wastes that had become a prison the moment Noah entered it.","\" It is like you had little Alexander there in one area of a burning fire, and you simply moved him to another area where you are standing.\"","A pause.","\" You are now standing together, but so what?\"","The visor oriented toward Noah with weight that pressed against his consciousness from across the distance between them.","\" Infinity-bearer, you are still burning inside this endless ring of fire.\"","HUUM!","The sound resonated through existence itself as THE Primordial Armor raised both massive gauntlets toward the sky.","And then, for surrounding light years in every direction, a crimson fiery ring of undifferentiation rose from the corrupted Wastes and encircled absolutely everything.","The ring blazed with authority that made the corruption saturating this region seem mild by comparison. It stretched upward and outward until it formed a dome, a barrier, a prison of undifferentiation that enclosed Noah and his forces and Alexander and Skoll and everything else within its burning circumference. The crimson light cast shadows across the corrupted ground that seemed to writhe with hunger for anything that tried to pass through.","Nothing would leave this place without Beowulf’s permission.","Nothing would escape this ring of fire that had no gaps, no weaknesses, no angles that Infinite perception could find.","It was a devastating scene.","And yet amidst it all, Noah turned his attention back to Alexander.","He made sure Skoll was okay first, running his perception across the loyal companion’s reforming body until he confirmed that the deterioration had fully reversed and the very good boy was healing properly.","Then Noah looked at the Peacemaker.","His hands waved again, infusing multiple Absolute Everythings into Alexander’s shattered existence while the healing of the Vital Chorus Absolutes focused their green-gold-blue light upon the cellular fragments that still twitched with the aftermath of torture.","But even then, Alexander’s existence was barely being stitched together.","The damage Beowulf had inflicted was too intricate.","Absolute Primus Inevitabilities surrounded them like impenetrable shields.","But before the grand Primordial Architect who had torn through one hundred eighty-nine of them with a casual gesture, would they truly be of any use?","\"...\"","Noah looked at Alexander as the Peacemaker slowly healed beneath the combined authority being poured into his shattered form.","The man who had endured millions of years of torture rather than give Noah up was trembling. His segmented body shook with echoes of pain that even Infinite healing could not immediately erase, and his eyes, though still holding that defiance that had survived everything Beowulf inflicted, now also held something that looked like grief.","Noah held that gaze for a moment, something unspoken passing between them that words could not have carried.","Then he looked away from Alexander and toward Beowulf.","THE Primordial Armor waited at the center of its domain with patience that spoke of absolute confidence. The crimson ring of fire blazed around them. The corrupted Wastes pressed against their existence. The gap between THE First Scale and THE Second Scale stretched impossibly vast between the army of Absolutes and the single armored titan that had demonstrated their helplessness with casual efficiency.","In Noah’s mind, countless threads of Infinite Undifferentiated Fate swirled with possibilities that his perception was desperately trying to find.","How would he get out of this?","The options were few.","Infinite Undifferentiated Fate churned and churned within Noah’s awareness, golden threads extending through connections and possibilities and pathways that should have led toward escape. He pushed his perception further, reaching across the Countable progressions of his authority, searching for angles that his conscious mind had not yet identified.","But the threads held no weavings.","Every path led back to the crimson ring of fire. Every possibility terminated against the qualitative gap between THE First Scale and THE Second Scale. Every angle his Infinity could find was an angle that Beowulf’s authority had already closed.","He had made it his goal not to reverse time, not to use an Anchor Point. But he also inherently knew right now that against THE Second Scale, even THE Existential Paradox Loop would not work. The gap was too vast!","The answer was as he always knew.","With Infinity.","But he could not find it. He could not perceive the angle that would make his endless authority meaningful against something that simply chose not to interact with THE First Scale. He could not...","HUUM!","In the next moment, Noah’s expression became one of anger as he bellowed a single word toward something only he could perceive.","\" No!\"","The word pressed against the corrupted Wastes with weight that made the proto-matter tremble, and in its wake, an illusory manifestation began forming beside him. RUINATION emerged from the connection they shared, her avatar taking shape with elegance that characterized her existence.","She gazed toward the enemy ahead with immensity that spoke of what she truly was, the weaponized aspect of Noah’s Infinite authority given form and consciousness. Her attention fixed upon Beowulf with calculation running beneath her gold-blue depths.","But Noah’s denial had not been directed at RUINATION.","It had been directed at another.","At the sister of RUINATION who had just sent him a message across their connection, a message that spoke of arrival, of embodiment, of combining her immensity with his foundations to face what he could not face alone. THE Infiniverse had communicated that if she fully embodied herself into him, if they put together the weight of everything she contained, this situation may be salvageable.","But bringing her here would jeopardize everything else.","It would jeopardize her. It would jeopardize the entire Infiniverse. It would jeopardize every being within her vast interior, every developing force that Noah had built across his journey.","So he said no. That he would find another way.","But on this day, for the first time in existence since her conception, THE Infiniverse did not listen.","\"I am sorry, Master.\"","The words emerged with weight that made Noah’s anger pulse as it was now moreso directed to himself, and then she was there. THE Infiniverse appeared beside her sister’s illusory form, her avatar manifesting with presence that carried the accumulated immensity of everything she contained.","For the first time in her existence, she did not follow the commands of her master.","She had come anyway.","Noah looked at THE Infiniverse with a complex expression burning in his blue-gold eyes.","She did not look back at him.","Her gaze remained fixed upon Beowulf, upon the armored titan that waited at the center of this prison of crimson fire, upon the threat that had drawn her here despite her master’s explicit command to stay away. She stared ahead with composure that seemed unshakeable, with presence that seemed unaffected by Noah’s obvious anger!","But one could barely perceive her hand trembling.","The tremor was subtle, almost invisible against the backdrop of power and authority that surrounded her avatar. And it was not from fear of THE Primordial Armor. It was not from recognition of the impossible odds they faced or the danger that coming here represented.","It was from the fact that she could see her master was angry at her and at himself for the first time.","This was why she could not look back!"]},{"number":4994,"title":"Chapter 4994: Chapter 4993: Finite III","paragraphs":["THE Primordial Armor observed this scene with visor that communicated interest.","Massive gauntlets came together in what could only be described as applause, the sound booming across the corrupted Wastes with weight that made the crimson ring of fire flicker.","\" How quaint.\"","The words emerged with amusement.","\" Are these supposed to be reinforcements? More things for me to experiment with?\"","Beowulf’s visor oriented toward THE Infiniverse with attention that made Noah’s anger transform into something colder.","\"In that one...\"","The armored titan pointed toward THE Infiniverse with shining interest.","\" On that one, I also sense Infinity and a bit more. What a work of wonder.\"","The helm tilted.","\" This will certainly work even better.\"","HUUM!","THE Primordial Armor moved.","The massive form that had been content to demonstrate and mock and establish the gap between Scales now surged into motion with speed that should have been impossible for something so vast. Its massive hand reached toward Noah and everyone around him, toward RUINATION and THE Infiniverse and Alexander and Skoll and the army of Absolutes that surrounded them all.","Noah looked at the hand of this massive entity at THE Second Scale of Existence.","His eyes burned with defiance that had not dimmed despite everything he had witnessed. His foundations blazed with Countable Infinity that meant nothing against something operating on fundamentally different levels of reality. His army stood ready to defend him against an assault they could not defend against.","And yet what could he do?","At such a time, a voice reached his awareness.","It was deep and heavy and filled with frustration that bordered on disgust!","\" This is...maddening to watch.\"","The voice did not seem to come from any direction. It simply existed within his perception, present without source, heard without origin.","\" You hold Infinity in our Observable Existence. You hold an endless sea.\"","A pause that communicated exasperation beyond what words could express.","\" Why do you keep channeling it through a straw? Why?\"","The frustration intensified.","\" Bah. I am leaving. I cannot watch this anymore.\"","...!","The voice faded as quickly as it had appeared.","Noah heard it as the presence departed, and something about its cadence, something about it reminded him immensely of THE Mnemonic Leviathan.","But the content of those complaints resonated within him!","He looked at the incoming hand of THE Primordial Armor.","Channeling an endless sea through a straw.","The words pulled forth something he knew but did not know. Something he understood but did not understand. Something that had lingered in the back of his mind since the moment he first touched Infinity, a truth he had never allowed himself to fully face.","HUUM!","His existence began to buzz with recognition that trembled through his foundations.","At this time, he was forced to face it.","In this moment of unprecedented danger where many things were at stake, in the face of an impossible enemy, in the presence of those who had come to stand beside him despite his commands otherwise, he had to face it.","The answer was Infinity.","He had thought this when he came here. He had believed it with everything he was. His authority was endless. His potential was unlimited. His power extended in sequences that would never terminate.","But there was something he feared.","He always knew it, lurking beneath the surface of his consciousness like something he could not bear to examine directly. But he could never bring himself to think of it, much less say it. He entirely blocked it within his mind and psyche, walling it away behind certainties and achievements and the accumulated weight of everything he had accomplished.","He was without Fear or Doubt.","And yet on this one thing, he was fearful to even admit it. It was paradoxical.","It felt like a violation of who he was to think it. It felt like it would break his very Civilization if he thought it, much less say it. The words seemed dangerous in ways that THE Second Scale did not, threatening in ways that Primordial Architects could never match.","But at this moment, he knew he had to.","He was afraid of the outcome as it was the one unknown of his existence, but that outcome might be exactly what he needed right now. Maybe. Maybe!","So before things became catastrophic, before the massive hand reached him and everyone he cared about, he opened his mouth to say what he thought he would never say.","\"I have Infinite Mana.\"","The words emerged with weight that pressed against reality.","\"I have laid the Claim to THE First Tongue.\"","His voice trembled with something that he did not allow himself to feel.","\" And yet I... I...\"","HUUM!","Existence began to buzz and tremble around him.","His own body began to buzz and tremble with warnings that seemed to emerge from his very foundations. His Civilization itself seemed to scream at him through sensations that had no name, through pressure that had no source, through urgency that communicated a single desperate message.","Do not say what you were about to say!","But...","DUM !","Noah felt the beat of his heart.","He closed his eyes and placed his hand on his chest, feeling the rhythm that had carried him through everything since his existence began. The beat was there beneath his palm, steady and present.","DUM!","The beat was melodious.","The beat was heavy.","It reminded him of his mother. Of his son. Of his women. He thought of himself, of everything he had been and everything he had become and everything he still wanted to be. As much as he wanted to say he had to do this for them, he actually had to do it for himself.","So he forced himself to finish the words.","\"I... Am Not Infinite.\"","...!","BOOM!","\"I...Am Finite.\"","...!","The beat of his heart could no longer be heard.","His body became unfathomably still in ways that transcended mere physical cessation. The flickering blue-gold flames of Infinity that had surrounded him, the aura that had defined his existence across his entire journey, simply disappeared.","The immensity around him vanished.","At this moment, he seemed no more than just a man. As if all authority had left him due to the words he said!","His robes dimmed from blazing blue-gold to simple fabric. His Depth no longer gave off any heaviness, no longer pressed against reality with the weight of what he carried. Everything about him seemed mundane, seemed ordinary, seemed like nothing more than a mortal standing in the midst of powers that should have crushed him without effort.","THE Infiniverse turned toward him with shock and incredulity.","RUINATION’s cold composure cracked.","And yet after saying something he had been terrified of saying, Noah felt...an unfathomable sense of freedom.","DUM!","He began to feel the beat of his heart again.","It was not grand or heavy. It was normal. It was mundane. It was the simple rhythm of a finite existence that had somehow come to wield something endless.","And yet when he looked at the massive incoming hand of THE Primordial Architect at an entirely different Scale of Existence, he had a thought that surprised him more than anything else that had occurred in this confrontation.","This hand did not seem so insurmountable.","Because for all of his existence, he was a Finite Being using Infinity who had been scared to even admit it.","At this moment in the history of Observable Existence, THE Genesis Monarch was finally truthful with himself.","He was not Infinite. He was finite. And in that simple, paradoxical, seemingly mundane statement that should have diminished him but somehow did not, everything would change.","Noah raised his right hand that still trembled as he...flung it forth simply.","HUUUM!","At this time, the color blue unlike any other, at any point in time...flourished.","And that massive unreachable hand of THE Primordial Armor that he could not even touch before...","BOOM!","Was smacked away."]},{"number":4995,"title":"Chapter 4995: Chapter 4994: Sensation I","paragraphs":["It was an odd sensation.","Admitting something he always knew but did not want to think about had placed him here, in this moment, facing truths he had walled away behind achievements and certainties and the accumulated weight of everything he had accomplished. For all his past, he had been trying to infuse his existence with Infinities. His Infinite Formless Depth. His infinite foundation. An infinite this, an infinite that. Layer upon layer of endlessness crammed into every aspect of his being.","But no matter how many parts of himself he infused with Infinities, the core of who he was remained finite.","His mind was finite. His mentality was finite. His identity was finite. And every time he tried cramming Infinity into something finite, he limited it. Every time he expressed Infinity through himself, he constrained it. He was a straw trying to channel an ocean, and no matter how wide he made the straw, it would never be the ocean itself.","Even if he was successful on his previously set path, even if he continued cramming aspects of Infinity into himself and changed absolutely everything about his existence, there would still be Noah Osmont. His identity would always be finite because identity itself was a finite thing. For Noah Osmont to truly be Infinite was to no longer be Noah Osmont at all.","He was Noah Osmont because he was a son.","He was Noah Osmont because he was a father.","He was Noah Osmont because he was a husband, a leader, a builder of Civilizations, someone who cared about specific people and specific outcomes and specific futures.","He would have to lose this very identity if he were to truly cram in all of Infinity. At that point, he would become something else entirely. The same as the Principles themselves. A loose law of existence. One of the endless strings that held together Observable Existence.","He would not be Noah Osmont because he would no longer care about the things Noah Osmont cared about. He would be everything and nothing that resembled the person who had started this journey.","He could not not be him.","So he would have always remained finite.","But even saying this had been a frightening thing, because he had always asked himself a question that lurked beneath all his achievements and all his confidence. What if he lost his Infinity?","That would be equally catastrophic. He would have lost such a significant part of himself, the authority that had defined him since the moment Mana first changed everything. Without Infinity, what was he? Without that endless potential, who was Noah Osmont?","So he had locked away this thought.","He had not even thought about it.","He had built walls around it so thoroughly that even his own consciousness could not perceive what he was hiding from himself. The fear was not that he was finite. The fear was that admitting it would somehow take away the Infinity he had gained, that speaking the truth would make the truth punish him for acknowledging it.","But he had to face it eventually.","Today, he admitted and declared it.","And he felt... free.","But it was unfathomably hard to explain how he felt beyond that single word.","He felt empty in a way that should have been terrifying but somehow was not. Those immense waves of power that had always surrounded him, that immensity of his Depth and the weight he could press down to change existence itself, he felt like all of it was gone. The blue-gold flames that had defined his presence since his advancement into Absolute had vanished. The pressure that made lesser beings tremble in his vicinity had disappeared.","He truly felt normal, as if he had returned back to that day before he even utilized that fireball skill book so long ago. That mundane Noah Osmont who had been nothing special, just someone going about their day to day. Just surviving, but not really...living.","But at the same time, he did not feel normal.","What he could see now was truly hard to explain.","The massive hand of THE Primordial Armor, for example. He could not even touch the body of this existence before. His Geodesic Negations had passed through like wind through open windows. His Maws had phased through platinum surfaces without finding purchase. Beowulf existed at THE Second Scale, a level of reality that THE First Scale simply could not interact with unless THE Second Scale chose to permit interaction.","That hand was coming at him unfathomably fast.","It should have been impossible to perceive, let alone respond to. The gap between Scales meant that Beowulf’s movements occurred on levels that beings at THE First Scale could not process. The hand should have reached him before he even registered that it had moved.","But at this moment, Noah felt like he could perceive it.","More than perceive it. He felt like he could understand it.","The hand was massive and terrible and carried authority that should have crushed everything it touched. But it was still just a hand. It was still just force being directed toward a target. And force, no matter how vast, could be met with other force if that other force was sufficient.","Noah did not want this hand to reach him and his people.","So he raised his own hand and tried smacking it away.","Instinctively.","Not with technique. Not with methodology. Not with any of the refined expressions of authority he had developed across his journey. He simply saw something coming toward those he cared about, and he responded in the most basic way possible.","He tried to push it away.","And...","HUUM!","Noah felt his eyes radiate with blue unlike anything he had experienced before.","Not the blue-gold that had characterized his Infinity. Not the crimson-blue. This was pure, fundamental blue that seemed to exist before color itself had been differentiated, a shade that predated the concepts of light and spectrum and visual perception entirely.","Then, for a brief moment, Noah felt something that exceeded everything he had ever experienced.","He was connected to an endless sea.","The sensation was overwhelming in its simplicity. He was not containing the sea. He was not drawing from the sea. He was not trying to fit the sea inside himself. He was simply connected to it, aware of it, able to feel its presence stretching out in every direction simultaneously.","And he could, with a little exertion, pull on this endless sea to do what he wanted.","The sea was the force of all Infinity in Observable Existence.","He could feel it now in ways he had never felt it before. The Infinity stretched out across corrupted proto-matter in THE Prima Indifferentia. The Infinity burning in THE Living Paradox. The Infinity that THE Primordial Paradox now carried after receiving the Lotus petal. The Infinity within THE Infiniverse who stood beside him at this very moment.","But it extended further than that.","The Infinity scattered across THE Wastes in every Seal he had ever placed. The Infinity burning in the foundations of every Primus Inevitability he had elevated. The Infinity growing in the Sacred Herbs of his cultivation sites. The Infinity that had spread through Observable Existence since the moment he first touched endless Mana. The Infinity of The First Tongue itself.","It could not truly be contained.","The only reason he was pulling what he was pulling, the only limitation on what he could access, was his own finite capacity. His finite mind could only direct so much. His finite comprehension could only process so many threads simultaneously. The sea was endless, but the one giving commands to that sea was not.","And somehow, that limitation did not diminish what was happening.","It defined it.","Noah channeled boundless Infinity not through him, not through his finite being that would have constrained it into shapes his existence could process. He simply directed it where he wanted it to go. He was the conductor. The Infinity was the orchestra. And the symphony they produced together did not need to fit inside him to be played.","He pointed at the incoming hand.","He willed the endless sea to respond.","And so, it had responded.","HUUUUM!"]},{"number":4996,"title":"Chapter 4996: Chapter 4995: Sensation II","paragraphs":["Endless blue had bloomed in front of him with radiance that defied description.","The color was so blinding that many beings had to instinctively turn their gazes away. THE Infiniverse shielded her jeweled eyes. RUINATION’s illusory form flickered with interference she could not control. The Primus Inevitabilities closest to Noah found their visual receptors overwhelmed by input that exceeded their capacity to process.","Even Alexander, broken and barely conscious, flinched away from light that seemed to bypass physical perception entirely and strike directly at awareness itself.","From all around, infinite rivers of blue began converging.","They came from the corrupted proto-matter surrounding them, where Noah’s Seals had saturated existence with his authority. They came from THE Infiniverse herself, whose very being was an expression of his Infinite nature. They came from the Primus Inevitabilities, whose Bounded Countable Infinity responded to their master’s command without their control.","They came from beyond this region entirely.","Rivers of blue that should not have been able to reach this place, that should have been contained by the crimson ring of fire Beowulf had established, poured in from directions that had nothing to do with physical space. They flowed along geodesic paths that transcended normal geometry, following connections that existed because Infinity itself was connected across all of Observable Existence.","Every Seal Noah had ever placed became a source.","Every being carrying or surrounded or influenced by Infinity became a tributary. Unique waves of infinity carrying the weavings of THE Primordial Paradox flowed in. Unique waves of infinity carrying the weavings of THE Living Paradox flowed in. Weavings from things Noah was not even perceiving...any Undivided One, any Formeless Terror, any Primordial Architect who currently was influenced by infinity in any way. Any weavings surrounding THE Creature, Horus...anywhere infinity shone!","Every point of Infinity across existence that was connected to his Claim began flowing toward this single moment, this single command, this single expression of will from a finite being who had finally stopped trying to contain what could not be contained.","Infinitely fast, the rivers converged.","They did not flow into Noah.","They did not pass through his existence.","They simply gathered before him, directed by his will, shaped by his intent, unified by the simple fact that he had the authority to command them and had finally learned how to use that authority properly.","The blue became a wave.","The wave became an impact.","BOOM!","It smashed onto the palm of THE Primordial Armor with force that should not have been possible from anything at THE First Scale of Existence.","And the massive hand of the Primordial Architect was actually smashed backward.","The fingers that had been reaching toward Noah and everyone he cared about jerked away from their trajectory. The palm that should have crushed everything it touched recoiled as if struck by something it had not anticipated. The arm connected to that hand bent at angles suggesting genuine physical response to force it had not expected to feel.","Beowulf’s visor oriented toward his own hand.","The platinum plates shifted with something that communicated confusion through their arrangement. THE Primordial Armor looked at the appendage that had just been struck, examining it as if checking for damage, as if verifying that what had just happened had actually happened.","Then the visor oriented toward Noah.","\"...\"","Then back to the hand.","Nothing should have been capable of touching him. He had demonstrated this with absolute clarity!","And yet something had touched him anyway.","Noah himself looked at his own hand with similar confusion.","The limb that had directed that impossible wave was trembling slightly. His fingers tingled with sensation that had no name, residue of endless force that had passed through his command without passing through his being.","He looked at THE Primordial Armor.","The blinding brilliance of Infinity he had conjured had already faded, leaving only the corrupted Wastes and the crimson ring of fire and the two of them staring at each other across a gap that had just become more complicated than either of them had anticipated.","A heavy silence bloomed all around.","The kind of silence that followed events no one present fully understood. The kind of silence that preceded fundamental reassessment of everything that had been assumed. The kind of silence that existed between moments when reality itself was catching up to what had just occurred!","Noah Osmont had just struck a Primordial Architect at THE Second Scale of Existence!","There was so much that he wanted to understand right away.","There was so much he wanted to feel, to examine, to break down into components he could analyze and replicate! The sensation of channeling Infinity without containing it, the experience of directing an endless sea through finite will, the implications of what he had just accomplished against something that should have been untouchable.","But he had to move rapidly!","So he went by instinct at this moment, trusting the new understanding that had bloomed within him rather than trying to force it into frameworks that might not apply anymore. Did he even still have THE Civilizational Instinctus? Did those old authorities still function now that his relationship with Infinity had fundamentally changed?","He shook his head at this and focused on that same glorious sensation of channeling Infinity.","He flashed the palm of his hand behind him.","HUUUUM!","The moment he did this, infinite instantaneous emergence of boundless blue waves of light formed a conical shape that defied conventional perception. One could not truly see their origin, as it seemed like they were coming from all around simultaneously, converging from every direction at once. But they began a few inches from Noah’s palm, crystallizing into coherent form at the point where his will gave them direction.","This endless conical radiance of blue barreled out with terrifying force toward the ring that THE Primordial Architect had established around them.","The force could not be properly placed on any certain Depth!","One could say it was at THE Surface Depth, and they would be correct.","One could say it was at THE Absolute Depth, and they would also be correct.","One could say it transcended Depth entirely, existing at scales that the classification system had never been designed to measure, and they would be most correct of all.","BOOM!","This force was so boundlessly heavy that it struck the ring Beowulf had made infinitely in the span of an instant. Not once. Not a thousand times. Infinitely. Each impact arriving simultaneously with all other impacts, sequential countable progression compressed into singular expression that hit the crimson barrier with the accumulated weight of endless strikes delivered in no time at all.","BOOM!","The ring shattered gloriously!","Fragments of crimson undifferentiation scattered across THE Wastes as the beam of blue light continued extending outward, carving a path through the corruption that had served as Beowulf’s prison. The barrier that nothing at THE First Scale should have been able to breach simply ceased to exist under the weight of what Noah had directed against it.","He did not stop to ascertain or understand how he was doing what he was doing.","His finite thoughts simply moved even faster than before, processing options and executing decisions with speed that felt natural despite being unprecedented. He tapped his fingers in a gesture that should have meant nothing but somehow meant everything, and strings of blue wrapped around Skoll, around Alexander, around THE Infiniverse, around RUINATION, around every Primus Inevitability that had accompanied him here.","Their bodies instantly became pulled by endless Infinity.","They disappeared into the horizon, following the magnificent beam of blue that stretched out into the distance, carried along its trajectory by force that moved them faster than conventional travel could have achieved. One moment they were beside Noah. The next moment they were simply gone, transported away from danger through methods that his old understanding could not have produced.","...!","In what seemed to be the span of an instant, it was only Noah and THE Primordial Architect looking at each other!","Noah’s chest rose and fell with breathing that came not from exertion or tiredness, but simply from the surreal sensation of it all. Everything that had just happened, everything that was still happening, everything that his finite mind was processing while his infinite authority waited for further direction. The combination created a state he had never experienced before!","He looked at THE Primordial Architect who was looking back at him.","Beowulf’s visor communicated something that transcended confusion now. There was genuine amazement in the arrangement of platinum plates!","And then THE Primordial Armor began to laugh!"]},{"number":4997,"title":"Chapter 4997: Chapter 4996: Paradox!","paragraphs":["The platinum helm shifted. The gaps between armor segments blazed with light that spoke of delight rather than threat, and the sound that emerged was not mockery.","It was appreciation.","\" Glorious! GLORIOUS!\"","The words boomed across THE Wastes with weight that made the corrupted proto-matter tremble.","\" That actually felt like a true glimmer of Infinity! So what is this? Even though you are of a lower Scale of Existence, because you carry the force of Infinity, you can bypass unsurpassable weavings?!\"","The armored titan’s helm tilted.","\"I do not accept it! Let me see more!\"","BOOM!","An apocalyptic burst of terrifying Depth and brilliance erupted from Beowulf’s form.","In the next moment, the surroundings filled with dozens of the massive figures of THE Primordial Armor. Not illusions. Not projections. Actual bodies, each one as vast and terrible as the original, each one carrying the same authority that had demonstrated the gap between Scales with such devastating clarity. They surrounded Noah from every direction, above and below and on all sides.","Existence itself began congealing.","Everything was becoming solid in ways that transcended physical states. The air thickened into something that felt like it could be grasped, could be crushed, could be compressed into density that would collapse anything trapped within it. Noah felt like all the air had been sucked away and he needed to breathe again, as if his very existence was being folded in on itself by pressure that came from everywhere simultaneously.","It was a heavy sensation!","Noah took a deep breath.","And he blew out.","HUUUUM!","From him blowing out seemingly nothing but air, boundless seas of blue instantly surged outward with force that defied the simple action that had produced them!","The congealing solid state that had been crushing everything found itself opposed by endless expansion that refused to be compressed. The pressure that had been collapsing existence encountered pressure that pushed back infinitely!","Some of the blue waves even pushed back the multiple bodies of THE Primordial Armor that had suddenly bloomed, forcing them to shift position as force they had not anticipated struck them from angles they had not guarded.","This radiant blue sea now surrounded the region around Noah like a barrier of his own making, stopping interferences that should have overwhelmed anything at THE First Scale. The blue blazed with Infinity that was not contained within him but simply directed by him, a wall of endless authority that the finite conductor had positioned where he needed it to be!","Oh!","But THE Primordial Architect was serious now.","Even though Beowulf had been rebuffed momentarily, even though the armored titan’s attacks had been pushed back by force that should not have existed at Noah’s Scale, the being at THE Second Scale still moved at speeds Noah could barely keep up with. The gap between Scales had not been eliminated. It had simply been complicated.","Armored crimson chains of undifferentiation surged from all around.","Trillions of them.","They pierced through the radiant circular blue sea around Noah with methodology that transcended brute force. Each chain seemed to know exactly where to strike, exactly how to slip between the endless waves he had erected, exactly how to find the finite conductor at the center of the infinite defense.","\" YOU ARE JUST LEARNING WHAT TO DO WITH THIS!\"","Beowulf’s voice thundered across THE Wastes with weight that made the blue sea flicker.","\"I WILL CHAIN YOU UP BEFORE YOU CAN EVEN UNDERSTAND WHAT YOU HAVE IN YOUR HANDS!\"","For the first time since his new state of mind, Noah felt a sense of danger.","Not the abstract recognition of threat he had maintained throughout this confrontation. Actual danger. The kind that made his finite instincts scream warnings that his infinite authority could not entirely dismiss. This entity at THE Second Scale of Existence was truly serious now, truly committed to capturing what had just demonstrated capabilities that exceeded all expectations.","He had stayed behind because he still wanted to see just how large the gap was even after achieving this new state of mind. He had wanted to test his new understanding against the impossible odds that had defined this confrontation from the beginning. But this monstrous being was right.","He was still learning about this and how to utilize it.","He needed time.","\" You...should have left with those you sent away when you had the chance.\"","Even before these words fully finished, Noah saw what was coming.","Above him, massive bodies of THE Primordial Armor with armored chains shooting toward his position.","Below him, more bodies emerging from corrupted proto-matter with chains already extending.","On all other directions of existence, the dozens of Beowulf’s forms had coordinated their assault into a cage that was closing around him from every conceivable angle.","But worse than the chains, worse than the bodies, worse than the physical assault that was converging on his position from all directions simultaneously, were the words.","In crimson obsidian letters and writing, etched across existence itself like banners that had been hung by authority that transcended normal expression, Noah saw the words that said:","| Existence is Bound and Not Bound|","These simple words seemingly repeated thousands of times, surrounding him from every direction, layered over each other until they formed walls of paradoxical declaration that pressed against everything they touched. They seemed grander than Embodiments. They seemed grander than Apophasis!","The speed was so terrifying that when Noah looked at everything surrounding him, he felt heavy undifferentiated weavings of Paradox constraining everything he was.","\" Paradox?\"","DUM!","Everything slowed down.","Noah felt that heavy beat of his heart again, the same rhythm that had anchored him when he first admitted his finite nature. The same steady pulse that had reminded him of his mother and his son and his women and everything that made him who he was rather than what he wielded.","THE Primordial Architect was trying to constrain him with Paradox.","But he was a finite being with Infinity.","What was more paradoxical than this?","Could anyone in Observable Existence be more paradoxical than him? He was finite and yet he wielded the boundless. Every aspect of his current existence was a contradiction that should not have been able to exist, and yet here he was, existing anyway.","The moment he had this thought, he moved by instinct once more.","He actually closed his eyes.","He placed his hand on his chest, feeling that finite heartbeat that served as his anchor to everything he was.","And he said lightly, almost gently:","\" Paradox.\"","As if he was coaxing it.","As if he was calling it.","As if he was inviting an old friend to join him rather than commanding a force to serve him.","When he opened his eyes, the marvellous scene that greeted him exceeded everything that had come before.","The blue seas around him were changing.","The radiant Infinity that had surrounded his position transformed, color shifting from the pure blue of endless potential into glorious paradoxical gold that blazed with weight his perception could barely process. This golden light shot upward and downward and in all other directions simultaneously, expanding outward with speed that matched the crimson chains that had been converging on his position.","It burned away the armored chains as they tried to reach him.","It burned away the paradoxical words that had been etched out like shields all around.","It burned away the very methodology Beowulf had been using to constrain him, treating the paradoxical weavings of a being at THE Second Scale as fuel rather than obstacle!","This Paradox felt boundlessly heavy and ancient.","It was not any normal Paradox.","It was THE Paradox.","It was THAT Primordial Paradox, the authority that THE Primordial Paradox himself had wielded since existence began, the aspect of the Oldest Paradox of Existence.","For the first time since his change, a prompt bloomed before Noah.","|For the first time in your existence, you are fully and truly expressing an extremely pure version of one of the Aspects of the Oldest Paradox of Existence: Paradox.|","|In addition to THE First Tongue, you have now expressed weavings of Paradox.|","...!","Noah was speechless.","He reached his hands out toward the boundlessly paradoxical gold that surrounded him, watching as the endless weavings of gold wrapped around his hand as if he could command them. And he could. The Paradox responded to his direction the same way the Infinity had responded, recognizing his authority not because he contained it but because he had the right to conduct it.","He grabbed onto these endless weavings of Paradox.","He looked toward THE Primordial Architect with eyes that were shining with a dim gold brilliance now, the blue and gold mixing in his gaze to create something that had never existed in Observable Existence before this moment.","\"I... will come back to fulfill my oath to you.\"","The words emerged with weight that pressed against THE Wastes themselves.","\"I just need some time to learn.\"","...!","The words were heavy and ridiculous.","A finite being at THE First Scale telling a Primordial Architect at THE Second Scale that he would return. That he needed time to learn. That the oath he had sworn would be fulfilled regardless of the gap between them!","It should have been the kind of statement that prompted mockery, the kind of declaration that a superior being would dismiss with casual contempt.","But Beowulf did not mock.","Beowulf did not dismiss.","In the next moment, Noah’s hand pulled down.","The endless boundless spreading seas of Paradox responded to his command, wrapping around his existence with golden light that blazed with the same contradictory nature he had just invoked. His figure was instantly swept away, paradoxically, as if he had never been here to begin with.","One moment he was standing before THE Primordial Armor.","The next moment there was simply empty space where he had been.","Not transportation. Not teleportation. Not any conventional method of movement that could be tracked or pursued.","He had simply ceased being here and become somewhere else, because Paradox permitted things that normal reality did not allow.","All that was left was an array of dozens of massive bodies of an entity at THE Second Scale of Existence.","Beowulf’s armored heads looked at the empty space where Noah had been, the platinum plates of each helm shifting with an expression that communicated dissatisfaction. Something so pristine had slipped right between his grasp. Something with potential that exceeded anything he had encountered in eons had escaped before he could properly examine it.","The armored titan was about to turn away to begin his search when something made him pause.","He turned around.","He looked toward all directions, his multiple bodies orienting in different angles as if trying to locate something his perception could barely perceive. There was a gaze somewhere out there.","Beowulf frowned, or produced the plate arrangement that suggested frowning.","He sensed nothing now.","He grunted with dissatisfaction.","Endless undifferentiation spilled from his form like a surging sea, corruption spreading across THE Wastes as his authority saturated the region!"]},{"number":4998,"title":"Chapter 4998: Chapter 4997: Research I","paragraphs":["Noah felt like he was stumbling through boundless Paradox.","Golden weavings wrapped around his existence as he moved through space that was not space, traveling across distances that should have required eons to traverse. The Paradox carried him with contradictory logic that permitted what should have been impossible, moving him somewhere while simultaneously keeping him nowhere, existing in transit while never truly being in transit at all.","Then the golden gave way to blue.","Paradox transformed into Infinity the further he went, the weavings shifting from borrowed authority to native authority as his own endless nature reasserted itself. He was no longer riding contradiction. He was riding sequence, progression, the simple forward momentum of something that extended without termination.","And when the Infinity finally released him, when he emerged from that endless glimmer of blue into coherent space once more, Noah found himself unfathomable distances away from where THE Primordial Architect had been.","THE Wastes were gone.","The crimson ring of fire was gone.","Beowulf and his dozens of massive bodies were gone.","Noah stood now in a place that defied description.","THE Wandering Territories.","That was how far an instant of Infinity had taken him.","Multicolored weavings flowed all around his position like rivers of liquid light moving through substanceless void. Reality here existed in layers that overlapped without truly touching, planes of existence stacked upon each other.","Colors that had no names pulsed through the environment, bleeding into each other and separating again.","Impossibilities drifted past him like debris carried on invisible currents. Fragments of space folded in on themselves, creating pocket dimensions that existed for moments before collapsing back into the chaotic flow. Light bent around objects that were not there, casting shadows from sources that could not be identified.","Everything seemed to exist at multiple scales simultaneously.","The Wandering Territories were where lost things gathered, where broken pieces of existence accumulated, where the boundaries between what was and what was not became suggestions rather than laws.","And Noah stood at the center of it all, looking not at the chaos around him but at himself.","His blue-gold robes were no longer so showy.","The blazing radiance that had characterized his appearance since his advancement into Absolute had dimmed to something softer, something less externally impressive. His existence did not seem as heavy and grand as before, did not press against reality with the weight of what he carried in the way that had defined him for so long.","To an outside observer, he might have seemed diminished.","But what he could do now was ridiculously marvelous.","A finite being that was unleashed. He had basically stopped standing in his own way, no longer limiting Infinity with his finite nature. He had only arrived here, only achieved this impossible transit across Observable Existence in a single instant, because he had finally been truthful with himself about his own fears.","He was without Fear and Doubt.","And yet he still had fear.","How paradoxical.","Noah looked at his hands that had pulled genuine Paradox from the endless sea.","Could he... do the same for Chaos and Existence?","The genuine Aspects of those weavings, the authorities that beings like THE Primordial Chaos and THE Creature wielded as native expressions of their nature, could he direct those as well?","He had many questions.","But there was the matter of the voice that had led him to admit his own finite nature.","Noah breathed out slowly.","When he wanted to ground himself in this new state of his existence, when he sought an anchor that would keep his finite identity coherent amid the infinite forces he now conducted rather than contained, he found his...","DUM!","His heartbeat.","He found his heartbeat helped him greatly. It was the last thing he had heard before admitting his finite nature, that heavy rhythm that had reminded him of his mother and his son and his women and everything that made him who he was. And it was the first thing he had heard after his admission, the simple mundane beat of a mortal heart.","His heartbeat was the anchor.","His heartbeat was what kept Noah Osmont coherent while wielding authorities that should have scattered his consciousness across infinite perspectives.","He focused on that rhythm while speaking aloud.","\" Thank you for the words that forced me to admit something about myself.\"","His voice carried across the chaotic flows of the Wandering Territories, pressing against the multicolored weavings with weight that belonged to THE First Tongue.","\" Who... are you?\"","The voice that had rung out with frustration during his confrontation with Beowulf. The voice that had called him maddening to watch. The voice that had asked why he kept channeling an endless sea through a straw before departing with disgust.","Was it another Primordial Architect? Something at THE Second Scale?","Or something even more unique?","Noah waited for response.","Nothing replied to him.","The Wandering Territories continued their chaotic flow around his position, multicolored weavings drifting past without acknowledgment of his question. Lost things tumbled through void that was not void.","Silence.","Noah kept his hand on his chest, feeling that finite heartbeat beneath his palm. He was getting ready to search infinitely, to extend his awareness across the endless sea he now conducted rather than contained, to find whoever had spoken to him during that critical moment.","And then...","\" What...do you understand about Infinity?\"","The voice boomed across existence with depth and majesty that exceeded anything Noah had heard before.","It was not loud in the conventional sense. Volume was irrelevant to what he perceived. The words simply existed with weight that pressed against his awareness from every direction simultaneously.","It was Deep and ancient and patient in ways that made THE Primordial Architects seem hasty. Composed in ways that made Absolutes seem emotional.","Noah smiled at the question.","\"I’m just someone who was finally able to admit that I am not the ocean.\"","His words emerged with certainty.","\" I’m the one who tells the ocean where to flow.\"","He paused.","\" What do you know about Infinity?\"","He asked such a question as sparkling star-like dots of Infinity filled everything nearby, responding to his attention with eagerness that had not existed before his admission. The endless sea was there, waiting for his direction, ready to flow wherever he commanded it to go.","And through that Infinity, through the connections that now extended from his finite awareness to every point where his authority had ever touched, Noah felt like he could see unfathomably vast.","He turned his gaze toward a certain direction.","He looked across the veils of existence and power and immensity, perception extending through layers of reality that should have been opaque to anything at THE First Scale. He saw through the Wandering Territories themselves. He saw through the boundaries that separated regions of Observable Existence. He saw through classifications and all the hierarchies that beings used to organize their understanding of what was.","And he saw a wonder that was looking at him.","...!","From the glimmers of Infinity all arouund...he received a name. A name that was told to infinity by this being, and now he learned it!","THE Beholder.","That was the only name that fit what Noah perceived, though he had no way of knowing if it was accurate.","The entity appeared as a floating eye like brilliance encased in a protective shell that seemed to be made of crystallized existence itself. At its center was a glowing spherical core that served as the actual eye, a luminous multicolored orb that could blink and look around just like a human’s might, tracking movement and focusing perception with organic fluidity that contrasted sharply with its geometric housing.","Surrounding this core were several sharp, geometric fragments that hovered in place without actually touching the center. They maintained perfect position relative to the eye despite having no visible connection, no support structure, no reason to remain where they were except that they chose to remain there. These outer pieces formed a star-like or diamond shape depending on the angle of observation, protective architecture that shielded the awareness within while permitting it to observe everything outside.","And its size constantly changed.","One moment it appeared to be a few inches across, something Noah could have held in his palm if such an action were possible. The next moment it expanded to span several gigaparsecs, becoming so vast that Wheels of Existence seemed small by comparison. Then it contracted again, then expanded differently, then existed at multiple scales simultaneously in ways that made the Wandering Territories’ shifting perspectives seem stable by comparison.","It stared at him.","He stared at it.","A moment of mutual observation that extended across distances that should have prevented any observation at all.","Then THE Beholder spoke.","\"In the age before Primordial Architects learned to call themselves ancient, before the first differentiation produced the first distinction between what was and what was not, there existed only potential.\"","The words emerged with calculated precision.","\"This potential was not Infinity as current beings understand the term. It was not sequence extending without termination. It was not density approaching limits that could not be reached. It was simply the absence of limitation itself, the state of existence before existence learned that boundaries were possible.\"","THE Beholder’s eye focused more intently upon Noah.","\"I emerged during that age. I gained cognizance when cognizance was the only thing that could be gained, when there was nothing to observe except the observation itself. Billions upon billions of eons passed in that state of pure potential, spans of duration so vast that the entirety of what beings now call Observable Existence represents merely a fraction of what came before.\"","Oh!","Noah’s eyes shone brightly!","\" When THE First Cause occurred, when differentiation and undifferentiation emerged to produce what would eventually become Primordial Architects and Absolutes and all the classifications of complex life, Infinity was present.\"","THE Beholder’s geometric shell contracted slightly, the eye within becoming more prominent.","\" The Oldest Paradox of Existence, as later beings came to call it. Four Aspects: Chaos, Existence, Paradox, and THE First Tongue. The foundational authorities from which all other authorities derived. The Keys that unlocked advancement to Civilization.\"","A pause that communicated something approaching contemplation.","\"I... reject this classification.\"","BOOM!","What?","What???!","The words emerged with coolly polite superiority that nonetheless carried absolute conviction!","\" The accepted wisdom states that Infinity is best expressed through THE First Tongue, that the linguistic nature of Observable Existence makes THE First Tongue the most suitable vehicle for Infinite expression. This wisdom is not incorrect. But it is incomplete in ways that those who repeat it fail to understand.\"","THE Beholder’s voice took on qualities that approached something like intensity, though the serene composure never wavered.","\" Infinity was present during THE First Cause alongside all other weavings. Chaos was present. Existence was present. Paradox was present. THE First Tongue was present. But consider: THE First Tongue is the language through which reality expresses itself. It is the medium of expression. Infinity is not a medium. Infinity is a state. A condition. A nature that exists independent of how it is communicated.\"","The geometric fragments rotated slowly around the central eye.","\" On THE Second Scale of Existence, where most Primordial Architects operate and where you have just demonstrated the impossible, what do you imagine those ancient beings seek? What authority do they pursue across eons of existence? What would make them capture and dissect a being like yourself rather than simply destroying you?\"","The question hung in the multicolored chaos of the Wandering Territories.","\" They seek Infinity.\"","It was a statement, not answer. Fact, not speculation!","\"Is Infinity merely something expressed through one Aspect of the Oldest Paradox of Existence? Or is Infinity its own grand separate authority, something that predates, something that exists alongside Existence? Was Infinity...not one of the ingredients of THE First Cause?\"","...!","BOOM!","Noah’s mind buzzed with unfathomable waves of wonder and possibility as at this time, the beat of his heart...felt oh so heavy!"]},{"number":4999,"title":"Chapter 4999: Chapter 4998: Research II","paragraphs":["The information was too grand.","So grand that...","The sparkling blue lights all around Noah began converging behind him with purpose that seemed almost comedic in its timing. They gathered and compressed and solidified into shape that had no business existing in this moment of existential revelation.","A chair.","The endless Infinity he now conducted had formed a chair behind him, and Noah fell onto it.","He had to sit down for this!","He genuinely had to sit down for this!","The Four Aspects of the Oldest Paradox of Existence. THE First Tongue. Existence. Chaos. Paradox.","They were the Keys of Civilization!","He had laid a Claim on Mana. On THE First Tongue. He had forged Phonemes and studied Logos and Philology and Archai and built his advancement around the linguistic architecture of Observable Existence. That was his path. That was his foundation. That was what he had believed defined his relationship with Infinity.","But before he did all of that, he had Infinity.","Before THE First Tongue. Before the Keys. Before the classifications and the methodologies and all the structures that beings used to understand how power worked.","He had Infinity.","THE Beholder was saying that he rejected the idea of the Four Aspects. That why would Infinity merely be something expressed through THE First Tongue? That during THE First Cause, Infinity was there.","By itself.","Without any expression through anything else!","...!","DUM!","Noah felt the beat of his heart again, heavy and grounding, as he thought about everything this implied.","If Infinity was its own grand thing by itself. Its own Civilization. Its own wonder that was not just expressed through THE First Tongue but existed independent of all expression entirely.","Did that not truly mean that it was THE Civilization that could become any Civilization?","He had just managed to wield Paradox by conducting Infinity. He had not spoken Phonemes. He had not invoked linguistic architecture. He had simply directed the endless sea toward an Aspect, and the Aspect had responded.","Could he...","Noah looked at his hand.","Skin, fingers, and lines across his palm that fortune tellers in his old world might have claimed held meaning. Mundane. Finite. Human in the most basic sense of what that word meant.","And yet.","\"O Chaos.\"","HUUM!","From above his palm, endless blue light began to gather with responsiveness that felt eager, that felt almost excited to demonstrate what was now possible. The blue compressed and darkened and transformed, shifting from the radiance of Infinity into something else entirely.","Obsidian light.","Chaotic obsidian light that churned with patterns that defied prediction, that moved in ways that contradicted themselves, that existed in states of constant flux without ever settling into stability.","It bloomed around Noah with majesty that exceeded anything he had consciously designed.","A black dahlia.","The flower formed from pure Chaos, its petals dark as the void between stars, its structure impossibly intricate. Each petal held endless rivers of obsidian flowing across its makeup, currents of Chaos that moved through the flower’s architecture like blood through veins. The dahlia surrounded Noah completely, massive and terrible and beautiful.","Noah looked at it mesmerizingly.","He had not claimed Chaos. He had simply directed Infinity toward that Aspect, and Infinity had expressed it because Infinity could express anything.","DUM!","His heart was pounding now.","More and more with each beat.","Simultaneously, he raised his left hand. His lips trembled as he spoke.","\" Existence.\"","HUUM!","Blue light bloomed above his other hand and transformed with the same eager responsiveness, shifting from endless potential into specific expression. But where Chaos had become obsidian darkness, this became radiant multicolored light that held every shade Observable Existence had ever produced.","The light rose upward from his palm.","It expanded and structured itself and became something grand.","A Dyson sphere.","Vibrant and beautiful, the multicolored construct represented Civilization itself made manifest. It was not a physical structure but a conceptual one, a sphere that contained the idea of what Civilization meant when taken to its ultimate expression. Worlds within worlds. Systems within systems. Life supporting life supporting life in endless cycles of existence perpetuating itself.","The sphere rotated slowly above his left hand, representing an immense Civilization that could have housed everything that had ever lived or would ever live.","...!","Noah was breathless.","But he kept going.","He could not stop now. He had to see. He had to know. He had to feel what this new understanding truly meant for everything he was and everything he could become.","\"O Paradox. O Mana!\"","HUUM!","The phenomena that bloomed behind him exceeded even what had come before.","In glorious blue-gold radiance, countless Phonemes began arranging themselves with purpose that spoke of THE First Tongue recognizing its own nature being invoked. The linguistic symbols of Observable Existence gathered and structured and became an endless book that stretched out behind Noah’s seated form.","Endless pages filled with Phonemes that had been written and Phonemes that had yet to be conceived. The book extended infinitely in all directions, containing all language that was and all language that could be, THE First Tongue made manifest as the medium through which reality expressed itself.","And beside it, intertwined with it, an endless gold and obsidian Mobius strip.","Paradox given form.","The strip twisted through dimensions that should not have permitted its geometry, a surface that had only one side and one edge despite appearing to have two of each. Gold and obsidian flowed across its surface in patterns that contradicted themselves, that existed and did not exist, that were true and false simultaneously.","THE First Tongue and Infinity were represented.","And Chaos and Existence and Paradox surrounded him.","Noah had conjured it all in one sitting.","\"...\"","It hung around him brilliantly at this moment in time. The black dahlia of Chaos with its rivers of obsidian. The multicolored Dyson sphere of Existence rotating with the weight of all Civilization. The endless Grimoire of THE First Tongue stretching infinitely. The Mobius strip of Paradox twisting through impossible geometry.","All of it responding to his direction.","All of it expressed through the Infinity he conducted rather than contained.","He could only look at it.","No prompts came because he did not want them to come. He wanted to be in this moment. He wanted to feel this Existence, this Paradox, this Chaos, this First Tongue. He wanted to exist within this unbelievable wonder that surrounded him and understand what it meant that he could produce it.","He wanted to just feel.","So he did.","In the distance, across spans of space that should have prevented any observation, THE Beholder watched.","The geometric fragments surrounding that ancient eye had expanded to their widest configuration, as if even a being who had existed since before differentiation needed to see more clearly what was occurring. The luminous core at the center of THE Beholder’s form blazed with brightness it had not displayed in eons.","After so long.","After billions upon billions of years of observation.","It was finally looking at something radiant. Something brilliant. Something that reminded it of that age of pure potential before complexity emerged to limit what existence could be.","THE Beholder spoke, and its voice carried across the Wandering Territories.","\"In the age of nothingness, potential had no form because form had not yet been conceived. Infinity was not a path or a methodology or an aspect of something greater. It was simply the nature of what existed before existence learned to have boundaries.\"","The eye focused upon Noah with attention.","\"What you display now is barely even the beginning of comprehension. But it is something I have not witnessed since that age ended and differentiation began its work of limiting what had been limitless.\"","The geometric fragments rotated with deliberate slowness.","THE Beholder’s voice deepened with significance.","\"You are beginning to go to the Civilization of Infinity itself. As what Infinity has always been and what complex life has always failed to perceive because perception itself requires limitation that Infinity does not possess. At this moment, you can be considered to have begun truly walking upon THE Civilization of Infinity.\"","BOOM!"]},{"number":5000,"title":"Chapter 5000: Chapter 4999: Research III","paragraphs":["The words of THE Beholder were always heavy to hear.","But right now, Noah seemed to be hearing them in passing, as if they were distant echoes rather than direct address. He was lost in the sensation of utilizing all Four Aspects of the Oldest Paradox of Existence simultaneously.","Chaos bloomed around him in that black dahlia of obsidian rivers.","Existence rotated above his left hand as that multicolored Dyson sphere of Civilization.","THE First Tongue stretched behind him as that endless Grimoire of Phonemes.","Paradox twisted through impossible geometry as that gold and obsidian Mobius strip.","All of it powered by Infinity that emanated from his finite form like light from a star.","And as he maintained this ridiculous display, he actually felt some form of strain. A sensation that came from something he had not actively sensed since he made his admission.","The strain came from his Depth.","When he truly looked at his existence, his Depth was still there. Even though he had declared himself finite, even though his external radiance had dimmed and his presence no longer pressed against reality with the weight it once carried, his Infinite Formless Depth remained.","But it was an odd thing.","Even though his Depth was there, paradoxically, it also was not there at the same time.","It seemed to have truly lived up to its name as his Formless Depth. Present and absent. Defined and undefined. Finite in nature while remaining Infinite in potential.","And when he dug into his existence further, when he examined the source of the strain he felt from doing this ridiculous action, he understood.","His weavings were still Countable.","Countable.","As immense as the jump he had made was, as unprecedented as his new ability to conduct rather than contain had become, the power he was currently utilizing remained Countable Infinity. Sequential. Numbered. Endless in progression but bounded in density.","Whenever he made that elevation toward Uncountable Infinity, whenever he achieved that density where infinite points existed between any two moments, what he would be able to do would be even more immense than this.","This was hit limitation as a finite being, not a limitation of infinity itself.","He could not even say this when he had not fully grasped what he could do currently.","He had to research and understand just what his current limits were. He had to explore what he could truly accomplish with the power he now held before reaching toward the next threshold.","So he opened his eyes and looked at THE Beholder in the distance.","The ancient entity looked back calmly.","Those geometric fragments maintained their expanded configuration, the luminous eye at the center tracking Noah’s attention with patience that spoke of eons of practice. There was no urgency in that gaze. No demand. Simply observation of the same quality it had maintained since before differentiation taught existence how to have boundaries.","Noah could not particularly get a read on this entity.","And the way THE Beholder was looking at him suggested that it also could not get a read on him.","He had many things that he wanted to ask. Questions about Infinity and THE First Cause and that age of nothingness and what exactly it was and why this being had chosen to speak to him during his confrontation with Beowulf.","He felt like even if he did ask, this being would not really answer.","He was about to ask anyway, because there was no harm in trying, when THE Beholder spoke first.","\" What do you think about Civilization and adversity?\"","...!","The question startled him.","It felt too simple at a glance. Too basic for a being that had existed since before complexity emerged. Too mundane for a conversation that had just covered the potential for Infinity to be its own Civilization independent of all other Keys.","But Noah also felt like he could not give too simple an answer.","He continued to test himself and his limits as he looked up at the manifestations still radiant around him. Infinity seemed to emanate from his seated form in waves of blue light, powering all four displays with authority that flowed rather than strained.","All of it around him.","All of it responding to his direction.","\" Civilization and adversity...\"","Noah spoke slowly, feeling his way through thoughts that had been building since long before this conversation began.","\" They are a unique thing. I am learning more and more about it, and as I learn, I want to question. Why adversity? Why must I struggle?\"","He paused, looking at his hands.","\"I want to change this. Struggle seems to be inherently built into existence. No matter what I do, I have to throw myself into struggles to make sure that I have enough power for when the next struggle descends. I dislike that cycle. I want to break that cycle.\"","His eyes grew distant.","\" And yet, if I do, it would feel like my Civilization has stalled and would not rise again. It feels like conflict and struggle and war is rewarded by Vakochev’s Scales. As if adversity itself is the fuel that drives advancement.\"","Noah leaned back in his chair of condensed Infinity.","\" Where I was from, the smallest versions of budding civilizations were measured in how those with no energy or Mana could kill each other. They began just fighting with their fists.\"","He raised one hand, closing it into a fist.","\" The one with the strongest physique. The one with the bigger body. They would use their fists to pummel anyone who opposed them, and their might would make them right. If you had a problem with anyone, you simply had to use your fists. That was the first expression of Civilization’s answer to adversity.\"","He opened his hand.","\" And with these weak beings trying to build a Civilization, they moved a step further. The advancements they made from their fists went to weapons. Swords and spears. Sharp and mighty. If they had conflict with anyone else, if they had adversity with anyone else, they would simply answer by swinging their swords and spears to cut them down.\"","His voice carried weight that spoke of genuine contemplation.","\" To advance their Civilizations further, they innovated and built bows and arrows. Now, if they had conflict or adversity against anyone, they could shoot them from afar. Their Civilizations had advanced to projectile warfare. They elevated the Scale of their Civilization and warfare to where ranged engagements allowed for the thinning of enemy ranks before physical contact.\"","Noah’s eyes hardened slightly.","\" From simple projectiles, they went to guns. The Scale of their Civilization and warfare drastically expanded. Battles became devastating as a single man did not simply have to rely on their fists or their sword or their bow and arrow. They could use a single gun and kill dozens. Even hundreds. You could have people that you did not even know kill each other from afar now, to accommodate the conflict and adversity of this now advanced Civilization.\"","He shook his head slowly.","\" But these Civilizations did not stop there. Adversity and conflict continued to build. They went a step further and built larger guns, faster guns. Eventually, missiles. Now a single person could operate a weapon to launch a devastating, long-range projectile that could kill hundreds or thousands. The higher the kill count rises from what a single person could do, the more advanced that Civilization was considered.\"","His voice grew heavier.","\"So the more destruction, the more adversity, all of this was rewarded. As if Vakochev’s Scales of Civilization were pervasive even at that small level.\"","...!"]}]);
